msgid "glass breaking!"
msgstr "¡cristal rompiéndose!"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "open gun safe"
msgstr "caja fuerte de armas abierta"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open gun safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A large, heavy container with thick metal walls, designed to securely store "
"firearms, weapon mods, and ammunition.  This one is wide open."
msgstr ""
"Un gran y pesado contenedor con gruesas paredes metálicas, diseñada para "
"guardar de manera segura armas de fuego, modificaciones de armas y munición."
" Esta esta abierta de par en par."

#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "open gun safe"
#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "closed gun safe"
#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "locked gun safe"
#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "jammed gun safe"
#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "electronic gun safe"
#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "safe"
#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "open safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "screeching metal!"
msgstr "¡chirrido de metal!"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "closed gun safe"
msgstr "caja fuerte de armas cerrada"

#. ~ Description of furniture "closed gun safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A large, heavy container with thick metal walls and a rotary combination "
"lock, designed to securely store firearms, weapon mods, and ammunition.  "
"This one is closed, but not locked."
msgstr ""
"Un gran y pesado contenedor con gruesas paredes metálicas, diseñada para "
"guardar de manera segura armas de fuego, modificaciones de armas y munición."
" Esta esta cerrada, pero no con llave."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "locked gun safe"
msgstr "caja fuerte de armas cerrada con llave"

#. ~ Description of furniture "locked gun safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A large, heavy container with thick metal walls and a rotary combination "
"lock, designed to securely store firearms, weapon mods, and ammunition.  If "
"you had something to pick its lock with, you could probably open it."
msgstr ""
"Un contenedor grande y pesado con gruesas paredes metálicas y una cerradura "
"de combinación giratoria, diseñada para almacenar de forma segura armas de "
"fuego, modificaciones de armas y munición. Si tuvieras algo con lo que "
"forzar su cerradura, probablemente podrías abrirlo."

#. ~ Lockpick message of furniture "locked gun safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock on the gun safe door opens."
msgstr ""
"Con un satisfactorio click, la cerradura de la caja fuerte de armas se abre."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "jammed gun safe"
msgstr "caja fuerte trabada de armas"

#. ~ Description of furniture "jammed gun safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A large, heavy container with thick metal walls and a rotary combination "
"lock, designed to securely store firearms, weapon mods, and ammunition.  "
"Unfortunately, the lock is completely broken, and short of some pretty "
"serious machinery, you have no possible way of opening it."
msgstr ""
"Un contenedor grande y pesado con gruesas paredes metálicas y una cerradura "
"de combinación giratoria, diseñada para almacenar de forma segura armas de "
"fuego, modificaciones de armas y munición. Por desgracia la cerradura esta "
"rota, y aparte de maquinaria seria, no tienes posibilidad de abrirla."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "electronic gun safe"
msgstr "caja fuerte electrónica de armas"

#. ~ Description of furniture "electronic gun safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A large, heavy container with thick metal walls and an electronic locking "
"system, designed to securely store firearms, weapon mods, and ammunition.  "
"If you had some way of hacking into it, you could probably crack it open."
msgstr ""
"Un contenedor grande y pesado con gruesas paredes de metal y un sistema de "
"cierre electrónico, diseñada para almacenar de forma segura armas de fuego, "
"modificaciones de armas y munición. Si tuvieras alguna forma de hackearlo, "
"probablemente podrías abrirlo."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "locker"
msgstr "armario"

#. ~ Description of furniture "locker"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A tall sheet metal cabinet, useful for storing just about anything that'll "
"fit."
msgstr ""
"Un armario alto de chapa, útil para guardar casi cualquier cosa que quepa."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "mailbox"
msgstr "buzón"

#. ~ Description of furniture "mailbox"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A small metal box on top of a wooden post, designed to receive mail "
"deliveries.  Although considering the circumstances, it will likely never "
"see proper use again."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña caja de metal en la parte superior de un poste de madera, "
"diseñada para recibir las entregas de correo. Aunque, dadas las "
"circunstancias, es probable que nunca vuelva a tener un uso adecuado."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "clothing rail"
msgstr "baranda para ropa"

#. ~ Description of furniture "clothing rail"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A metal frame on a set of wheels used for hanging large amounts of clothes."
"  Usually used in theater or retail environments, it's easy to use and quick"
" to access."
msgstr ""
"Una estructura metálica sobre un conjunto de ruedas utilizado para colgar "
"grandes cantidades de ropa. Suele utilizarse en teatros o comercios, es "
"fácil de usar y de rápido acceso."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "display rack"
msgstr "estante"

#. ~ Description of furniture "display rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A sheet metal shelving unit, with the storage surfaces angled in such a way "
"as to show off the items stored."
msgstr ""
"Una estantería de chapa, con las superficies de almacenamiento inclinadas de"
" forma que se vean los artículos almacenados."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "locked display rack"
msgstr "estante de exhibición con cerradura"

#. ~ Description of furniture "locked display rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A sheet metal shelving unit, with the storage surfaces angled in such a way "
"as to show off the items stored.  Metal fasteners with a lock hold the items"
" securely to the rack."
msgstr ""
"Una estantería de chapa, con las superficies de almacenamiento inclinadas de"
" forma que se vean los artículos almacenados. Los cierres metálicos con "
"cerradura sujetan los artículos de forma segura a la estantería."

#. ~ Lockpick message of furniture "locked display rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock opens."
msgstr "Con un satisfactorio clic, la cerradura se abre."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "wooden rack"
msgstr "El estante de madera"

#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A wooden shelving unit with angled storage surfaces designed to show off "
"whatever is stored on it."
msgstr ""
"Una estantería de madera con superficies de almacenamiento en ángulo "
"diseñadas para mostrar lo que se almacena en ella."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "coat rack"
msgstr "perchero"

#. ~ Description of furniture "coat rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A tall wooden pole with a set of hooks used to store outdoor jackets and "
"hats to allow easy access."
msgstr ""
"Un poste alto de madera con un conjunto de ganchos que se utiliza para "
"guardar las chaquetas y los sombreros de exterior para facilitar el acceso."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "recycle bin"
msgstr "papelera de reciclaje"

#. ~ Description of furniture "recycle bin"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A large plastic bin painted green with a 'recycle' symbol emblazoned on it."
"  While intended to store discarded things to be processed back into a "
"factory, the drastic change in priorities as of late means that these may "
"hold valuable materials."
msgstr ""
"Un gran contenedor de plástico pintado de verde con el símbolo de "
"\"reciclaje\". Aunque su finalidad es almacenar los desechos que se van a "
"procesar en una fábrica, el cambio drástico de prioridades de los últimos "
"tiempos significa que pueden contener materiales valiosos."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "safe"
msgstr "caja fuerte"

#. ~ Description of furniture "safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A small, heavy, and near-unbreachable metal box with a rotary combination "
"lock.  This one isn't actually locked, just closed."
msgstr ""
"Una caja metálica pequeña, pesada y casi infranqueable con una cerradura de "
"combinación giratoria. Aunque, en realidad, esta no está sellada, sólo "
"cerrada."

#. ~ Description of furniture "safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A small, heavy, and near-unbreachable metal box with a rotary combination "
"lock.  With something to listen really closely and a hell of a lot of time, "
"you might be able to crack it."
msgstr ""
"Una caja metálica pequeña, pesada y casi infranqueable con una cerradura de "
"combinación giratoria. Con algo para escuchar muy de cerca y un montón de "
"tiempo, podrías ser capaz de descifrarla."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "open safe"
msgstr "caja fuerte abierta"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open safe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A small, heavy, and near-unbreachable metal box with a rotary combination "
"lock, albeit significantly less secure with the door open."
msgstr ""
"Una caja metálica pequeña, pesada y casi infranqueable con una cerradura de "
"combinación giratoria, aunque bastante menos segura con la puerta abierta."

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/items/containers/generic.json
msgid "trash can"
msgid_plural "trash cans"
msgstr[0] "cubo para basura"
msgstr[1] "cubos para basura"
msgstr[2] "cubos para basura"

#. ~ Description of furniture "trash can"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A plastic bin for storing discarded waste as to be disposed of later.  "
"Although, considering the circumstances, it might be worth seeing what's "
"inside."
msgstr ""
"Un contenedor de plástico para almacenar los residuos que se desechan "
"después. Aunque, teniendo en cuenta las circunstancias, podría valer la pena"
" ver lo que hay dentro."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "metal trash can"
msgstr "cubo de basura de metal"

#. ~ Description of furniture "metal trash can"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "A crude metal bin typically used to dispose of waste."
msgstr ""
"Un contenedor metálico tosco que suele utilizarse para eliminar los "
"residuos."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "wardrobe"
msgstr "armario"

#. ~ Description of furniture "wardrobe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A very large wooden cabinet for storing clothes, effectively an upright "
"closet.  Could technically be used to store anything else that would fit, "
"though."
msgstr ""
"Un armario de madera muy grande para guardar la ropa, efectivamente un "
"armario vertical. Aunque técnicamente podría utilizarse para guardar "
"cualquier otra cosa que cupiera."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "Torah Ark"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "Torah Ark"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"An ornately-carved cabinet designed to hold a Torah scroll.  This one is "
"decorated with a tree motif, referencing Proverbs 3:18."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "filing cabinet"
msgstr "fichero"

#. ~ Description of furniture "filing cabinet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A rack of metal drawers designed to hold various files and paperwork.  "
"Paperwork that has more than likely lost all relevance and value by now."
msgstr ""
"Una estantería de cajones metálicos diseñada para guardar varios archivos y "
"papeles. Papeles que probablemente ya han perdido todo su valor ahora."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "utility shelf"
msgstr "estante de utilería"

#. ~ Description of furniture "utility shelf"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A simple heavy-duty plastic and metal shelving unit, intended to store tools"
" and materials for easy access to workers."
msgstr ""
"Una sencilla estantería de plástico y metal de alta resistencia, destinada a"
" almacenar herramientas y materiales para facilitar el acceso de los "
"trabajadores."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "warehouse shelf"
msgstr "estantería del almacén"

#. ~ Description of furniture "warehouse shelf"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A huge, sturdy steel shelf for storing pallets of crates in warehouses."
msgstr ""
"Una enorme y robusta estantería de acero para almacenar palés de cajas en "
"los almacenes."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "wooden keg"
msgstr "barril de madera"

#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden keg"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A large standing wooden barrel, completely watertight.  Good for storing "
"liquids of all kinds."
msgstr ""
"Un gran barril de madera de pie, completamente hermético. Sirve para "
"almacenar líquidos de todo tipo."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "display case"
msgstr "vitrina"

#. ~ Description of furniture "display case"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A secure wooden case at about waist-height, with glass panelling on top.  "
"Useful for storing valuable things while still showing them off.  Not "
"actually as secure as it looks, as the display windows are easily broken."
msgstr ""
"Una caja de madera segura a la altura de la cintura, con paneles de cristal "
"en la parte superior. Es útil para guardar cosas valiosas y al mismo tiempo "
"mostrarlas. En realidad no es tan seguro como parece, ya que los cristales "
"se rompen con facilidad."

#. ~ Lockpick message of furniture "display case"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock and the display case opens."
msgstr "Con un satisfactorio clic, la cerradura y la vitrina se abren."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "open display case"
msgstr "expositor abierto"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open display case"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A secure wooden case at about waist-height, with glass panelling on top.  "
"Useful for storing valuable things while still showing them off.  Not "
"actually as secure as it looks, as the display windows are easily broken.  "
"This one has had its lock picked and is open."
msgstr ""
"Una caja de madera segura a la altura de la cintura, con paneles de cristal "
"en la parte superior. Es útil para guardar cosas valiosas y al mismo tiempo "
"mostrarlas. En realidad no es tan seguro como parece, ya que los cristales "
"se rompen con facilidad. A esta le han forzado la cerradura y está abierta."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "broken display case"
msgstr "vitrina rota"

#. ~ Description of furniture "broken display case"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A secure wooden case at about waist-height, with glass panelling on top.  "
"Would be useful for storing valuable things while still showing them off, if"
" the glass hadn't been shattered.  Careful not to cut yourself when looting."
msgstr ""
"Una caja de madera segura a la altura de la cintura, con paneles de cristal "
"en la parte superior. Sería útil para guardar cosas valiosas sin dejar de "
"mostrarlas, si el cristal no se hubiera roto. Cuidado con cortarte al "
"saquear."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "map board"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "map board"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "A secure metal board with a locked glass panel used to display a map."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Lockpick message of furniture "map board"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "With a satisfying click, the locked glass panel opens."
msgstr "Con un satisfactorio clic, la taquilla de cristal cerrada se abre."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "open map board"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "open map board"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A successfully picked metal board with an open glass panel used to display a"
" map."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "broken map board"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "broken map board"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "A metal board with a smashed glass panel used to display a map."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "fireman's cabinet"
msgstr "armario de bombero"

#. ~ Description of furniture "fireman's cabinet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A metallic cabinet painted to stand out, visibly holding tools behind a thin"
" panel of tempered glass."
msgstr ""
"Un armario metálico pintado para destacar, que sostiene visiblemente las "
"herramientas detrás de un fino panel de vidrio templado."

#. ~ Lockpick message of furniture "fireman's cabinet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock on the cabinet opens."
msgstr "Con un satisfactorio clic, se abre la cerradura del armario."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "unlocked fireman's cabinet"
msgstr "armario de bombero sin cerrar"

#. ~ Description of furniture "unlocked fireman's cabinet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A metallic cabinet painted to stand out.  Its glass panel door was left "
"unlocked and slightly ajar."
msgstr ""
"Un armario metálico pintado para destacar. Su puerta de panel de cristal se "
"dejó sin cerrar y ligeramente entreabierta."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "open fireman's cabinet"
msgstr "armario de bombero abierto"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open fireman's cabinet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A metallic cabinet painted to stand out.  Its protective glass panel lies "
"broken from some past emergency or looting attempt."
msgstr ""
"Un armario metálico pintado para destacar. Su panel de cristal protector "
"yace roto por alguna emergencia o intento de saqueo del pasado."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "standing tank"
msgstr "depósito horizontal"

#. ~ Description of furniture "standing tank"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A huge metal tank that can be used to safely store large amounts of liquid."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme tanque de metal que puede utilizarse para almacenar de forma "
"segura grandes cantidades de líquido."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "bulk storage tank"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "bulk storage tank"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A 2 meters high tank that can store up to 1500 liters of liquid.  That's a "
"lot."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "fuel tank"
msgstr "tanque de gasolina"

#. ~ Description of furniture "fuel tank"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "A tank filled with gasoline."
msgstr "Un tanque lleno de gasolina."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "broken fuel tank"
msgstr "tanque de combustible roto"

#. ~ Description of furniture "broken fuel tank"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "A broken tank which was filled with gasoline."
msgstr "Un tanque roto que estaba lleno de gasolina."

#. ~ Description of furniture "fuel tank"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "A tank filled with diesel."
msgstr "Un depósito lleno de gasoil."

#. ~ Description of furniture "broken fuel tank"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "A broken tank which was filled with diesel."
msgstr "Un tanque roto que estaba lleno de diesel."

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Snippet in category "<name_b>"
#. ~ generic negative/hostile pronouns
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/npcs/talk_tags.json
msgid "dumpster"
msgstr "contenedor"

#. ~ Description of furniture "dumpster"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A large metal dumpster that will likely not be getting picked up by the "
"city's waste management any time soon.  Despite the unpleasant nature of "
"climbing inside, it could make for a viable hiding spot."
msgstr ""
"Un gran contenedor de metal que probablemente no será recogido por la "
"administración de residuos de la ciudad en un futuro próximo. A pesar de lo "
"desagradable que resulta trepar por su interior, podría ser un buen "
"escondite."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "butter churn"
msgstr "mantequera"

#. ~ Description of furniture "butter churn"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A metal tube with a built-in mixer for making butter.  Rather than needing "
"electricity, it is pedal-driven, allowing use without power."
msgstr ""
"Un tubo de metal con un mezclador incorporado para hacer mantequilla. En "
"lugar de necesitar electricidad, se acciona con un pedal, lo que permite su "
"uso sin energía."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "riveted metal crate"
msgstr "caja metálica remachada"

#. ~ Description of furniture "riveted metal crate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"This huge box is made of a dull metal, riveted together.  There is no "
"obvious opening mechanism, and the rivets don't match any of your tools.  "
"The only way in would be to smash it."
msgstr ""
"Esta enorme caja está hecha de un metal opaco, remachado. No hay ningún "
"mecanismo de apertura evidente, y los remaches no coinciden con ninguna de "
"sus herramientas. La única forma de entrar sería rompiéndola."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "sealed metal crate"
msgstr "caja metálica sellada"

#. ~ Description of furniture "sealed metal crate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A huge, tightly sealed storage crate made from welded and riveted sheet "
"metal.  The sealing mechanism is too tight to open bare-handed and would "
"need some kind of prying instrument to release."
msgstr ""
"Se trata de un enorme cajón de almacenamiento hermético hecho de chapa "
"soldada y remachada. El mecanismo de sellado es demasiado hermético para "
"abrirlo con la mano y se necesitaría algún tipo de instrumento de palanca "
"para liberarlo."

#. ~ Prying action message of furniture "sealed metal crate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "You wrench open the metal crate."
msgstr "Abres con una llave la caja de metal."

#. ~ Prying failure message of furniture "sealed metal crate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "The lid is sealed more tightly than you thought."
msgstr "La tapa está más sellada de lo que pensabas."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "open metal crate"
msgstr "caja metálica abierta"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open metal crate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"This large metal crate’s lid is unsealed, and hinges open easily to reveal a"
" number of storage shelves inside.  Once open, the side panels also swing "
"wider for easy access."
msgstr ""
"La tapa de este gran cajón metálico no está sellada y se abre fácilmente con"
" bisagras para revelar una serie de estantes de almacenamiento en el "
"interior. Una vez abierta, los paneles laterales también se abren para "
"facilitar el acceso."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "wooden chest"
msgstr "cofre de madera"

#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden chest"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A sealed wooden storage container.  Lacking any labels, it could hold just "
"about anything inside.  It has a simple metal latch."
msgstr ""
"Un contenedor de madera sellado. Sin etiquetas, podría contener casi "
"cualquier cosa en su interior. Tiene un simple cierre de metal."

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Based on https://www.duluthtrading.com/best-made-footlocker-B1098.html
#. with the weight calculated from surface area with the use of
#. https://www.engineeringtoolbox.com/gauge-sheet-d_915.html.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/storage.json
msgid "steel foot locker"
msgid_plural "steel foot lockers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "steel foot locker"
#. ~ Based on https://www.duluthtrading.com/best-made-footlocker-B1098.html
#. with the weight calculated from surface area with the use of
#. https://www.engineeringtoolbox.com/gauge-sheet-d_915.html.
#. ~ Description of "steel foot locker"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/storage.json
msgid ""
"A steel storage box, capable of holding any number of things.  The lid has a"
" small lock."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Weight and pocket data recalculated from foot_locker with the use of the
#. same resources but with the assumption that walls are gauge 16 aluminum.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/storage.json
msgid "aluminum foot locker"
msgid_plural "aluminum foot lockers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "aluminum foot locker"
#. ~ Weight and pocket data recalculated from foot_locker with the use of the
#. same resources but with the assumption that walls are gauge 16 aluminum.
#. ~ Description of "aluminum foot locker"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/storage.json
msgid ""
"An aluminum storage box, capable of holding any number of things.  The lid "
"has a small lock."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ todo: replace with some better rubber material
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/items/containers/military.json
msgid "big collapsible drum"
msgid_plural "big collapsible drums"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "big collapsible drum"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A black collapsible drum with a valve and D-Rings.  Yellow text on its top "
"clearly says \"FLAMMABLE\"."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "packed pallet"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "packed pallet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A wooden pallet loaded with cargo, wrapped with a watertight cover, and "
"belted to secure the contents."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "packed pallet"
#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "damaged pallet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "rip!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid "damaged pallet"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "damaged pallet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
msgid ""
"A wooden pallet, containing cargo and possessing a torn cover.  You can "
"reach the contents, but it’s awfully hard due to the belts still being in "
"place."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "counter"
msgstr "mostrador"

#. ~ Description of furniture "counter"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid ""
"A plain wooden countertop, either free-standing or affixed to a wall.  Makes"
" a decent surface for storage or crafting."
msgstr ""
"Un mostrador simple de madera, que se sostiene por si mismo o fijado a una "
"pared. Es una buena superficie para guardar o fabricar."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "cupboard"
msgstr "alacena"

#. ~ Description of furniture "cupboard"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "Store your cups.  Or other things, if you're feeling wild."
msgstr "Guarda tus vasos. O cualquier otra cosa, si te sientes salvaje."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "closed counter gate"
msgstr "puerta del mostrador cerrada"

#. ~ Description of furniture "closed counter gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid ""
"A commercial-quality swinging door made of wood that allows passage behind "
"counters.  It's currently closed."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta giratoria de calidad comercial hecha de madera que permite el "
"paso detrás de los mostradores. Ahora esta cerrada."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "open counter gate"
msgstr "abrir la puerta del mostrador"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open counter gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid ""
"A commercial-quality swinging door made of wood that allows passage behind "
"counters.  It's open, allowing passage."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta giratoria de calidad comercial hecha de madera que permite el "
"paso detrás de los mostradores. Esta abierta, permitiendo el paso."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "desk"
msgstr "escritorio"

#. ~ Description of furniture "desk"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid ""
"A wooden desk with drawers.  You could decorate it with trinkets, eat a meal"
" off it, use it as a workbench, read a book, write in a journal, put a "
"laptop on it, put your feet up, rest your head for a nap if you're sitting "
"down… who knew desks were so useful?"
msgstr ""
"Un escritorio de madera con cajones. Podrías decorarlo con cacharros, comer "
"en el, usarlo como mesa de trabajo, leer un libro, escribir un diario, poner"
" un portátil, poner tus pies en alto, echar una siestas con tu cabeza encima"
" si estas sentado... ¿quien iba a decir que los escritorios eran tan útiles?"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "workbench"
msgstr "mesa de trabajo"

#. ~ Description of furniture "workbench"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy workbench built out of metal.  It is perfect for crafting large and"
" heavy things."
msgstr ""
"Un robusto banco de trabajo construido de metal. Es perfecto para hacer "
"cosas grandes y pesadas."

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "leather tarp"
msgid_plural "leather tarps"
msgstr[0] "lona de cuero"
msgstr[1] "lonas de cuero"
msgstr[2] "lonas de cuero"

#. ~ Description of furniture "leather tarp"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid ""
"A large sheet of leather lying on the ground.  You could use it as a picnic "
"blanket, but it's more valuable as a surface for butchering as it does not "
"soak up blood."
msgstr ""
"Una gran sabana de cuero cosido. Podría desplegarse en lugar de una manta de"
" acampada, pero es más valiosa como aparato de descuartizado ya que no se "
"empapa de sangre."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "plastic groundsheet"
msgstr "hoja de tierra de plástico"

#. ~ Description of furniture "plastic groundsheet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid ""
"A large sheet of thick plastic lying on the ground.  It could be a useful "
"surface for butchering, perhaps."
msgstr ""
"Una gran lámina de plástico grueso ha sido arrojada al suelo aquí. Sería un "
"lugar útil para descuartizado, tal vez."

#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "plastic groundsheet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "whuff!"
msgstr "¡whuff!"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound of furniture "plastic groundsheet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "crinkle."
msgstr "arruga."

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "fiber mat"
msgid_plural "fiber mats"
msgstr[0] "alfombra de fibra"
msgstr[1] "alfombras de fibra"
msgstr[2] "alfombras de fibra"

#. ~ Description of furniture "fiber mat"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid ""
"A large mat woven from fibrous material.  You could use it as a picnic "
"blanket, but it's more valuable as a surface for butchering.  Too thin to be"
" used as a comfortable sleeping mat."
msgstr ""
"Una gran alfombra tejida de material fibroso que puede ser utilizada en "
"lugar de una manta de acampada, pero es más valiosa como un aparato de "
"descuartizado. Demasiado delgada para ser un lugar cómodo para dormir."

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ values based on real world collapsible camping table
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "folding table"
msgid_plural "folding tables"
msgstr[0] "mesa plegable"
msgstr[1] "mesas plegables"
msgstr[2] "mesas plegables"

#. ~ Description of furniture "folding table"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid ""
"A small metal folding table, ideal for off-road trips.  Can be used as a "
"workbench in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña mesa plegable de metal, ideal para viajes fuera de la carretera "
"en la naturaleza. Puede ser usada como un banco de trabajo en caso de "
"necesidad."

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "table"
msgstr "mesa"

#. ~ Description of furniture "table"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden table.  You could sit down at it to eat like a civilized "
"person."
msgstr ""
"Una mesa de madera común. Podrías sentarte en ella para comer como una "
"persona civilizada."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "coffee table"
msgstr "mesa de café"

#. ~ Description of furniture "coffee table"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid ""
"A low table usually found in living rooms, it makes an ideal surface for "
"playing games, showing off some tasteful books, or presumably for putting "
"coffee cups on.  No one cares if you use a coaster anymore."
msgstr ""
"Una mesa baja usualmente encontrada en los salones, es una superficie ideal "
"para jugar a juegos de mesa, mostrando algunos libros de buen gusto, o "
"presumiblemente para poner tazas de café. A nadie le importa si usas "
"posavasos ahora."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "metal table"
msgstr "mesa de metal"

#. ~ Description of furniture "metal table"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "A serviceable but simple table made of scrap metal."
msgstr "Una mesa útil pero sencilla hecha de chatarra."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "tatami mat"
msgstr "tatami"

#. ~ Description of furniture "tatami mat"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A type of mat used as a flooring material in traditional Japanese-style "
"rooms."
msgstr ""
"Una especie de alfombra que se utiliza como material para el suelo en las "
"habitaciones de estilo tradicional japonés."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "pillow fort"
msgstr "fortaleza de la almohada"

#. ~ Description of furniture "pillow fort"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A comfy place to hide from the world.  Not very defensible, though."
msgstr ""
"Un lugar cómodo para esconderse del mundo. Aunque no es muy defendible."

#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "pillow fort"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "paf!"
msgstr "¡paf!"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "cardboard fort"
msgstr "fuerte de cartón"

#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard fort"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A fort built by tipping a cardboard box on its side, lining it with "
"blankets, and partly weather-sealing it with a plastic sheet."
msgstr ""
"Un fuerte construido inclinando una caja de cartón a un lado, forrándola con"
" mantas, y en parte sellándola con una lámina de plástico."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "cardboard wall"
msgstr "muro de cartón"

#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A pile of cardboard boxes that have been filled with rags and junk and "
"stacked together like bricks to form a wall."
msgstr ""
"Un montón de cajas de cartón que han sido llenadas con trapos, basura y "
"apiladas como ladrillos para formar una pared."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "cardboard floor"
msgstr "piso de cartón"

#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A flat floor made of sheets of cardboard duct-taped together, covering a "
"plastic sheet on the ground."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo plano hecho con láminas de cartón pegadas con cinta adhesiva sobre "
"una lámina de plástico."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "cardboard roof"
msgstr "techo de cartón"

#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A sloped roof made of cardboard boxes, stuffed with scrap cardboard and "
"paper and layered atop each other.  Sheets of plastic are carefully arranged"
" on top to shed water.  It looks like it could last a season or two at least"
" before crumbling."
msgstr ""
"Un techo inclinado hecho de cajas de cartón, rellenadas con restos de cartón"
" y papel superpuestas. Encima hay láminas de plástico colocadas "
"cuidadosamente para evitar el agua. Parece que podría durar una o dos "
"temporadas al menos, antes de desmoronarse."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "cardboard door"
msgstr "puerta de cartón"

#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A pile of cardboard boxes that have been filled with rags and junk and "
"stacked together like bricks to form a wall.  The largest box has been cut "
"open and folded to form a makeshift door, which is open."
msgstr ""
"Un montón de cajas de cartón que se han llenado de trapos, trastos y se han "
"apilado como si fueran ladrillos para formar una pared. La caja más grande "
"fue cortada y doblada para formar una puerta improvisada, que está abierta."

#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A pile of cardboard boxes that have been filled with rags and junk and "
"stacked together like bricks to form a wall.  The largest box has been cut "
"open and folded to form a makeshift door, which is closed."
msgstr ""
"Un montón de cajas de cartón que se han llenado de trapos, trastos y se han "
"apilado como si fueran ladrillos para formar una pared. La caja más grande "
"fue cortada y doblada para formar una puerta improvisada, que está cerrada."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "beaded curtain"
msgstr "cortina de cuentas"

#. ~ Description of furniture "beaded curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A curtain of wooden beads, thick enough that you can't see through them.  "
"They could be pulled aside effortlessly."
msgstr ""
"Una cortina hecha de cuentas de madera, lo suficientemente espesa para no "
"poder ver a través de ella. Podrías apartarlas sin mucho esfuerzo."

#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "beaded curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "clickity clack… clack… clack"
msgstr "clickity clack… clack… clack"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound of furniture "beaded curtain"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of furniture "open beaded curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "clickity clack… clack"
msgstr "clickity clack… clack"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "open beaded curtain"
msgstr "cortina de cuentas abierta"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open beaded curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A curtain of wooden beads that has been pulled aside."
msgstr "Una cortina de cuentas de madera que ha sido apartada."

#. ~ Bashing sound of furniture "open beaded curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "clickity clack… clack… clack!"
msgstr "¡clickity clack… clack… clack!"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "canvas floor"
msgstr "piso de tela"

#. ~ Description of furniture "canvas floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"Flooring made out of stretched, waterproof cloth.  Helps keep dirt out of "
"the tent."
msgstr ""
"Suelos hechos de tela estirada e impermeable. Ayuda a mantener la suciedad "
"fuera de la tienda."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "canvas wall"
msgstr "muro de tela"

#. ~ Description of furniture "canvas wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A tent wall made of stretched, waterproof cloth."
msgstr "Una pared de tienda hecha de tela estirada e impermeable."

#. ~ Description of furniture "canvas wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A tent wall made of stretched, heavy-duty, waterproof cloth."
msgstr "Una pared de tienda hecha de tela estirada, resistente e impermeable."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "large skin wall"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "large skin wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A large tent wall made out of stretched animal skin.  It'll keep the rain "
"out, but anything trying to get in could rip through it fairly easily."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "large skin groundsheet"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "large skin groundsheet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A large animal-skin groundsheet to keep your feet dry inside the shelter."
msgstr ""
"Una lámina de piel animal para mantener tus pies secos dentro del refugio."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "large animalskin flap"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "large animalskin flap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A large animal-skin flap that can be pulled aside."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "open animalskin flap"
msgstr "solapa abierta de piel de animal"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open animalskin flap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A large animal-skin flap that has been pulled aside."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "canvas flap"
msgstr "solapa de tela"

#. ~ Description of furniture "canvas flap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A canvas flap door that can be pulled aside."
msgstr "Una puerta de lona que puede ser apartada."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "open canvas flap"
msgstr "solapa abierta de tela"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open canvas flap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A canvas flap door that has been pulled aside."
msgstr "Una puerta de lona que ha sido apartada."

#. ~ Description of furniture "canvas flap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A heavy canvas flap door that can be pulled aside."
msgstr "Una pesada puerta de lona que puede ser apartada."

#. ~ Description of furniture "open canvas flap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A heavy canvas flap door that has been pulled aside."
msgstr "Una pesada puerta de lona que ha sido apartada."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "groundsheet"
msgstr "lona impermeable"

#. ~ Description of furniture "groundsheet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A plastic groundsheet to keep your feet dry inside the tent."
msgstr ""
"Una lámina de plástico para mantener tus pies secos dentro de la tienda."

#. ~ Description of furniture "groundsheet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A large plastic groundsheet to keep your feet dry inside the tent."
msgstr ""
"Un gran lámina de plástico para mantener tus pies secos dentro de la tienda."

#. ~ Description of furniture "groundsheet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A government-issue plastic groundsheet to keep your feet dry, it was clearly"
" made by the lowest bidder."
msgstr ""
"Una lámina de plástico emitida por el gobierno que podría mantenerte seco, "
"pero fue claramente hecha por el peor postor."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "animalskin wall"
msgstr "muro de piel de animal"

#. ~ Description of furniture "animalskin wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A tent wall made out of stretched animal skin.  It'll keep the rain out, but"
" anything trying to get in could rip through it fairly easily."
msgstr ""
"Una pared de tienda hecha de piel de animal estirada. Mantendrá la lluvia "
"fuera, pero cualquier cosa que intente entrar podría romperla fácilmente."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "animalskin flap"
msgstr "solapa de piel de animal"

#. ~ Description of furniture "animalskin flap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "An animal-skin flap that can be pulled aside."
msgstr "Un colgajo de piel de animal podría ser apartado."

#. ~ Description of furniture "open animalskin flap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "An animal-skin flap that has been pulled aside."
msgstr "Un colgajo de piel de animal que ha sido apartado."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "animalskin floor"
msgstr "piso de piel de animal"

#. ~ Description of furniture "animalskin floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "An animal-skin groundsheet to keep your feet dry inside the shelter."
msgstr ""
"Una lámina de piel animal para mantener tus pies secos dentro del refugio."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "pile of rubble"
msgstr "pila de escombros"

#. ~ Description of furniture "pile of rubble"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A pile of various metals, bricks, and other building materials.  You could "
"clear it with a shovel."
msgstr ""
"Un montículo de varios metales, ladrillos y otros materiales de "
"construcción. Podrías limpiarlo con una pala."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "pile of rocky rubble"
msgstr "pila de escombros de piedra"

#. ~ Description of furniture "pile of rocky rubble"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A loose pile of rocks.  Useless?"
msgstr "Un montículo mezclado de piedras. ¿Inútil?"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "pile of trashy rubble"
msgstr "pila de escombros de basura"

#. ~ Description of furniture "pile of trashy rubble"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A pile of trash topped with dirt and grass.  It smells gross, but one man's "
"trash…"
msgstr ""
"Un montículo de basura coronado con suciedad y hierba. Huele fatal, pero la "
"basura de un hombre..."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "metal wreckage"
msgstr "restos de metal"

#. ~ Description of furniture "metal wreckage"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A pile of various bent and twisted metals.  Some of it looks pretty rusty, "
"you wouldn't want to cut yourself on this."
msgstr ""
"Un montículo de varios metales doblados y torcidos. Algunos parecen bastante"
" oxidados, no querrías cortarte con esto."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "radioactive slag"
msgstr "desecho radioactivo"

#. ~ Description of furniture "radioactive slag"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A pile of melted slag from a destroyed nuclear reactor.  What are you doing "
"looking at it?  Get the hell out of here, you nutcase!"
msgstr ""
"Un montículo de  escoria fundida de un reactor nuclear destruido. ¿Qué haces"
" mirando esto? ¡Lárgate de aquí, chiflado!"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "pile of ash"
msgstr "pila de ceniza"

#. ~ Description of furniture "pile of ash"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A pile of ash, from wood or possibly corpses."
msgstr "Un montículo de ceniza, de madera o de cadáveres."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "small boulder"
msgstr "roca pequeña"

#. ~ Description of furniture "small boulder"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A big rock.  Should be easy to roll around, but too heavy to carry with you."
"  It can be used as a primitive anvil, or broken into a bunch of smaller "
"rocks."
msgstr ""
"Un gran roca. Debería ser fácil hacerla rodar, pero demasiado pesada para "
"llevarla contigo. Puede ser usada como un yunque primitivo, o roto en rocas "
"mas pequeñas."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "medium boulder"
msgstr "roca mediana"

#. ~ Description of furniture "medium boulder"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A pretty big boulder, but still small enough to see and climb over.  It "
"would be a struggle to move it.  It can be used as a primitive anvil, or "
"broken into a bunch of smaller rocks."
msgstr ""
"Un montículo bastante grande, pero lo suficientemente pequeño para ver y "
"subirte encima. Costaría bastante moverlo. Puede ser usado como un yunque "
"primitivo, o roto en rocas mas pequeñas."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "large boulder"
msgstr "roca grande"

#. ~ Description of furniture "large boulder"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A boulder that's taller than you.  Now how are you going to move this?"
msgstr "Un pedrusco mas alto que tu. ¿Como vas a mover esto?"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "street light"
msgstr "luz de la calle"

#. ~ Description of furniture "street light"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A raised light source which used to illuminate streets and their surrounding"
" area, but it's useless without electricity."
msgstr ""
"Una fuente de luz elevada que solía iluminar las calles y sus alrededores, "
"pero es inútil sin electricidad."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "traffic light"
msgstr "luz de tráfico"

#. ~ Description of furniture "traffic light"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A signaling device positioned at road intersections and pedestrian crossings"
" to control the flow of traffic, but it's useless without electricity."
msgstr ""
"Un dispositivo de señalización ubicado en las intersecciones de carreteras y"
" cruces peatonales para controlar los flujos de tráfico, pero es inútil sin "
"electricidad."

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json data/json/vehicleparts/cargo.json
msgid "bike rack"
msgid_plural "bike racks"
msgstr[0] "soporte para bicicleta"
msgstr[1] "soportes para bicicleta"
msgstr[2] "soportes para bicicleta"

#. ~ Description of furniture "bike rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A loop of metal in the shape of an upside down U used to securely park "
"bikes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "flagpole"
msgstr "mástil"

#. ~ Description of furniture "flagpole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A 6-meter tall metal flagpole.  You could hoist up a flag here."
msgstr ""
"Un mástil de metal de 6 metros de altura. Podrías izar una bandera con esto."

#. ~ Description of furniture "flagpole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A 5-meter tall wooden flagpole.  You could hoist up a flag here."
msgstr ""
"Un mástil de madera de 5 metros de altura. Podrías izar una bandera con "
"esto."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "utility pole"
msgstr "poste de utilidades"

#. ~ Description of furniture "utility pole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid ""
"A long wooden post which used to support overhead power lines and other "
"public utilities, but it doesn't work anymore."
msgstr ""
"Un largo poste de madera que solía soportar las líneas eléctricas aéreas y "
"otros servicios públicos, pero ya no funciona."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "scrap metal bridge"
msgstr "puente de chatarra"

#. ~ Description of furniture "scrap metal bridge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A simple bridge made of riveted sheet metal."
msgstr "Un simple puente de hojas de metal remachadas."

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "room divider"
msgstr "divisor de habitación"

#. ~ Description of furniture "room divider"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
msgid "A tall piece of furniture used to divide rooms into separate areas."
msgstr ""
"Un pieza alta de mueble usado para dividir habitaciones en áreas separadas."

