msgstr "Esta sección del suelo de cera ha sido pintada."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "radiation platform"
msgstr "plataforma de radiación"

#. ~ Description of terrain "radiation platform"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A dual-purpose platform that exposes items placed on it to a radioactive "
"source by temporarily hoisting the radioactive material stored within, while"
" also safely containing all objects to avoid contaminating its surroundings."
"  Operated from an external console."
msgstr ""
"Una plataforma de doble propósito que expone objetos puestos en ella a una "
"fuente radioactiva elevando temporalmente el material radioactivo guardado "
"en ella, mientras también contiene todos lo objetos para evitar "
"contaminación a las cercanías. Operado con una terminal externa."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "junk metal floor"
msgstr "piso de metal chatarra"

#. ~ Description of terrain "junk metal floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A simple roof and floor of rusty scrap metal bolted and wire-tied to a "
"makeshift frame.  Very fashionable in post-apocalyptic shantytowns.  Hope "
"you like the sound of rain on corrugated metal."
msgstr ""
"Un simple techo y piso de chatarra oxidada atornillada y atada con alambre a"
" un marco improvisado. Muy de moda en los barrios de chabolas post-"
"apocalípticos. Espero que te guste el sonido de la lluvia sobre el metal "
"corrugado."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_groundxeno.json
msgid "dirt"
msgstr "tierra"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dirt"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"It's dirt.  Looks like some fine soil for tillage.  Could also be dug out "
"for construction projects."
msgstr ""
"Tierra. Parece que es buena para cultivar. También se puede excavar para "
"proyectos de construcción."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "sand"
msgstr "arena"

#. ~ Description of terrain "sand"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A large area of fine sand that could be useful in a number of ways, if it "
"was extracted properly."
msgstr ""
"Es un área grande con arena que podría utilizarse de varias maneras, si se "
"la extrae de manera apropiada."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "mud"
msgstr "barrobarro"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mud"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "An area of wet, slick mud."
msgstr "Un área de barro húmedo y resbaladizo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "moss"
msgstr "musgo"

#. ~ Description of terrain "moss"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A patch of moist, spongy moss."
msgstr "Un parche de húmedo y esponjoso musgo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "clay"
msgstr "arcilla"

#. ~ Description of terrain "clay"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A large area of malleable clay, suitable for kiln firing if it was extracted"
" properly."
msgstr ""
"Un área grande lleno de arcilla maleable, adecuado para cocer en el horno si"
" se extrae correctamente."

#. ~ Description of terrain "mound of clay"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "A mound of clay soil."
msgstr "Un montículo de tierra arcillosa."

#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "mound of clay"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "mound of clay"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "glacial ice"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "dirt"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "basalt floor"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "snow"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "singing sand"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_groundxeno.json
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/tropical_terrain.json
msgid "splosh!"
msgstr "¡splash!"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "paper floor"
msgstr "piso de papel"

#. ~ Description of terrain "paper floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "A floor made of ambiguous pulpy matter, covered in sticky wasp saliva."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo hecho de masa pulposa, cubierto de saliva pegajosa de avispa."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "hard paper floor"
msgstr "piso duro de papel"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hard paper floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A hardened cardboard floor made of chewed-up trees and resin mixed with wasp"
" saliva."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo de cartón duro hecho con árboles y resina machacados y mezclados "
"con saliva de avispa."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "paper brood cap"
msgstr "cobertura de papel de crías"

#. ~ Description of terrain "paper brood cap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A thin paper floor, protecting the pupating wasp larva until it's ready to "
"emerge."
msgstr ""
"Un piso de papel fino, que protege a la larva de avispa pupante hasta que "
"esta lista para emerger."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_commercial.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_hardcoded.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_lab.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_mall.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_recreational.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_retirement_community.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_robofachq.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_special.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_waste_junk.json
#: data/mods/Graphical_Overmap/go_overmap_terrain_ranch_camp.json
#: data/mods/Graphical_Overmap/go_overmap_terrain_waste_junk.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/overmap/overmap_terrain.json
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/furniture_and_terrain.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/mapgen/overmap_terrain.json
#: data/mods/alt_map_key/overmap_terrain.json
msgid "open air"
msgstr "aire libre"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open air"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "An area of open air."
msgstr "Un área de aire despejado."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plants.json
msgid "forest floor"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "forest floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "Covered in twigs and lots of brown, decaying leaves."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "mound of sand"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "A mound of sand."
msgstr "Un montón de arena."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "glassed sand"
msgstr "arena vitrificada"

#. ~ Description of terrain "glassed sand"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A patch of sand with a crust of natural glass atop it from exposure to "
"intense heat."
msgstr ""
"Un poco de arena que tiene una corteza de vidrio natural encima, por haber "
"sido expuesta a un calor intenso."

#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "glassed sand"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "black glass dust"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
msgid "crunch"
msgstr "crujido"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "upturned dirt"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "upturned dirt"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An area of loose dirt, not easily traversable.  If examined more closely, "
"it's quite favorable for planting seeds and the like."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "mound of upturned dirt"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "mound of upturned dirt"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A giant hill of dirt that looks like you could crawl inside for shelter."
msgstr ""
"Es una pilla gigante de tierra en la que parece que podrías meterte para "
"usar de refugio."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "odd fault"
msgstr "desperfecto extraño"

#. ~ Description of terrain "odd fault"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An unnaturally humanoid-shaped hole, it seems oddly familiar.  You feel a "
"strange urge to examine it closer, as if it belongs to you somehow."
msgstr ""
"Un agujero antinatural con forma humanoide, y que te resulta extrañamente "
"familiar. Sientes una extraña sensación al examinarlo, como si te "
"perteneciera de alguna manera."

#. ~ Message about the player in an effect
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"This wall is perfectly vertical.  Odd, twisted holes are set in it, leading "
"as far back into the solid rock as you can see.  The holes are humanoid in "
"shape, but with long, twisted, distended limbs."
msgstr ""
"Esta pared es perfectamente vertical. En ella hay agujeros extraños y "
"retorcidos que se adentran en la roca sólida hasta donde se puede ver. Los "
"agujeros tienen forma humanoide, pero con miembros largos, retorcidos y "
"distendidos."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "grave"
msgstr "tumba"

#. ~ Description of terrain "grave"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A dirt grave, with some grass growing on it.  At least some of the dead do "
"actually rest in peace."
msgstr ""
"Una tumba de tierra, con algo de hierba creciendo en ella. Al menos algunos "
"de los muertos descansan en paz."

#. ~ Description of terrain "grave"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A fresh grave, covered with stones, either to keep something from digging it"
" up or to keep one inside from digging out of it.  Or both.  Two planks mark"
" this place of someone's eternal rest."
msgstr ""
"Una tumba fresca, cubierta con piedras, ya sea para evitar que algo las "
"saque o para evitar que alguien de dentro las saque. Dos tablones marcan "
"este lugar de descanso eterno de alguien."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "rubber mulch"
msgstr "suelo de caucho"

#. ~ Description of terrain "rubber mulch"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A large area mulched with shredded rubber.  It's a softer place to land than"
" regular dirt."
msgstr ""
"Una gran superficie cubierta con caucho triturado. Es un lugar más suave "
"para aterrizar que la tierra normal."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "pavement"
msgstr "pavimento"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pavement"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A segment of asphalt, slowly degrading from cracks, frost heaves, and lack "
"of maintenance."
msgstr ""
"Un segmento de asfalto, que se degrada lentamente por las grietas, las "
"heladas y la falta de mantenimiento."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "yellow pavement"
msgstr "pavimento amarillo"

#. ~ Description of terrain "yellow pavement"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Streaks of carefully aligned yellow paint mark the road to inform drivers "
"not to cross.  No one is enforcing these rules anymore."
msgstr ""
"Son rayas de pintura amarilla cuidadosamente alineadas en la ruta para "
"informar a los conductores que no deben cruzarlas. Aunque ya nadie cuida que"
" estas cosas se cumplan."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "pedestrian crossing"
msgstr "paso de peatones"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pedestrian crossing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"White polymer lines painted on the pavement which indicate places where "
"pedestrians should cross the road."
msgstr ""
"Líneas blancas de polímero pintadas en el pavimento que indican los lugares "
"donde los peatones deben cruzar la carretera."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "sidewalk"
msgstr "acera"

#. ~ Description of terrain "sidewalk"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An area of common poured concrete, damaged by frost heaves and large cracks "
"due to lack of maintenance."
msgstr ""
"Una zona de hormigón vertido común, dañada por los fuertes vientos de las "
"heladas y las grandes grietas debido a la falta de mantenimiento."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "concrete"
msgid_plural "concrete"
msgstr[0] "hormigón"
msgstr[1] "hormigón"
msgstr[2] "hormigón"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A newer segment of poured concrete with surface finishes for aesthetics and "
"resistance to freeze-thaw cycles."
msgstr ""
"Un nuevo segmento de hormigón vertido con acabados superficiales para la "
"estética y la resistencia a los ciclos de congelación-descongelación."

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A newer segment of poured concrete with surface finishes for aesthetics and "
"resistance to freeze-thaw cycles.  Covered with a streak of yellow paint."
msgstr ""
"Un nuevo segmento de hormigón vertido con acabados superficiales para la "
"estética y la resistencia a los ciclos de congelación-descongelación. "
"Cubierto con una raya de pintura amarilla."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "wooden floor"
msgstr "Piso de madera"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A wooden floor created from boards, packed tightly together and nailed down."
"  Common on patios."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo de madera creado a partir de tablas, apretadas y clavadas. Es común"
" en los patios."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "wooden floor gangway"
msgstr "pasarela con suelo de madera"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden floor gangway"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A wooden gangway bridging a short gap.  Sturdy enough to act as a floor, but"
" not sufficient to support additional flooring."
msgstr ""
"Una pasarela de madera que cubre un corto espacio. Lo suficientemente "
"resistente como para servir de suelo, pero no lo suficiente como para "
"soportar un suelo adicional."

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"High-quality and tough checkered metal flooring to reduce the risk of slips "
"and falls."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo a cuadros de alta calidad y resistente para reducir el riesgo de "
"resbalones y caídas."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "metal floor gangway"
msgstr "pasarela con suelo metálico"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floor gangway"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A metal gangway bridging a short gap.  Sturdy enough to act as a floor, but "
"not sufficient to support additional flooring."
msgstr ""
"Una pasarela metálica que cubre un corto espacio. Suficientemente resistente"
" para actuar como suelo, pero no lo suficiente para soportar un suelo "
"adicional."

#. ~ Description of terrain "dirt floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "A floor consisting of finely mixed earth that has been tamped down."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo que consiste en tierra finamente mezclada que ha sido apisonada."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "gelatinous ground"
msgstr "suelo gelatinoso"

#. ~ Description of terrain "gelatinous ground"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An incursion of a large area of otherworldly substrate, it feels like "
"walking on hardened gelatin."
msgstr ""
"Una incursión en una gran área de sustrato de otro mundo, se siente como "
"caminar sobre gelatina endurecida."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "orifice"
msgstr "orificio"

#. ~ Description of terrain "orifice"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A large round orifice, with trails of fresh and dried-up strange green "
"liquid with a strongly acidic odor covering its inner sides."
msgstr ""
"Un gran orificio redondo, con estelas de un extraño líquido verde fresco y "
"seco con un fuerte olor ácido que cubre sus lados interiores."

#. ~ Description of terrain "elevator"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "An elevator section of the flight deck."
msgstr "Una sección del ascensor de la cabina de vuelo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "deck coating"
msgstr "cubierta"

#. ~ Description of terrain "deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A thick metal hull coating, covered with a military-grade epoxy mix.  Used "
"for runways, and can't be melted by jet engine nozzles."
msgstr ""
"Revestimiento metálico grueso de un armazón, cubierto con una mezcla de "
"epoxi de grado militar. Se utiliza para las pistas de aterrizaje, y no puede"
" ser fundido por las boquillas de los motores de los aviones."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "yellow deck coating"
msgstr "cubierta amarilla"

#. ~ Description of terrain "yellow deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A thick metal hull covering, covered with a military-grade epoxy mix and "
"painted yellow."
msgstr ""
"Revestimiento metálico grueso de un armazón, cubierto con una mezcla de "
"epoxi de grado militar, y pintado de color amarillo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "red deck coating"
msgstr "cubierta roja"

#. ~ Description of terrain "red deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A thick metal hull covering, covered with a military-grade epoxy mix, and "
"painted red."
msgstr ""
"Revestimiento metálico grueso de un armazón, cubierto con una mezcla de "
"epoxi de grado militar, y pintado de color rojo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "white deck coating"
msgstr "cubierta blanca"

#. ~ Description of terrain "white deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A thick metal hull covering, covered with a military-grade epoxy mix and "
"painted white."
msgstr ""
"Revestimiento metálico grueso de un armazón, cubierto con una mezcla de "
"epoxi de grado militar, y pintado de color blanco."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "walnut tree"
msgstr "nogal"

#. ~ Description of terrain "walnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus.  If you look closely, you "
"can see some unharvested walnuts."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme árbol perteneciente al género 'Juglans'. Si te fijas bien, puedes "
"ver algunas nueces sin cosechar."

#. ~ Description of terrain "walnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus."
msgstr "Un enorme árbol perteneciente al género 'Juglans'."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "butternut tree"
msgstr "árbol de nogal blanco"

#. ~ Description of terrain "butternut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus, but with lighter bark and "
"more elongated fruits than the more common black walnut.  If you look "
"closely, you can see some unharvested butternuts."
msgstr ""
"Una masivo árbol que pertenece a los 'Juglans', pero con una corteza mas "
"clara y unos frutos mas alargados que el nogal negro mas común. Si lo miras "
"de cerca, puede ver algunos butternuts sin recoger."

#. ~ Description of terrain "butternut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus, but with lighter bark and "
"more elongated fruits than the more common black walnut."
msgstr ""
"Una masivo árbol que pertenece a los 'Juglans', pero con una corteza mas "
"clara y unos frutos mas alargados que el nogal negro mas común."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "blackjack oak"
msgstr "roble negro"

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackjack oak"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the genus 'Quercus', with bark cracked into rectangular "
"black plates split by narrow orange fissures.  You could peel off the bark "
"sections if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol caducifolio del género 'Quercus', con la corteza agrietada formando"
" placas negras rectangulares, separadas por estrechas fisuras naranjas. "
"Podrías arrancar secciones de la corteza si examinas el árbol."

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackjack oak"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the genus 'Quercus', with bark cracked into rectangular "
"black plates split by narrow orange fissures.  All the usable bark has been "
"stripped off."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol caducifolio del género 'Quercus', con la corteza agrietada formando"
" placas negras rectangulares, separadas por estrechas fisuras naranjas. Toda"
" la corteza utilizable ha sido retirada."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "alder tree"
msgstr "aliso"

#. ~ Description of terrain "alder tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous flowering tree with serrated, scalloped, round-obovate leaves, "
"commonly forming dense groves alongside water."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol de floración caducifolio con hojas serradas, festoneadas y "
"redondeadas-obovadas, que suele formar densas arboledas junto al agua."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/furniture_and_terrain/tropical_terrain_flora.json
msgid "chestnut tree"
msgstr "castaño"

#. ~ Description of terrain "chestnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Castanea' genus.  If you look closely, you "
"can see some unharvested chestnuts."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme árbol perteneciente al género 'Castanea'. Si te fijas bien, puedes"
" ver algunas castañas sin cosechar."

#. ~ Description of terrain "chestnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Castanea' genus."
msgstr "Un enorme árbol perteneciente al género 'Castanea'."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "beech tree"
msgstr "haya"

#. ~ Description of terrain "beech tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Fagus' genus.  If you look closely, you can"
" see some unharvested beech nuts."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme árbol perteneciente al género 'Fagus'. Si te fijas bien, puedes "
"ver algunas nueces de haya sin cosechar."

#. ~ Description of terrain "beech tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Fagus' genus."
msgstr "Un enorme árbol perteneciente al género 'Fagus'."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "hazelnut tree"
msgstr "avellano"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hazelnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A stubby tree belonging to the 'Corylus' genus.  If you look closely, you "
"can see some unharvested hazelnuts."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol rechoncho perteneciente al género 'Corylus'. Si te fijas bien, "
"puedes ver algunas avellanas sin cosechar."

#. ~ Description of terrain "hazelnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A stubby tree belonging to the 'Corylus' genus."
msgstr "Un árbol rechoncho perteneciente al género 'Corylus'."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_flora.json
msgid "oak tree"
msgstr "roble"

#. ~ Description of terrain "oak tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive deciduous tree belonging to the 'Quercus' genus, commonly found "
"throughout the New England region.  If you look closely, you can see some "
"acorns the squirrels haven't gotten yet."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme árbol caducifolio perteneciente al género 'Quercus', que se "
"encuentra comúnmente en toda la región de Nueva Inglaterra. Si te fijas "
"bien, puedes ver algunas bellotas que las ardillas aún no han conseguido."

#. ~ Description of terrain "oak tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive deciduous tree belonging to the 'Quercus' genus, commonly found "
"throughout the New England region."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme árbol caducifolio perteneciente al género 'Quercus', que se "
"encuentra comúnmente en toda la región de Nueva Inglaterra."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "basswood tree"
msgstr "tilo rojo"

#. ~ Description of terrain "basswood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The American linden.  It has pretty and sweet-smelling flowers in the "
"summer, and you might be able to eat its young leaves in the spring."
msgstr ""
"El tilo americano. Tiene unas bonitas y olorosas flores en verano y se "
"pueden comer sus hojas jóvenes en primavera."

#. ~ Description of terrain "basswood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The American linden.  It has pretty and sweet-smelling flowers in the "
"summer, and its edible young leaves have already been harvested."
msgstr ""
"El tilo americano. Tiene unas bonitas y olorosas flores en verano y sus "
"hojas jóvenes comestibles ya se han cosechado."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "cottonwood tree"
msgstr "árbol del algodoncillo"

#. ~ Description of terrain "cottonwood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large tree belonging to the 'Populus' genus, commonly found throughout the"
" New England region.  You see some cottonwood tree bolls that can be "
"harvested."
msgstr ""
"Un gran árbol perteneciente al género 'Populus', que se encuentra comúnmente"
" en toda la región de Nueva Inglaterra. Se ven algunas cápsulas de "
"algodoncillo que se pueden cosechar."

#. ~ Description of terrain "cottonwood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large tree belonging to the 'Populus' genus, commonly found throughout the"
" New England region.  All the cottonwood tree bolls have been harvested."
msgstr ""
"Un gran árbol perteneciente al género 'Populus', que se encuentra comúnmente"
" en toda la región de Nueva Inglaterra. Se han recogido todo el algodoncillo"
" que se puede cosechar."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "elm tree"
msgstr "olmo"

#. ~ Description of terrain "elm tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large tree belonging to the 'Ulmus' genus, commonly found throughout the "
"New England region."
msgstr ""
"Árbol de gran tamaño perteneciente al género 'Ulmus', que se encuentra "
"comúnmente en toda la región de Nueva Inglaterra."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "dead tree"
msgstr "árbol seco"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An indiscernible tree that has withered away due to weather, fire, or "
"otherworldly causes."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol indiscernible que se ha marchitado, ya sea por el clima, por el "
"fuego o por causas de otro mundo."

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An indiscernible tree that has withered away due to weather, fire, or "
"otherworldly causes.  Someone or something has broken most of its dead "
"branches, leaving little but its gnarled trunk."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "warped dead tree"
msgstr "árbol muerto retorcido"

#. ~ Description of terrain "warped dead tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This deciduous tree's branches are warped into a spiral.  This appears to "
"have killed it."
msgstr ""
"Las ramas de este árbol de hoja caduca están retorcidas formando una "
"espiral.  Eso parece haber matado al árbol."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "young tree"
msgstr "árbol joven"

#. ~ Description of terrain "young tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A relatively young sapling of an indeterminate species.  It could take "
"decades before reaching maturity, so there's no use waiting around."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol joven de una especie indeterminada. Podría tardar décadas en "
"alcanzar la madurez, así que no sirve de nada esperar."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "mega fern"
msgstr "mega helecho"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mega fern"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A gigantic fern like nothing you've seen before.  The leaves are a bright "
"scarlet with a net-like structure of green veins.  The multipronged trunks "
"have the texture of balsa wood."
msgstr ""
"Un helecho gigantesco como nada que haya visto antes. Las hojas son de un "
"color escarlata brillante con una estructura similar a una red de venas "
"verdes. Los troncos con múltiples puntas parecen tener la consistencia de la"
" madera de balsa."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "apple tree"
msgstr "manzano"

#. ~ Description of terrain "apple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as apples.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could probably "
"find a few mature ones in autumn."
msgstr ""
"Este árbol pertenece al género 'Malus', que produce los frutos comúnmente "
"conocidos como manzanas. Este árbol pertenece al género 'Malus', que produce"
" los frutos comúnmente conocidos como manzanas."

#. ~ Description of terrain "apple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as apples.  There do not appear to be any ripe apples now."
msgstr ""
"Este árbol pertenece al género 'Malus', que produce los frutos comúnmente "
"conocidos como manzanas. Actualmente no parece haber manzanas maduras."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "pear tree"
msgstr "peral"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pear tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'Pyrus communis', or the common pear tree, which produces fruit in "
"the fall.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could probably "
"find a few mature ones."
msgstr ""
"Este es el 'Pyrus communis', o peral común, que produce peras viables en "
"otoño. Si examinas las ramas más de cerca, probablemente podrás encontrar "
"algunas maduras."

#. ~ Description of terrain "pear tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'Pyrus communis', or the common pear tree, which produces fruit in "
"the fall.  Looks like all the ripe pears have been picked."
msgstr ""
"Este es el 'Pyrus communis', o peral común, que produce peras viables en "
"otoño. Parece que todas las peras maduras han sido recogidas."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "coffee tree"
msgstr "árbol del café"

#. ~ Description of terrain "coffee tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'gymnocladus dioicus', or the kentucky coffee tree, which produces "
"roastable coffee pods and brewable leaves in the fall.  If you examined the "
"branches more closely, you could probably find a few mature ones."
msgstr ""
"Este es el 'gymnocladus dioicus', o cafeto de Kentucky, que produce vainas "
"de café que se pueden tostar y hojas que se pueden preparar en otoño. Si "
"examinaras las ramas más de cerca, probablemente podrías encontrar algunas "
"maduras."

#. ~ Description of terrain "coffee tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'gymnocladus dioicus', or the kentucky coffee tree, which produces "
"roastable coffee pods and brewable leaves in the fall.  Looks like all the "
"ripe pods have been picked."
msgstr ""
"Este es el 'gymnocladus dioicus', o cafeto de Kentucky, que produce vainas "
"de café que se pueden tostar y hojas que se pueden preparar en otoño. Parece"
" que todas las vainas maduras han sido recogidas."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "cherry tree"
msgstr "cerezo"

#. ~ Description of terrain "cherry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"cherries in the summer.  If you examined the foliage more closely, you could"
" probably find some viable clusters."
msgstr ""
"Una de las varias especies de árboles 'Prunus' que se encuentran en Nueva "
"Inglaterra, da cerezas en verano. Si examinas el follaje más de cerca, "
"probablemente podrá encontrar algunos racimos viables."

#. ~ Description of terrain "cherry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"cherries in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe bunches of cherries have "
"been picked."
msgstr ""
"Una de las varias especies de árboles 'Prunus' que se encuentran en Nueva "
"Inglaterra, da cerezas en verano. Parece que se han recogido todos los "
"racimos de cerezas maduras."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "juniper tree"
msgstr "Enebro"

#. ~ Description of terrain "juniper tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the species of 'Juniperus' that grows in New England, juniper berries"
" grow over two to three years.  It flowers in the first year, produces a "
"green berry the second, and in the third produces the more famed blue "
"varieties.  If you examined the foliage more closely, you could probably "
"find some viable clusters."
msgstr ""
"Una de las especies de 'Juniperus' que crece en Nueva Inglaterra, las bayas "
"de enebro crecen a lo largo de dos o tres años, primero floreciendo. Al "
"segundo año producen una baya verde, y al final, sus más afamadas variedades"
" azules. Si examinara el follaje más de cerca, probablemente podría "
"encontrar algunos racimos viables."

#. ~ Description of terrain "juniper tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the species of 'Juniperus' that grows in New England, juniper berries"
" grow over two to three years.  It flowers in the first year, produces a "
"green berry the second, and in the third produces the more famed blue "
"varieties.  Looks like all the ripe bunches of berries have been picked."
msgstr ""
"Una de las especies de 'Juniperus' que crece en Nueva Inglaterra, las bayas "
"de enebro crecen a lo largo de dos o tres años, primero floreciendo. Al "
"segundo año producen una baya verde, y al final, sus más afamadas variedades"
" azules. Parece que se han recogido todos los racimos maduros de bayas."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "peach tree"
msgstr "melocotonero"

#. ~ Description of terrain "peach tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"peaches in the summer.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could"
" probably find some mature peaches."
msgstr ""
"Una de las varias especies de árboles 'Prunus' que se encuentran en Nueva "
"Inglaterra, y da melocotones en verano. Si examinaras las ramas más de "
"cerca, probablemente podrías encontrar algunos melocotones maduros."

#. ~ Description of terrain "peach tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"peaches in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe peaches have been picked."
msgstr ""
"Una de las varias especies de árboles 'Prunus' que se encuentran en Nueva "
"Inglaterra, y da melocotones en verano. Parece que se han recogido todos los"
" melocotones maduros."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "apricot tree"
msgstr "albaricoquero"

#. ~ Description of terrain "apricot tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A transplanted species of 'Prunus armeniaca', rarely found in New England.  "
"It produces apricots in the summer.  If you examined the spurs more closely,"
" you could probably find some mature apricots."
msgstr ""
"Especie trasplantada de 'Prunus armeniaca', que rara vez se encuentra en "
"Nueva Inglaterra. Produce albaricoques en verano. Si se examinan los brotes "
"más de cerca, probablemente se puedan encontrar algunos albaricoques "
"maduros."

#. ~ Description of terrain "apricot tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A transplanted species of 'Prunus armeniaca', rarely found in New England.  "
"It produces apricots in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe apricots have "
"been picked."
msgstr ""
"Especie trasplantada de 'Prunus armeniaca', que rara vez se encuentra en "
"Nueva Inglaterra. Produce albaricoques en verano. Parece que todos los "
"albaricoques maduros han sido recogidos."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "plum tree"
msgstr "ciruelo"

#. ~ Description of terrain "plum tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it "
"produces plums in the summer.  If you examined the spurs more closely, you "
"could probably find some ripe plums."
msgstr ""
"Una de las varias especies de árboles 'Prunus' que se encuentran en Nueva "
"Inglaterra y produce ciruelas en verano. Si examinaras los brotes más de "
"cerca, probablemente podrías encontrar algunas ciruelas maduras."

#. ~ Description of terrain "plum tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it "
"produces plums in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe plums have been "
"picked."
msgstr ""
"Una de las varias especies de árboles 'Prunus' que se encuentran en Nueva "
"Inglaterra y produce ciruelas en verano. Parece que se han recogido todas "
"las ciruelas maduras."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "mulberry tree"
msgstr "Morera"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mulberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Morus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as mulberries.  In the summer, many berries can be picked."
msgstr ""
"Este árbol pertenece al género \"Morus\" y produce los frutos comúnmente "
"conocidos como moras. En verano, se pueden recoger muchas bayas."

#. ~ Description of terrain "mulberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Morus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as mulberries.  There do not appear to be any ripe mulberries now."
msgstr ""
"Este árbol pertenece al género 'Morus', que produce los frutos comúnmente "
"conocidos como moras. En la actualidad no parece haber moras maduras."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "elderberry tree"
msgstr "árbol de saúco"

#. ~ Description of terrain "elderberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sambucus' genus, producing fruit commonly "
"known as elderberries.  In the summer, many berries can be picked."
msgstr ""
"Este árbol pertenece al género \"Sambucus\" y produce los frutos comúnmente "
"conocidos como bayas de saúco. En verano, se pueden recoger muchas bayas."

#. ~ Description of terrain "elderberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sambucus' genus, producing fruit commonly "
"known as elderberries.  There do not appear to be any ripe elderberries now."
msgstr ""
"Este árbol pertenece al género \"Sambucus\" y produce los frutos conocidos "
"comúnmente como bayas de saúco. En la actualidad no parece que haya bayas de"
" saúco maduras."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "pine tree"
msgstr "pino"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New "
"England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  "
"If you examined the tree more closely, you might find usable sticky whorls, "
"resin clumps, and pinecones."
msgstr ""
"Una conífera imponente que pertenece al género 'Pinus', con las especies de "
"Nueva Inglaterra que varían entre 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' y 'P. rigida'."
" Si se examina el árbol con más detenimiento, se pueden encontrar verticilos"
" pegajosos utilizables, acumulaciones de resina y piñas sin recoger."

#. ~ Description of terrain "pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New "
"England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  "
"Some of the branches and resin clumps have been stripped away and many of "
"the pinecones aren't developed fully yet, but given a season, it could be "
"harvestable again."
msgstr ""
"Una imponente conífera que pertenece al género 'Pinus', con las especies de "
"Nueva Inglaterra que varían entre 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' y 'P. rigida'."
" Algunas de las ramas y los grupos de resina han sido despojados y muchas de"
" las piñas aún no se han desarrollado completamente, pero si se le da una "
"temporada, podría volver a ser cosechable."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "dead pine tree"
msgstr "pino seco"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New "
"England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  "
"This tree's branches are bare, and it appears to be dead."
msgstr ""
"Una imponente conífera que pertenece al género 'Pinus', con las especies de "
"Nueva Inglaterra que varían entre 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' y 'P. rigida'."
" Las ramas de este árbol están peladas y parece estar muerto."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "warped dead pine tree"
msgstr "pino muerto retorcido"

#. ~ Description of terrain "warped dead pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The branches of this pine tree have been twisted into a shape that remind "
"you of Sierpinski triangles.  It did not survive being warped like this."
msgstr ""
"Las ramas de este pino muerto han sido retorcidas en una forma que te hace "
"recordar los triángulos de Sierpinski.  No sobrevivió al ser retorcido de "
"esa manera."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "birch tree"
msgstr "abedul"

#. ~ Description of terrain "birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Betula' genus, with the characteristic peeling"
" bark.  Species like 'B. alleghaniensis', 'B. papyrifera', and 'B. "
"populifolia' are the most common in the New England region.  You could tear "
"off some strips of bark if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Árbol alto de hoja perenne del género 'Betula', con la característica "
"corteza desconchada. Especies como 'B. alleghaniensis', 'B. papyrifera' y "
"'B. populifolia' son las más comunes en la región de Nueva Inglaterra. Se "
"pueden arrancar algunas tiras de corteza si se examina el árbol más de "
"cerca."

#. ~ Description of terrain "birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Betula' genus, with the characteristic peeling"
" bark.  Species like 'B. alleghaniensis', 'B. papyrifera', and 'B. "
"populifolia' are the most common in the New England region.  Looks like "
"there isn't enough rhytidome to peel off yet."
msgstr ""
"Árbol alto de hoja perenne del género 'Betula', con la característica "
"corteza desconchada. Especies como 'B. alleghaniensis', 'B. papyrifera' y "
"'B. populifolia' son las más comunes en la región de Nueva Inglaterra. "
"Parece que aún no hay suficiente ritidoma para pelar."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "willow tree"
msgstr "sauce"

#. ~ Description of terrain "willow tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall, wide deciduous tree of the 'Salix' genus, with long, thin, leafy "
"branches that hang down like curtains.  You could tear off some bark."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol caducifolio alto y ancho del género 'Salix', con largas y finas "
"ramas frondosas que cuelgan como cortinas. Se puede arrancar la corteza."

#. ~ Description of terrain "willow tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall, wide deciduous tree of the 'Salix' genus, with long, thin, leafy "
"branches that hang down like curtains.  Looks like all usable bark has been "
"torn off, and new rhytidomes have not formed yet."
msgstr ""
"Árbol caducifolio, alto y ancho, del género 'Salix', con largas ramas de "
"hojas finas que cuelgan como cortinas. Parece que toda la corteza utilizable"
" ha sido arrancada, y aún no se han formado nuevos ritidios."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "maple tree"
msgstr "arce"

#. ~ Description of terrain "maple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large deciduous tree of the 'Acer' genus.  The leaves are distinctively "
"shaped with five prongs.  It could be tapped in order to extract maple sap."
msgstr ""
"Un gran árbol caducifolio del género 'Acer'. Las hojas tienen una forma "
"distintiva con cinco puntas. Se puede aprovechar para extraer jarabe de "
"arce."

#. ~ Description of terrain "maple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large deciduous tree of the 'Acer' genus.  The leaves are distinctively "
"shaped with five prongs.  A spigot is wedged into the trunk, and sweet maple"
" sap can be extracted."
msgstr ""
"Un gran árbol caducifolio del género 'Acer'. Las hojas tienen una forma "
"distintiva con cinco puntas. En el tronco hay una espiga de la que se puede "
"extraer el dulce jarabe de arce."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "hickory tree"
msgstr "árbol nueces pecanas"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  You could look for hickory nuts"
" if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol alto de hoja perenne del género 'Carya'. Podrías buscar nueces de "
"nogal si examinaras el árbol más de cerca."

#. ~ Description of terrain "hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  It looks like the tree has been"
" picked clean of hickory nuts."
msgstr ""
"Un alto árbol caducifolio del género 'Carya'. Parece que el árbol ha sido "
"limpiado de nueces de nogal."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "pistachio tree"
msgstr "árbol de pistacho"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pistachio tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Pistacia' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is"
" not native to this region.  You could look for pistachio nuts if you "
"examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Árbol de hoja perenne del género 'Pistacia'. Se trata de un árbol cultivado,"
" y no es nativo de esta región. Podrías buscar pistachos si examinaras el "
"árbol más de cerca."

#. ~ Description of terrain "pistachio tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Pistacia' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is"
" not native to this region.  Unfortunately, it looks like it has been picked"
" clean of pistachio nuts."
msgstr ""
"Árbol de hoja perenne del género 'Pistacia'. Se trata de un árbol cultivado "
"y no es nativo de esta región. Desgraciadamente, parece que le han quitado "
"los pistachos."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "almond tree"
msgstr "nogal"

#. ~ Description of terrain "almond tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Prunus' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is "
"not native to this region.  You could look for fresh almonds if you examined"
" the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Árbol de hoja perenne del género 'Prunus'. Se trata de un árbol cultivado y "
"no es nativo de esta región. Se podrían buscar almendras frescas si se "
"examinara el árbol más de cerca."

#. ~ Description of terrain "almond tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Prunus' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is "
"not native to this region.  There are no almonds left to pick on the tree."
msgstr ""
"Árbol de hoja perenne del género 'Prunus'. Se trata de un árbol cultivado, y"
" no es nativo de esta región. No quedan almendras para recoger en el árbol."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "pecan tree"
msgstr "árbol de nuez"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pecan tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  You could look for pecan nuts "
"if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol alto de hoja caduca del género 'Carya'. Podrías buscar nueces de "
"pecanero si examinaras el árbol más de cerca."

#. ~ Description of terrain "pecan tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  It doesn't look like there are "
"any pecan nuts left on the tree."
msgstr ""
"Un alto árbol caducifolio del género 'Carya'. No parece que queden nueces en"
" el árbol."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "dead hickory tree"
msgstr "árbol nueces pecanas muerto"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The dead remnants of a tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  Nothing "
"useful can be foraged from this poor, dead tree."
msgstr ""
"Los restos muertos de un alto árbol caducifolio del género 'Carya'. No se "
"puede extraer nada útil de este pobre árbol muerto."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "sassafras tree"
msgstr "árbol de sasafrás"

#. ~ Description of terrain "sassafras tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sassafras' genus, known for its aromatic "
"qualities.  In the winter and spring, the sap rich roots can be harvested to"
" make a sweet beverage."
msgstr ""
"Este árbol es un miembro del genero 'Sasafrás', conocido por sus cualidades "
"aromáticas. En invierno y primavera, las raíces ricas en savia pueden ser "
"cosechadas para hacer una dulce bebida."

#. ~ Description of terrain "sassafras tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sassafras' genus, known for its aromatic "
"qualities.  This tree's roots have been harvested, any more and the tree "
"will die."
msgstr ""
"Este árbol es un miembro del genero 'Sasafrás', conocido por sus cualidades "
"aromáticas. Las raíces han sido cosechadas, hacerlo otra vez lo mataría."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "underbrush"
msgid_plural "underbrushes"
msgstr[0] "maleza"
msgstr[1] "malezas"
msgstr[2] "malezas"

#. ~ Description of terrain "underbrush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Small plants and shrubs that decorate the forest.  An observant forager "
"could obtain edible plants, acorns, eggs, and mushrooms from it."
msgstr ""
"Son pequeñas plantas y arbustos que decoran el bosque. Un buscador de comida"
" avezado puede obtener plantas comestibles, bellotas, huevos y hongos ahí."

#. ~ Description of terrain "underbrush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Small plants and shrubs that decorate the forest.  It has been rummaged "
"through and doesn't have anything useful left to forage from it."
msgstr ""
"Pequeñas plantas y arbustos que decoran el bosque. Ha sido escarbado y no "
"queda nada útil que buscar en él."

#. ~ Description of terrain "underbrush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Small plants and shrubs that decorate the forest.  It has been rummaged "
"through and doesn't have anything useful left to forage from it.  Frost "
"covers it."
msgstr ""
"Pequeñas plantas y arbustos que decoran el bosque. Ha sido escarbado y no "
"queda nada útil que buscar en él. La escarcha lo cubre."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain.json
#: data/mods/alt_map_key/overmap_terrain.json
msgid "bee hive"
msgstr "colmena"

#. ~ Description of terrain "bee hive"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A hive of bees located in a cavity inside a tree, swarming in and out at a "
"feverish pace.  There's probably honey inside."
msgstr ""
"Una colmena de abejas en un hueco dentro de un árbol, con abejas entrando y "
"saliendo a un ritmo frenético. Probablemente hay miel dentro."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "apiary"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "apiary"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A man-made wooden box designed to hold honeybees and facilitate the care for"
" a hive.  The modular construction allows for inspecting the bees and "
"harvesting their bounty without destroying the hive completely.  This year's"
" harvest should be ready by now."
msgstr ""
"Una caja de madera de manufactura humana diseñada para mantener abejas y "
"facilitar el cuidado de una colmena. La construcción modular permite "
"inspeccionar las abejas y cosechar su botín sin destrozar la colmena "
"completamente. La cosecha de este año debería estar lista ahora."

#. ~ Description of terrain "apiary"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A man-made wooden box designed to host honeybees and facilitate the care for"
" a hive.  The modular construction allows for inspecting the bees and "
"harvesting their bounty without destroying the hive completely.  It will be "
"some time before this one is ready to harvest."
msgstr ""
"Una caja de madera de manufactura humana diseñada para mantener abejas y "
"facilitar el cuidado de una colmena. La construcción modular permite "
"inspeccionar las abejas y cosechar su botín sin destrozar la colmena "
"completamente. Todavía le falta bastante para estar lista para la cosecha."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "shrub"
msgstr "arbusto"

#. ~ Description of terrain "shrub"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small shrub."
msgstr "Un pequeño arbusto."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "peanut bush"
msgstr "arbusto de cacahuete"

#. ~ Description of terrain "peanut bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of crunchy peanuts."
msgstr "Es un pequeño arbusto de crujientes cacahuetes."

#. ~ Description of terrain "peanut bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small peanut bush that's fruitless."
msgstr "Un pequeño arbusto de cacahuetes sin cacahuetes"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "blueberry bush"
msgstr "arbusto de arándanos"

#. ~ Description of terrain "blueberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of sweet blueberries."
msgstr "Un pequeño arbusto de arándanos dulces."

#. ~ Description of terrain "blueberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small blueberry bush that's fruitless."
msgstr "Un pequeño arbusto de arándanos que sin frutos."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "strawberry bush"
msgstr "arbusto de fresas"

#. ~ Description of terrain "strawberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of juicy strawberries."
msgstr "Un pequeño arbusto de fresas jugosas."

#. ~ Description of terrain "strawberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small strawberry bush that's fruitless."
msgstr "Un pequeño arbusto de fresas vacío."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "blackberry bush"
msgstr "arbusto de zarzamoras"

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of delicious blackberries.  Watch out for its thorns!"
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño arbusto de deliciosas zarzamoras. Ten cuidado con las espinas."

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small blackberry bush that's fruitless.  Watch out for its thorns!"
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño arbusto de zarzamoras sin frutos. Ten cuidado con las espinas."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "huckleberry bush"
msgstr "arbusto de arándanos agrios"

#. ~ Description of terrain "huckleberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of huckleberries, often mistaken for blueberries."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño arbusto de arándanos de ciervo, a menudo confundido con los "
"arándanos."

#. ~ Description of terrain "huckleberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small huckleberry bush that's fruitless."
msgstr "Un pequeño arbusto de arándanos agrios sin frutos."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "raspberry bush"
msgstr "arbusto de frambuesas"

#. ~ Description of terrain "raspberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of delicious raspberries.  Watch out for its thorns!"
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño arbusto de deliciosas frambuesas. Ten cuidado con las espinas."

#. ~ Description of terrain "raspberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small raspberry bush that's fruitless.  Watch out for its thorns!"
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño arbusto de frambuesas sin frutos. ¡Cuidado con sus espinas!"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "grape bush"
msgstr "arbusto de uvas"

#. ~ Description of terrain "grape bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A bush of a different species invaded by grape vines."
msgstr "Un arbusto de una especie diferente invadido por vides de uva."

#. ~ Description of terrain "grape bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A bush of a different species invaded by grape vines, but they're fruitless."
msgstr ""
"Un arbusto de diferente especie invadido por la vid de la uva pero sin "
"frutos."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "rose bush"
msgstr "rosal"

#. ~ Description of terrain "rose bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A fat bush of beautiful red roses, if only you could get a date!  Watch out "
"for its thorns!"
msgstr ""
"Un arbusto gordo de hermosas rosas rojas, ¡si tan sólo pudieras conseguir "
"una cita! ¡Cuidado con sus espinas!"

#. ~ Description of terrain "rose bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A fat rose bush that currently has no blooms.  Watch out for its thorns!"
msgstr ""
"Un rosal gordo que actualmente no tiene flores. ¡Cuidado con sus espinas!"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "hydrangea bush"
msgstr "arbusto de hortensia"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hydrangea bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A dense bush of fragrant blue hydrangeas."
msgstr "Un denso arbusto de fragantes hortensias azules."

#. ~ Description of terrain "hydrangea bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A fat hydrangea bush that currently has no blooms."
msgstr "Es un arbusto gordo de hortensias pero sin flores."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "lilac bush"
msgstr "arbusto de lilas"

#. ~ Description of terrain "lilac bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A wide bush of bright pinkish-purple lilacs."
msgstr "Una amplia zarza de lilas de color rosado brillante."

#. ~ Description of terrain "lilac bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A wide lilac bush that currently has no blooms."
msgstr "Es un arbusto ancho de lilas pero sin flores."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "tree trunk"
msgstr "Tronco"

#. ~ Description of terrain "tree trunk"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A section of trunk from a tree that has been cut down.  Can be sawn into "
"logs with the right tool."
msgstr ""
"Una sección del tronco de un árbol que ha sido cortado. Puede ser serrado en"
" leños con la herramienta adecuada."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "tree stump"
msgstr "tocón"

#. ~ Description of terrain "tree stump"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A tree stump, a remnant of a tree that has been cut down."
msgstr "Un tocón de árbol, remanente de un árbol que ha sido cortado."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "woodchips"
msgstr "astillas de madera"

#. ~ Description of terrain "woodchips"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Small splinters of wood laid out in a layer to prevent unwanted plants from "
"growing."
msgstr ""
"Pequeñas astillas de madera tiradas formando una capa para evitar que "
"crezcan plantas no deseadas."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "grass"
msgid_plural "grass"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An area of hardy Kentucky bluegrass about ankle high.  Cutting the grass "
"short enough would destroy the root system, causing this area to turn into a"
" patch of dirt."
msgstr ""
"Un área de resistente hierba azul de Kentucky a la altura del tobillo. "
"Cortar la hierba lo suficientemente corta destruiría el sistema de raíces, "
"causando que esta área se convierta en un parche de tierra."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "white grass"
msgstr "hierba blanca"

#. ~ Description of terrain "white grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An area of Kentucky bluegrass covered in white latex-based paint, with neat "
"lines designed for recreational sports."
msgstr ""
"Una sección de hierba azul de Kentucky cubierta de pintura a base de látex "
"blanco, con líneas limpias diseñadas para deportes recreativos."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "long grass"
msgstr "hierba crecida"

#. ~ Description of terrain "long grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of long, shaggy grass about shin high."
msgstr "Un área de hierba larga y peluda que te llega por la espinilla."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "tall grass"
msgstr "hierba alta"

#. ~ Description of terrain "tall grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of tall grass about head high."
msgstr "Un área de hierba alta a la altura de la cabeza."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "dead grass"
msgstr "hierba muerta"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of long, shaggy grass that hasn't been cut recently."
msgstr "Un área de larga hierba espesa que no ha sido cortada recientemente."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "golf green"
msgstr "verde golf."

#. ~ Description of terrain "golf green"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of grass mowed very short and neat."
msgstr "Un área de hierba segada muy corta y cuidada."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid "alien grass"
msgstr "hierba alienígena"

#. ~ Description of terrain "alien grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An area of something that almost looks like grass.  The blades are serrated "
"and move on their own."
msgstr ""
"Una zona de algo que casi parece hierba. Las hojas son dentadas y se mueven "
"solas."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "golf hole"
msgstr "hoyo de golf"

#. ~ Description of terrain "golf hole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small plastic cup embedded in an area of very short, neat grass."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño vaso de plástico incrustado en un área de hierba muy corta, muy "
"bonita."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "young bamboo shoots"
msgstr "brotes jóvenes de bambú"

#. ~ Description of terrain "young bamboo shoots"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An area of young bamboo shoots about ankle high.  Many shoots are just "
"barely pushing above the ground."
msgstr ""
"Un área de brotes jóvenes de bambú a la altura de los tobillos. Muchos "
"brotes apenas sobresalen del suelo."

#. ~ Description of terrain "young bamboo shoots"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An area of young bamboo shoots about ankle high.  The smallest shoots have "
"already been harvested."
msgstr ""
"Una zona de brotes jóvenes de bambú de una altura aproximada de un tobillo. "
"Los brotes más pequeños ya han sido cosechados."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "long bamboo shoots"
msgstr "brotes largos de bambú"

#. ~ Description of terrain "long bamboo shoots"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of long bamboo shoots about shin high."
msgstr "Un área de brotes de bambú largos que te llegan por la espinilla."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "tall bamboo"
msgstr "bambú alto"

#. ~ Description of terrain "tall bamboo"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A tall bamboo thicket about head high."
msgstr "Un matorral alto de bambú a la altura de la cabeza."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "dead bamboo"
msgstr "bambú muerto"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead bamboo"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of long, brown, dead bamboo shoots covered in white fungus."
msgstr ""
"Un área de largos brotes de bambú muertos de color marrón cubiertos de "
"hongos blancos."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "fern"
msgstr "helecho"

#. ~ Description of terrain "fern"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A short plant with thousands of leaves which grow in a fractal pattern from "
"the stem."
msgstr ""
"Una planta corta con miles de hojas que crecen en un patrón fractal desde el"
" tallo."

#. ~ Description of terrain "fern"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A short plant with thousands of leaves which grow in a fractal pattern.  All"
" of the curled shoots have been harvested."
msgstr ""
"Una planta corta con miles de hojas que crecen en un patrón fractal. Todos "
"lo brotes han sido cosechados."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "mushroom colony"
msgstr "colonia de hongos"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mushroom colony"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large pile of organic matter which has molded over with fungus.  The caps "
"of many mundane mushrooms spring from the top, you can even recognise some."
"  The fungi growing here don't seem edible, though."
msgstr ""
"Un gran montón de materia orgánica que ha sido cubierta con hongos. Las "
"cabezas de muchos hongos mundanos sobresalen por encima, incluso puedes "
"reconocer algunos. Los hongos que crecen aquí no son comestibles."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid "Marloss bush"
msgstr "Arbusto de Marloss"

#. ~ Description of terrain "Marloss bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid ""
"This alien plant superficially resembles a blueberry bush, and hangs with "
"large, juicy pink pomes that emit a heady, fruity aroma."
msgstr ""
"Esta planta alienígena se parece superficialmente a un arbusto de arándanos,"
" y cuelga con grandes y jugosas cúpulas rosadas que emiten un aroma "
"embriagador y frutal."

#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "Marloss bush"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "fungal wall"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "fungal mound"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "fungal shrub"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "fungal tree"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "young fungal tree"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "Marloss tree"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "branches with leaves"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "alien tree"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "underground fungus"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_fungal_termite.json
msgid "poof!"
msgstr "¡puf!"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid "fungal bed"
msgstr "cama fúngica"

#. ~ Description of terrain "fungal bed"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid "Fungus grows thick here, obscuring the ground beneath it."
msgstr ""
"Los hongos crecen gruesos aquí, oscureciendo el suelo debajo de ellos."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid "fungal floor"
msgstr "suelo fúngico"

#. ~ Description of terrain "fungal floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid ""
"Grayish mold coats both the floor and the roof here, silent and still.  "
"Stray spores waft through the air."
msgstr ""
"El moho gris cubre tanto el suelo como el techo aquí, silencioso y quieto. "
"Las esporas vagabundas flotan por el aire."

#. ~ Description of terrain "fungal floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid "Grayish mold coats the floor here, silent and still."
msgstr "El moho gris cubre el suelo aquí, silencioso y quieto."

#. ~ Description of terrain "fungal floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid "Grayish mold coats the ground here, silent and still."
msgstr "El moho gris cubre el suelo aquí, silencioso y quieto."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid "fungal wall"
msgid_plural "fungal walls"
msgstr[0] "muro fúngico"
msgstr[1] "muros fúngicos"
msgstr[2] "muros fúngicos"

#. ~ Description of terrain "fungal wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid ""
"Several thick, large tendrils of fungus perforate the wall here, piercing "
"straight through it from the outside.  Despite the apparent damage, the wall"
" is still structurally sound."
msgstr ""
"Varios gruesos y grandes zarcillos de hongos perforan el muro aquí, "
"atravesándola directamente desde el exterior. A pesar del daño aparente, el "
"muro sigue siendo estructuralmente sólida."

#. ~ Description of terrain "fungal wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid ""
"The fungus here has grown thickly and tightly enough to form a solid wall.  "
"It feels very stiff to the touch, and seems to be very strong."
msgstr ""
"El hongo aquí ha crecido lo suficientemente grueso y apretado como para "
"formar un muro sólido. Se siente muy rígido al tacto, y parece ser muy "
"fuerte."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid "fungal mound"
msgstr "montículo fúngico"

#. ~ Description of terrain "fungal mound"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid "A mound of fungal matter, intertwined in itself."
msgstr "Un montículo de materia fúngica, entrelazado en sí mismo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid "fungal shrub"
msgstr "maleza fúngica"

#. ~ Description of terrain "fungal shrub"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid ""
"This shrub has been completely absorbed by the mushrooms.  Its branches "
"droop and have lost much of their structure, and its leaves have vanished, "
"replaced by fleshy gray sacks that visibly expand and contract."
msgstr ""
"Este arbusto ha sido completamente absorbido por los hongos. Sus ramas se "
"caen y han perdido gran parte de su estructura, y sus hojas se han "
"desvanecido, reemplazadas por sacos carnosos grises que se expanden y "
"contraen visiblemente."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid "fungal tree"
msgstr "árbol fúngico"

#. ~ Description of terrain "fungal tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid ""
"Once tall and majestic, this tree is now a slave to the fungus like the "
"landscape around it.  Its bark is penetrated by and covered with fungal "
"tendrils, and the canopy has rotted away, leaving only the branches, "
"stretching forlornly to the sky as if to escape the infection overrunning "
"it."
msgstr ""
"Una vez alto y majestuoso, este árbol es ahora un esclavo del hongo como el "
"paisaje que lo rodea. Su corteza está penetrada y cubierta de zarcillos de "
"hongos, y el dosel se ha podrido, dejando sólo las ramas, extendiéndose "
"desoladamente hacia el cielo como para escapar de la infección que lo "
"invade."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid "young fungal tree"
msgstr "árbol joven fúngico"

#. ~ Description of terrain "young fungal tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid "A small sapling poking through the ground, infested by fungal mold."
msgstr "Un pequeño arbolito que se asoma por el suelo, infestado de moho."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid "Marloss tree"
msgstr "Árbol de Marloss"

#. ~ Description of terrain "Marloss tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
msgid ""
"This tree stands as a stark outlier to the landscape around it.  Despite its"
" infestation, its leaves wave proudly in the wind, colored pinkish-white.  "
"Its branches are heavy with pink fruit that looks both mutated and "
"delicious."
msgstr ""
"Este árbol se erige como un claro ejemplo del paisaje que lo rodea. A pesar "
"de su infestación, sus hojas se agitan orgullosamente en el viento, de color"
" blanco-rosado. Sus ramas están llenas de frutos rosados que parecen mutados"
" y deliciosos."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "shallow water"
msgstr "agua poco profunda"

#. ~ Description of terrain "shallow water"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"The water isn't too deep here.  With a watertight container, you could "
"gather fresh water from here.  Not safe to drink as is."
msgstr ""
"El agua no es muy profunda aquí. Con un recipiente hermético, se podría "
"recoger agua fresca de aquí. No es seguro beberla tal como está."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "deep water"
msgstr "agua profunda"

#. ~ Description of terrain "deep water"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"You're having trouble seeing the bottom through the deep water here.  With a"
" watertight container, you could gather fresh water from here.  Not safe to "
"drink as is."
msgstr ""
"Tienes problemas para ver el fondo a través de las aguas profundas. Con un "
"recipiente hermético, podrías recoger agua fresca de aquí. No es seguro "
"beberla tal como está."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "murky shallow water"
msgstr "aguas turbias y poco profundas"

#. ~ Description of terrain "murky shallow water"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"The water isn't too deep here but is murky with organic matter.  With a "
"watertight container, you could gather fetid water from here.  Not safe to "
"drink as is."
msgstr ""
"El agua no es muy profunda aquí, pero está turbia por la materia orgánica. "
"Con un recipiente hermético, se podría recoger agua fétida de aquí. No es "
"seguro beberla tal como está."

#. ~ Description of terrain "murky shallow water"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"The water isn't too deep here but it is murky with organic matter.  With a "
"watertight container, you could gather fetid water from here.  Not safe to "
"drink as is."
msgstr ""
"El agua no es muy profunda aquí, pero está turbia por la materia orgánica. "
"Con un recipiente hermético, se podría recoger agua fétida de aquí. No es "
"seguro beberla tal como está."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "flowing shallow water"
msgstr "corrientes de agua poco profunda"

#. ~ Description of terrain "flowing shallow water"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"The streaming water isn't too deep here.  With a watertight container, you "
"could gather fresh water from here.  Not safe to drink as is, although "
"probably safer than stagnant water."
msgstr ""
"El agua corriente no es muy profunda aquí. Con un recipiente hermético, se "
"podría recoger agua fresca de aquí. No es seguro beberla tal cual, aunque "
"probablemente sea más segura que el agua estancada."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "flowing deep water"
msgstr "corriente de agua profunda"

#. ~ Description of terrain "flowing deep water"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"The streaming water looks deep here.  With a watertight container, you could"
" gather fresh water from here.  Not safe to drink as is, although probably "
"safer than stagnant water."
msgstr ""
"El agua que fluye parece profunda aquí. Con un recipiente hermético, se "
"podría recoger agua fresca de aquí. No es seguro beberla tal cual, aunque "
"probablemente sea más segura que el agua estancada."

#. ~ Description of terrain "shallow water"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"The water isn't too deep here.  With a watertight container, you could "
"gather salt water from here."
msgstr ""
"El agua no es muy profunda aquí. Con un recipiente hermético, se podría "
"recoger agua salada de aquí."

#. ~ Description of terrain "deep water"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"You're having trouble seeing the bottom through the deep water here.  With a"
" watertight container, you could gather salt water from here."
msgstr ""
"Tienes problemas para ver el fondo a través de las aguas profundas. Con un "
"recipiente hermético, podrías recoger agua salada de aquí."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "surf"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "surf"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "A broad area of fine sand, washed by waves coming in from the sea."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "pool water"
msgstr "charco de agua"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pool water"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"A deep pool full of water.  Never swim without a lifeguard present.  Even "
"though monsters probably ate them."
msgstr ""
"Una piscina profunda llena de agua. Nunca nades sin un salvavidas presente. "
"Aunque los monstruos probablemente se los comieron."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "shallow pool water"
msgstr "agua de piscina poco profunda"

#. ~ Description of terrain "shallow pool water"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "A shallow pool of water."
msgstr "Una piscina de agua poco profunda."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "sewage"
msgstr "agua cloacal"

#. ~ Description of terrain "sewage"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"Gross.  Sewage water flows through here.  As if it needed saying, this isn't"
" safe to drink."
msgstr ""
"Asqueroso. Las aguas residuales vienen por aquí. No hace falta decirlo, no "
"es seguro beber de aquí."

#. ~ Description of terrain "lava"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"An extremely hot, glowing liquid, composed of molten rock and/or metal.  In "
"some places, lava-grilled steak is a delicacy."
msgstr ""
"Un líquido extremadamente caliente y brillante, compuesto de roca y/o metal "
"fundido. En algunos lugares, el filete de lava a la parrilla es un manjar."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "submersed water"
msgstr "agua sumergida"

#. ~ Description of terrain "submersed water"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"You are submerged below the surface of the water, your feet can't touch the "
"ground.  With a watertight container, you could gather fresh water from "
"here.  Not safe to drink as is."
msgstr ""
"Estás sumergido bajo la superficie del agua, tus pies no pueden tocar el "
"suelo. Con un recipiente hermético, podrías recoger agua fresca de aquí. No "
"es seguro beberla tal como está."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "submersed salt water"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "submersed salt water"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"You are submerged below the surface of the water, your feet can't touch the "
"ground.  With a watertight container, you could gather salt water from here."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
#: data/mods/desert_region/overmap/desert_overmap_terrain.json
msgid "lake bed"
msgstr "lecho del lago"

#. ~ Description of terrain "lake bed"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"You are standing at the bottom of a body of fresh water.  With a watertight "
"container, you could gather fresh water from here.  Not safe to drink as is."
msgstr ""
"Estás parado en el fondo de un cuerpo de agua dulce. Con un recipiente "
"hermético, podrías recoger agua fresca de aquí. No es seguro beberla tal "
"como está."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "ocean bed"
msgstr "lecho oceánico"

#. ~ Description of terrain "ocean bed"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"You are standing at the bottom of a body of salt water.  With a watertight "
"container, you could gather salt water from here.  Not safe to drink as is."
msgstr ""
"Estás parado en el fondo de un cuerpo de agua salada. Con un recipiente "
"hermético, podrías recoger agua salada de aquí. No es seguro beberla tal "
"como está."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "bulkhead"
msgstr "mamparo"

#. ~ Description of terrain "bulkhead"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"The top of a submerged structure.  With a watertight container, you could "
"gather fresh water from here.  Not safe to drink as is."
msgstr ""
"La parte superior de una estructura sumergida. Con un recipiente hermético, "
"podrías recoger agua dulce de aquí. No es seguro beberla tal como está."

#. ~ Description of terrain "bulkhead"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "The bottom of a submerged structure."
msgstr "El fondo de una estructura sumergida."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "submerged concrete"
msgstr "hormigón sumergido"

#. ~ Description of terrain "submerged concrete"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"You are standing at the bottom of a body of fresh water on a pad of "
"concrete.  With a watertight container, you could gather fresh water from "
"here.  Not safe to drink as is."
msgstr ""
"Estás parado en el fondo de un cuerpo de agua dulce, sobre una plataforma de"
" hormigón. Con un recipiente hermético, podrías recoger agua fresca de aquí."
" No es seguro beberla tal como está."

#. ~ Description of terrain "submerged concrete"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"You are standing at the bottom of a body of fresh water on a pad of yellow-"
"painted concrete.  With a watertight container, you could gather fresh water"
" from here.  Not safe to drink as is."
msgstr ""
"Estás de pie en el fondo de una masa de agua dulce sobre una plataforma de "
"hormigón pintada de amarillo. Con un recipiente hermético, podrías recoger "
"agua dulce de aquí. No es seguro beberla tal como está."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "hot spring water"
msgstr "agua termal"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hot spring water"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid ""
"Scalding hot water, not particularly safe for swimming.  With a watertight "
"container, you could gather fresh water from here.  Not safe to drink as is."
msgstr ""
"Agua caliente hirviendo, no es particularmente segura para nadar. Con un "
"recipiente hermético, podrías recoger agua fresca de aquí. No es segura para"
" beber tal cual."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "recess"
msgstr "huecos"

#. ~ Description of terrain "recess"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
msgid "A shallow pit in the ground."
msgstr "Un pozo poco profundo en el suelo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "metal compactor"
msgstr "compactadora de metal"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal compactor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A hydraulic machine for squeezing scrap into more compact chunks.  Useless "
"now that there's no power."
msgstr ""
"Una máquina hidráulica para exprimir la chatarra en trozos más compactos. "
"Inútil ahora que no hay energía."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "gasoline pump"
msgstr "surtidor de gasolina"

#. ~ Description of terrain "gasoline pump"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"Precious GASOLINE.  The former world bowed to their petroleum god as it led "
"them to their ruin.  There's plenty left over to fuel your inner road "
"warrior.  If this gas dispenser doesn't give up the goods for free, you may "
"have to pay at a nearby terminal."
msgstr ""
"Preciosa GASOLINA. El mundo anterior se inclinó ante su dios del petróleo "
"mientras los llevaba a su ruina. Hay mucho que queda para alimentar a su "
"guerrero interior del camino. Si este dispensador de gasolina no entrega la "
"mercancía gratis, puede que tengas que pagar en una terminal cercana."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "smashed gas pump"
msgstr "surtidor de gasolina roto"

#. ~ Description of terrain "smashed gas pump"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"The horror!  This gasoline pump has been destroyed, denying you access to "
"the liquid gold."
msgstr ""
"¡El horror! Esta bomba de gasolina ha sido destruida, negándote el acceso al"
" oro líquido."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "diesel pump"
msgstr "surtidor diésel"

#. ~ Description of terrain "diesel pump"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A diesel fuel pump.  This roadside attraction provides all the thick, gloopy"
" liquid POWER you need to move your sensibly oversized APOCALYPTIC "
"SUPERTRUCK from point A to points beyond.  If it doesn't dispense fuel "
"immediately, try banging on it or grunt your way over the nearby payment "
"terminal."
msgstr ""
"Una bomba de combustible diésel. Esta atracción en la carretera proporciona "
"todo el líquido espeso y pegajoso PODER que necesitas para mover tu "
"sobredimensionado SUPERCAMIÓN APOCALÍPTICO desde el punto A a los puntos más"
" allá. Si no suministra combustible inmediatamente, intenta golpear o gruñir"
" sobre la terminal de pago cercana."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "smashed diesel pump"
msgstr "surtidor diésel roto"

#. ~ Description of terrain "smashed diesel pump"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"You're not getting any diesel out of this pump any time soon.  Some "
"barbarian decided to take their frustration out on it."
msgstr ""
"No vas a sacar nada de diesel de esta bomba en un futuro próximo. Algún "
"bárbaro decidió descargar su frustración en ella."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "JP8 pump"
msgstr "surtidor JP8"

#. ~ Description of terrain "JP8 pump"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A pump that dispenses JP8.  If this gas dispenser doesn't give up the goods "
"for free, you may have to pay at a nearby terminal."
msgstr ""
"Un surtidor que sirve tiene JP8. Si este surtidor no da su contenido de "
"forma gratuita, es posible que tengas que pagar en una terminal cercana."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "smashed JP8 pump"
msgstr "surtidor JP8 aplastado"

#. ~ Description of terrain "smashed JP8 pump"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"You're not getting any JP8 out of this pump any time soon.  Some barbarian "
"decided to take their frustration out on it."
msgstr ""
"No vas a sacar nada de JP8 de esta surtidor en un futuro próximo. Algún "
"bárbaro decidió descargar su frustración en el."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "avgas pump"
msgstr "surtidor de avgas"

#. ~ Description of terrain "avgas pump"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A pump that dispenses avgas.  If this gas dispenser doesn't give up the "
"goods for free, you may have to pay at a nearby terminal."
msgstr ""
"Un surtidor que sirve avgas. Si este surtidor no da su contenido de forma "
"gratuita, es posible que tengas que pagar en una terminal cercana."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "smashed avgas pump"
msgstr "surtidor roto de avgas"

#. ~ Description of terrain "smashed avgas pump"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"You're not getting any avgas out of this pump any time soon.  Some barbarian"
" decided to take their frustration out on it."
msgstr ""
"No vas a poder conseguir avgas de este surtidor. Algún bárbaro decidió "
"liberar toda su frustración en él."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "ATM"
msgstr "cajero automático"

#. ~ Description of terrain "ATM"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"For your banking convenience, this Automated Teller Machine is fully capable"
" of operating autonomously in the event of complete network failure.  You "
"can deposit funds from cash cards and migrate all of your inflation-adjusted"
" earnings to a single card.  This thing has seen better days; there's been a"
" run on the bank, and this machine has the dents and cracks to prove it."
msgstr ""
"Para su conveniencia bancaria, este cajero automático es totalmente capaz de"
" operar de forma autónoma en caso de fallo completo de la red. Puede "
"depositar fondos de tarjetas de efectivo y migrar todas sus ganancias "
"ajustadas a la inflación a una sola tarjeta. Estas cosas han visto días "
"mejores. Ha habido una carrera en el banco, y esta máquina tiene las "
"abolladuras y grietas para probarlo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "ticket vendor"
msgstr "vendedor de entradas"

#. ~ Description of terrain "ticket vendor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A machine with a little screen and slots, intended to take your money and "
"provide you with a ticket."
msgstr ""
"Una máquina que tiene una pequeña pantalla, y ranuras destinadas a tomar su "
"dinero y proporcionarle un billete."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "ticket machine"
msgstr "máquina de billetes"

#. ~ Description of terrain "ticket machine"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A machine that will provide you access to whatever lies beyond it - for the "
"price of a ticket, of course."
msgstr ""
"Una máquina le dará acceso a todo lo que esté más allá de ella - por el "
"precio de un billete, por supuesto."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "ventilation shutters"
msgstr "persianas de ventilación"

#. ~ Description of terrain "ventilation shutters"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A large wall-mounted panel, covered with fragile metal sheets that regulate "
"airflow."
msgstr ""
"Un gran panel montado en la pared, cubierto de frágiles láminas metálicas "
"que regulan el flujo de aire."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "missile"
msgstr "misil"

#. ~ Description of terrain "missile"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A section of an ICBM, an Intercontinental Ballistic Missile.  This isn't the"
" kind of rocket that goes to the moon."
msgstr ""
"Una sección de un ICBM, un Misil Balístico Intercontinental. Este no es el "
"tipo de cohete que va a la luna."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "blown-out missile"
msgstr "misil explotado"

#. ~ Description of terrain "blown-out missile"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A section of an ICBM, an Intercontinental Ballistic Missile.  This isn't the"
" kind of rocket that's going anywhere."
msgstr ""
"Una sección de un ICBM, un Misil Balístico Intercontinental. Este no es el "
"tipo de cohete que va a ninguna parte."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "faction_base_fire_lookout_tower_radio"
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "faction_base_helipad_radio"
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "faction_base_lightindustry_00_radio"
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "faction_base_lightindustry_10_radio"
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "faction_base_outpost_cross_radio"
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "faction_base_outpost_normal_radio"
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "fbmh_2_radio_tower"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_commercial.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/base/fbmc_fire_lookout_tower/recipe_modular_fire_lookout_tower_common.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/base/fbmc_helipad/recipe_modular_helipad_common.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/base/fbmc_lightindustry/recipe_modular_lightindustry_00.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/base/fbmc_lightindustry/recipe_modular_lightindustry_10.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/base/fbmc_outpost/recipe_modular_outpost_cross.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/base/fbmc_outpost/recipe_modular_outpost_normal.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/base/recipe_modular_hub/version_2/recipe_modular_field_common.json
#: data/mods/alt_map_key/overmap_terrain.json
msgid "radio tower"
msgstr "torre de radio"

#. ~ Description of terrain "radio tower"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "The structure of a radio transmission tower."
msgstr "La estructura de una torre de transmisión de radio."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/furniture.json
msgid "radio controls"
msgstr "radiocontroles"

#. ~ Description of terrain "radio controls"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A console that appears to control a nearby radio transmission tower.  It "
"doesn't seem to be fully operational."
msgstr ""
"Una consola que parece controlar una torre de transmisión de radio cercana. "
"No parece estar completamente operativa."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "high gauge pipe"
msgstr "tubería de gran diámetro"

#. ~ Description of terrain "high gauge pipe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "A section of high gauge pipe."
msgstr "Una sección de un tubo de alto calibre."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "high gauge pump"
msgstr "bomba de alto calibre"

#. ~ Description of terrain "high gauge pump"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"An unpowered pump that previously would have moved fluids around in a hurry."
msgstr ""
"Una bomba sin energía que anteriormente habría movido los fluidos de un lado"
" a otro a toda prisa."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "CVD machine"
msgstr "máquina CVD"

#. ~ Description of terrain "CVD machine"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"The bulk of a highly technical-looking apparatus controlled by a nearby "
"console."
msgstr ""
"El grueso de un aparato de aspecto muy técnico controlado por una consola "
"cercana."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "CVD control panel"
msgstr "panel de control de CVD"

#. ~ Description of terrain "CVD control panel"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A VERY expensive-looking apparatus that's labeled 'Chemical Vapor Deposition"
" Machine'.  With the input of certain exceptionally rare chemicals and "
"elements, one could conceivably coat one's weapon with diamond.  While the "
"process is extremely complicated, a previous user has helpfully sketched: "
"Hydrogen + charcoal = smiley face."
msgstr ""
"Un aparato de aspecto MUY caro que se llama \"Máquina de Depósito de Vapor "
"Químico\". Con la entrada de ciertos químicos y elementos excepcionalmente "
"raros, uno podría en teoría cubrir su arma con diamantes. Aunque que el "
"proceso es extremadamente complicado, un usuario anterior hizo un bosquejo "
"útil: Hidrógeno + carbón vegetal = cara sonriente."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "nanofabricator"
msgstr "nanofabricador"

#. ~ Description of terrain "nanofabricator"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A great column of advanced machinery.  Within this self-contained, "
"miniaturized factory, several 3D printers work in tandem with a robotic "
"assembler to manufacture nearly any inorganic object."
msgstr ""
"Una gran columna de maquinaria avanzada. Dentro de esta fábrica autónoma y "
"miniaturizada, varias impresoras 3D trabajan en tándem con un ensamblador "
"robótico para fabricar casi cualquier objeto inorgánico."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_manufactured.json
msgid "nanofabricator control panel"
msgstr "panel de control del nanofabricante"

#. ~ Description of terrain "nanofabricator control panel"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A small computer panel attached to a nanofabricator.  It has a single slot "
"for reading templates."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño panel de computadora conectado a un nanofabricador. Tiene una "
"sola ranura para leer plantillas."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "cloning vat"
msgstr "tanque de clonación"

#. ~ Description of terrain "cloning vat"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A vat full of solution, probably intended to hold growing clones of people "
"or other life forms."
msgstr ""
"Una cuba llena de una solución, probablemente destinada a albergar clones "
"crecientes de personas u otras formas de vida."

#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "cloning vat"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "Osiris chamber"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_tanks.json
msgid "plunk."
msgstr "plank"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "slot machine"
msgstr "tragaperras"

#. ~ Description of terrain "slot machine"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A machine with a bright screen flashing hypnotic promises of wealth.  If "
"gambling with your life on a daily basis isn't enough for you, you can also "
"gamble with this."
msgstr ""
"Una máquina con una pantalla brillante que muestra hipnóticas promesas de "
"riqueza. Si apostar con tu vida diariamente no es suficiente para ti, "
"también puedes apostar con esto."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "water pump"
msgstr "bomba de agua"

#. ~ Description of terrain "water pump"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A deep well, collecting groundwater.  An installed pump allows you to draw "
"water from it."
msgstr ""
"Un pozo profundo usado para recolectar agua subterránea. Tiene instalada una"
" bomba que permite sacar el agua."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "wooden well"
msgstr "pozo de madera"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden well"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A deep well, collecting groundwater.  A wooden frame with a rope and bucket "
"allows you to draw water from it, with some elbow grease."
msgstr ""
"Un pozo profundo que recoge el agua subterránea. Un chasis de madera con una"
" soga y un cubo permiten sacar agua de él, con algo de esfuerzo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "salt water pump"
msgstr "bomba de agua salada"

#. ~ Description of terrain "salt water pump"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A water pump connected to a pipe supplying it with salt water.  Not good to "
"drink, but it has other uses."
msgstr ""
"Una bomba de agua conectada a una tubería que le suministra agua salada. No "
"sirve para beber, pero tiene otros usos."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "water dispenser"
msgstr "dispensador de agua"

#. ~ Description of terrain "water dispenser"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "A machine with several taps that dispenses clean water."
msgstr "Una máquina con varios grifos que dispensa agua limpia."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "telecom cabinet"
msgstr "cabina de telecomunicación"

#. ~ Description of terrain "telecom cabinet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A cabinet full of telecom equipment.  With the lines down, you might be able"
" to take it apart for its useful electronics."
msgstr ""
"Un armario lleno de equipos de telecomunicaciones. Con las líneas caídas, "
"podrías ser capaz de desmontarlo por su útil electrónica."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "damaged telecom cabinet"
msgstr "cabina dañada de telecomunicación"

#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged telecom cabinet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A damaged telecom cabinet.  You might still be able to salvage some useful "
"electronic scrap from it."
msgstr ""
"Un armario de telecomunicaciones dañado. Puede que todavía seas capaz de "
"salvar algunos desechos electrónicos útiles de él."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "HV oil circuit breaker"
msgstr "disyuntor en aceite de alta tensión"

#. ~ Description of terrain "HV oil circuit breaker"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "A circuit breaker that uses oil in its arc suppression chamber."
msgstr ""
"Un disyuntor que usa aceite en su cámara de supresión de arco.Un disyuntor "
"que usa aceite en su cámara de supresión de arco."

#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "HV oil circuit breaker"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "small HV oil circuit breaker"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "pow!"
msgstr "¡pam!"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "small HV oil circuit breaker"
msgstr "disyuntor en aceite pequeño de alta tensión"

#. ~ Description of terrain "small HV oil circuit breaker"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "A small circuit breaker that uses oil in its arc suppression chamber."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño disyuntor que usa aceite en su cámara de supresión de arco."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "large switchgear"
msgstr "dispositivo de distribución grande"

#. ~ Description of terrain "large switchgear"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A switchgear panel.  It's covered in breaker switches, fuses, and gauges."
msgstr ""
"Un panel de interruptores. Está cubierto de interruptores, fusibles y "
"medidores."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "small switchgear"
msgstr "conmutadores pequeños"

#. ~ Description of terrain "small switchgear"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A small switchgear panel.  It's covered in breaker switches, fuses, and "
"gauges."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño panel de interruptores. Está cubierto de interruptores, fusibles "
"y medidores."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "lightning arrester"
msgstr "pararrayos"

#. ~ Description of terrain "lightning arrester"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A component designed to protect insulation and conductors in an electrical "
"system by directing lightning through itself and into the ground."
msgstr ""
"Un componente diseñado para proteger el aislamiento y los conductores en un "
"sistema eléctrico dirigiendo el rayo a través de sí mismo y al suelo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "disconnect switch"
msgstr "interruptor de desconexión"

#. ~ Description of terrain "disconnect switch"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A switch used to make sure an electrical system doesn't have any current "
"flowing through it, for maintenance periods."
msgstr ""
"Un interruptor que se usa para asegurarse de que un sistema eléctrico no "
"tiene ninguna corriente que fluya a través de él, para los períodos de "
"mantenimiento."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "current transformer"
msgstr "transformador de corriente"

#. ~ Description of terrain "current transformer"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "An electronic component used to transform the voltage of a current."
msgstr ""
"Un componente electrónico usado para transformar el voltaje de una "
"corriente."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "potential transformer"
msgstr "transformador de potencial"

#. ~ Description of terrain "potential transformer"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "A specialized type of electrical transformer."
msgstr "Un tipo especializado de transformador eléctrico, "

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "conveyor belt"
msgstr "cinta transportadora"

#. ~ Description of terrain "conveyor belt"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "A conveyor belt.  Used to transport things."
msgstr "Una cinta transportadora. Se usa para transportar cosas."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "milking machine"
msgstr "máquina de ordeño"

#. ~ Description of terrain "milking machine"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "A machine used in the dairy industry to milk cows."
msgstr "Una máquina utilizada en la industria lechera para ordeñar vacas."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "bulk tank"
msgstr "tanque de carga"

#. ~ Description of terrain "bulk tank"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "A heavy, high capacity tank."
msgstr "Un tanque pesado y de gran capacidad."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "rocky obstacle"
msgstr "obstáculo rocoso"

#. ~ Description of terrain "rocky obstacle"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"Some larger rocks arranged and crudely rammed into the ground to slow down "
"who or whatever is trying to cross."
msgstr ""
"Algunas piedras grandes colocadas y juntadas de manera burda en el suelo "
"para frenar a cualquiera que intente pasar."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting
#. "faction_base_fire_lookout_tower_root_cellar"
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "faction_base_helipad_root_cellar"
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "faction_base_lighthouse_root_cellar"
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting
#. "faction_base_lightindustry_00_root_cellar"
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting
#. "faction_base_lightindustry_10_root_cellar"
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting
#. "faction_base_outpost_cross_root_cellar"
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting
#. "faction_base_outpost_normal_root_cellar"
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "faction_base_radio_tower_root_cellar"
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "fbmh_2_root_cellar"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/base/fbmc_fire_lookout_tower/recipe_modular_fire_lookout_tower_common.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/base/fbmc_helipad/recipe_modular_helipad_common.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/base/fbmc_lighthouse/recipe_modular_lighthouse_common.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/base/fbmc_lightindustry/recipe_modular_lightindustry_00.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/base/fbmc_lightindustry/recipe_modular_lightindustry_10.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/base/fbmc_outpost/recipe_modular_outpost_cross.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/base/fbmc_outpost/recipe_modular_outpost_normal.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/base/fbmc_radio_tower/recipe_modular_radio_tower_common.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/base/recipe_modular_hub/version_2/recipe_modular_field_common.json
msgid "root cellar"
msgstr "bodega de raíz"

#. ~ Description of terrain "root cellar"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "A cellar dug into the earth for storing food in a cool environment."
msgstr ""
"Un sótano excavado en la tierra para almacenar alimentos en un ambiente "
"fresco."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "covered well"
msgstr "pozo de agua cubierto"

#. ~ Description of terrain "covered well"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A deep well, collecting groundwater.  You won't be able to get any water "
"unless you add some mechanism for drawing it up to the surface."
msgstr ""
"Un pozo profundo, con agua subterránea. No podrás sacar agua a menos que "
"añadas algún mecanismo para subirlo a la superficie."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "covered salt water well"
msgstr "pozo cubierto de agua salada"

#. ~ Description of terrain "covered salt water well"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A deep well, collecting salt water from a surrounding swamp.  You won't be "
"able to get any water unless you add some mechanism for drawing it up to the"
" surface."
msgstr ""
"Un pozo profundo, con agua salada de una ciénaga cercana. No podrás sacar "
"agua a menos que añadas algún mecanismo para subirlo a la superficie."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "pit filled with straw"
msgstr "foso lleno con paja"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pit filled with straw"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A shallow pit filled with some straw.  Very crude.  Itchy and uncomfortable,"
" but better than the bare ground."
msgstr ""
"Un foso poco profundo relleno con algo de paja. Muy tosco. Pica y es "
"incómodo, pero es mejor que el suelo desnudo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "improvised shelter"
msgstr "refugio improvisado"

#. ~ Description of terrain "improvised shelter"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"An improvised shelter providing a little bit of protection, that can be used"
" to take refuge from the elements or to protect a campfire from the rain."
msgstr ""
"Un refugio improvisado que proporciona un poco de protección, que puedes "
"utilizar para protegerte de la intemperie o proteger una fogata de la "
"lluvia."

#. ~ Description of terrain "improvised shelter"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"An improvised shelter which has been made a bit more comfortable by filling "
"it with dry plant matter, which should provide some more insulation.  Trying"
" to contain a fire here would be a bad idea."
msgstr ""
"Un refugio improvisado que se ha hecho un poco más cómodo llenándolo de "
"materia vegetal seca, lo que debería proporcionar algo más de aislamiento. "
"Intentar contener un fuego aquí sería una mala idea."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "pine lean-to"
msgstr "cobertizo de pino"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pine lean-to"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A small shelter, roofed with pine branches, that can be used to take refuge "
"from the elements or to protect a campfire from the rain."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño refugio techado con hojas de pino, que puede utilizarse para "
"refugiarse de la intemperie o para proteger una fogata de la lluvia."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "tarp lean-to"
msgstr "cobertizo de lona"

#. ~ Description of terrain "tarp lean-to"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A small shelter, covered by a waterproof tarp, that can be used to take "
"refuge from the elements or to protect a campfire from the rain."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño refugio cubierto por una lona impermeable, que puede utilizarse "
"para refugiarse de la intemperie o para proteger una fogata de la lluvia."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "brick oven base"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "brick oven base"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "A flat assembly of carefully stacked bricks that is not quite an oven."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid "exposed brick oven"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "exposed brick oven"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
msgid ""
"A large brick oven that could make several pizzas at once.  This one seems "
"to be missing its door, and cannot be used in such a state."
msgstr ""

