msgstr ""
"Un puñado de nueces duras de un árbol nogal, todavía con sus cáscaras."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "butternuts"
msgid_plural "butternuts"
msgstr[0] "nuez"
msgstr[1] "nueces"
msgstr[2] "nueces"

#. ~ Description of "butternuts"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A handful of nuts from a butternut tree, still in their shell."
msgstr ""
"Un puñado de nueces duras de un árbol avellano, todavía en sus cáscaras."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "sewage water"
msgid_plural "sewage water"
msgstr[0] "agua de alcantarillado"
msgstr[1] "aguas de alcantarillado"
msgstr[2] "aguas de alcantarillado"

#. ~ Description of "sewage water"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "Turbid liquid from the sewers with an awful stench."
msgstr ""
"Líquido turbio proveniente de las alcantarillas con un hedor horrible."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "detergent"
msgid_plural "detergent"
msgstr[0] "detergente"
msgstr[1] "detergentes"
msgstr[2] "detergentes"

#. ~ Description of "detergent"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A popular pre-Cataclysm washing powder."
msgstr "Un detergente en polvo muy popular pre-Cataclismo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "soap flakes"
msgid_plural "soap flakes"
msgstr[0] "escamas de jabón"
msgstr[1] "escamas de jabón"
msgstr[2] "escamas de jabón"

#. ~ Description of "soap flakes"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of flakes shaved off a bar of soap, suitable for use in a washing "
"machine."
msgstr ""
"Un puñado de escamas de barra de jabón cortada adecuado para usar en "
"lavadora."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "lye"
msgid_plural "lye"
msgstr[0] "sosa caústica"
msgstr[1] "sosa caústica"
msgstr[2] "sosa caústica"

#. ~ Description of "lye"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A liquid form of sodium hydroxide.  It is highly corrosive; handle with "
"care."
msgstr ""
"Una forma líquida de hidróxido de sodio. Es altamente corrosiva; manejar con"
" cuidado."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "potassium lye"
msgid_plural "potassium lye"
msgstr[0] "lejía potásica"
msgstr[1] "lejía potásica"
msgstr[2] "lejía potásica"

#. ~ Description of "potassium lye"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A liquid form of potassium hydroxide.  It is highly corrosive; handle with "
"care."
msgstr ""
"Una forma líquida de hidróxido de potasio. Es altamente corrosiva; manejar "
"con cuidado."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "nanomaterial canister"
msgid_plural "nanomaterial canisters"
msgstr[0] "contenedor de nanomaterial"
msgstr[1] "contenedores de nanomaterial"
msgstr[2] "contenedores de nanomaterial"

#. ~ Description of "nanomaterial canister"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A steel canister containing carbon, iron, titanium, copper, and other "
"elements in specifically engineered atomic-scale configurations.  A "
"nanofabricator can assemble them into usable items."
msgstr ""
"Un bote de acero que contiene carbono, hierro, titanio, cobre y otros "
"elementos en configuraciones específicamente diseñadas en escala atómica. Un"
" nanofabricador puede ensamblar estos elementos en objetos útiles."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "wood ashes"
msgid_plural "wood ashes"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "wood ashes"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of almost-weightless residue left after the burning of some "
"substance."
msgstr ""
"Un puñado de un residuo casi sin peso dejado después de quemar alguna "
"sustancia."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "corpse ashes"
msgid_plural "corpse ashes"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "corpse ashes"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "The burnt remains of a person or animal."
msgstr "Los restos quemados de una persona o animal."

#. ~ 0.7134 g/cm3
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "ether"
msgid_plural "ether"
msgstr[0] "éter"
msgstr[1] "éter"
msgstr[2] "éter"

#. ~ 0.7134 g/cm3
#. ~ Description of "ether"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A useful industrial solvent, and the first inhalative anesthetic in "
"widespread use.  Its uncomfortable side effects and tendency to explode "
"caused it to fall out of favor decades ago in the developed world.  If you "
"can't get the good stuff, however, it might make a passable substitute."
msgstr ""
"Un disolvente industrial útil, y el primer anestésico inhalatorio de uso "
"generalizado. Sus incómodos efectos secundarios y su tendencia a explotar "
"hicieron que cayera en desgracia hace décadas en el mundo desarrollado. Si "
"no puedes conseguir uno bueno, sin embargo, puede ser un sustituto pasable."

#. ~ 1.1004 g/cm3
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "dimethyl sulfoxide"
msgid_plural "dimethyl sulfoxide"
msgstr[0] "dimetilsulfóxido"
msgstr[1] "dimetilsulfóxido"
msgstr[2] "dimetilsulfóxido"

#. ~ 1.1004 g/cm3
#. ~ Description of "dimethyl sulfoxide"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Dimethyl sulfoxide, or DMSO, is a common and important aprotic solvent, "
"capable of dissolving a huge range of things.  It has the unusual property "
"of being absorbed very quickly through the skin, causing a garlic flavor in "
"the mouth, even if it touched your arm."
msgstr ""
"El dimetilsulfóxido, o DMSO, es un disolvente aprótico común e importante, "
"capaz de disolver una enorme variedad de cosas. Tiene la extraña propiedad "
"absorberse muy rápidamente a través de la piel, provocando un sabor a ajo en"
" la boca, incluso si solo te tocó el brazo."

#. ~ 1.489 g/cm3 at 25C
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "chloroform"
msgid_plural "chloroform"
msgstr[0] "cloroformo"
msgstr[1] "cloroformo"
msgstr[2] "cloroformo"

#. ~ 1.489 g/cm3 at 25C
#. ~ Description of "chloroform"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Famous for its properties as an illicit sedative, this substance is also a "
"very good solvent.  In particular, it's used a lot in nuclear magnetic "
"resonance spectroscopy."
msgstr ""
"Famosa por su capacidad como sedante ilícito, esta sustancia es también un "
"muy buen disolvente. En particular, se usa mucho en la espectroscopia de "
"resonancia magnética nuclear."

#. ~ 1.07 g/cm3
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "phenol"
msgid_plural "phenol"
msgstr[0] "fenol"
msgstr[1] "fenol"
msgstr[2] "fenol"

#. ~ 1.07 g/cm3
#. ~ Description of "phenol"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A useful and potent solvent with a wide range of reactive applications.  It "
"can be used to make a huge number of plastics and polymers, it can be an "
"antiseptic, it can strip paint and break down epoxy, and it can burn your "
"skin away like tissue paper under a heat gun.  Wear gloves."
msgstr ""
"Un útil y potente disolvente que tiene una amplia gama de aplicaciones "
"reactivas. Puede utilizarse para fabricar un gran número de plásticos y "
"polímeros, como antiséptico, para decapar la pintura, descomponer epoxi, y "
"puede quemar la piel como si fuera un pañuelo de papel bajo una pistola de "
"calor. Ponte guantes."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "benzene"
msgid_plural "benzene"
msgstr[0] "benceno"
msgstr[1] "benceno"
msgstr[2] "benceno"

#. ~ Description of "benzene"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A colorless, highly flammable liquid with a sweet odor, one of the "
"elementary petrochemicals.  Being used primarily as a precursor to the "
"manufacture of chemicals with more complex structure, it's a major "
"industrial chemical, but finds limited use in consumer items because of its "
"toxicity."
msgstr ""
"Un líquido incoloro altamente inflamable con olor dulce, uno de los "
"productos petroquímicos elementales. Utilizado principalmente como precursor"
" para la fabricación de productos químicos de estructura más compleja, es un"
" producto químico industrial importante, pero encuentra un uso limitado en "
"artículos de consumo debido a su toxicidad."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "toluene"
msgid_plural "toluene"
msgstr[0] "tolueno"
msgstr[1] "tolueno"
msgstr[2] "tolueno"

#. ~ Description of "toluene"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A colorless, toxic, and highly flammable liquid which smells like paint "
"thinner.  It's predominantly used as an industrial feedstock and a solvent, "
"and is also used as an intoxicative inhalant in a manner unintended by "
"manufacturers."
msgstr ""
"Un líquido incoloro, tóxico y altamente inflamable que huele a disolvente. "
"Se utiliza principalmente como materia prima industrial, como disolvente, y "
"también con fines de inhalación de sustancias tóxicas de forma no "
"intencionada por los fabricantes."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "glycerol"
msgid_plural "glycerol"
msgstr[0] "glicerol"
msgstr[1] "glicerol"
msgstr[2] "glicerol"

#. ~ Description of "glycerol"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Also called glycerin, this clear, odorless liquid is both a handy skin "
"moisturizer and an ingredient necessary to make dynamite."
msgstr ""
"También llamado glicerina, este líquido claro e inodoro es a la vez un "
"práctico humectante para la piel y un ingrediente necesario para fabricar "
"dinamita."

#. ~ Bulk density is around 0.5 g/mL
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "peptone broth powder"
msgid_plural "peptone broth powder"
msgstr[0] "caldo de peptona en polvo"
msgstr[1] "caldo de peptona en polvo"
msgstr[2] "caldo de peptona en polvo"

#. ~ Bulk density is around 0.5 g/mL
#. ~ Description of "peptone broth powder"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A pre-mixed salty solution of protein and sugar.  It's meant for bacteria to"
" eat, but if you were desperate, you could eat it too; it's not much "
"different from cup noodle stock."
msgstr ""
"Una solución salada premezclada de proteína y azúcar. Está diseñada para ser"
" consumida por las bacterias, pero si estás desesperado también puedes "
"comerla. No es muy distinta a una de esas sopas de fideos en vaso."

#. ~ Bulk density is around 0.55 g/mL
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "agar"
msgid_plural "agar"
msgstr[0] "agar"
msgstr[1] "agar"
msgstr[2] "agar"

#. ~ Bulk density is around 0.55 g/mL
#. ~ Description of "agar"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Clear flakes of processed seaweed that can be dissolved in boiling water to "
"create a very sturdy, temperature-resistant gel.  Not only is it good for "
"making gels to separate molecules by size, but it's a great cheat ingredient"
" to make sure your jellies set properly."
msgstr ""
"Escamas claras de alga procesada que puede ser disuelta en agua hirviendo "
"para crear un gel muy fuerte y resistente a la temperatura. No solamente es "
"bueno para hacer gel para separar las moléculas por tamaño, también sirve "
"como ingrediente para hacer que tus gelatinas estén firmes."

#. ~ Bulk density is around 0.5 g/mL (because it's a powder, the actual
#. density of 1.12 g/mL is not useful)
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "acrylamide"
msgid_plural "acrylamide"
msgstr[0] "acrilamida"
msgstr[1] "acrilamida"
msgstr[2] "acrilamida"

#. ~ Bulk density is around 0.5 g/mL (because it's a powder, the actual
#. density of 1.12 g/mL is not useful)
#. ~ Description of "acrylamide"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of highly carcinogenic white powder that can be readily "
"polymerized into a whole bunch of useful water-soluble gels."
msgstr ""
"Un puñado de polvo blanco altamente cancerígeno puede ser fácilmente "
"polimerizado en un montón de útiles geles solubles en agua."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "steel grille"
msgid_plural "steel grilles"
msgstr[0] "rejilla de acero"
msgstr[1] "rejillas de acero"
msgstr[2] "rejillas de acero"

#. ~ Description of "steel grille"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A metal grille.  It can be used as a framework for making a chemical "
"catalyst."
msgstr ""
"Una rejilla de metal. Puede ser usada como estructura para hacer un "
"catalizador químico."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "cobalt-60 pellet"
msgid_plural "cobalt-60 pellets"
msgstr[0] "perdigón de cobalto 60"
msgstr[1] "perdigones de cobalto 60"
msgstr[2] "perdigones de cobalto 60"

#. ~ Description of "cobalt-60 pellet"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A piece of unshielded radioactive material that used to be a part of some "
"nuclear industry equipment.  You have yet to find some use for it, and you "
"probably shouldn't stand near it."
msgstr ""
"Una pieza de material radioactivo que antes era parte de algún equipamiento "
"industrial nuclear. Todavía tienes que encontrarle alguna utilidad, y no "
"deberías estar muy cerca."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "wooden bead"
msgid_plural "wooden beads"
msgstr[0] "cuenta de madera"
msgstr[1] "cuentas de madera"
msgstr[2] "cuentas de madera"

#. ~ Description of "wooden bead"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A wooden bead.  It can be used to craft inscribable jewelry or create a "
"beaded curtain door."
msgstr ""
"Una cuenta de madera. Puede usarse para fabricar joyería o crear una puerta "
"de cortina de cuentas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "gravelbag"
msgid_plural "gravelbags"
msgstr[0] "bolsa de grava"
msgstr[1] "bolsas de grava"
msgstr[2] "bolsas de grava"

#. ~ Description of "gravelbag"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A canvas sack filled with gravel.  It can be used to construct simple "
"barricades."
msgstr ""
"Un saco de lona lleno de gravilla. Puede ser usado para construir barricadas"
" simples."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "earthbag"
msgid_plural "earthbags"
msgstr[0] "bolsa de tierra"
msgstr[1] "bolsas de tierra"
msgstr[2] "bolsas de tierra"

#. ~ Description of "earthbag"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A canvas sack filled with soil.  It can be used to construct simple "
"barricades."
msgstr ""
"Un saco de lona lleno de tierra. Puede ser usado para construir barricadas "
"simples."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "rosin"
msgid_plural "rosin"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "rosin"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A chunk of yellowish rosin, usable as a flux for soldering."
msgstr "Un trozo de resina amarillenta, utilizable como fundente para soldar."

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ roughly 35grams of acetylene per cubic foot at STP. Volume given is when
#. compressed - B tank has 9.17 L tank and holds 40 cubic feet.
#: data/json/items/ammo/weldgas.json
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "acetylene"
msgid_plural "acetylene"
msgstr[0] "acetileno"
msgstr[1] "acetileno"
msgstr[2] "acetileno"

#. ~ Description of "acetylene"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A flammable gas that explodes under pressure.  Combined with oxygen, "
"acetylene makes a great welding gas."
msgstr ""
"Un gas inflamable que explota bajo presión. Combinado con el oxígeno, el "
"acetileno es un gran gas para soldar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "formic acid"
msgid_plural "formic acid"
msgstr[0] "ácido fórmico"
msgstr[1] "ácido fórmico"
msgstr[2] "ácido fórmico"

#. ~ Description of "formic acid"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Common in nature as an insect venom, this substance has a number of "
"industrial uses such as preservation and manufacturing."
msgstr ""
"Común en la naturaleza como veneno de insecto, esta sustancia tiene una "
"serie de usos industriales como la preservación y la fabricación."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "latex"
msgid_plural "latex"
msgstr[0] "latex"
msgstr[1] "latex"
msgstr[2] "latex"

#. ~ Description of "latex"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A liquid precursor to rubber found in some plants."
msgstr ""
"Un precursor líquido del plastico que se encuentra en algunas plantas."

#. ~ Bulk density is around 0.5 g/mL (because it's a powder, the actual
#. density of 1.12 g/mL is not useful)
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "citric acid"
msgid_plural "citric acid"
msgstr[0] "ácido cítrico"
msgstr[1] "ácido cítrico"
msgstr[2] "ácido cítrico"

#. ~ Bulk density is around 0.5 g/mL (because it's a powder, the actual
#. density of 1.12 g/mL is not useful)
#. ~ Description of "citric acid"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A manufactured form of citric acid that is commonly used as an additive in "
"food, cleaning agents, and nutritional supplements."
msgstr ""
"Una forma manufacturada de ácido cítrico que se utiliza comúnmente como "
"aditivo en alimentos, agentes de limpieza y suplementos nutricionales."

#. ~ 100 ml venom
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "venom gland"
msgid_plural "venom glands"
msgstr[0] "glándula de veneno"
msgstr[1] "glándulas de veneno"
msgstr[2] "glándulas de veneno"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "wasp venom gland"
msgid_plural "wasp venom glands"
msgstr[0] "glándula de veneno de avispa"
msgstr[1] "glándulas de veneno de avispa"
msgstr[2] "glándulas de veneno de avispa"

#. ~ Description of "wasp venom gland"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A fragile, slightly quivering organ for the production and storage of wasp "
"venom.  You could extract some very useful chemicals from it with the right "
"know-how, but only if you hurry."
msgstr ""
"Un órgano frágil y ligeramente tembloroso para la producción y "
"almacenamiento del veneno de avispas. Se podrían extraer algunos productos "
"químicos muy útiles de él con los conocimientos adecuados, pero sólo si te "
"das prisa."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "bee venom gland"
msgid_plural "bee venom glands"
msgstr[0] "glándula de veneno de abeja"
msgstr[1] "glándulas de veneno de abeja"
msgstr[2] "glándulas de veneno de abeja"

#. ~ Description of "bee venom gland"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A fragile, slightly quivering organ for the production and storage of "
"honeybee venom.  You could extract some very useful chemicals from it with "
"the right know-how, but only if you hurry."
msgstr ""
"Un órgano frágil y ligeramente tembloroso para la producción y "
"almacenamiento del veneno de las abejas de miel. Se podrían extraer algunos "
"productos químicos muy útiles de él con los conocimientos adecuados, pero "
"sólo si te das prisa."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "sac of paralytic venom"
msgid_plural "sacs of paralytic venom"
msgstr[0] "saco de veneno paralizante"
msgstr[1] "sacos de veneno paralizante"
msgstr[2] "sacos de veneno paralizante"

#. ~ Description of "sac of paralytic venom"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A grayish, flexible vesicle filled to the brim with the potent paralytic "
"agent the triffids use to subdue still-moving fertilizer such as yourself.  "
"If you know your way around poisons you might be able to find a use for it."
msgstr ""
"Una vesícula grisácea y flexible llena hasta el borde con el potente agente "
"paralizante que los trífidos utilizan para someter a los fertilizantes "
"inmóviles como tú. Si conoces los venenos podrías encontrarle un uso."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "sac of triffid fungicide"
msgid_plural "sacs of triffid fungicide"
msgstr[0] "saco trífido con fungicida"
msgstr[1] "sacos de fungicida trífido"
msgstr[2] "sacos de fungicida trífido"

#. ~ Description of "sac of triffid fungicide"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A triffid sac filled with what appears to be a triffid-produced antifungal "
"agent.  It will likely already work as an antifungal compound for more "
"offensive applications, but requires further refining before it can be used "
"as a medical drug."
msgstr ""
"Un saco de trífidos lleno de lo que parece ser un agente antifúngico "
"producido por trífidos. Es probable que ya funcione como compuesto "
"antifúngico para aplicaciones más ofensivas, pero requiere un mayor "
"refinamiento antes de que pueda utilizarse como medicamento."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "concentrated venom"
msgid_plural "concentrated venom"
msgstr[0] "veneno concentrado"
msgstr[1] "veneno concentrado"
msgstr[2] "veneno concentrado"

#. ~ Description of "concentrated venom"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A transparent, lightly greenish liquid, refined from the venom of bees and "
"wasps.  Active ingredients include (nor-)adrenaline, dopamine, histamine, "
"and protein toxins.  It is now relatively stable, but will require further "
"separation to be useful for anything other than killing you."
msgstr ""
"Un líquido transparente ligeramente verdoso, refinado a partir del veneno de"
" abejas y avispas. Los ingredientes activos incluyen (nor-)adrenalina, "
"dopamina, histamina y toxinas provenientes de proteínas. Ahora es "
"relativamente estable, pero requerirá una mayor separación para ser útil "
"para cualquier otra cosa que no sea matarte."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "concentrated paralytic"
msgid_plural "concentrated paralytic"
msgstr[0] "concentrado paralizante"
msgstr[1] "concentrado paralizante"
msgstr[2] "concentrado paralizante"

#. ~ Description of "concentrated paralytic"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A concentrated paralytic agent, originally from a triffid.  Given your "
"experience with its effects (chiefly gathered while sourcing this batch) and"
" their striking similarity to earthly flora, you figure it's related to "
"curarines.  Might come in handy in crafting more useful things."
msgstr ""
"Un agente paralizante concentrado, originalmente de un trífido. Dada tu "
"experiencia con sus efectos (principalmente reunidos mientras obtenías este "
"lote) y su sorprendente similitud con la flora terrestre, te imaginas que "
"está relacionado con las curarinas. Podría venir bien para hacer cosas más "
"útiles."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "rocuronium"
msgid_plural "rocuronium"
msgstr[0] "rocuronio"
msgstr[1] "rocuronio"
msgstr[2] "rocuronio"

#. ~ Description of "rocuronium"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Rocuronium bromide, a fast-acting muscle relaxant.  Used primarily in "
"emergency medicine because of its relative stability, it can serve as a "
"component of a balanced anesthesia in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Bromuro de rocuronio, un relajante muscular de acción rápida. Utilizado "
"principalmente en la medicina de emergencia por su relativa estabilidad, "
"puede servir como componente de una anestesia balanceada en caso de "
"necesidad."

#. ~ Density around 2.2g/cm3, but since it's a powder, it's a bit lower,
#. around 1.8-2.0 g/cm3
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "red phosphorous"
msgid_plural "red phosphorous"
msgstr[0] "fósforo rojo"
msgstr[1] "fósforo rojo"
msgstr[2] "fósforo rojo"

#. ~ Density around 2.2g/cm3, but since it's a powder, it's a bit lower,
#. around 1.8-2.0 g/cm3
#. ~ Description of "red phosphorous"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"An allotrope of the element phosphorous.  It's what you use to light "
"matches, but can also be used in the synthesis of methamphetamine.  You "
"could use it to make bombs, and if you were truly desperate you might even "
"be able to use it as a propellant for bullets."
msgstr ""
"Un alótropo del elemento del fósforo. Es lo que usas con las cerillas, pero "
"que también se puede usar para hacer meta anfetaminas. Lo podrías usar para "
"hacer bombas, y si estuvieras verdaderamente desesperado podrías usarlo como"
" propelente de balas."

#. ~ 1.082 g/cm3
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "acetic anhydride"
msgid_plural "acetic anhydride"
msgstr[0] "anhídrido acético"
msgstr[1] "anhídrido acético"
msgstr[2] "anhídrido acético"

#. ~ 1.082 g/cm3
#. ~ Description of "acetic anhydride"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A colorless liquid that smells strongly of vinegar.  If you have enough "
"chemical knowledge, you could use it to easily convert morphine into heroin."
msgstr ""
"Un líquido incoloro que huele fuertemente a vinagre. Si tienes suficientes "
"conocimientos químicos, podrías utilizarlo para convertir fácilmente la "
"morfina en heroína."

#. ~ Density around 5.1g/cm3, but since it's in crystal form, it's lower,
#. around 3.5 g/cm3
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "iodine crystals"
msgid_plural "iodine crystals"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Density around 5.1g/cm3, but since it's in crystal form, it's lower,
#. around 3.5 g/cm3
#. ~ Description of "iodine crystals"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of resublimed crystals of the element iodine, they can be used as "
"an antiseptic, but are also used in the making of methamphetamine."
msgstr ""
"Un puñado de cristales resublimados de yodo que pueden usarse como "
"antiséptico pero también se utilizan en la fabricación de metanfetamina."

#. ~ Density of around 0.92 g/ml
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "liquid soap"
msgid_plural "liquid soap"
msgstr[0] "jabón líquido"
msgstr[1] "jabones líquido"
msgstr[2] "jabones líquido"

#. ~ Density of around 0.92 g/ml
#. ~ Description of "liquid soap"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Standard skin-safe liquid soap, the type you might see on a kitchen sink, "
"shower shelf, or bathroom soap dispenser, but it should work reasonably well"
" for cleaning anything that's filthy."
msgstr ""
"Jabón liquido común, el típico que encuentras en la pica de una cocina, "
"estantería de ducha, o dispensador de jabón del baño, pero debería funcionar"
" razonablemente bien para limpiar cualquier cosa que este sucia."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "pine resin"
msgid_plural "pine resin"
msgstr[0] "resina de pino"
msgstr[1] "resina de pino"
msgstr[2] "resina de pino"

#. ~ Description of "pine resin"
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A sticky, sludgy mass of sap harvested from a pine tree."
msgstr "Una masa pegajosa y fangosa de savia extraída de un pino."

#. ~ density: 0.76–4.20 g/cm3 according to google, I'm going with the middle
#. ground
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
