msgid ""
"A pair of optics with a neck strap attached.  Useful for seeing long "
"distances.  Wearing this item or carrying it in your inventory will double "
"the distance around you that is mapped during your travels.  You could also "
"use them to focus the sunlight."
msgstr ""
"Un par de ópticas con una correa para el cuello. Útiles para ver a grandes "
"distancias. Llevar este artículo o llevarlo en su inventario duplicará la "
"distancia alrededor de usted que se cartografíe durante sus viajes. También "
"puedes usarlos para enfocar la luz del sol."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "headlamp"
msgid_plural "headlamps"
msgstr[0] "linterna de cabeza"
msgstr[1] "linternas de cabeza"
msgstr[2] "linternas de cabeza"

#. ~ Description of "headlamp"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid ""
"An LED headlamp with an adjustable strap so as to be comfortably worn on "
"your head or attached to your helmet.  Use it to turn it on."
msgstr ""
"Una linterna de cabeza led con una correa ajustable para que sea cómoda de "
"ponerse en la cabeza o fijada en un casco. Usar para encender."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "headlamp"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "You turn the headlamp on."
msgstr "Enciendes la linterna de cabeza."

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "headlamp"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "The headlamp batteries are dead."
msgstr "La batería de la linterna de cabeza está descargada."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "wearable camera"
msgid_plural "wearable cameras"
msgstr[0] "cámara portátil"
msgstr[1] "cámaras portátiles"
msgstr[2] "cámaras portátiles"

#. ~ Description of "wearable camera"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid ""
"A point-and-shoot digital camera with a digital viewfinder, a backup 'iron-"
"sight', and flash.  You can look at your photos on the digital screen, or "
"transfer them with a memory card.  Takes conventional batteries.  This one "
"can be worn over your neck."
msgstr ""
"Una cámara digital automática, con visor digital, una \"mira de hierro\" de "
"apoyo y flash. Puedes ver tus fotos en la pantalla digital o transferirlas a"
" una tarjeta de memoria. Funciona con baterías convencionales. Se puede "
"llevar en el cuello."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "wearable professional camera"
msgid_plural "wearable professional cameras"
msgstr[0] "cámara profesional portátil"
msgstr[1] "cámaras profesionales portátiles"
msgstr[2] "cámaras profesionales portátiles"

#. ~ Description of "wearable professional camera"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid ""
"A 35mm digital SLR (single-lens reflex) camera with optical and digital "
"viewfinders, a zoom lens with auto-focus and stabilizer, and flash.  You can"
" view your photos on it or transfer them with a memory card; it runs on "
"conventional batteries.  Before the Cataclysm, you could have taken "
"professional-grade photos using this.  This one can be worn over your neck"
msgstr ""
"Una cámara digital SLR (réflex de un solo objetivo) de 35 mm, con visores "
"ópticos y digitales, un objetivo de ampliación con auto enfoque, "
"estabilizador y un flash. Puedes ver tus fotos en ella o transferirlas a una"
" tarjeta de memoria; funciona con baterías convencionales. Antes del "
"Cataclismo, podrías haber tomado fotos de calidad profesional con esta "
"cámara. Se puede llevar alrededor del cuello."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "headlamp (on)"
msgid_plural "headlamps (on)"
msgstr[0] "linterna de cabeza (on)"
msgstr[1] "linternas de cabeza (on)"
msgstr[2] "linternas de cabeza (on)"

#. ~ Description of "headlamp (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid ""
"An LED headlamp with an adjustable strap so as to be comfortably worn on "
"your head or attached to your helmet.  It is turned on, and continually "
"draining batteries.  Use it to turn it off."
msgstr ""
"Una linterna de cabeza LED con una correa ajustable para llevarla "
"cómodamente en la cabeza o fijada al casco. Está encendida y las baterías se"
" agotan continuamente. Usar para apagar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "atomic headlamp"
msgid_plural "atomic headlamps"
msgstr[0] "linterna de cabeza atómica"
msgstr[1] "linternas de cabeza atómica"
msgstr[2] "linternas de cabeza atómica"

#. ~ Description of "atomic headlamp"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid ""
"A custom-made, reinforced headlamp powered by the magic of nuclear decay, "
"focused for more usable brightness.  The adjustable strap allows it to be "
"comfortably worn on your head or attached to your helmet.  Use it to close "
"the cover and hide the light."
msgstr ""
"Una linterna de cabeza reforzada hecha a medida, alimentada por la magia de "
"la decadencia nuclear, enfocada para un brillo más utilizable. La correa "
"ajustable permite que se lleve cómodamente en la cabeza o que se fije en el "
"casco. Usar para cerrar la cubierta y ocultar la luz."

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "atomic headlamp"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "atomic lamp"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "atomic reading light"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "magical reading light"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "everglow matrix lamp (uncovered)"
