#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "Desert Tech bullpup carbine"
msgid_plural "Desert Tech bullpup carbines"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "Desert Tech bullpup carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"Produced by the Desert Tech gun company, this is a highly modular, semi-"
"automatic rifle of remarkably modest dimensions.  The weapon is notable for "
"the simplicity of converting it to fire a wide number of different "
"cartridges, with retool kits for .223 Remington, .308 Winchester, and .300 "
"AAC Blackout being available."
msgstr ""
"Producida por la compañía de armas Desert Tech, este rifle semi-automático, "
"altamente modular, tiene unas dimensiones modestas. El arma es interesante "
"por su simplicidad de convertirla para disparar un amplio número de "
"municiones, con equipos de reemplazo para .223 Remington, .308 Winchester, y"
" .300 AAC Blackout disponibles."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Desert Tech bullpup carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "Desert Tech MDRX"
msgid_plural "Desert Tech MDRXs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "Desert Tech bullpup carbine" of gun "Desert Tech
#. MDRX"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"Bringing a compact, highly modular, and soft-recoiling weapon system to the "
"table, the Desert Tech Micro Dynamic Rifle Extreme (MDRX) is a gas-operated "
"bullpup carbine originally unveiled in 2014, with this updated model of the "
"weapon having been released in 2019.  One of the rifle’s most notable "
"features is the utter simplicity of swapping the carbine's chambering, with "
"an easy change of the barrel, bolt, and a handful of other components being "
"all the steps required to chamber the MDRX for either .223 Remington, .308 "
"Winchester, or .300 AAC Blackout."
msgstr ""
"Presentando un sistema de arma compacto, altamente modular y de bajo "
"retroceso, la Desert Tech Micro Dynamic Rifle Extreme (MDRX) es una carabina"
" operada por gas bullup originalmente revelada en 2014, con este modelo "
"actualizado en 2019. Una de las características mas destacables es la "
"simplicidad para cambiar el calibre de la carabina, con un simple cambio de "
"cañón, cerrojo, y un puñado de otros componentes como los únicos "
"requerimientos para cambiar el MDRX a .223 Remington, .308 Winchester, o "
".300 AAC Blackout."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "Bren 5.56x45mm carbine"
msgid_plural "Bren 5.56x45mm carbines"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "Bren 5.56x45mm carbine"
#. ~ Description of gun "Bren 7.62mm carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic clone of the Czech Republic’s standard infantry carbine, "
"sold for civilian sport shooting and recreational use, this modular rifle "
"makes use of the 7.62x39mm Soviet cartridge and uses proprietary magazines."
msgstr ""
"Un clon semiautomático de la carabina común de la república checa, vendida "
"para caza civil y usos recreativos, este rifle modular hace uso del cartucho"
" 7.62x39mm soviético y usa cargadores propietarios."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Bren 5.56x45mm carbine"
#. ~ Variant name of gun "Bren 7.62mm carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "CZ Bren 2"
msgid_plural "CZ Bren 2s"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "Bren 5.56x45mm carbine" of gun "CZ Bren 2"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"Hailing from the Czech Republic, this modular carbine supplanted the older "
"CZ 805 rifle within Czech military use, improving upon the former’s features"
" and bringing fully ambidextrous controls, a streamlined design, and an "
"easily adjustable gas system to the table.  Chambered for the 5.56x45mm NATO"
" cartridge, this particular weapon possesses a 16.5-inch barrel and is a "
"civilian MS, 'modular semi-automatic,' model.  Incorporating a number of US-"
"made parts, the weapon features a removable muzzle break rather than the "
"flash hider that comes standard with military rifles."
msgstr ""
"Con origen en la república checa, esta carabina modular suplanto al viejo "
"rifle CZ 805 usado por el ejercito checo, mejorando a su predecesor y "
"permitiendo un uso ambidiestro completo, un diseño regular, y un sistema de "
"gas ajustable. Con recamara para cartuchos 5.56x45mm NATO, esta arma en "
"particular posee un cañón de 41 centímetros y es un modelo civil MS, "
"\"modular semiautomático\". Incorporando una serie de partes hechas en USA, "
"el arma tiene un freno de boca que se puede quitar en vez de tenerlo "
"escondido como en los rifles militares comunes."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "bolt-action trail carbine"
msgid_plural "bolt-action trail carbines"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "bolt-action trail carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"Compact, svelte, and lightweight, this Leen bolt-action rifle packs the same"
" features of larger sporting weapons into a backpack-sized package.  "
"Possessing an adjustable buttstock, a detachable magazine-based system, and "
"a quick-swap barrel that can be exchanged to accommodate the firing of .223 "
"Remington or 7.62x39mm Soviet ammunition, the weapon is a commendable "
"backpacker or prepper rifle."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "bolt-action trail carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "CZ 600 TRAIL"
msgid_plural "CZ 600 TRAILs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "bolt-action trail carbine" of gun "CZ 600 TRAIL"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"A handy bolt-action offering from CZ, the 600 Trail is a box magazine-fed "
"ranch rifle that utilizes an aluminum chassis to keep its overall heft to a "
"minimum.  Possessing an extendable buttstock, extensive modularity, and a "
"quick-swap barrel assembly switchable to accommodate the firing of either "
".223 or 7.62x39mm ammunition, the rifle was intended for use by backpackers,"
" trail hikers, and preppers."
msgstr ""
"Una oferta apañada de cerrojo de CZ, el 600 Trail es un rifle alimentado por"
" cargadores de caja que utiliza un armazón de aluminio para mantener su peso"
" total en mínimos. Con una culata extensible, modularidad extendida, y un "
"cañón fácilmente intercambiable para poder disparar munición calibre .223 o "
"7.62x39mm, el rifle estaba pensado para mochileros, montañeros o "
"supervivientes."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "5.56x45mm bullpup rifle"
msgid_plural "5.56x45mm bullpup rifles"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "5.56x45mm bullpup rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"This is a semi-automatic bullpup rifle with a lightened body due to the use "
"of polymers and aluminum, using standard magazines of the AR-15 platform and"
" a 5.56x45mm cartridge."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle semiautomático bullup con un armazón aligerado debido al uso de "
"polímeros y aluminio, usando cargadores comunes para la plataforma AR-15 y "
"el cartucho 5.56x45mm."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "5.56x45mm bullpup rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "Kel-Tec RDB"
msgid_plural "Kel-Tec RDB"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "5.56x45mm bullpup rifle" of gun "Kel-Tec RDB"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"This is a semi-automatic bullpup rifle with a lightened body due to the use "
"of polymers and aluminum, using standard magazines from the AR-15 platform "
"and the 5.56 NATO cartridge.  The name stands for rifle, downward-ejection, "
"bullpup, and its design was intended to incorporate some technical "
"solutions, such as downward case ejection and convenience for left-handers, "
"to solve some problems with bullpup guns.  However, the good idea's "
"execution is not as perfect as the manufacturer (and user) would like.  No "
"good idea from Kel-Tec is immune to Kel-Tec manufacturing issues, sadly."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle semiautomático bullpup con un armazón aligerado debido al uso de "
"polímeros y aluminio, usando cargadores estándar de una plataforma AR-15 y "
"cartuchos 5.56 NATO. El nombre significa rifle, eyección trasera, bullpup, y"
" su diseño tenia la intención de incorporar algunas soluciones técnicas, "
"para solventar algunos problemas con las armas bullpup. Aun así, la "
"ejecución de la idea no es tan perfecta como el fabricante (y el usuario) "
"pretendían. Por desgracia, no hay una buena idea de Kel-Tec inmune a los "
"problemas de fabricación de Kel-Tec."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
msgid "bolt-action hunting rifle"
msgid_plural "bolt-action hunting rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de caza de cerrojo"
msgstr[1] "rifles de caza de cerrojo"
msgstr[2] "rifles de caza de cerrojo"

#. ~ Description of gun "bolt-action hunting rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
msgid ""
"Featuring a handsome set of wooden furnishings, a classic design, and a no "
"nonsense .270 caliber chambering, this is a powerful hunting rifle.  With a "
"tried and proven pedigree dating back over 60 years, millions of such rugged"
" arms have been made, exported, and used throughout the United States and "
"the world at large.  Where hunting is concerned, this is a highly capable "
"and well proven weapon in all respects.  Fortunate, given that your prey in "
"these dark days may turn out to be a little bit more feisty than typical "
"White-Tailed deer, moose, and black bears."
msgstr ""
"Este poderoso rifle de caza posee un elegante conjunto de accesorios de "
"madera, un diseño clásico y un entendible calibre .270. Con un linaje "
"probado de más de 60 años, millones de estas robustas armas han sido "
"fabricadas, exportadas y utilizadas a lo largo de Estados Unidos y el mundo "
"entero. En cuanto a la caza se refiere, este es un rifle muy capaz y bien "
"probado en todos sus aspectos. Y eso es una suerte, ya que en estos días "
"oscuros tu presa puede resultar un poco más peleadora que los típicos "
"ciervos de cola blanca, alces y osos negros."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "bolt-action hunting rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
msgid "Remington 700 .270 Win"
msgid_plural "Remington 700 .270 Win"
msgstr[0] "Remington 700 .270 Win"
msgstr[1] "Remington 700 .270 Win"
msgstr[2] "Remington 700 .270 Win"

#. ~ Description of variant "bolt-action hunting rifle" of gun "Remington 700
#. .270 Win"
#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
msgid ""
"A classic bolt-action rifle chambered for .270 Winchester, very popular "
"among hunters.  This is a CDL SF model with a forged, fluted, 416 stainless "
"steel barrel threaded into the receiver and a recessed bolt face.  It has "
"checkered walnut furniture and a recoil pad to reduce perceived recoil."
msgstr ""
"Un clásico rifle de cerrojo con recámara para Winchester .270, muy popular "
"entre los cazadores. Este es un modelo CDL SF con un cañón de acero "
"inoxidable 416 forjado y estriado, roscado en el cañón y con una cara del "
"cerrojo empotrada. Tiene armazones de nogal a cuadros y una almohadilla de "
"retroceso para reducir el retroceso percibido."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid "M2010 ESR"
msgid_plural "M2010 ESR"
msgstr[0] "M2010 ESR"
msgstr[1] "M2010 ESR"
msgstr[2] "M2010 ESR"

#. ~ Description of gun "M2010 ESR"
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid ""
"A bolt-action, box-magazine-fed sniper rifle chambered in the powerful .300 "
"Winchester Magnum round.  The M2010 had completely replaced the M24 rifle "
"series by 2017."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de francotirador de acción de bombeo y alimentado con cargador de "
"caja con la poderosa munición Winchester Magnum .300. El M2010 fue "
"reemplazado por la serie M24 en 2017."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid "Weatherby Mark V"
msgid_plural "Weatherby Mark V"
msgstr[0] "Weatherby Mark V"
msgstr[1] "Weatherby Mark V"
msgstr[2] "Weatherby Mark V"

#. ~ Description of gun "Weatherby Mark V"
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid ""
"The Weatherby Mark V is one of the world's finest bolt-action rifles.  "
"Designed in 1955 by Roy Weatherby and Fred Jennie, it has a strong action "
"designed to safely fire high-pressure cartridges.  These rifles were "
"presented to celebrities as part of a marketing campaign."
msgstr ""
"El Weatherby Mark V es uno de los mejores rifles de cerrojo del mundo. "
"Diseñado en 1955 por Roy Weatherby y Fred Jennie, posee un diseño fuerte "
"para poder disparar de manera segura cartuchos de alta presión. Estos rifles"
" fueron regalados a celebridades como parte de una campaña publicitaria."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
msgid "Winchester Model 70"
msgid_plural "Winchester Model 70s"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "Winchester Model 70"
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid ""
"The Winchester Model 70 is a bolt-action sporting rifle.  It has an iconic "
"place in American sporting culture and has been held in high regard by "
"shooters since it was introduced in 1936."
msgstr ""
"El Winchester Model 70 es un rifle de cerrojo para tiro deportivo. Ocupa un "
"lugar icónico en la cultura deportiva estadounidense, y ha sido tenido en "
"gran consideración por los tiradores desde que fue presentada en 1936."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid "Ruger Precision Rifle"
msgid_plural "Ruger Precision Rifles"
msgstr[0] "Rifle de Precisión Ruger"
msgstr[1] "Rifles de Precisión Ruger"
msgstr[2] "Rifles de Precisión Ruger"

#. ~ Description of gun "Ruger Precision Rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid ""
"Originally introduced to the Ruger gun corporation’s family of high-end "
"marksman rifles in 2015, the Ruger Precision Rifle is a modern and highly "
"modular long-range bolt-action weapon.  By incorporating a unique in-line "
"recoil path that manages recoil from the rear of the receiver to the "
"buttstock, as opposed to traditional bedding, the rifle offers maximal "
"accuracy potential, while the arm's additional bells and whistles, an "
"incorporated marksman’s trigger, muzzle brake, and this particular rifle's "
"powerhouse chambering of .300 Win Mag, help to make the most from any long-"
"range engagement."
msgstr ""
"Originalmente introducido en 2015 en la familia de rifles de alta gama de la"
" corporación Ruger, el Ruger Precision Rifle es un arma de cerrojo moderna y"
" altamente modular de largo alcance. Al incorporar un retroceso en linea "
"único que maneja el retroceso de la parte trasera del receptor de la culata,"
" al contrario a lo tradicional, el rifle ofrece un potencial máximo de "
"precisión, con añadidos adicionales, como un gatillo de competición "
"incorporado, freno de boca y este en particular, con el calibre .300 Win "
"Mag, que ayudan a sacar el máximo partido en cualquier enfrentamiento a "
"larga distancia."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid "Browning BLR"
msgid_plural "Browning BLR"
msgstr[0] "Browning BLR"
msgstr[1] "Browning BLR"
msgstr[2] "Browning BLR"

#. ~ Description of gun "Browning BLR"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid ""
"A highly accurate lever-action hunting rifle chambered for the powerful "
".30-06 round.  Notable for using a detachable magazine instead of a "
"traditional tube."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de caza de acción de palanca, con muy buena precisión y calibre "
"para la poderosa .30-06. Conocido por utilizar un cargador extraíble en "
"lugar de la tradicional cámara."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
msgid "M1 Garand"
msgid_plural "M1 Garands"
msgstr[0] "M1 Garand"
msgstr[1] "M1 Garand"
msgstr[2] "M1 Garand"

#. ~ Description of gun "M1 Garand"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic .30-06 battle rifle, developed to replace the M1903 "
"Springfield.  It didn't completely supplant the older bolt-action until "
"after World War II."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de combate semiautomático de calibre .30-06, desarrollado para "
"reemplazar el M1903 Springfield. No llegó a reemplazarlo completamente hasta"
" después de la Segunda Guerra Mundial."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
msgid "M1903 Springfield"
msgid_plural "M1903 Springfields"
msgstr[0] "M1903 Springfield"
msgstr[1] "M1903 Springfield"
msgstr[2] "M1903 Springfield"

#. ~ Description of gun "M1903 Springfield"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid ""
"A powerful military rifle chambered in .30-06, developed to replace the US "
"Army's older Krag rifle.  It served as the main American rifle in World War "
"I, was used alongside the M1 Garand in World War II, and was used as a "
"sniper rifle as late as the Vietnam War."
msgstr ""
"Un poderoso rifle militar calibre .30-06, desarrollado para reemplazar el "
"viejo rifle Krag del ejército de Estados Unidos. Fue el arma principal de "
"los estadounidenses durante la Primera Guerra Mundial, usado junto al M1 "
"Garand durante la Segunda Guerra Mundial, y llegó a ser usado como rifle de "
"francotirador incluso en la guerra de Vietnam."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
msgid "Browning Automatic Rifle"
msgid_plural "Browning Automatic Rifles"
msgstr[0] "Rifle Automático Browning"
msgstr[1] "Rifles Automáticos Browning"
msgstr[2] "Rifles Automáticos Browning"

#. ~ Description of gun "Browning Automatic Rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid ""
"Designed near the end of World War I, the BAR provided fire support for the "
"US Army from World War II all the way to the Vietnam War.  Too much "
"firepower to serve as a battle rifle, but not enough to be an ideal light "
"machine gun, it still found a niche on the battlefield."
msgstr ""
"Diseñado a fines de la Primera Guerra Mundial, el BAR (por sus siglas en "
"inglés) brindó apoyo al ejército de Estados Unidos desde la Segunda Guerra "
"Mundial hasta la guerra de Vietnam. Posee demasiada potencia como para ser "
"un rifle de combate, pero no la suficiente para ser una ametralladora "
"liviana ideal. De todas maneras, tiene su funcionalidad en el campo de "
"batalla."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid "Remington 700 .30-06"
msgid_plural "Remington 700 .30-06"
msgstr[0] "Remington 700 .30-06"
msgstr[1] "Remington 700 .30-06"
msgstr[2] "Remington 700 .30-06"

#. ~ Description of gun "Remington 700 .30-06"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid ""
"A very popular and durable hunting or sniping rifle.  Popular among SWAT and"
" US Marine snipers.  Highly damaging, but perhaps not as accurate as the "
"competing Browning BLR."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de caza o francotirador muy popular y duradero. Popular entre los "
"francotiradores de SWAT y de la Marina de Estados Unidos. Causa mucho daño, "
"pero tal vez no sea tan preciso como su competidor, el Browning BLR."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid "Ruger Guide rifle"
msgid_plural "Ruger Guide rifles"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "Ruger Guide rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid ""
"This is a popular and sturdy long-range rifle that has been in production by"
" the Ruger gun company for several decades.  Using a bolt-action feed "
"system, the rifle features a four round capacity of .30-06 cartridges and "
"has the capability to dispatch said rounds with a level of accuracy that "
"would make comparable hunting rifles blush."
msgstr ""
"Este es un rifle de largo alcance popular y robusto que ha sido producido "
"por la empresa de armas Ruger durante décadas. Usando un sistema de carga de"
" cerrojo, el rifle tiene una capacidad de cuatro cartuchos .30-06 y tiene la"
" capacidad de soltarlos con un nivel de precisión que hacen palidecer a "
"rifles de caza parecidos. "

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Ruger Guide rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid "Ruger M77 Hawkeye"
msgid_plural "Ruger M77 Hawkeyes"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "Ruger Guide rifle" of gun "Ruger M77 Hawkeye"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid ""
"A popular bolt-action hunting rifle first introduced in 2006, the Ruger M77 "
"was originally intended to be a modernized Mauser 98-style long gun.  To "
"this end, the weapon features a Mauser-type fixed blade extractor and an "
"angled large screw that tightly beds the action into the stock.  This "
"particular rifle is a variant with additional features, a smoother trigger, "
"and a recontoured buttstock."
msgstr ""
"Un popular rifle de acción de cerrojo introducido en 2006, el Ruger M77 fue "
"originalmente pensado como un reemplazo del Mauser 98. Con este fin, el arma"
" tiene un extractor fijo tipo hoja estilo Mauser y un tornillo largo en "
"angulo que aprieta el cerrojo contra el armazón. Este rifle en particular es"
" una variante con mejoras adicionales, un gatillo mas suave y una culata "
"biselada."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid "Remington ACR .300BLK"
msgid_plural "Remington ACR .300BLKs"
msgstr[0] "Remington ACR .300BLK"
msgstr[1] "Remington ACR .300BLKs"
msgstr[2] "Remington ACR .300BLKs"

#. ~ Description of gun "Remington ACR .300BLK"
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid ""
"This carbine was developed for military use in the early 21st century.  It "
"is damaging and accurate, though its rate of fire is a bit slower than "
"competing carbines.  This version is chambered for the .300 AAC Blackout "
"round."
msgstr ""
"Esta carabina fue desarrollada para uso militar a principios del siglo XXI. "
"Es dañina y precisa, aunque su velocidad de disparo es un poco más lenta que"
" la de las carabinas de la competencia. Esta versión está preparada para "
"balas de .300 AAC Blackout round."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLK"
msgid_plural "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLKs"
msgstr[0] "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLK"
msgstr[1] "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLKs"
msgstr[2] "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLKs"

#. ~ Description of gun "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLK"
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid ""
"The IWI Tavor X95 (also called Micro-Tavor or MTAR) is an Israeli bullpup "
"assault rifle designed and produced by Israel Weapon Industries.  This is "
"the civilian version chambered for .300 AAC Blackout."
msgstr ""
"El IWI Tavor X95 (también llamado Micro-Tavor o MTAR) es un rifle de asalto "
"israelí diseñado y producido por Israel Weapon Industries. Esta es la "
"versión civil con cámara para un .300 AAC Blackout."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
msgid_plural "SIG MCX Rattler SBRs"
msgstr[0] "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
msgstr[1] "SIG MCX Rattler SBRs"
msgstr[2] "SIG MCX Rattler SBRs"

#. ~ Description of gun "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid ""
"A gas-operated rifle, with a short 5.5 inch barrel, built-in thin folding "
"stock, and full rail mount on the upper receiver.  This particular one is a "
"select-fire military version."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de cañón corto operado por gas, con un cañón de 14 centímetros, "
"culata plegable fina incorporada y montura de riel completa en el receptor "
"superior. Esta en particular es una versión militar con disparo selectivo."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
msgid "Enfield battle rifle"
msgid_plural "Enfield battle rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de combate Enfield"
msgstr[1] "rifles de combate Enfield"
msgstr[2] "rifles de combate Enfield"

#. ~ Description of gun "Enfield battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
msgid ""
"An iconic weapon of both the First and Second World Wars, this bolt-action "
"rifle has seen deployment in the hands of Commonwealth troops across Europe "
"and beyond.  Firing the .303-caliber cartridge and making use of 10-round "
"Enfield magazines, the firearm’s reputation precedes it."
msgstr ""
"Una emblemática arma de la Primera y Segunda Guerra Mundiales, este rifle de"
" cerrojo ha servido en las manos de las tropas de la Commonwealth por toda "
"Europa y mas allá. Usando la munición calibre .303 y haciendo uso de "
"cargadores Enfield de 10 balas, la reputación de este arma le precede."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Enfield battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
msgid "SMLE No. 1 Mk III"
msgid_plural "SMLE No. 1 Mk IIIs"
msgstr[0] "SMLE No. 1 Mk III"
msgstr[1] "SMLE No. 1 Mk IIIs"
msgstr[2] "SMLE No. 1 Mk IIIs"

#. ~ Description of variant "Enfield battle rifle" of gun "SMLE No. 1 Mk III"
#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
msgid ""
"An English darling and icon of the First World War, the Short Magazine Lee-"
"Enfield Mk III was the standard issue battle rifle of the British "
"commonwealth from 1907.  Chambered for .303 ammunition, the rifle makes use "
"of ten-round detachable magazines.  With its full-length wooden handguard, "
"brass buttplate, and smooth action, the Lee-Enfield cuts a recognizable "
"profile in either the trenches of the Great War or the zombie-strewn "
"wastelands."
msgstr ""
"Una belleza inglesa un emblema de la Primera Guerra Mundial, el Lee-Enfield "
"Mk III de Cargador Corto fue común como rifle de guerra para la commonwealth"
" Británica desde 1907. Con una recamara de munición .303, el rifle hace uso "
"de cargadores de diez municiones intercambiables. Con su guarda de madera "
"completa, culata de latón, y suave acción, el Lee-Enfield tiene un perfil "
"reconocible en las trincheras de la Gran Guerra o los desolados paramos "
"llenos de zombis."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
msgid "updated Enfield rifle"
msgid_plural "updated Enfield rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle actualizado Enfield"
msgstr[1] "rifles actualizados Enfield"
msgstr[2] "rifles actualizados Enfield"

#. ~ Description of gun "updated Enfield rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
msgid ""
"An evolution of Britain’s First World War battle rifle, this bolt-action "
"firearm uses the same .303-caliber cartridge as its forerunner.  Much "
"beloved across the globe by collectors, rifles like this served as England’s"
" infantry rifle well into the 1950s, with a specialized sniper variant "
"remaining in service until the early nineties."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "updated Enfield rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
msgid "Lee-Enfield No. 4 Mk I"
msgid_plural "Lee-Enfield No. 4 Mk Is"
msgstr[0] "Lee-Enfield No. 4 Mk I"
msgstr[1] "Lee-Enfield No. 4 Mk Is"
msgstr[2] "Lee-Enfield No. 4 Mk Is"

#. ~ Description of variant "updated Enfield rifle" of gun "Lee-Enfield No. 4
#. Mk I"
#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
msgid ""
"A Second World War progression of the British Commonwealth's Lee-Enfield "
"battle rifle, the No. 4 began its decades-long service life in 1939.  "
"Externally similar to its forefather, the rifle possesses a reinforced "
"receiver, an adjusted nose cap, and a heavier barrel.  Still chambered for "
"the same .303-caliber cartridge, the No. 4 represents one of the most "
"populous firearm imports in U.S. history."
msgstr ""
"Una evolución del rifle de guerra Lee-Enfield de la Segunda Guerra Mundial "
"de la Commonwealth Británica, el No. 4 empezó su servicio hace décadas en "
"1939. Externamente parecido a su predecesor, el rifle posee un receptor "
"reforzado, un ajuste para la nariz, y un cañón mas pesado. Todavía usando la"
" misma munición calibre .303, el No. 4 representa una de las importaciones "
"mas populares en la historia de U.S."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "Belgian battle rifle"
msgid_plural "Belgian battle rifle"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "Belgian battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"Originally designed during the Cold War, this gun is probably the most "
"successful battle rifle ever designed.  Despite being labeled as obsolete, "
"its tunable gas system ensures both reliability and low recoil, allowing the"
" FAL to keep up even amongst modern competitors.  This is a semi-automatic "
"clone built by a domestic manufacturer."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Belgian battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "DSA SA-58"
msgid_plural "DSA SA-58"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "Belgian battle rifle" of gun "DSA SA-58"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"Originally designed during the Cold War, the FAL is probably the most "
"successful battle rifle ever designed.  Despite being labeled as obsolete, "
"its tunable gas system ensures both reliability and low recoil, allowing the"
" FAL to keep up even amongst modern competitors.  This is a semi-automatic "
"clone of the SA-58 pattern built by DSA."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "German battle rifle"
msgid_plural "German battle rifle"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "German battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic, domestically produce clone of an early battle rifle "
"developed after the end of WWII.  The PTR 91 is a fantastically reliable, "
"cheap to produce rifle that continues to serve in conflict regions.  Though "
"the action is legendary, its handling characteristics and harsher recoil "
"leave something to be desired."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "German battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "PTR 91"
msgid_plural "PTR 91"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "German battle rifle" of gun "PTR 91"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic, domestically produced clone of an early battle rifle "
"developed after the end of WWII.  The PTR 91 is a fantastically reliable, "
"cheap to produce rifle that continues to serve in conflict regions.  Though "
"the action is legendary, its handling characteristics and harsher recoil "
"leave something to be desired."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "German battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "Century C308"
msgid_plural "Century C308"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "German battle rifle" of gun "Century C308"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic, domestically produced clone of the CETME Model C, the "
"progenitor of the famous H&K G3 battle rifle.  The CETME is a fantastically "
"reliable, cheap to produce rifle that continues to serve in conflict "
"regions.  Though the action is legendary, its handling characteristics and "
"harsher recoil leave something to be desired."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M134D-H Minigun"
msgid_plural "M134D-H Miniguns"
msgstr[0] "Minigun M134D-H"
msgstr[1] "Minigun M134D-H"
msgstr[2] "Minigun M134D-H"

#. ~ Description of gun "M134D-H Minigun"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"The M134D-H Minigun is a (relatively) lightweight heavy rotary machine gun."
"  Its six barrels are rotated by an electric motor, powered by UPS or "
"vehicle.  If you could find enough ammo for it, it would become a "
"devastating weapon.  It must be mounted on a vehicle before use."
msgstr ""
"El Minigun M134D-H es una ametralladora rotativa (relativamente) ligera y "
"pesada. Sus seis cañones giran con un motor eléctrico, impulsado por un UPS "
"o un vehículo. Si pudieras encontrar suficiente munición para ella, se "
"convertiría en un arma devastadora. Debe ser montada en un vehículo antes de"
" su uso."

#. ~ Firing mode of gun "M134D-H Minigun"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "low auto"
msgstr "bajo auto"

#. ~ Firing mode of gun "M134D-H Minigun"
#. ~ Firing mode of gun "CMES laser cannon"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json data/json/items/gun/ups.json
msgid "high auto"
msgstr "alto auto"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M14 EBR-RI"
msgid_plural "M14 EBR-RI"
msgstr[0] "M14 EBR-RI"
msgstr[1] "M14 EBR-RI"
msgstr[2] "M14 EBR-RI"

#. ~ Description of gun "M14 EBR-RI"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A highly modified version of the M14 rifle designed to cover both CQB and "
"designated marksman roles.  A very powerful and versatile rifle, if somewhat"
" heavy."
msgstr ""
"Una versión modificada del rifle M14, diseñado para cubrir tanto el combate "
"cercano como lejano. Un rifle muy poderoso y versátil, aunque un poco "
"pesado."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "American battle rifle"
msgid_plural "American battle rifle"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "American battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"This civilian variant of an American battle rifle is essentially a rifle "
"from World War 2 with a detachable magazine stuck in it that was sold to the"
" military as a cheap, do-all rifle that could replace many other weapon "
"systems.  While it delivered none of those things, it was an acceptable "
"rifle, if marginally inferior to its contemporaries."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "American battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M1A"
msgid_plural "M1A"
msgstr[0] "M1A"
msgstr[1] "M1As"
msgstr[2] "M1As"

#. ~ Description of variant "American battle rifle" of gun "M1A"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"This civilian variant of the M14 is essentially the M1 Garand from World War"
" 2 with a detachable magazine stuck in it that was sold to the military as a"
" cheap, do-all rifle that could replace many other weapon systems.  While it"
" delivered none of those things, it was an acceptable rifle, if marginally "
"inferior to its contemporaries."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M240"
msgid_plural "M240s"
msgstr[0] "M240"
msgstr[1] "M240"
msgstr[2] "M240"

#. ~ Description of gun "M240"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"The M240 is a medium machine gun used by the US military, replacing the "
"older M60.  Quite inaccurate and difficult to control, the M240 is designed "
"to fire many rounds very quickly."
msgstr ""
"La M240 es una ametralladora mediana utilizada por el Ejército de Estados "
"Unidos, y reemplaza la vieja M60. Bastante poco precisa y difícil de "
"controlar, la M240 está diseñada para disparar rápidamente muchas balas."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M60"
msgid_plural "M60s"
msgstr[0] "M60"
msgstr[1] "M60s"
msgstr[2] "M60s"

#. ~ Description of gun "M60"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"The M60 is a general-purpose machine gun developed to replace the "
".30-caliber M1918 and M1919.  Heavy and difficult to handle fired from the "
"shoulder, as most people aren't action-movie heroes."
msgstr ""
"La M60 es una ametralladora de varios usos, desarrollada para reemplazar la "
"M1918 y M1919 de calibre .30. Pesada y difícil de controlar aguantándola con"
" el hombro, ya que casi nadie es un héroe de película de acción."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M60 Semi Auto"
msgid_plural "M60 Semi Autos"
msgstr[0] "M60 Semi Auto"
msgstr[1] "M60 Semi Autos"
msgstr[2] "M60 Semi Autos"

#. ~ Description of gun "M60 Semi Auto"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic civilian variant of the M60 machine gun, retaining the "
"ability to be belt fed, an uncommon feature in civilian firearms."
msgstr ""
"Una variante civil semiautomática de la ametralladora M60, retiene la "
"habilidad de usar alimentación por cinta, una característica inusual en las "
"armas civiles."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "Savage 111F"
msgid_plural "Savage 111F"
msgstr[0] "Savage 111F"
msgstr[1] "Savage 111F"
msgstr[2] "Savage 111F"

#. ~ Description of gun "Savage 111F"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A very accurate rifle chambered for the powerful .308 round.  Its very low "
"ammo capacity is offset by its accuracy and near-complete lack of recoil."
msgstr ""
"Es un rifle muy preciso con el poderoso calibre .308. El precio que hay que "
"pagar por su precisión y casi ausencia de retroceso es su capacidad muy "
"limitada para la munición."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "FN SCAR-H"
msgid_plural "FN SCAR-H"
msgstr[0] "FN SCAR-H"
msgstr[1] "FN SCAR-H"
msgstr[2] "FN SCAR-H"

#. ~ Description of gun "FN SCAR-H"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A highly accurate and modular battle rifle specially designed for the United"
" States Special Operations Command.  The 'H' in its name stands for heavy, "
"as it uses the powerful .308 round."
msgstr ""
"Es un rifle de combate modular y muy preciso, especialmente diseñado para el"
" Comando de Operaciones Especiales de Estados Unidos. La 'H' en el nombre "
"significa pesado (heavy), porque utiliza la poderosa bala .308."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M24"
msgid_plural "M24"
msgstr[0] "M24"
msgstr[1] "M24"
msgstr[2] "M24"

#. ~ Description of gun "M24"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"The M24 Sniper is the military and police version of the Remington Model 700"
" rifle, M24 being the model name assigned by the United States Army after "
"adoption as their standard sniper rifle in 1988.  The M24 is referred to as "
"a 'weapon system' because it consists of not only a rifle, but also a "
"detachable telescopic sight and other accessories."
msgstr ""
"El francotirador M24 es la versión militar y policial del rifle Remington "
"Modelo 700, siendo M24 el nombre del modelo asignado por el Ejército de los "
"Estados Unidos tras su adopción como su rifle de francotirador estándar en "
"1988. El M24 se denomina \"sistema de armas\" porque no sólo consiste en un "
"rifle, sino también en una mira telescópica desmontable y otros accesorios."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "HK417 A2"
msgid_plural "HK417 A2s"
msgstr[0] "HK417 A2"
msgstr[1] "HK417 A2s"
msgstr[2] "HK417 A2s"

#. ~ Description of gun "HK417 A2"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A German battle rifle with a 13\" barrel and telescopic stock.  It is a gas-"
"operated, rotating bolt rifle with a short-stroke piston design similar to "
"that of the G36."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de batalla alemán con un cañón de 13\" y un telescopio. Es un rifle"
" de cerrojo giratorio operado por gas con un diseño de pistón de carrera "
"corta similar al del G36."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M110A1"
msgid_plural "M110A1s"
msgstr[0] "M110A1"
msgstr[1] "M110A1s"
msgstr[2] "M110A1s"

#. ~ Description of gun "M110A1"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A derivative of H&K's G28 with an aluminum upper receiver to meet US Army "
"weight requirements.  It is a gas-operated, rotating bolt rifle accurate to "
"1.5 MOA with standard ammunition."
msgstr ""
"Un derivado del G28 de H&K con un receptor superior de aluminio para cumplir"
" con los requisitos de peso del ejército de EE.UU. Es un rifle de cerrojo "
"giratorio operado por gas con una precisión de 1,5 MOA con munición "
"estándar."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "7.62x51mm AK"
msgid_plural "7.62x51mm AKs"
msgstr[0] "7.62x51mm AK"
msgstr[1] "7.62x51mm AK"
msgstr[2] "7.62x51mm AK"

#. ~ Description of gun "7.62x51mm AK"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "A civilian AK pattern rifle, chambered in 7.62x51mm NATO."
msgstr "Un rifle tipo AK civil con calibre 7.62x51mm NATO."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "7.62x51mm AK"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "PAP M77"
msgid_plural "PAP M77s"
msgstr[0] "PAP M77"
msgstr[1] "PAP M77"
msgstr[2] "PAP M77"

#. ~ Description of variant "7.62x51mm AK" of gun "PAP M77"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A Serbian-made AK pattern rifle made by Zastava in 7.62x51mm NATO.  To avoid"
" import restrictions, Zastava USA has added a number of American-made parts."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de tipo AK serbio fabricado por Zastava con calibre 7.62x51mm NATO."
" Para evitar las restricciones de importación, Zastava USA le agregó algunas"
" partes fabricadas en Estados Unidos."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "AR-10"
msgid_plural "AR-10s"
msgstr[0] "AR-10"
msgstr[1] "AR-10s"
msgstr[2] "AR-10s"

#. ~ Description of gun "AR-10"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"Somewhat similar to the later AR-15, the AR-10 is a gas-operated, rotating "
"bolt rifle chambered for 7.62x51mm rounds."
msgstr ""
"Similar al posterior AR-15, el AR-10 es un rifle rotativo de cerrojo "
"accionado por gas con calibre para balas 7.62x51mm."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "7.62x51mm bullpup rifle"
msgid_plural "7.62x51mm bullpup rifles"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "7.62x51mm bullpup rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"This is a semi-automatic bullpup rifle with a lightened body due to the use "
"of polymers and aluminum, using standard magazines of the heavy automatic "
"rifle and a 7.62x51mm cartridge."
msgstr ""
"Este es un rifle semiautomático bullup con un armazón ligero debido al uso "
"de polímeros y aluminio, usando cargadores comunes del rifle pesado "
"automático y el cartucho 7.62x51mm."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "7.62x51mm bullpup rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "Kel-Tec RFB"
msgid_plural "Kel-Tec RFB"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "7.62x51mm bullpup rifle" of gun "Kel-Tec RFB"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"This is a semi-automatic bullpup rifle with a lightweight, polymer frame, "
"using magazines from the FN FAL and the .308 Winchester cartridge.  The "
"rifle, forward-ejection, bullpup (abbreviated as RFB) features forward case "
"ejection, ambidextrous controls, and structural use of the barrel, uncommon "
"in modern designs."
msgstr ""
"Este es un rifle semiautomático bullup con un armazón ligero hecho con "
"polímero, usando cargadores FN FAL y el cartucho .308 Winchester. El rifle, "
"con eyección delantera, bullup (abreviado como RFB) tiene eyección del "
"casquillo por delante, controles ambidiestros, y uso estructural del cañón, "
"poco común en diseños modernos."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "scouting rifle"
msgid_plural "scouting rifles"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "scouting rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"This is a versatile, all-purpose hunting rifle.  To this end, it is "
"exceedingly lightweight, contains an inbuilt polymer bipod, and fits a spare"
" magazine inside the stock for fast reloading.  While these features made "
"for a hunting rifle too universal for widespread adoption, they might yet "
"fulfill a vital scouting niche for survivors in the post-Cataclysm world."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "scouting rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "Steyr Scout rifle"
msgid_plural "Steyr Scout rifles"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "scouting rifle" of gun "Steyr Scout rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"The Steyr Scout is Steyr's interpretation of Jeff Cooper's concept of a "
"'scout rifle', a versatile, all-purpose hunting rifle.  To this end, it is "
"exceedingly lightweight, and contains a built-in polymer bipod, and fits a "
"spare magazine inside the stock for fast reloading.  While these features "
"made for a hunting rifle too universal for widespread adoption, they might "
"yet fulfill a vital scouting niche for survivors in the post-Cataclysm "
"world."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/30carbine.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
msgid "M1 carbine"
msgid_plural "M1 carbines"
msgstr[0] "carabina M1"
msgstr[1] "carabinas M1"
msgstr[2] "carabinas M1"

#. ~ Description of gun "M1 carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/30carbine.json
msgid ""
"A light rifle developed during the Second World War to provide a less "
"cumbersome weapon for soldiers that didn't need the firepower of the M1 "
"Garand.  Firing the .30 Carbine cartridge, it provides more firepower than a"
" pistol and is easier to carry than most other rifles."
msgstr ""
"Es un rifle ligero desarrollado durante la Segunda Guerra Mundial para que "
"los soldados tuvieran un arma menos incómoda cuando no necesitaban el poder "
"de fuego del M1 Garand. El cartucho Carabina .30 brinda más potencia que una"
" pistola y es más fácil de llevar que la mayoría de los demás rifles."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/30carbine.json
msgid "M2 carbine"
msgid_plural "M2 carbines"
msgstr[0] "carabina M2"
msgstr[1] "carabinas M2"
msgstr[2] "carabinas M2"

#. ~ Description of gun "M2 carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/30carbine.json
msgid ""
"An improved version of the M1 carbine offering full-auto capability, the M2 "
"carbine was rare and coveted among collectors even before the world ended.  "
"Takes M1 carbine magazines."
msgstr ""
"Una versión mejorada de la carabina M1 que ofrece capacidad automática. La "
"carabina M2 fue rara y codiciada por los coleccionistas incluso antes de que"
" el mundo llegara a su fin. Utiliza los cartuchos de la carabina M1."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/32.json
msgid "SIG Sauer P230"
msgid_plural "SIG Sauer P230"
msgstr[0] "SIG Sauer P230"
msgstr[1] "SIG Sauer P230"
msgstr[2] "SIG Sauer P230"

#. ~ Description of gun "SIG Sauer P230"
#: data/json/items/gun/32.json
msgid ""
"The SIG Sauer P230 is a small, semi-automatic handgun chambered in .32 ACP."
"  Due to its small dimensions, it was often carried as a backup weapon."
msgstr ""
"La SIG Sauer P320 es una pistola pequeña semi-automática con calibre .32 "
"ACP. Debido a su pequeño tamaño, a menudo se la lleva como arma de apoyo."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/32.json data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
msgid "Walther PPK"
msgid_plural "Walther PPKs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "Walther PPK"
#: data/json/items/gun/32.json
msgid ""
"One of the most famous handguns of the 20th century.  Your name is not Bond,"
" but you might find this little gun still useful."
msgstr ""
"Es una de las pistolas más famosas del siglo XX. Tu nombre no es Bond, pero "
"igual vas a encontrarle utilidad a esta pequeña pistola."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/32.json
msgid "Kel-Tec P-32"
msgid_plural "Kel-Tec P-32s"
msgstr[0] "Kel-Tec P-32"
msgstr[1] "Kel-Tecs P-32"
msgstr[2] "Kel-Tecs P-32"

#. ~ Description of gun "Kel-Tec P-32"
#: data/json/items/gun/32.json
msgid ""
"One of Kel-Tec's oldest designs, the P-32 is a popular option for deep "
"concealment and backup usage.  Despite its extreme light weight and small "
"size, its .32 ACP chambering makes for good handling and recoil control."
msgstr ""
"Uno de los diseños más antiguos de Kel-Tec, el P-32 es una opción popular "
"como arma oculta y uso de apoyo. A pesar de ser extremadamente ligera y "
"pequeña, tiene un calibre .32 ACP que hace fácil de manejar y controlar su "
"retroceso."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/32.json
msgid "pipe rifle: .32"
msgid_plural "pipe rifles: .32"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/338lapua.json
msgid ".338 bolt-action sniper rifle"
msgid_plural ".338 bolt-action sniper rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de cerrojo de francotirador calibre .338"
msgstr[1] "rifles de cerrojo de francotirador calibre .338"
msgstr[2] "rifles de cerrojo de francotirador calibre .338"

#. ~ Description of gun ".338 bolt-action sniper rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/338lapua.json
msgid ""
"A high-precision bolt-action sniper rifle, in service with special "
"operations members of the US Navy prior to the cataclysm.  Firing the "
"powerful .338 Lapua cartridge, the weapon feeds from detachable five round "
"Accuracy International magazines."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de francotirador de cerrojo de alta precisión, en servicio con los "
"miembros de operaciones especiales del US Navy previo al cataclismo. "
"Disparando el poderoso cartucho .338 Lapua, este arma se alimenta con "
"cargadores Accuracy International intercambiables de cinco municiones."

#. ~ Variant name of gun ".338 bolt-action sniper rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/338lapua.json
msgid "McMillan Tac-338"
msgid_plural "McMillan Tac-338"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of variant ".338 bolt-action sniper rifle" of gun "McMillan
#. Tac-338"
#: data/json/items/gun/338lapua.json
msgid ""
"Chambering the .338 Lapua cartridge, the Tac-338 is a high-precision, bolt-"
"action sniper rifle that, before the Cataclysm, complemented the arsenal of "
"the US Navy Special Warfare unit.  Providing Navy SEAL marksmen with the "
"capability to land effective shots on targets at a typical range of 1600 "
"meters, a valuable capability for the long-distance engagements prevalent "
"during the US army’s war on terror, the rifle comes kitted with an "
"adjustable cheek pad, butt hook, and muzzle break."
msgstr ""
"Con recamara .338 Lapua, el Tac-338 es un rifle de cerrojo de francotirador "
"de alta precisión, que antes del Cataclismo, complemento el arsenal de la "
"unidad Operaciones Especiales Táctica. Provee al tirador Navy SEAL con la "
"capacidad de impactar con efectividad en los objetivos a una distancia "
"típica de 1600 metros, una capacidad valiosa para enfrentamientos de larga "
"distancia que prevaleció durante la guerra contra el terrorismo del ejercito"
" US, el rifle venia con una almohadilla de culata ajustable, gancho de "
"culata y freno de boca."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/338lapua.json
msgid "single-shot target rifle"
msgid_plural "single-shot target rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle target de un solo disparo"
msgstr[1] "rifles target de un solo disparo"
msgstr[2] "rifles target de un solo disparo"

#. ~ Description of gun "single-shot target rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/338lapua.json
msgid ""
"A bolt-action precision rifle with the potential for impressive accuracy, "
"this particular weapon makes use of the powerful .338 Lapua cartridge and is"
" decked in a handsome set of wooden furniture, providing the rifle with a "
"classical mystique.  Unfortunately, the weapon's single-round magazine and a"
" lack of factory iron sights, which makes target acquisition an exercise in "
"futility unless a gunsight is installed, make the rifle limited in its post-"
"Cataclysm utility."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de cerrojo de precisión con el potencial de tener una puntería "
"impresionante, este arma en particular hace uso del poderoso cartucho .338 "
"Lapua y esta montado en un bonito armazón de madera, que provee al rifle con"
" una mística clásica. Por desgracia, el cargador de una sola munición y la "
"falta de mirilla de hierro, hace que la adquisición de objetivos sea un "
"ejercicio fútil a menos que instales una mirilla, y convierte al rifle en "
"algo limitado en una época posterior al cataclismo."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "single-shot target rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/338lapua.json
msgid "Savage 112 Magnum Target"
msgid_plural "Savage 112 Magnum Target"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "single-shot target rifle" of gun "Savage 112
#. Magnum Target"
#: data/json/items/gun/338lapua.json
msgid ""
"A highly-accurate precision rifle chambered for the powerful .338 Lapua "
"cartridge, the Savage 112 Magnum Target is a classically designed bolt-"
"action rifle in both its fit and finish, with a heavy barrel, a hardwood "
"stock, and an attached muzzle brake.  Unfortunately for the weapon and its "
"users, a traditional veneer, no matter how admittedly swanky, isn’t "
"conducive to tactical effectiveness, as demonstrated by the 112 Magnum "
"Target’s mighty magazine size of one entire cartridge and lack of any "
"factory-attached sights."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de precisión altamente preciso con la recamara del potente cartucho"
" .338 Lapua, el Savage 112 Magnum Target es un rifle de cerrojo clásicamente"
" diseñado en su encaje y acabado, con un pesado cañón, una culata de madera "
"dura, y un freno de boca incorporado. Por desgracia para el arma y sus "
"usuarios, una chapa tradicional, no importa cuan ostentosa, no hace que sea "
"tácticamente efectivo, como demuestra el descomunal tamaño del cargador del "
"112 Magnum Target y la falta de montura de miras incorporado de fabrica."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/338lapua.json
msgid "Barrett precision rifle"
msgid_plural "Barrett precision rifles"
msgstr[0] "Rifle de precisión Barrett"
msgstr[1] "Rifles de precisión Barrett"
msgstr[2] "Rifles de precisión Barrett"

#. ~ Description of gun "Barrett precision rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/338lapua.json
msgid ""
"A box magazine-fed bolt-action precision rifle developed by the Barrett Arms"
" Company, firing the .338 Lapua cartridge.  A civilian copy of more "
"versatile military weapons, this rifle is a remarkably well-crafted piece of"
" anti-personnel engineering despite lacking the sheer modularity of its "
"Marshal sister, and is still capable of engaging targets at extreme "
"distances."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de cerrojo de precisión alimentado con un cargador de caja "
"desarrollado por Barrett Arms Company, que dispara el cartucho .338 Lapua. "
"Una copia civil de armas militares mas versátiles, este rifle es una pieza "
"remarcablemente bien fabricada de ingeniería anti personal, a pesar de la "
"falta de la gran modularidad de su hermana Marshal, todavía es capaz de "
"enfrentarse a objetivos a distancias extremas."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Barrett precision rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/338lapua.json
msgid "Barrett MRAD SMR"
msgid_plural "Barrett MRAD SMR"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "Barrett precision rifle" of gun "Barrett MRAD
#. SMR"
#: data/json/items/gun/338lapua.json
msgid ""
"Chambered for the .338 Lapua cartridge, the Barrett MRAD SMR is a civilian "
"variant of the MK22 MRAD sniper rifle, which was in service with elements of"
" the US army and is often regarded as one of the finest bolt-action sniper "
"rifles ever developed.  The primary differences that set this weapon apart "
"from its Marshal sibling are the removal of the MRAD’s caliber conversion "
"capabilities and the installation of a fixed buttstock.  These changes have "
"resulted in a lighter and slimmer rifle that, most importantly for the "
"discerning pre-Cataclysmic precision shooter, didn’t require a second "
"mortgage to purchase."
msgstr ""
"Con recamara para el cartucho .338 Lapua, el Barret MRAD SMR es una variante"
" civil del rifle de francotirador MK22 MRAD, que estuvo en servicio en el "
"ejercito US y que es reconocido como uno de los rifles de acción de cerrojo "
"mas finos jamas desarrollados. Las diferencias principales que hace de este "
"arma única ademas de su conocido hermano son la falta de capacidades de "
"conversión de calibre y la instalación de una culata fija. Estos cambios "
"hacen que sea mas ligero y fino, y mas importante para el tirador de "
"precisión previo al Cataclismo, no hacia falta hacer una segunda hipoteca "
"para comprarlo."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/338lapua.json
msgid "modular sniper rifle"
msgid_plural "modular sniper rifles"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "modular sniper rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/338lapua.json
msgid ""
"A weapon platform that prides itself on modularity and customizability, this"
" highly accurate precision rifle may be configured with various caliber "
"conversion kits that can allow it to fire either the .338 Lapua, .300 Win "
"Mag, or .308 Winchester cartridges.  The rifle's size prevents it from being"
" a particularly mobile piece of equipment, but the weapon's folding "
"buttstock aids in portability."
msgstr ""
"Una plataforma de amas que se enorgullece de ser modular y personalizable, "
"este rifle certero de alta precisión puede ser configurado con equipos de "
"conversión de varios calibres que permiten disparar cartuchos .338 Lapua, "
".300 Win Mag, o .308 Winchester. El tamaño del rifle no lo hace "
"particularmente portable, pero la culata plegable ayuda a transportarlo."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "modular sniper rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/338lapua.json
msgid "Accuracy International AXMC"
msgid_plural "Accuracy International AXMC"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of variant "modular sniper rifle" of gun "Accuracy
#. International AXMC"
#: data/json/items/gun/338lapua.json
msgid ""
"Produced by the British precision rifle company Accuracy International, the "
"AX Modular Caliber Weapon System is a highly-accurate combat sniper rifle "
"offered to military, law enforcement, and civilian precision marksmen.  The "
"rifle is compatible with a wide range of aftermarket components, including "
"caliber conversion kits, and is built upon a base aluminum chassis, into "
"which the weapon's parts may be installed or removed at the user's "
"discretion."
msgstr ""
"Producido por la compañía británica de rifles Accuracy International, el "
"Sistema de Armas de Calibre Modular AX es un rifle de francotirador de "
"combate altamente preciso vendido a militares, fuerzas de seguridad, y "
"tiradores civiles de precisión. Este rifle es compatible con un amplio "
"catalogo de componentes comerciales, incluidos los equipos de conversión de "
"calibre, y esta construido sobre un armazón de aluminio, donde las partes "
"del arma pueden ser instaladas o quitadas a conveniencia del usuario."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/357sig.json
msgid "SIG P226"
msgid_plural "SIG P226s"
msgstr[0] "SIG P226"
msgstr[1] "SIG P226s"
msgstr[2] "SIG P226s"

#. ~ Description of gun "SIG P226"
#: data/json/items/gun/357sig.json
msgid ""
"A SIG Sauer P226 chambered for .357 SIG.  The P226 is a DA/SA, short-recoil "
"operated semi-automatic pistol."
msgstr ""
"Es una SIG Sauer P226 calibre .357 SIG. La P226 es una DA/SA, una pistola "
"semiautomática con poco retroceso."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/357sig.json
msgid "Glock 31"
msgid_plural "Glock 31s"
msgstr[0] "Glock 31"
msgstr[1] "Glock 31s"
msgstr[2] "Glock 31s"

#. ~ Description of gun "Glock 31"
#: data/json/items/gun/357sig.json
msgid ""
"A full size .357 SIG Glock pistol.  It is extremely similar to the Glock 22,"
" and could be converted to fire .40 S&W by switching the barrel."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola Glock .357 SIG de tamaño completo. Es extremadamente similar a "
"la Glock 22, y podría ser convertida en una pistola de .40 S&W cambiando el "
"cañón."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/357sig.json
msgid "SIG P320 Compact"
msgid_plural "SIG P320 Compacts"
msgstr[0] "SIG P320 Compact"
msgstr[1] "SIG P320 Compacts"
msgstr[2] "SIG P320 Compacts"

#. ~ Description of gun "SIG P320 Compact"
#: data/json/items/gun/357sig.json
msgid ""
"The P320 Compact is a semi-automatic, short recoil operated pistol.  This "
"one is chambered for .357 SIG."
msgstr ""
"La P320 Compact es una pistola semiautomática de retroceso corto. Esta tiene"
" recámara para .357 SIG."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/36paper.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
msgid "Colt M1861 Navy"
msgid_plural "Colt M1861 Navy"
msgstr[0] "Colt M1861 Navy"
msgstr[1] "Colt M1861 Navy"
msgstr[2] "Colt M1861 Navy"

#. ~ Description of gun "Colt M1861 Navy"
#: data/json/items/gun/36paper.json
msgid ""
"The Colt Model 1861 Navy cap & ball .36-caliber revolver was a six-shot, "
"single-action percussion weapon produced by Colt's Manufacturing Company "
"from 1861 until 1873."
msgstr ""
"El Colt Model 1861 Navy, revólver de llave de percusión, calibre .36, era un"
" arma de percusión de una sola acción, con seis disparos, producida por "
"Colt's Manufacturing Company desde 1861 hasta 1873."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid "2 Shot Special"
msgid_plural "2 Shot Specials"
msgstr[0] "2 Tiros Especial"
msgstr[1] "2 Tiros Especial"
msgstr[2] "2 Tiros Especial"

#. ~ Description of gun "2 Shot Special"
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid ""
"A crudely made double barrel pistol firing .38 Special ammo.  Unfortunately,"
" the name is less about the double barrels and more about the number of "
"shots you'll get before it breaks down on you."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola de doble cañón hecha toscamente, que dispara munición .38 "
"Especial.  Lamentablemente, el nombre tiene poco que ver con el doble cañon,"
" pero más con el número de disparos que podrás hacer antes de que se rompa."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid "COP .357 Derringer"
msgid_plural "COP .357 Derringers"
msgstr[0] "COP .357 Derringer"
msgstr[1] "COP .357 Derringers"
msgstr[2] "COP .357 Derringers"

#. ~ Description of gun "COP .357 Derringer"
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid ""
"A small, chubby derringer pistol bearing a slight resemblance to the "
"Mossberg Brownie.  It uses a rotating firing pin to fire the individual "
"hammers of the four barrels arranged in a square formation."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña y regordeta pistola Derringer con un ligero parecido a la "
"Brownie de Mossberg. Utiliza un percutor giratorio para disparar los "
"martillos individuales de los cuatro barriles dispuestos en una formación "
"cuadrada."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
msgid "S&W Model 10"
msgid_plural "S&W Model 10s"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of gun "S&W Model 10"
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid ""
"A six-shot revolver, produced since 1899 and known as the most popular "
"handgun of the 20th century.  It has a swing-out cylinder for ease of "
"reloading."
msgstr ""
"Un revólver de seis disparos, producido desde 1899 y conocido como el arma "
"de mano más popular del siglo XX. Tiene un cilindro giratorio para facilitar"
" su recarga."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid "Manurhin MR 73"
msgid_plural "Manurhin MR 73"
msgstr[0] "Manurhin MR 73"
msgstr[1] "Manurhin MR 73"
msgstr[2] "Manurhin MR 73"

#. ~ Description of gun "Manurhin MR 73"
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid ""
"A finely made .357 Magnum revolver with a 4 inch barrel.  It has adjustable "
"sights, big plastic grips and a very smooth trigger."
msgstr ""
"Un revolver .357 Magnum con un cañon de 10 centimetros de largo (4 pulgadas)"
" finamente hecho. Sus miras son ajustables, con empuñadura de plástico "
"grande y un gatillo muy suave."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid "pipe rifle: .38 Special"
msgid_plural "pipe rifles: .38 Special"
msgstr[0] "rifle de tubo: .38 Especial"
msgstr[1] "rifles de tubo: .38 Especial"
msgstr[2] "rifles de tubo: .38 Especial"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid "Ruger LCR .38"
msgid_plural "Ruger LCR .38"
msgstr[0] "Ruger LCR .38"
msgstr[1] "Ruger LCR .38"
msgstr[2] "Ruger LCR .38"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid "S&W 619"
msgid_plural "S&W 619"
msgstr[0] "S&W 619"
msgstr[1] "S&W 619"
msgstr[2] "S&W 619"

#. ~ Description of gun "S&W 619"
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid ""
"A seven-round .357 revolver sold by Smith & Wesson.  Can also fire .38 "
"Special.  It features a fixed rear sight and a reinforced frame."
msgstr ""
"Un revólver de siete disparos calibre .357, vendido por Smith & Wesson. "
"También puede usar el .38 Special. Posee una mira trasera fija y una "
"estructura reforzada."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid "MAC-11"
msgid_plural "MAC-11s"
msgstr[0] "MAC-11"
msgstr[1] "MAC-11s"
msgstr[2] "MAC-11s"

#. ~ Description of gun "MAC-11"
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid ""
"A lesser known variant of the MAC-10, this machine pistol is chambered in "
".380 ACP for a smaller overall size while remaining inherently subsonic.  "
"Smaller in almost every dimension, this inexpensive automatic weapon was "
"declared 'fit only for combat in a phone booth' due to its low weight and "
"absurd fire rate ranging from 1200 to 1400 rounds per minute."
msgstr ""
"Una variante menos conocida de la MAC-10, esta pistola de máquina está "
"alojada en una cámara de .380 ACP para un tamaño general más pequeño, "
"mientras que sigue siendo inherentemente subsónica. Más pequeña en casi "
"todas las dimensiones, esta arma automática barata fue declarada \"apta sólo"
" para el combate en una cabina telefónica\" debido a su bajo peso y a su "
"absurda velocidad de disparo que va de 1200 a 1400 disparos por minuto."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid "Kel-Tec P-3AT"
msgid_plural "Kel-Tec P-3ATs"
msgstr[0] "Kel-Tec P-3AT"
msgstr[1] "Kel-Tecs P-3AT"
msgstr[2] "Kel-Tecs P-3AT"

#. ~ Description of gun "Kel-Tec P-3AT"
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid ""
"Essentially a slightly scaled up Kel-Tec P-32 in .380 ACP, the ever popular "
"P-3AT offers better ballistics in a small, concealable lightweight package."
"  Handling leaves something to be desired due to snappier recoil and "
"diminutive controls."
msgstr ""
"Esencialmente una Kel-tec P-32 ligeramente escalada en .380 ACP, la popular "
"P3AT ofrece una mejor balística en un paquete pequeño, ligero y ocultable. "
"El manejo deja algo que desear debido a un retroceso más rápido y a unos "
"controles más reducidos."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
msgid "FN 1910 .380"
msgid_plural "FN 1910 .380s"
msgstr[0] "FN 1910 .380"
msgstr[1] "FN 1910 .380s"
msgstr[2] "FN 1910 .380s"

#. ~ Description of gun "FN 1910 .380"
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid ""
"Made infamous in Sarajevo in 1914, the FN1910 was a popular pocket pistol, "
"albeit in .32 ACP.  Collectors value the .380 model for its notoriety and "
"more modern terminal performance.  If such a humble firearm could start a "
"world war, could it perhaps protect you from the undead?"
msgstr ""
"Hecha infame en Sarajevo en 1914, la FN1910 era una popular pistola de "
"bolsillo, aunque en .32 ACP. Los coleccionistas valoran el modelo .380 por "
"su notoriedad y su rendimiento terminal más moderno. Si un arma de fuego tan"
" humilde pudiera iniciar una guerra mundial, ¿podría quizás protegerte de "
"los no-muertos?"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid "Ruger LCP"
msgid_plural "Ruger LCPs"
msgstr[0] "Ruger LCP"
msgstr[1] "Ruger LCPs"
msgstr[2] "Ruger LCPs"

#. ~ Description of gun "Ruger LCP"
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid ""
"One of the best-selling modern day 'pocket pistols', the LCP is an "
"affordable, polymer framed pistol chambered in .380 ACP.  Despite the "
"round's relatively low power, the pistol's low weight and short sight radius"
" make for moderately poor handling."
msgstr ""
"Una de las \"pistolas de bolsillo\" más vendidas en la actualidad, la LCP es"
" una pistola de marco polimérico asequible, con una cámara de .380 ACP.  A "
"pesar de la potencia relativamente baja del cartucho, el bajo peso de la "
"pistola y su corto radio de visión hacen que sea una pistola de manejo "
"moderadamente pobre."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid "Hi-Point CF-380"
msgid_plural "Hi-Point CF-380s"
msgstr[0] "Hi-Point CF-380"
msgstr[1] "Hi-Point CF-380s"
msgstr[2] "Hi-Point CF-380s"

#. ~ Description of gun "Hi-Point CF-380"
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid ""
"The Hi-Point CF-380 is a blowback operated semi-automatic pistol designed by"
" Hi-Point Firearms, which is known for making inexpensive firearms, and for "
"making said firearms bulky and uncomfortable.  Hi-Points have slides made "
"with a zinc pot-metal which is relatively fragile compared to steel slides."
msgstr ""
"La Hi-Point CF-380 es una pistola semiautomática operada por retroceso "
"diseñada por Hi-Point Firearms, conocida por fabricar armas de fuego baratas"
" y por hacer dichas armas voluminosas e incómodas. Las Hi-Point tienen "
"correderas hechas con una aleación de zinc que es relativamente frágil "
"comparada con las correderas de acero."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid "Taurus Spectrum"
msgid_plural "Taurus Spectrum"
msgstr[0] "Taurus Spectrum"
msgstr[1] "Taurus Spectrum"
msgstr[2] "Taurus Spectrum"

#. ~ Description of gun "Taurus Spectrum"
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid ""
"A .380 subcompact pistol.  Designed for concealed carry and built from high-"
"quality, durable materials."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola subcompacta del calibre 380. Diseñada para llevarla oculta y "
"construida con materiales de alta calidad y durabilidad."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid "pipe rifle: .380 ACP"
msgid_plural "pipe rifles: .380 ACP"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid ".380 ACP pistol-caliber carbine"
msgid_plural ".380 ACP pistol-caliber carbines"
msgstr[0] "carabina con calibre de pistola .380 ACP"
msgstr[1] "carabinas con calibre de pistola .380 ACP"
msgstr[2] "carabinas con calibre de pistola .380 ACP"

#. ~ Description of gun ".380 ACP pistol-caliber carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid ""
"A pistol-caliber carbine chambered in .380 ACP.  It is more powerful and "
"accurate than an equivalent pistol but the .380 ACP round is nonetheless "
"fairly weak.  Accepts 10-round magazines, which are not shared with any .380"
" ACP pistol unlike many other similar pistol-caliber carbines."
msgstr ""
"Una carabina con calibre de pistola con recamara .380 ACP. Es mas potente y "
"precisa que su pistola equivalente pero la munición .380 ACP es bastante "
"débil. Acepta cargadores de 10 balas, que no se pueden compartir con "
"cualquier pistola .380 ACP a diferencia de otras carabinas con calibre de "
"pistola similares."

#. ~ Variant name of gun ".380 ACP pistol-caliber carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid "Hi-Point 3895"
msgid_plural "Hi-Point 3895s"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of variant ".380 ACP pistol-caliber carbine" of gun "Hi-Point
#. 3895"
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid ""
"A pistol-caliber carbine chambered in .380 ACP, designed by Hi-Point "
"Firearms.  Its 16.5\" barrel provides extra stopping power over an "
"equivalent pistol, but .380 is still a relatively weak caliber.  Accepts "
"10-round magazines, which are notably not interchangeable with those of "
"CF380 pistols."
msgstr ""
"Una carabina con calibre de pistola con recamara .380 ACP, diseñada por Hi-"
"Point Firearms. Su cañón de 16.5\" provee un poder de parada por encima de "
"una pistola equivalente, pero el .380 es un calibre relativamente débil. "
"Acepta cargadores de 10 balas, que son notablemente intercambiables con las "
"pistolas CF380."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/38super.json
msgid "AF2011A1 .38 Super"
msgid_plural "AF2011A1 .38 Super"
msgstr[0] "AF2011A1 .38 Super"
msgstr[1] "AF2011A1 .38 Super"
msgstr[2] "AF2011A1 .38 Super"

#. ~ Description of gun "AF2011A1 .38 Super"
#: data/json/items/gun/38super.json
msgid ""
"A double-barrel semi-automatic pistol of Italian origin, firing two bullets "
"per shot, a derivative of the M1911 pistol."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola semiautomática de doble cañón de origen italiano, que dispara "
"dos balas por disparo, un derivado de la pistola M1911."

