"A small, 16-layer thick ballistic Kevlar panel.  This kind of Kevlar is "
"precision-made by machine and features an extremely tight weave which cannot"
" be replicated by hand.  Due to this, any damage incurred to your ballistic "
"armor will necessitate complete replacement with a new panel.  It is not as "
"effective as loose-woven Kevlar at stopping stab wounds, but it has no equal"
" against the threat posed by firearms."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño panel de kevlar balístico grueso de 16 capas. Este tipo de kevlar"
" esta hecho a maquina con precisión y tiene un cosido extremadamente "
"apretado que no puede ser replicado a mano. Debido a esto, cualquier daño en"
" tu armadura balística necesitara reemplazarse con un nuevo panel. No es tan"
" efectivo como el kevlar cosido suelto al parar heridas punzantes, pero no "
"tiene rival contra la amenaza que suponen las armas de fuego."

#. ~ same as above but adding superglue. IRL this is how they are made, though
#. using 2 part resin instead.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "rigid Kevlar plate"
msgid_plural "rigid Kevlar plates"
msgstr[0] "placa de Kevlar rígida"
msgstr[1] "placas de Kevlar rígidas"
msgstr[2] "placas de Kevlar rígidas"

#. ~ same as above but adding superglue. IRL this is how they are made, though
#. using 2 part resin instead.
#. ~ Description of "rigid Kevlar plate"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A compressed panel of Kevlar treated with epoxy or other adhesive.  It could"
" be used to repair items made of rigid Kevlar, and makes a decent substitute"
" for damaged carbon fiber and the like even if it isn't exactly the same."
msgstr ""
"Un panel de kevlar comprimido tratado con epoxi u otros adhesivos. Se podría"
" usar para reparar objetos hecho de kevlar rígido y es un buen sustituto "
"para la fibra de carbono dañada y similares incluso si no es exactamente lo "
"mismo."

#. ~ 180GSM
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "patchwork Lycra sheet"
msgid_plural "patchwork Lycra sheets"
msgstr[0] "lámina de retazos de Licra"
msgstr[1] "láminas de retazos de Licra"
msgstr[2] "láminas de retazos de Licra"

#. ~ 180GSM
#. ~ Description of "patchwork Lycra sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A 12-inch by 24-inch sheet of fabric sewn together from Lycra patches.  "
"Suitable for making flexible, yet strong clothing if you lack proper "
"material sheets."
msgstr ""
"Una lámina de tela de licra de 30 por 60 centímetros cosidos juntos usando "
"parches. Ideal para hacer ropa flexible pero fuerte si no tienes las láminas"
" de material apropiadas."

#. ~ 110GSM, 1mm thick neoprene
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "neoprene sheet"
msgid_plural "neoprene sheets"
msgstr[0] "sábana de neopreno"
msgstr[1] "sábanas de neopreno"
msgstr[2] "sábanas de neopreno"

#. ~ 110GSM, 1mm thick neoprene
#. ~ Description of "neoprene sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A sheet of neoprene, a synthetic rubber, suitable for making underwater "
"gear."
msgstr ""
"Una sábana de neopreno, una goma sintética, adecuada para fabricar equipo "
"subacuático."

#. ~ Density of 1.23 grams per mL
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "patchwork neoprene sheet"
msgid_plural "patchwork neoprene sheets"
msgstr[0] "lámina de retazos de neopreno"
msgstr[1] "láminas de retazos de neopreno"
msgstr[2] "láminas de retazos de neopreno"

#. ~ Density of 1.23 grams per mL
#. ~ Description of "patchwork neoprene sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A sheet of neoprene sewn together from patches, with waterproofed seams.  "
"Suitable for making underwater gear if you lack proper material sheets."
msgstr ""
"Una lámina de tela de neopreno de 30 por 60 centímetros cosidos usando "
"parches, con juntas impermeables. Ideal para hacer aparatos subacuáticos si "
"no tienes las láminas de materiales apropiadas."

#. ~ Taken from duponts chemical reference sheets. 170GSM
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "Nomex sheet"
msgid_plural "Nomex sheets"
msgstr[0] "sábana de Nomex"
msgstr[1] "sábanas de Nomex"
msgstr[2] "sábanas de Nomex"

#. ~ Taken from duponts chemical reference sheets. 170GSM
#. ~ Description of "Nomex sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A sheet of Nomex synthetic fabric, suitable for making heat-resistant "
"clothing."
msgstr ""
"Una sábana de tejido sintético Nomex, adecuada para hacer ropa resistente al"
" calor."

#. ~ Taken from duponts chemical reference sheets. 170GSM
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "patchwork Nomex sheet"
msgid_plural "patchwork Nomex sheets"
msgstr[0] "lámina de retazos de Nomex"
msgstr[1] "láminas de retazos de Nomex"
msgstr[2] "láminas de retazos de Nomex"

#. ~ Taken from duponts chemical reference sheets. 170GSM
#. ~ Description of "patchwork Nomex sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A sheet of Nomex synthetic fabric, sewn together from patches using Nomex "
"thread.  Suitable for making heat-resistant clothing if you lack proper "
"material sheets."
msgstr ""
"Una lámina de tela de Nomex de 30 por 60 centímetros cosidos usando parches,"
" con juntas impermeables. Ideal para hacer ropa ignífuga si no tienes las "
"láminas de materiales apropiadas."

#. ~ .25mm thick, 288 GSM (nylon 6,6 ranges 250-300 gsm)
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "synthetic fabric sheet"
msgid_plural "synthetic fabric sheets"
msgstr[0] "sábana de tejido sintético"
msgstr[1] "sábanas de tejido sintético"
msgstr[2] "sábanas de tejido sintético"

#. ~ .25mm thick, 288 GSM (nylon 6,6 ranges 250-300 gsm)
#. ~ Description of "synthetic fabric sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A sheet of synthetic fabric, suitable for making clothing."
msgstr "Una sábana de tela sintética, adecuada para hacer ropa."

#. ~ .25mm thick, 288 GSM (nylon 6,6 ranges 250-300 gsm)
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "patchwork synthetic fabric sheet"
msgid_plural "patchwork synthetic fabric sheet"
msgstr[0] "lámina de retazos de tela sintética"
msgstr[1] "láminas de retazos de tela sintética"
msgstr[2] "láminas de retazos de tela sintética"

#. ~ .25mm thick, 288 GSM (nylon 6,6 ranges 250-300 gsm)
#. ~ Description of "patchwork synthetic fabric sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A sheet of fabric, sewn together from synthetic fabric patches in a "
"patchwork fashion.  Suitable for making most clothing, though it's much less"
" time-efficient than if using proper material sheets."
msgstr ""
"Una lámina de tela hecha con retazos de tela sintética cosidos entre sí. "
"Útil para fabricar ropa aunque es mucho menos eficiente que utilizar telas "
"apropiadas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "gambeson batting"
msgid_plural "clumps of gambeson batting"
msgstr[0] "relleno de gambesón"
msgstr[1] "restos de relleno de gambesón"
msgstr[2] "restos de relleno de gambesón"

#. ~ Description of "gambeson batting"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A pile of shredded fabric, dry grass, hair or other cheap materials which "
"could be used to stuff the fabric layers of a gambeson to create armor more "
"cheaply and easily than properly layering and quilting the entire product."
msgstr ""
"Un montón de tela destrozada, hierba seca, pelo u otro material barato que "
"se puede usar para juntar capas de tela de gambesón para crear armadura mas "
"barata y fácil que un acolchado por capas en todo el producto."

#. ~ 30 meters of thread per 1g, roughly 6 inches of thread per unit.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "Kevlar thread"
msgid_plural "Kevlar thread"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ 30 meters of thread per 1g, roughly 6 inches of thread per unit.
#. ~ Description of "Kevlar thread"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"Very durable Kevlar thread that would be particularly useful for making "
"ballistic armor, though it's fine to use in place of normal thread too, in "
"most cases.  Making armor-grade Kevlar sheets from this would need a "
"particularly tight weave, and so would require some specialized machinery."
msgstr ""
"Hilo de Kevlar muy resistente que sería particularmente útil para hacer "
"armaduras balísticas, aunque también está bien usarlo en lugar del hilo "
"normal en la mayoría de los casos. Hacer láminas de kevlar para armaduras a "
"partir de esto necesitaría un cosido particularmente apretado, y por lo "
"tanto necesitaría alguna maquinaria especializada."

#. ~ 30 meters of thread per 1g, roughly 6 inches of thread per unit.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "Nomex thread"
msgid_plural "Nomex thread"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ 30 meters of thread per 1g, roughly 6 inches of thread per unit.
#. ~ Description of "Nomex thread"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"Heat-resistant Nomex thread that would be particularly useful for making "
"heat protection gear, though it's fine to use in place of normal thread too,"
" in most cases."
msgstr ""
"Hilo de Nomex resistente al calor que es particularmente útil para hacer "
"equipos de protección contra el calor, aunque también se puede usar en lugar"
" del hilo normal, en la mayoría de los casos."

#. ~ Usually lightweight 10-12 oz denim.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "denim sheet"
msgid_plural "denim sheets"
msgstr[0] "lámina de tela vaquera"
msgstr[1] "láminas de tela vaquera"
msgstr[2] "láminas de tela vaquera"

#. ~ Usually lightweight 10-12 oz denim.
#. ~ Description of "denim sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A 12 inch by 24 inch sheet of durable blue denim, suitable for making jeans,"
" jorts, or jirts."
msgstr ""
"Una lámina de 30 por 60 centímetros de tela vaquera durable, perfecto para "
"hacer pantalones vaqueros largos y cortos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "denim scraps"
msgid_plural "denim scraps"
msgstr[0] "resto de tela vaquera"
msgstr[1] "restos de tela vaquera"
msgstr[2] "restos de tela vaquera"

#. ~ Description of "denim scraps"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"Oddly-shaped smallish denim patches, waste material from tailoring projects."
msgstr ""
"Pequeños parches de tela vaquera con forma irregular, material de desecho de"
" proyectos de sastrería."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "denim patch"
msgid_plural "denim patches"
msgstr[0] "parche de tela vaquera"
msgstr[1] "parches de tela vaquera"
msgstr[2] "parches de tela vaquera"

#. ~ Description of "denim patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A small, 6 inch square patch of blue denim.  It could be used to repair "
"items made of denim or stitched into patchwork sheets for tailoring "
"projects."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño parche de tela vaquera de 15 centímetros cuadrados. Podría usarse"
" para reparar objetos hechos con tela vaquera o cosidos juntos para formar "
"láminas de retazos para proyectos de sastrería."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "patchwork denim sheet"
msgid_plural "patchwork denim sheets"
msgstr[0] "lámina de retazos de tela vaquera"
msgstr[1] "láminas de retazos de tela vaquera"
msgstr[2] "láminas de retazos de tela vaquera"

#. ~ Description of "patchwork denim sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A selection of various sections of denim, sewn together in a patchwork "
"fashion.  Suitable for tailoring, though it's much less time-efficient than "
"if using proper material sheets."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de diversos pedazos de tela vaquera, cosidos para formar una "
"tela de retales. Útil para trabajos de sastrería aunque es mucho menos "
"eficiente que utilizar telas apropiadas."

#. ~ heavyweight cotton canvas with a GSM of 406
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "canvas sheet"
msgid_plural "canvas sheets"
msgstr[0] "tela de lona"
msgstr[1] "telas de lona"
msgstr[2] "telas de lona"

#. ~ heavyweight cotton canvas with a GSM of 406
#. ~ Description of "canvas sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A 12 inch by 24 inch sheet of durable and waterproof waxed canvas fabric, "
"suitable for making tough bags and clothing."
msgstr ""
"Una tela de lona de 30x60cm, fuerte e impermeable, ideal para hacer ropa y "
"bolsos resistentes."

#. ~ 30 meters of thread per 1g, roughly 6 inches of thread per unit.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "heavy duty thread"
msgid_plural "heavy duty thread"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ 30 meters of thread per 1g, roughly 6 inches of thread per unit.
#. ~ Description of "heavy duty thread"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"Some tough canvas-weight thread, sturdier than ordinary thread.  You could "
"meticulously weave this into a sheet of canvas cloth.  It would also be "
"useful for stitching such sheets together, though it's fine to use for "
"normal tailoring projects too."
msgstr ""
"Un poco de hilo reforzado de lona, más fuerte que el hilo común. Podrías "
"tejerlo meticulosamente y hacer una tela de lona. También sería útil para "
"coser esas telas aunque se puede usar para los trabajos de sastrería "
"normales."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "canvas scraps"
msgid_plural "canvas scraps"
msgstr[0] "pedazo de lona"
msgstr[1] "pedazos de lona"
msgstr[2] "pedazos de lona"

#. ~ Description of "canvas scraps"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"Oddly-shaped smallish bits of canvas, waste material from tailoring "
"projects.  Not useful for much and usually disposed of, but can be recycled "
"into some tough thread."
msgstr ""
"Pequeños pedazos irregulares de lona, desperdicio de algún trabajo de "
"sastrería. No son muy útiles pero pueden ser reciclados para hacer hilo "
"resistente."

#. ~ Roughly 406 GSM cotton, with a size of 6 inches square
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "canvas patch"
msgid_plural "canvas patches"
msgstr[0] "parche de lona"
msgstr[1] "parches de lona"
msgstr[2] "parches de lona"

#. ~ Roughly 406 GSM cotton, with a size of 6 inches square
#. ~ Description of "canvas patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A small, 6 inch square patch of tough canvas.  It could be used to repair "
"items made of canvas or stitched into patchwork sheets for tailoring "
"projects."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño parche cuadrado de 15 centímetros de lona resistente. Se puede "
"usar para reparar objetos hechos de tela o coser con otros para armar una "
"lona de retales para algún trabajo de sastrería."

#. ~ heavyweight cotton canvas with a GSM of 406
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "patchwork canvas sheet"
msgid_plural "patchwork canvas sheets"
msgstr[0] "lamina de retazos de lona"
msgstr[1] "laminas de retazos de lona"
msgstr[2] "laminas de retazos de lona"

#. ~ heavyweight cotton canvas with a GSM of 406
#. ~ Description of "patchwork canvas sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A selection of various sections of canvas, sewn together in a patchwork "
"fashion.  Suitable for tailoring, though it's much less time-efficient than "
"if using proper material sheets."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de diversos pedazos de lona, cosidos para formar una tela de "
"retales. Útil para trabajos de sastrería aunque es mucho menos eficiente que"
" utilizar telas apropiadas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "log"
msgid_plural "logs"
msgstr[0] "leño"
msgstr[1] "leños"
msgstr[2] "leños"

#. ~ Description of "log"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A large log of wood, cut from a tree.  (a)ctivate a wood axe or wood saw to "
"cut it into planks."
msgstr ""
"Un gran trozo de leño, cortado de un árbol. (a)ctiva un hacha de madera o "
"una sierra de madera para cortarlo en tablones."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "splintered wood"
msgid_plural "splintered wood"
msgstr[0] "astilla de madera"
msgstr[1] "astillas de madera"
msgstr[2] "astillas de madera"

#. ~ Description of "splintered wood"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "A splintered piece of wood, could be used as a skewer or for kindling."
msgstr ""
"Una trozo de astilla de madera que puede ser usada como un pincho o leña."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json data/mods/MMA/bludgeons.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/weapon_copy_extensions.json
msgid "stick"
msgid_plural "sticks"
msgstr[0] "palo"
msgstr[1] "palos"
msgstr[2] "palos"

#. ~ Description of "stick"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A respectable length of wood, just big enough to wrap your hand around.  "
"Makes a decent melee weapon."
msgstr ""
"Una longitud respetable de madera, lo suficientemente grande como para "
"envolver tu mano. Un arma de combate c. a c. decente."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "long stick"
msgid_plural "long sticks"
msgstr[0] "palo largo"
msgstr[1] "palos largos"
msgstr[2] "palos largos"

#. ~ Description of "long stick"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A straight section of wood, about eight feet long and a couple of inches in "
"diameter.  Makes a decent melee weapon, and can be broken into shorter "
"pieces for crafting."
msgstr ""
"Una sección recta de madera, de unos dos metros de largo y un par de "
"centímetros de diámetro. Constituye un arma de c. a c. decente, y puede "
"romperse en trozos más cortos para la fabricación."

#. ~ a long pole is a single piece of wood, and the heavy stick just isn't
#. large enough.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "long pole"
msgid_plural "long poles"
msgstr[0] "palo largo"
msgstr[1] "palos largos"
msgstr[2] "palos largos"

#. ~ a long pole is a single piece of wood, and the heavy stick just isn't
#. large enough.
#. ~ Description of "long pole"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A stout, ten-foot pole.  Could be used similarly to a spear.  The Cataclysm "
"gives fresh meaning to walking softly and carrying a big stick."
msgstr ""
"Un palo robusto de tres metros. Podría usarse de forma similar a una lanza. "
"El Cataclismo le da un nuevo significado a caminar suavemente y llevar un "
"gran palo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "spear shaft"
msgid_plural "spear shaft"
msgstr[0] "lanza de palo"
msgstr[1] "lanzas de palo"
msgstr[2] "lanzas de palo"

#. ~ Description of "spear shaft"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A long stick, sanded and treated with oil for integrity and carved into a "
"smooth staff with a slight taper, for use in making spears.  It can also be "
"used as a makeshift quarterstaff as-is, but is too thin to be very effective"
" for just hitting people."
msgstr ""
"Un palo largo lijado, tratado con aceite para mayor solidez y tallado para "
"hacerlo suave y estrecho, utilizado para hacer lanzas. También puede usarse "
"para hacer una vara larga improvisada pero es demasiado fina para ser "
"efectiva para golpear."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/weapon_copy_extensions.json
msgid "plank"
msgid_plural "planks"
msgstr[0] "tablón"
msgstr[1] "tablones"
msgstr[2] "tablones"

#. ~ Description of "plank"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A flat, thick plank of wood, like a 2 by 4 or similar piece of dimensional "
"lumber.  Makes a decent melee weapon if you're desperate, and can be used "
"for all kinds of construction projects."
msgstr ""
"Un tablón de madera estrecha y gruesa, como una pieza de madera de 2 por 4 o"
" similar. Es un arma c. a c. si estas desesperado, y se puede utilizar para "
"todo tipo de construcciones."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/weapon_copy_extensions.json
msgid "short plank"
msgid_plural "short planks"
msgstr[0] "tablón corto"
msgstr[1] "tablones cortos"
msgstr[2] "tablones cortos"

#. ~ Description of "short plank"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A short 2 by 4 plank of wood.  While less common and smaller than its 4 foot"
" cousin it can still be very useful in carpentry."
msgstr ""
"Un tablón corto de madera de 60cm por 120cm. Es menos común y pequeño que su"
" primo de 120cm pero aun es útil en materia de carpintería."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "long plank"
msgid_plural "long planks"
msgstr[0] "tablón largo"
msgstr[1] "tablones largos"
msgstr[2] "tablones largos"

#. ~ Description of "long plank"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A long 2 by 4 plank of wood.  While not as common as the 4 foot variant, "
"still makes a decent melee weapon, and can be used for all kinds "
"construction."
msgstr ""
"Un tablón de madera de 60cm por 120cm. Aunque no es tan común como su "
"variante de 120cm, todavía es un arma de c. a c. decente, y se puede "
"utilizar para todo tipo de construcciones."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "heavy wooden beam"
msgid_plural "heavy wooden beams"
msgstr[0] "viga de madera pesada"
msgstr[1] "vigas de madera pesadas"
msgstr[2] "vigas de madera pesadas"

#. ~ Description of "heavy wooden beam"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"An enormous beam of solid wood, very heavy and hard to lug around, but also "
"very sturdy for construction.  You could saw or chop it into smaller pieces,"
" like planks or panels."
msgstr ""
"Una enorme viga de madera maciza, muy pesada y difícil de arrastrar, pero "
"también muy resistente para la construcción. Podrías serrarla o cortarla en "
"trozos más pequeños, como tablones o paneles."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "wooden post"
msgid_plural "wooden posts"
msgstr[0] "poste de madera"
msgstr[1] "postes de madera"
msgstr[2] "postes de madera"

#. ~ Description of "wooden post"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A wooden post with a 4 by 4 square base.  Posts with a length similar to "
"this are commonly used in mailboxes or as table legs."
msgstr ""
"Un poste de madera de 4 por 4 con base cuadrada. Postes con una longitud "
"similar a este son usados comúnmente en buzones y patas de mesas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "short wooden post"
msgid_plural "short wooden posts"
msgstr[0] "poste de madera corto"
msgstr[1] "postes de madera cortos"
msgstr[2] "postes de madera cortos"

#. ~ Description of "short wooden post"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A wooden post with a 4 by 4 square base.  Posts with a length similar to "
"this are commonly used as chair legs."
msgstr ""
"Un poste de madera de 4 por 4 con base cuadrada. Postes con una longitud "
"similar a este son usados comúnmente en patas de sillas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "long wooden post"
msgid_plural "long wooden posts"
msgstr[0] "poste de madera largo"
msgstr[1] "postes de madera largos"
msgstr[2] "postes de madera largos"

#. ~ Description of "long wooden post"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A wooden post with a 4 by 4 square base.  Posts with a length similar to "
"this are commonly used in the construction of walls and floors."
msgstr ""
"Un poste de madera de 4 por 4 con base cuadrada. Postes con una longitud "
"similar a este son usados comúnmente en la construcción de muros y suelos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "small wood block"
msgid_plural "small wood blocks"
msgstr[0] "pequeño bloque de madera"
msgstr[1] "pequeños bloques de madera"
msgstr[2] "pequeños bloques de madera"

#. ~ Description of "small wood block"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A small 2x2x5 inches block of wood, primarily used for carving out small "
"wooden objects."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño bloque de madera de 5x5x12 centímetros, principalmente usado para"
" tallar objetos pequeños."

#. ~ Weight and volume assumes 16 square feet of 1/2 inch plywood.  The actual
#. size of the panel likely varies wildly and the item entry may represent
#. several smaller pieces.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "wooden panel"
msgid_plural "wooden panels"
msgstr[0] "panel de madera"
msgstr[1] "paneles de madera"
msgstr[2] "paneles de madera"

#. ~ Weight and volume assumes 16 square feet of 1/2 inch plywood.  The actual
#. size of the panel likely varies wildly and the item entry may represent
#. several smaller pieces.
#. ~ Description of "wooden panel"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A wide, thin wooden board - plywood, OSB, MDF, tongue-in-groove boards, or "
"similar, already cut to shape.  Good for all kinds of construction, but for "
"really big projects you'd need a proper sheet of uncut plywood or the like."
msgstr ""
"Un tablero de madera ancho y delgado - contrachapado, OSB, MDF, tablas de "
"lengüeta en ranura, o similar, ya cortado en forma. Estos grandes tableros "
"planos son buenos para todo tipo de construcción, pero para proyectos "
"realmente grandes se necesita una hoja adecuada de madera contrachapada sin "
"cortar o similar."

#. ~ Weight and volume assumes 32 square feet of 1/2 inch plywood.  Due to its
#. enormously bulky shape, volume is higher than actual displacement volume
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "large wooden sheet"
msgid_plural "large wooden sheets"
msgstr[0] "lamina de madera grande"
msgstr[1] "laminas de madera grandes"
msgstr[2] "laminas de madera grandes"

#. ~ Weight and volume assumes 32 square feet of 1/2 inch plywood.  Due to its
#. enormously bulky shape, volume is higher than actual displacement volume
#. ~ Description of "large wooden sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A standard 4 by 8 sheet of flat wood - usually plywood, OSB, or MDF.  Heavy "
"and bulky, it is extremely useful for all manner of construction, but you "
"might have to cut it to size before doing smaller projects."
msgstr ""
"Una hoja estándar de 4x8 de madera plana, normalmente de contrachapado, OSB "
"o MDF. Pesada y voluminosa, es extremadamente útil para todo tipo de "
"construcción, pero puede que tengas que cortarla a medida antes de hacer "
"proyectos más pequeños."

#. ~ weight for a bit less than 3x3x4 wooden beam at 0.60 g/cm3 density,
