"most tailoring projects, it's a necessity for stitching neoprene."
msgstr ""
"Una aguja curva y afilada hecha de acero. Su forma redondeada permite hacer "
"puntos que solo perforan un lado del material. Aunque no es adecuada para "
"muchas tareas de sastrería, es necesaria para coser neopreno."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "wooden needle"
msgid_plural "wooden needles"
msgstr[0] "aguja de madera"
msgstr[1] "agujas de madera"
msgstr[2] "agujas de madera"

#. ~ Description of "wooden needle"
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A wooden needle whittled down to a sharp point.  It has a narrow hole carved"
" into the head for threading.  Its low quality makes it rather unsuitable "
"for anything requiring speed or precision, or involving tougher materials "
"like Kevlar."
msgstr ""
"Una aguja de madera tallada con una punta afilada. Tiene un estrecho agujero"
" tallado en la cabeza para enhebrar. Su baja calidad la hace bastante "
"inadecuada para cualquier cosa que requiera velocidad o precisión, o que "
"implique materiales más duros como el Kevlar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "needle"
msgid_plural "needles"
msgstr[0] "aguja"
msgstr[1] "agujas"
msgstr[2] "agujas"

#. ~ Description of "needle"
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A stainless steel needle.  It would be useful for making clothing and items."
msgstr ""
"Una aguja afilada hecha de acero. Seria útil para confeccionar ropa y otros "
"objetos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json data/mods/Magiclysm/items/tools.json
#: data/mods/innawood/items/tool_tailoring.json
msgid "sewing kit"
msgid_plural "sewing kits"
msgstr[0] "costurero"
msgstr[1] "costureros"
msgstr[2] "costureros"

#. ~ Description of "sewing kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A plastic kit with a variety of needles, some plastic spools for thread, "
"small scissors, and a few other useful textile tools.  Use a sewing kit on "
"an article of clothing to attempt to repair or refit if applicable.  This "
"uses your tailoring skill."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "wooden shed stick"
msgid_plural "wooden shed sticks"
msgstr[0] "palos de madera de tejer"
msgstr[1] "palos de madera de tejer"
msgstr[2] "palos de madera de tejer"

#. ~ Description of "wooden shed stick"
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A short, thin, flat wooden stick, used as a tool while weaving cloth with a "
"frame loom."
msgstr ""
"Este es un palo corto y plano de madera, usado como herramienta mientras se "
"teje la tela con un telar de bastidor."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "tanning leather hide"
msgid_plural "tanning leather hides"
msgstr[0] "pellejo de cuero curtiéndose"
msgstr[1] "pellejos de cuero curtiéndose"
msgstr[2] "pellejos de cuero curtiéndose"

#. ~ Description of "tanning leather hide"
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A treated animal hide that is undergoing the chemical processes required to "
"become leather.  You will be able to activate it to unroll and make use of "
"it when it is done."
msgstr ""
"El pellejo tratado de un animal que está en pleno proceso químico requerido "
"para convertirse en cuero. Podrás activarlo para desenrollarlo y usarlo "
"cuando termine el proceso."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "tanning leather hide"
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "You carefully unfold the tanning leather hide and shake it clean."
msgstr ""
"Cuidadosamente, desdoblas el pellejo que está curtiéndose y lo sacudes para "
"limpiarlo."

#. ~ "not_ready_msg" action message of item "tanning leather hide"
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "The tanning leather hide isn't done yet."
msgstr "El pellejo todavía no terminó el proceso de curtido."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "tanning fur pelt"
msgid_plural "tanning fur pelts"
msgstr[0] "pelaje curándose"
msgstr[1] "pelajes curándose"
msgstr[2] "pelajes curándose"

#. ~ Description of "tanning fur pelt"
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A treated animal pelt that is undergoing the chemical processes required to "
"become fur.  You will be able to activate it to unroll and make use of it "
"when it is done."
msgstr ""
"Un pelaje tratado de un animal que está en pleno proceso químico que "
"necesita para convertirse en piel. Vas a poder activarlo para desenrollarlo "
"y usarlo cuando termine el proceso."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "tanning fur pelt"
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "You carefully unfold the tanning fur pelt and shake it clean."
msgstr ""
"Cuidadosamente, desdoblas el pelaje que está curándose y lo sacudes para "
"limpiarlo."

#. ~ "not_ready_msg" action message of item "tanning fur pelt"
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "The tanning fur pelt isn't done yet."
msgstr "El pelaje todavía no terminó el proceso de curado."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "tailoring pattern set"
msgid_plural "tailoring pattern sets"
msgstr[0] "conjunto de patrones de tejidos"
msgstr[1] "conjuntoñ de patrones de tejidos"
msgstr[2] "conjuntoñ de patrones de tejidos"

#. ~ Description of "tailoring pattern set"
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A large set of tailoring patterns made from paper.  They're useful for "
"making any kind of cloth or leather items from scratch, but are necessary "
"for more advanced projects."
msgstr ""
"Un gran conjunto de patrones de confección hechos de papel. Son útiles para "
"hacer cualquier tipo de tela o artículos de cuero desde cero, pero son "
"necesarios para proyectos más avanzados."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "pair of Kevlar shears"
msgid_plural "pairs of Kevlar shears"
msgstr[0] "par de tijeras para Kevlar"
msgstr[1] "pares de tijeras para Kevlar"
msgstr[2] "pares de tijeras para Kevlar"

#. ~ Description of "pair of Kevlar shears"
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A pair of heavy-duty shears suitable for cutting particularly tough "
"materials, from polyaramid fabrics to tough plastics and thin metals.  The "
"blades feature flat shearing edges and fine serrations."
msgstr ""
"Un par de cizallas para trabajos pesados con una hoja adecuada para cortar "
"materiales especialmente resistentes, desde tejidos de poliacrilamida hasta "
"plásticos resistentes y metales finos. Las hojas tienen un filo de corte "
"plano y un fino dentado."

#. ~ Based roughly off an Ashford E-Spinner 3 because that was the first thing
#. I looked at.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid "electric spinwheel"
msgid_plural "electric spinwheels"
msgstr[0] "hiladora eléctrica"
msgstr[1] "hiladoras eléctricas"
msgstr[2] "hiladoras eléctricas"

#. ~ Based roughly off an Ashford E-Spinner 3 because that was the first thing
#. I looked at.
#. ~ Description of "electric spinwheel"
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A device for spinning thread or yarn from fibers.  This particular model is "
"electrically-powered and easily portable."
msgstr ""
"Un dispositivo capaz de deshilachar fibras para producir hilo o lana.  Este "
"modelo en particular es eléctrico y fácil de transportar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json data/mods/Magiclysm/items/tools.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/tools.json
#: data/mods/innawood/items/tool_tailoring.json
msgid "tailor's kit"
msgid_plural "tailor's kits"
msgstr[0] "equipo de sastre"
msgstr[1] "equipos de sastre"
msgstr[2] "equipos de sastre"

#. ~ Description of "tailor's kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A high-quality kit consisting of a variety of needles, some plastic spools "
"for thread, scissors and shears, and an awl.  Use a tailor's kit on an "
"article of clothing to attempt to repair or refit if applicable.  This uses "
"your tailoring skill."
msgstr ""
"Un equipo de muy buena calidad con una variedad de agujas, algunos carretes "
"plásticos de hilo, tijeras normales, tijeras para esquilar y un punzón. "
"Puedes usar el equipo de sastre para reparar un articulo de ropa o reajustar"
" si se puede. Esto utiliza tu habilidad de sastrería."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "bathroom scale"
msgid_plural "bathroom scales"
msgstr[0] "báscula de baño"
msgstr[1] "básculas de baño"
msgstr[2] "básculas de baño"

#. ~ Description of "bathroom scale"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "A small bathroom scale, meant to weigh a person while naked."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña báscula de baño, destinada a pesar a una persona mientras está "
"desnuda."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "scrub brush"
msgid_plural "scrub brushes"
msgstr[0] "cepillo de fregar"
msgstr[1] "cepillos de fregar"
msgstr[2] "cepillos de fregar"

#. ~ Description of "scrub brush"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "A simple scrub brush for cleaning soft objects."
msgstr "Un simple cepillo de fregar para limpiar objetos suaves."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "dish towel"
msgid_plural "dish towels"
msgstr[0] "paño de cocina"
msgstr[1] "paños de cocina"
msgstr[2] "paños de cocina"

#. ~ Description of "dish towel"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "A dish towel, useful for cleaning hard surfaces."
msgstr "Un paño de cocina, útil para limpiar superficies duras."

#. ~ Snippet of item "dish towel"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"An elegant, monogrammed dish towel.  Unfortunately, they aren't your "
"initials."
msgstr ""
"Un elegante paño de cocina con monograma. Desgraciadamente, no son tus "
"iniciales."

#. ~ Snippet of item "dish towel"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "An elegant, monogrammed dish towel.  It even has your initials!"
msgstr ""
"Un elegante paño de cocina con monograma. Incluso tiene tus iniciales."

#. ~ Snippet of item "dish towel"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "A well-used dish towel, judging by the stains."
msgstr "Un paño de cocina bien usado, a juzgar por las manchas."

#. ~ Snippet of item "dish towel"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "A novelty dish towel featuring a popular children's cartoon character."
msgstr ""
"Un novedoso paño de cocina con un popular personaje de dibujos animados para"
" niños."

#. ~ Snippet of item "dish towel"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "A novelty dish towel which reads \"IT'S WINE O CLOCK\"."
msgstr "Un novedoso paño de cocina que dice \"SON LAS VINO EN PUNTO\"."

#. ~ Snippet of item "dish towel"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "A dish towel with a floral pattern."
msgstr "Un paño de cocina con motivos florales."

#. ~ Snippet of item "dish towel"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "A dish towel with a gingham pattern."
msgstr "Un paño de cocina con estampado gingham."

#. ~ Snippet of item "dish towel"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "A dish towel with a cat pattern."
msgstr "Un paño de cocina con un patrón de gatos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "electric hair trimmer"
msgid_plural "electric hair trimmers"
msgstr[0] "cortadora eléctrica de pelo"
msgstr[1] "cortadoras eléctricas de pelo"
msgstr[2] "cortadoras eléctricas de pelo"

#. ~ Description of "electric hair trimmer"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"A pocket-sized electric trimmer made for cutting hair.  You can use it to "
"cut your hair if it's supplied with batteries.  It requires 10 units of "
"charge per use."
msgstr ""
"Una maquinilla eléctrica de bolsillo para cortar el pelo. Puedes utilizarla "
"para cortar el pelo si tiene batería. Requiere 10 unidades de carga por uso."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "mop"
msgid_plural "mops"
msgstr[0] "fregona"
msgstr[1] "fregonas"
msgstr[2] "fregonas"

#. ~ Description of "mop"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"An unwieldy mop.  Good for cleaning up spills.  Use to mop up any 'mess' you"
" may have made."
msgstr ""
"Una fregona difícil de manejar. Útil para limpiar derrames. Úsala para "
"limpiar cualquier 'lio' que hayas hecho."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "collapsible mop"
msgid_plural "collapsible mops"
msgstr[0] "fregona plegable"
msgstr[1] "fregonas plegables"
msgstr[2] "fregonas plegables"

#. ~ Description of "collapsible mop"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"A long, unwieldy mop with a collapsible handle for convenient "
"transportation.  You may use it to clean up any 'mess' you have made."
msgstr ""
"Una fregona pesada con un mango plegable para facilitar el transporte. "
"Puedes usarla para limpiar cualquier 'lio' que hayas cometido."

#. ~ This is much, much bigger than it should be.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "rag"
msgid_plural "rags"
msgstr[0] "trapo"
msgstr[1] "trapos"
msgstr[2] "trapos"

#. ~ This is much, much bigger than it should be.
#. ~ Description of "rag"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"A largish piece of cloth, useful in crafting and possibly for staunching "
"bleeding."
msgstr ""
"Una larga pieza de tela, útil para la fabricación y posiblemente para "
"detener sangrados."

#. ~ This is calculated from medium weight cotton at 203 GSM, with a size of 6
#. inches square
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "cotton patch"
msgid_plural "cotton patches"
msgstr[0] "parche de algodón"
msgstr[1] "parches de algodón"
msgstr[2] "parches de algodón"

#. ~ This is calculated from medium weight cotton at 203 GSM, with a size of 6
#. inches square
#. ~ Description of "cotton patch"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"A 6-inch square cotton patch, suitable for repairing and tailoring clothing."
msgstr ""
"Un parche cuadrado de algodón de 15 centímetros cuadrados, adecuado para "
"usar en la reparación y confección de ropa."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "razor blade"
msgid_plural "razor blades"
msgstr[0] "hojita de afeitar"
msgstr[1] "hojitas de afeitar"
msgstr[2] "hojitas de afeitar"

#. ~ Description of "razor blade"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "A double-edged razor blade."
msgstr "Una cuchilla de doble filo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "shaving kit"
msgid_plural "shaving kits"
msgstr[0] "equipo de afeitar"
msgstr[1] "equipos de afeitar"
msgstr[2] "equipos de afeitar"

#. ~ Description of "shaving kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"A compact, lightweight shaving kit made for travelers.  You can use it to "
"shave if it's supplied with soap.  It requires 1 unit of soap per use."
msgstr ""
"Un equipo de afeitar compacto y liviano hecho para los que viajan. Lo puedes"
" usar para afeitarte si se le agrega jabón. Necesita 1 unidad de jabón por "
"uso."

#. ~ Based on https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08RFC3VH7
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "sponge"
msgid_plural "sponges"
msgstr[0] "esponja"
msgstr[1] "esponjas"
msgstr[2] "esponjas"

#. ~ Based on https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08RFC3VH7
#. ~ Description of "sponge"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"A cleaning aid made of soft, porous material.  Typically used for cleaning "
"hard objects."
msgstr ""
"Una esponja es una herramienta de limpieza hecha de material suave y poroso."
" Típicamente utilizada para limpiar objetos duras."

#. ~ Snippet of item "sponge"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "A round smiley-face sponge."
msgstr "Una esponja redonda con cara sonriente."

#. ~ Snippet of item "sponge"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "A rectangular sponge with a green abrasive back."
msgstr "Es una esponja rectangular con el reverso verde y abrasivo."

#. ~ Snippet of item "sponge"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "A dolphin-shaped sponge.  It looks at home in the water."
msgstr "Una esponja con forma de delfín. Parece estar en casa en el agua."

#. ~ Snippet of item "sponge"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "A rectangular sponge."
msgstr "Una esponja rectangular."

#. ~ Snippet of item "sponge"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "A sponge cake-shaped sponge, the abrasive pad looks like frosting."
msgstr ""
"Una esponja con forma de bizcocho, la almohadilla abrasiva parece un "
"glaseado."

#. ~ Snippet of item "sponge"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"A sponge in the shape of a beloved character from a children's cartoon."
msgstr ""
"Una esponja con la forma de un entrañable personaje de dibujos animados para"
" niños."

#. ~ Snippet of item "sponge"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "A cat-shaped sponge."
msgstr "Una esponja con forma de gato."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "makeshift haircut kit"
msgid_plural "makeshift haircut kits"
msgstr[0] "equipo improvisado cortapelo"
msgstr[1] "equipos improvisados cortapelo"
msgstr[2] "equipos improvisados cortapelo"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift haircut kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "A kit containing various improvised tools for cutting hair."
msgstr ""
"Un equipo que contiene varias herramientas improvisadas para cortar el pelo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "makeshift shaving kit"
msgid_plural "makeshift shaving kits"
msgstr[0] "equipo improvisado de afeitar"
msgstr[1] "equipos improvisados de afeitar"
msgstr[2] "equipos improvisados de afeitar"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift shaving kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"A makeshift shaving kit.  You can use it to shave if it's supplied with "
"soap.  It requires 1 unit of soap per use."
msgstr ""
"Un equipo de afeitar improvisado. Lo puedes usar para afeitarte si se le "
"agrega jabón. Necesita 1 unidad de jabón por uso."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "washboard"
msgid_plural "washboards"
msgstr[0] "tabla de lavar"
msgstr[1] "tablas de lavar"
msgstr[2] "tablas de lavar"

#. ~ Description of "washboard"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"A wooden washboard.  You can use it to wash filthy clothing if it's supplied"
" with cleansing agent."
msgstr ""
"Una tabla de madera para lavar. La puedes usar para lavar la ropa sucia si "
"tienes algún tipo de producto de limpieza."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid "washing kit"
msgid_plural "washing kits"
msgstr[0] "kit de lavado"
msgstr[1] "kits de lavado"
msgstr[2] "kits de lavado"

#. ~ Description of "washing kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/toiletries.json
msgid ""
"A combination of a washboard and a scrubbing tool.  Everything you need to "
"clean items after the apocalypse."
msgstr ""
"Una combinación de una tabla de lavar y una herramienta de fregar. Todo lo "
"que necesitas para limpiar los artículos después del apocalipsis."

#. ~ Description of "bear trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A spring-loaded pair of steel jaws connected to a sensitive pressure plate."
"  Use it to set it on the ground, creating a trap that will ensnare and "
"damage anything that steps on it.  If you are carrying a shovel, you will "
"have the option of burying it."
msgstr ""
"Un par de mandíbulas de acero conectadas a una placa de presión sensitiva. "
"Úsala para ponerla en el suelo, creando una trampa que va a capturar y dañar"
" cualquier cosa que la pise. Si tienes una pala, vas a tener la opción de "
"enterrarla."

#. ~ "bury_question" action message of item "bear trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "Bury the beartrap?"
msgstr "¿Quieres enterrar la trampa para oso?"

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "bear trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You set the beartrap."
msgstr "Pones la trampa para osos."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "bear trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You bury the beartrap."
msgstr "Entierras la trampa para osos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "light snare kit"
msgid_plural "light snare kits"
msgstr[0] "equipo de trampa ligera de lazo"
msgstr[1] "equipos de trampa ligera de lazo"
msgstr[2] "equipos de trampa ligera de lazo"

#. ~ Description of "light snare kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A simple loop snare, comprising a carefully wound loop of string, two anchor"
" points, and a tool to hammer them in.  It is suitable for immobilizing only"
" small animals.  It has no means of harming its target, as live meat lasts "
"longer."
msgstr ""
"Una simple trampa de lazo, compuesta por un lazo de cuerda cuidadosamente "
"anudado, con dos puntos de anclado, y una herramienta para martillar. Es "
"solo útil para inmovilizar pequeños animales. No tiene intención de herir a "
"su presa, ya que la carne viva dura mas."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "light snare kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You set the snare trap."
msgstr "Pones la trampa de lazo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "blade trap"
msgid_plural "blade traps"
msgstr[0] "trampa de cuchilla"
msgstr[1] "trampas de cuchilla"
msgstr[2] "trampas de cuchilla"

#. ~ Description of "blade trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A machete attached laterally to a motor, with a tripwire controlling its "
"throttle.  When the tripwire is pulled, the blade is swung around with great"
" force.  The trap forms a 3x3 area of effect."
msgstr ""
"Un machete agarrado al costado de un motor, con una cuerda controlando su "
"acelerador. Cuando se tira de la cuerda, la cuchilla se mueve con mucha "
"fuerza. La trampa tiene un área de efecto de 3x3."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "blade trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You set the blade trap 2 squares away."
msgstr "Colocas la trampa de cuchillas a 2 espacios de distancia."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "nailboard trap"
msgid_plural "nailboard traps"
msgstr[0] "trampa de tabla con clavos"
msgstr[1] "trampas de tabla con clavos"
msgstr[2] "trampas de tabla con clavos"

#. ~ Description of "nailboard trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"Several pieces of wood nailed together, with some nails sticking straight "
"up.  If an unsuspecting victim steps on it, they'll get nails through the "
"foot."
msgstr ""
"Varias piezas de madera clavadas juntas, con algunos clavos que sobresalen "
"por arriba. Si una víctima desprevenida la pisa, se va a ensartar los clavos"
" en el pie."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "nailboard trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
#, c-format
msgid "You set the board trap on the %s, nails facing up."
msgstr "Pones la trampa de tablas en el %s, clavos hacia arriba."

#. ~ Description of "booby trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A crude explosive device triggered by a piece of string.  Use it to set it "
"up and wait for some poor bastard to trigger it."
msgstr ""
"Un simple dispositivo explosivo disparado por un trozo de cuerda. Úsalo para"
" montarlo y ver cómo lo activa algún pobre bastardo."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "booby trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You set the booby trap up and activate the grenade."
msgstr "Pones la trampa bomba y activas la granada."

#. ~ Description of "bubble wrap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A sheet of plastic covered with air-filled bubbles.  Use it to set it on the"
" ground, creating a trap that will warn you with noise when something steps "
"on it."
msgstr ""
"Una lámina de plástico cubierta con burbujas de aire. Úsala para ponerlo en "
"el suelo, creando una trampa que te advertirá con el ruido si alguien la "
"pisa."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "bubble wrap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You set the bubble wrap on the ground, ready to be popped."
msgstr ""
"Pones el plástico de burbuja en el suelo, listo para que alguien lo pise."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "loose caltrops"
msgid_plural "loose caltrops"
msgstr[0] "abrojo metálico sueltos"
msgstr[1] "abrojos metálicos sueltos"
msgstr[2] "abrojos metálicos sueltos"

#. ~ Description of "loose caltrops"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A handful of small metal objects covered with many sharp points.  If an "
"unsuspecting victim steps on one, they'll get a spine through the foot."
msgstr ""
"Un puñado de pequeños objetos de metal cubiertos con muchas puntas afiladas."
" Si una víctima desprevenida los pisa, se va a llevar una púa atravesándole "
"el pie."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "loose caltrops"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
#, c-format
msgid "You scatter the caltrops on the %s."
msgstr "Desparramas los abrojos metálicos en el %s."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "loose glass caltrops"
msgid_plural "loose glass caltrops"
msgstr[0] "abrojos de vidrio suelto"
msgstr[1] "abrojos de vidrio suelto"
msgstr[2] "abrojos de vidrio suelto"

#. ~ Description of "loose glass caltrops"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A handful of glass shards glued together to expose all their sharp edges.  "
"If an unsuspecting victim steps on one, they'll get cut."
msgstr ""
"Un puñado de fragmentos de vidrio pegados para exponer sus bordes afilados. "
"Si una víctima desprevenida pisa uno, se cortará."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "loose glass caltrops"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
#, c-format
msgid "You scatter the glass caltrops on the %s."
msgstr "Dispersas los abrojos de vidrio en el %s."

#. ~ Description of "crossbow trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A simple tripwire attached to the trigger of a loaded crossbow.  When the "
"tripwire is pulled, the crossbow fires.  Only a single bolt can be used, "
"after which the trap is disabled."
msgstr ""
"Una trampa de cuerda, que tiene la punta atada al gatillo de una ballesta "
"cargada. Cuando se tira de la cuerda, la ballesta se dispara. Solo se puede "
"usar una saeta, y la trampa queda deshabilitada."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "crossbow trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You set the crossbow trap."
msgstr "Pones la trampa de ballesta."

#. ~ Description of "land mine"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A military anti-personnel fragmentation mine that is triggered when stepped "
"on."
msgstr ""
"Una mina militar antipersonal de fragmentación que se activa al ser pisada."

#. ~ "bury_question" action message of item "land mine"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "Bury the land mine?"
msgstr "¿Quieres enterrar la mina?"

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "land mine"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You set the land mine."
msgstr "Pones la mina."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "land mine"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You bury the land mine."
msgstr "Entierras la mina."

#. ~ Description of "shotgun trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A simple tripwire attached to the trigger of a loaded double slam-fire "
"shotgun.  When the tripwire is pulled, the shotgun fires.  Two shells are "
"loaded; the first time the trigger is pulled, one or both shells may be "
"discharged."
msgstr ""
"Un cable trampa que se conecta al gatillo de una escopeta de doble cañón "
"cargada. Cuando se tira de ella, la escopeta se dispara. Tiene dos cartuchos"
" cargados; la primera vez que se aprieta el gatillo, se puede descargar uno "
"o ambos cartuchos."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "shotgun trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You set the shotgun trap."
msgstr "Pones la trampa de escopeta."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "tripwire trap"
msgid_plural "tripwire traps"
msgstr[0] "trampa de cuerda"
msgstr[1] "trampas de cuerda"
msgstr[2] "trampas de cuerda"

#. ~ Description of "tripwire trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A length of thin string with some affixing tools on either end.  It must be "
"placed across a doorway or other thin passage to function.  Its purpose is "
"to trip up trespassers, causing them to stumble and possibly hurt themselves"
" slightly."
msgstr ""
"Una cuerda fina y resistente con algunas herramientas de fijación en ambos "
"extremos. Debe colocarse a través de una puerta u otro pasaje estrecho. Su "
"objetivo es hacer tropezar a los intrusos, haciéndoles tambalear y "
"posiblemente herirse ligeramente."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "tripwire trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You string up the tripwire."
msgstr "Le colocas las sogas a la trampa de cuerdas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/unfoldable.json
msgid "folded Bicycle"
msgid_plural "folded Bicycles"
msgstr[0] "Bicicleta plegada"
msgstr[1] "Bicicletas plegadas"
msgstr[2] "Bicicletas plegadas"

#. ~ Description of "folded Bicycle"
#: data/json/items/tool/unfoldable.json
msgid "A folded Bicycle."
msgstr "Una Bicicleta plegada."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/unfoldable.json
msgid "folded wheelchair"
msgid_plural "folded wheelchairs"
msgstr[0] "silla de rueda plegable"
msgstr[1] "sillas de ruedas plegables"
msgstr[2] "sillas de ruedas plegables"

#. ~ Description of "folded wheelchair"
#: data/json/items/tool/unfoldable.json
msgid "A folded Wheelchair."
msgstr "Una Silla de ruedas plegada."

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Vehicle name
#: data/json/items/tool/unfoldable.json data/json/vehicles/boats.json
msgid "inflatable boat"
msgid_plural "inflatable boats"
msgstr[0] "bote inflable"
msgstr[1] "botes inflables"
msgstr[2] "botes inflables"

#. ~ Description of "inflatable boat"
#: data/json/items/tool/unfoldable.json
msgid ""
"This rubber rowboat (with oars included) is deflated for storage.  Activate "
"it with an air pump in your inventory to inflate and launch it."
msgstr ""
"Este bote de goma (con remos incluidos) está desinflado para ser más fácil "
"de guardar. Activar para inflarlo, si tienes una bomba de aire o inflador en"
" el inventario, y lanzarlo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/unfoldable.json
msgid "skateboard"
msgid_plural "skateboards"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "skateboard"
#: data/json/items/tool/unfoldable.json
msgid "A Skateboard."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "wood axe"
msgid_plural "wood axes"
msgstr[0] "hacha de madera"
msgstr[1] "hachas de madera"
msgstr[2] "hachas de madera"

#. ~ Description of "wood axe"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A large, two-handed wood axe.  It makes a good melee weapon, but is a bit "
"slow to recover between swings."
msgstr ""
"Un gran hacha de dos manos de leñador. Sirve bastante bien como arma c. a "
"c., pero es un poco lenta entre hachazo y hachazo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "bow saw"
msgid_plural "bow saws"
msgstr[0] "sierra de arco"
msgstr[1] "sierras de arco"
msgstr[2] "sierras de arco"

#. ~ Description of "bow saw"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A saw that is more at home outdoors than inside.  It's used for trimming "
"trees, pruning, and cutting firewood, but may be used for other rough cuts "
"as well."
msgstr ""
"Una sierra de arco se usa más a gusto en el exterior que en el interior. Las"
" sierras de arco se utilizan para recortar árboles, podar y cortar leña, "
"pero también pueden utilizarse para otros cortes toscos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "chainsaw (off)"
msgid_plural "chainsaws (off)"
msgstr[0] "motosierra (off)"
msgstr[1] "motosierras (off)"
msgstr[2] "motosierras (off)"

#. ~ Description of "chainsaw (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A treecutting tool moonlighting as a weapon of opportunity.  If loaded with "
"gas, using this item will turn it on, turning it into a very powerful but "
"unwieldy melee weapon."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta para cortar árboles pero también con la posibilidad de "
"usarse como arma. Si tiene combustible, al usar este objeto se enciende, lo "
"que la convierte en una arma c. a c. muy poderosa pero incómoda."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "chainsaw (on)"
msgid_plural "chainsaws (on)"
msgstr[0] "motosierra (on)"
msgstr[1] "motosierras (on)"
msgstr[2] "motosierras (on)"

#. ~ Description of "chainsaw (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "This chainsaw is on and making a lot of noise.  Use it to turn it off."
msgstr "La motosierra está encendida y hace mucho ruido. Usar para apagar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "polesaw (off)"
msgid_plural "polesaws (off)"
msgstr[0] "sierra de poste (apag.)"
msgstr[1] "sierras de poste (apag.)"
msgstr[2] "sierras de poste (apag.)"

#. ~ Description of "polesaw (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A lumbering tool intended for trimming hedges and tree branches at a "
"distance.  If loaded with gas, using this item will cause it to turn on, "
"making it into an unwieldy polearm."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta de leñador usada para podar setos y ramas de árboles a "
"distancia. Si esta cargada con gas, usar este objeto causara que se "
"encienda, convirtiéndolo en un arma de asta difícil de controlar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "polesaw (on)"
msgid_plural "polesaws (on)"
msgstr[0] "sierra de poste (enc.)"
msgstr[1] "sierras de poste (enc.)"
msgstr[2] "sierras de poste (enc.)"

#. ~ Description of "polesaw (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "This polesaw is on and making a lot of noise.  Use it to turn it off."
msgstr ""
"La sierra de poste está encendida y hace mucho ruido. Usar para apagar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "circular saw (off)"
msgid_plural "circular saws (off)"
msgstr[0] "sierra circular (off)"
msgstr[1] "sierras circulares (off)"
msgstr[2] "sierras circulares (off)"

#. ~ Description of "circular saw (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A lightweight, handheld cordless circular saw.  Spins a circular blade fast "
"enough to cut wood, zombies, or in an emergency, pizza.  The blade, while "
"effective in combat, is hard to hit with due to its small size."
msgstr ""
"Una ligera sierra circular sin cable de mano. Gira una hoja circular lo "
"suficientemente rápido como para cortar madera, zombis, o en una emergencia,"
" pizza. La hoja, aunque es efectiva en el combate, es difícil que impacte "
"por su pequeño tamaño."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "circular saw (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "You turn on the circular saw."
msgstr "Enciendes la sierra circular."

#. ~ Circular saw would be very fast but imprecise butchering tool - alas the
#. qualities are not separate and so speed is sacrificed.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "circular saw (on)"
msgid_plural "circular saws (on)"
msgstr[0] "sierra circular (on)"
msgstr[1] "sierras circulares (on)"
msgstr[2] "sierras circulares (on)"

#. ~ Circular saw would be very fast but imprecise butchering tool - alas the
#. qualities are not separate and so speed is sacrificed.
#. ~ Description of "circular saw (on)"
#. ~ Description of "chainsaw spear (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/inventor/melee.json
msgid ""
"A lightweight, handheld cordless circular saw.  It is currently on and the "
"blade is spinning; use this item to turn it off."
msgstr ""
"Una sierra circular liviana de mano, sin cable. Está encendida y la cuchilla"
" está girando. Usar para apagar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "copper hatchet"
msgid_plural "copper hatchets"
msgstr[0] "hacha de cobre"
msgstr[1] "hachas de cobre"
msgstr[2] "hachas de cobre"

#. ~ Description of "copper hatchet"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A primitive axe made from a small wedge of copper affixed to a short haft."
msgstr ""
"Un primitivo hacha hecho con una pequeña cuña de cobre atada a un mango "
"corto."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "bronze axe"
msgid_plural "bronze axes"
msgstr[0] "hacha de bronce"
msgstr[1] "hachas de bronce"
msgstr[2] "hachas de bronce"

#. ~ Description of "bronze axe"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A socketed bronze axe with a work-hardened edge, tightly bound to the shaft "
"with cords."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "hatchet"
msgid_plural "hatchets"
msgstr[0] "hachuela"
msgstr[1] "hachuelas"
msgstr[2] "hachuelas"

#. ~ Description of "hatchet"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A one-handed hatchet.  Makes a great melee weapon, and is useful both for "
"chopping things and hammering them."
msgstr ""
"Un hacha de una sola mano. Es útil como arma de c. a c., se puede usar para "
"cortar cosas y como martillo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "electric chainsaw (off)"
msgid_plural "electric chainsaws (off)"
msgstr[0] "motosierra eléctrica (off)"
msgstr[1] "motosierras eléctricas (off)"
msgstr[2] "motosierras eléctricas (off)"

#. ~ Description of "electric chainsaw (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A treecutting tool moonlighting as a weapon of opportunity.  If loaded with "
"batteries, using this item will turn it on, turning it into a very powerful "
"but unwieldy melee weapon."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta para cortar árboles pero también con la posibilidad de "
"usarse como arma. Si tiene baterías, al usar este objeto se enciende, lo que"
" la convierte en una arma c. a c. muy poderosa pero incómoda."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "electric chainsaw (on)"
msgid_plural "electric chainsaws (on)"
msgstr[0] "motosierra eléctrica (on)"
msgstr[1] "motosierras eléctricas (on)"
msgstr[2] "motosierras eléctricas (on)"

#. ~ Description of "electric chainsaw (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"This electric chainsaw is on and making a lot of noise.  Use it to turn it "
"off."
msgstr ""
"Esta motosierra eléctrica está encendida y hace mucho ruido. Usar para "
"apagar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "corded electric chainsaw (off)"
msgid_plural "corded electric chainsaws (off)"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "corded electric chainsaw (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A treecutting tool moonlighting as a weapon of opportunity.  It has a short "
"electric cord, which you can connect to the generator or your home grid.  "
"Extension cord not included."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "corded electric chainsaw (on)"
msgid_plural "corded electric chainsaws (on)"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "stone axe head"
msgid_plural "stone axe heads"
msgstr[0] "cabeza de hacha de piedra"
msgstr[1] "cabezas de hacha de piedra"
msgstr[2] "cabezas de hacha de piedra"

#. ~ Description of "stone axe head"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A broad piece of stone with an edge narrow enough to roughly chop wood."
msgstr ""
"Una pieza ancha de piedra con un borde lo suficientemente estrecho como para"
" cortar madera."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "metal axe head"
msgid_plural "metal axe heads"
msgstr[0] "cabeza de hacha de metal"
msgstr[1] "cabezas de hacha de metal"
msgstr[2] "cabezas de hacha de metal"

#. ~ Description of "metal axe head"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A chunk of steel with one edge hammered down to something resembling a "
"cutting edge.  It works passably well, but really can't compare to a proper "
"axe."
msgstr ""
"Un trozo de acero con un borde martillado hasta algo parecido a un borde de "
"corte. Funciona bien como un hacha, pero no se puede comparar con uno de "
"verdad."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "stone adze"
msgid_plural "stone adzes"
msgstr[0] "azuela de piedra"
msgstr[1] "azuelas de piedra"
msgstr[2] "azuelas de piedra"

#. ~ Description of "stone adze"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "A stone adze, a primitive tool for smoothing or scraping wood objects."
msgstr ""
"Una azuela de piedra, una herramientas primitiva para suavizar o raspar "
"objetos de madera."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "stone axe"
msgid_plural "stone axes"
msgstr[0] "hacha de piedra"
msgstr[1] "hachas de piedra"
msgstr[2] "hachas de piedra"

#. ~ Description of "stone axe"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A stone with a narrow edge affixed to a stick.  It can chop wood, but "
"requires much more effort than a modern axe."
msgstr ""
"Una piedra con un borde estrecho fijada a un palo. Puede cortar madera, pero"
" requiere mucho más esfuerzo que un hacha moderna."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "wood saw"
msgid_plural "wood saws"
msgstr[0] "sierra para madera"
msgstr[1] "sierras para madera"
msgstr[2] "sierras para madera"

#. ~ Description of "wood saw"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A thin saw, useful for cutting through wood objects.  Activate it to turn "
"pre-cut logs into planks."
msgstr ""
"Una sierra fina, útil para cortar objetos de madera. Activar para convertir "
"troncos previamente cortados en tablones."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid "stone chisel"
msgid_plural "stone chisels"
msgstr[0] "cincel de piedra"
msgstr[1] "cinceles de piedra"
msgstr[2] "cinceles de piedra"

#. ~ Description of "stone chisel"
#: data/json/items/tool/woodworking.json
msgid ""
"A short, primitive chisel made from hard stone, usually used for primitive "
"woodworking."
msgstr ""
"Un cincel corto primitivo de piedra dura, que suele utilizarse para el "
"trabajo primitivo de la madera."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "pallet of wet adobe bricks"
msgid_plural "pallets of wet adobe bricks"
msgstr[0] "palet de ladrillos de adobe húmedos"
msgstr[1] "palets de ladrillos de adobe húmedos"
msgstr[2] "palets de ladrillos de adobe húmedos"

#. ~ Description of "pallet of wet adobe bricks"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A pallet full of heavy mud bricks which need to dry slowly to be usable."
msgstr ""
"Una palet lleno de pesados ladrillos de barro que necesitan secarse "
"lentamente para ser utilizables."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "pallet of wet adobe bricks"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "You test the bricks, and they're solid enough to use."
msgstr "Pruebe los ladrillos, y son lo suficientemente sólidos para usarlos."

#. ~ "not_ready_msg" action message of item "pallet of wet adobe bricks"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "The bricks are still too damp to bear weight."
msgstr "Los ladrillos están todavía demasiado húmedos para soportar el peso."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "pallet of dry adobe bricks"
msgid_plural "pallets of dry adobe bricks"
msgstr[0] "palet de ladrillos de adobe seco"
msgstr[1] "palets de ladrillos de adobe seco"
msgstr[2] "palets de ladrillos de adobe seco"

#. ~ Description of "pallet of dry adobe bricks"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A pallet of humble mud bricks that have dried for a week while you were out "
"risking your life.  Disassemble it to retrieve your frame and building "
"supplies."
msgstr ""
"Un palet de humildes ladrillos de barro que se han secado durante una "
"semana, mientras estabas fuera arriesgando tu vida. Desmóntalo para "
"recuperar su estructura y los suministros de construcción."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "acetylene-gas machine"
msgid_plural "acetylene-gas machines"
msgstr[0] "máquina de gas de acetileno"
msgstr[1] "máquinas de gas de acetileno"
msgstr[2] "máquinas de gas de acetileno"

#. ~ Description of "acetylene-gas machine"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A bulky device that turns water and calcium carbide into unpressurized "
"acetylene."
msgstr ""
"Un voluminoso dispositivo que toma agua y carburo de calcio para producir "
"acetileno sin presión."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "angle grinder"
msgid_plural "angle grinders"
msgstr[0] "amoladora angular"
msgstr[1] "amoladoras angulares"
msgstr[2] "amoladoras angulares"

#. ~ Description of "angle grinder"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A widespread power tool, often used for removing excess material or "
"polishing surfaces."
msgstr ""
"Esta potente y común herramienta se utiliza a menudo para eliminar el exceso"
" de material o pulir las superficies."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "cutoff disc"
msgid_plural "cutoff discs"
msgstr[0] "disco de corte"
msgstr[1] "discos de corte"
msgstr[2] "discos de corte"

#. ~ Description of "cutoff disc"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A manufactured disc for an angle grinder, with a thin, abrasive edge "
"designed for cutting metal."
msgstr ""
"Un disco fabricado para una amoladora angular, con un borde abrasivo fino "
"diseñado para cortar metal."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "metal grinding disc"
msgid_plural "metal grinding discs"
msgstr[0] "disco de lijado de metal"
msgstr[1] "discos de lijado de metal"
msgstr[2] "discos de lijado de metal"

#. ~ Description of "metal grinding disc"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A manufactured disc for an angle grinder, with a thick, abrasive surface "
"designed for grinding and shaping metal."
msgstr ""
"Un disco fabricado para una amoladora angular, con una gruesa superficie "
"abrasiva gruesa diseñada para esmerilar y dar forma al metal."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "brick kiln"
msgid_plural "brick kilns"
msgstr[0] "horno de ladrillos"
msgstr[1] "hornos de ladrillos"
msgstr[2] "hornos de ladrillos"

#. ~ Description of "brick kiln"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A portable coal-or-charcoal-fired kiln.  It is designed for firing bricks, "
"but you could use it to fire anything made of clay."
msgstr ""
"Un horno de ladrillos portátil que funciona con carbón vegetal. Está "
"diseñado para cocinar ladrillos, pero lo puedes usar para cocinar cualquier "
"cosa hecha de arcilla."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "carding paddles"
msgid_plural "pairs of carding paddles"
msgstr[0] "cardadoras de mano"
msgstr[1] "pares de cardadoras de mano"
msgstr[2] "pares de cardadoras de mano"

#. ~ Description of "carding paddles"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A pair of toothy wooden paddles used to clean fibers for use in textile "
"production."
msgstr ""
"Un par de paletas de madera dentadas que se usan para limpiar las fibras "
"para poder usarlas en la producción textil."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "makeshift vacuum mold"
msgid_plural "makeshift vacuum molds"
msgstr[0] "molde de vacio improvisado"
msgstr[1] "moldes de vacio improvisados"
msgstr[2] "moldes de vacio improvisados"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift vacuum mold"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A homemade vacuum-forming machine with an air pump.  It's used for creating "
"plastic molds."
msgstr ""
"Una máquina casera de formación de vacío con una bomba de aire. Se utiliza "
"para crear moldes de plástico."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "vacuum molder"
msgid_plural "vacuum molders"
msgstr[0] "moldeador de vacio"
msgstr[1] "moldeadores de vacio"
msgstr[2] "moldeadores de vacio"

#. ~ Description of "vacuum molder"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A vacuum-forming machine with an air pump.  It's used for creating plastic "
"molds."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "paint chipper"
msgid_plural "paint chippers"
msgstr[0] "espátula"
msgstr[1] "espátulas"
msgstr[2] "espátulas"

#. ~ Description of "paint chipper"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "A tool similar to a chisel, designed to remove paint."
msgstr "Una herramienta similar a un cincel, diseñado para sacar la pintura."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "clamp"
msgid_plural "clamps"
msgstr[0] "abrazadera"
msgstr[1] "abrazaderas"
msgstr[2] "abrazaderas"

#. ~ Description of "clamp"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A metal clamp, useful for holding things in place, especially if you have "
"several of them."
msgstr ""
"Una abrazadera útil para mantener las cosas en su sitio, especialmente si "
"tienes varias."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "claw bar"
msgid_plural "claw bars"
msgstr[0] "pata de cabra"
msgstr[1] "patas de cabra"
msgstr[2] "patas de cabra"

#. ~ Description of "claw bar"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A small prying tool with a clawed bend at one end for pulling spikes.  Use "
"it to open locked doors without destroying them or to lift manhole covers.  "
"You could also wield it to bash some heads in."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña herramienta con una curva de garra en un extremo para tirar de "
"los clavos. Se usa para abrir puertas cerradas sin destruirlas o para "
"levantar tapas de alcantarilla. También puedes usarla como arma contundente "
"para golpear algunas cabezas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "concrete mixer"
msgid_plural "concrete mixers"
msgstr[0] "hormigonera"
msgstr[1] "hormigoneras"
msgstr[2] "hormigoneras"

#. ~ Description of "concrete mixer"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A portable concrete mixer.  It is still large and heavy, but it can be "
"operated solo, and runs on batteries.  It also has a heater built in."
msgstr ""
"Una mezcladora portátil de hormigón. Igual, es grande y pesada, pero puede "
"ser operada por una sola persona, y anda con baterías. También tiene un "
"calentador incorporado."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "cordless drill"
msgid_plural "cordless drills"
msgstr[0] "taladro inalámbrico"
msgstr[1] "taladros inalámbricos"
msgstr[2] "taladros inalámbricos"

#. ~ Description of "cordless drill"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "A cordless battery-powered drill with a selection of drill bits."
msgstr ""
"Un taladro sin cable, alimentado con baterías, con una variedad de puntas "
"para el taladro."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "power drill"
msgid_plural "power drills"
msgstr[0] "taladro eléctrico"
msgstr[1] "taladros eléctricos"
msgstr[2] "taladros eléctricos"

#. ~ Description of "power drill"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A black power drill with a selection of bits.  Uses a power cord, so it will"
" have to be plugged into a power grid or vehicle to function."
msgstr ""
"Un taladro eléctrico negro con un conjunto de puntas. Funciona con cable, "
"por lo que tendrá que ser conectado a una red eléctrica o un vehículo para "
"funcionar."

#. ~ Loosely based on DeWalt DCF899B 20V 1/2-inch cordless impact wrench, $220
#. on Amazon, 6.4 pounds.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "cordless impact wrench"
msgid_plural "cordless impact wrenches"
msgstr[0] "llave de impacto sin cables"
msgstr[1] "llaves de impacto sin cables"
msgstr[2] "llaves de impacto sin cables"

#. ~ Loosely based on DeWalt DCF899B 20V 1/2-inch cordless impact wrench, $220
#. on Amazon, 6.4 pounds.
#. ~ Description of "cordless impact wrench"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A cordless battery-powered impact wrench, designed to deliver high torque "
"via an internal rotating hammer.  It comes with a standard set of sockets, "
"and makes a loud ratcheting sound when it operates.  You could use it to "
"turn large bolts or change a vehicle wheel."
msgstr ""
"Una llave de impacto con batería inalámbrica, diseñada para proporcionar un "
"alto par de torsión a través de un martillo giratorio interno. Viene con un "
"juego de llaves estándar y emite un fuerte sonido de trinquete cuando "
"funciona. Puedes utilizarla para girar tornillos grandes, o incluso para "
"cambiar una rueda de un vehículo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "distaff and spindle"
msgid_plural "distaves and spindles"
msgstr[0] "huso y aspa"
msgstr[1] "husos y aspas"
msgstr[2] "husos y aspas"

#. ~ Description of "distaff and spindle"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A pair of specialized wooden rods used to spin fibers into thread and yarn."
msgstr ""
"Es un par de palos de madera especializados para hacer hilos y ovillos "
"hilando fibra."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "electric jackhammer"
msgid_plural "electric jackhammers"
msgstr[0] "martillo neumático eléctrico"
msgstr[1] "martillos neumáticos eléctricos"
msgstr[2] "martillos neumáticos eléctricos"

#. ~ Description of "electric jackhammer"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A construction tool for drilling through hard rock or other surfaces.  It "
"runs on a cell compatible with a UPS.  Use it to blast a hole in adjacent "
"solid terrain."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta de construcción para perforar a través de roca dura u otras "
"superficies. Funciona con una célula compatible con UPS. Se usa para hacer "
"un agujero en un terreno sólido adyacente."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "hacksaw"
msgid_plural "hacksaws"
msgstr[0] "sierra para metales"
msgstr[1] "sierras para metales"
msgstr[2] "sierras para metales"

#. ~ Description of "hacksaw"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "A sturdy saw, useful for cutting through metal objects."
msgstr "Una sierra resistente, útil para cortar objetos de metal."

#. ~ Based on https://www.amazon.com/dp/B00009OYFY
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "tin snips"
msgid_plural "tin snips"
msgstr[0] "tijera de hojalata"
msgstr[1] "tijeras de hojalata"
msgstr[2] "tijeras de hojalata"

#. ~ Based on https://www.amazon.com/dp/B00009OYFY
#. ~ Description of "tin snips"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A pair of tin snips, resembling a sturdy pair of scissors with beefy blades "
"designed to cut through thin sheets of soft metal.  These cannot cut through"
" thick metals like a hacksaw can, but are better suited to precision work "
"and leave a cleaner edge."
msgstr ""
"Un par de tijeras de hojalatero que se asemejan a un par de tijeras robustas"
" con hojas diseñadas para cortar láminas finas de metal blando. No pueden "
"cortar metales gruesos como una sierra para metales, pero son más adecuadas "
"para trabajos de precisión y dejan un borde más limpio."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "hammer"
msgid_plural "hammers"
msgstr[0] "martillo"
msgstr[1] "martillos"
msgstr[2] "martillos"

#. ~ Description of "hammer"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A demagnetized steel claw hammer with a wooden grip.  With a hammer, nails, "
"and planks in your inventory, you could board up adjacent doors and windows."
"  It has myriad other uses as well."
msgstr ""
"Un martillo de garra de acero desmagnetizado con empuñadura de madera. Con "
"un martillo, clavos y tablones en tu inventario, podrías tapiar puertas y "
"ventanas adyacentes. También tiene muchos otros usos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "bronze hammer"
msgid_plural "bronze hammers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "bronze hammer"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A simple crude bronze hammer.  It is not as sophisticated or useful as its "
"steel alternative but it does get the job of hammering in nails well enough."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "bronze nail puller"
msgid_plural "bronze nail pullers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "bronze nail puller"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A crude nail puller made of bronze.  Not really as good as its steel "
"alternative but it gets job of pulling out nails good enough."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "bronze wood saw"
msgid_plural "bronze wood saws"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "bronze wood saw"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A simple wood saw made of bronze.  Not as great as its steel equivalent, but"
" it's good enough."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "hand drill"
msgid_plural "hand drills"
msgstr[0] "taladro manual"
msgstr[1] "taladros manuales"
msgstr[2] "taladros manuales"

#. ~ Description of "hand drill"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A primitive manual drill with a single drill bit.  It is slow to use, and "
"will exhaust you quickly."
msgstr ""
"Un primitivo taladro manual con una sola mecha. Es lenta y agotadora de "
"utilizar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "rubber hose"
msgid_plural "rubber hoses"
msgstr[0] "manguera de goma"
msgstr[1] "mangueras de goma"
msgstr[2] "mangueras de goma"

#. ~ Description of "rubber hose"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A flexible rubber hose.  It could be used for crafting or siphoning fuel "
"from a vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Una manguera de goma flexible. Puede ser usada para fabricar alguna cosa, o "
"para transvasar la gasolina a un vehículo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "bottle jack"
msgid_plural "bottle jacks"
msgstr[0] "gato hidráulico de botella"
msgstr[1] "gatos hidráulicos de botella"
msgstr[2] "gatos hidráulicos de botella"

#. ~ Description of "bottle jack"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "A portable hydraulic bottle jack used for lifting vehicles."
msgstr ""
"Es un gato hidráulico portátil de tipo botella usado para levantar "
"vehículos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "makeshift jack"
msgid_plural "makeshift jacks"
msgstr[0] "gato hidráulico improvisado"
msgstr[1] "gatos hidráulicos improvisados"
msgstr[2] "gatos hidráulicos improvisados"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift jack"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A poorly-constructed improvised scissor jack used for lifting vehicles if "
"you're brave enough to use it."
msgstr ""
"Un gato hidráulico improvisado de tipo tijera, bastante mal construido, "
"capaz de levantar vehículos si eres tan valiente como para usarlo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "scissor jack"
msgid_plural "scissor jacks"
msgstr[0] "gato hidráulico de tipo tijera"
msgstr[1] "gatos hidráulicos de tipo tijera"
msgstr[2] "gatos hidráulicos de tipo tijera"

#. ~ Description of "scissor jack"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "A compact scissor jack used for lifting vehicles."
msgstr ""
"Es un gato hidráulico compacto de tipo tijera, usado para levantar "
"vehículos."

#. ~ Consumes 0.6 L/h
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "jackhammer"
msgid_plural "jackhammers"
msgstr[0] "martillo neumático"
msgstr[1] "martillos neumáticos"
msgstr[2] "martillos neumáticos"

#. ~ Consumes 0.6 L/h
#. ~ Description of "jackhammer"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A construction tool for drilling through hard rock or other surfaces.  It "
"runs on gasoline.  Use it (if loaded) to blast a hole in adjacent solid "
"terrain."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta de construcción que se usa para agujerear roca sólida u "
"otras superficies. Utiliza gasolina. Úsalo para hacer un agujero en terreno "
"adyacente (si tiene gasolina)."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "electric kiln"
msgid_plural "electric kilns"
msgstr[0] "horno eléctrico"
msgstr[1] "hornos eléctricos"
msgstr[2] "hornos eléctricos"

#. ~ Description of "electric kiln"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"An electric kiln, powered by your electric grid.  It is designed for firing "
"bricks, but you could use it to fire anything made of clay.  With a little "
"mechanical know-how, you could probably even convert it to run directly off "
"a vehicle's power system."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "gunsmith repair kit"
msgid_plural "gunsmith repair kits"
msgstr[0] "equipo armero de reparación"
msgstr[1] "equipos armeros de reparación"
msgstr[2] "equipos armeros de reparación"

#. ~ Description of "gunsmith repair kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A complete tool kit made to repair damaged firearms.  Powered by standard "
"batteries, it is a vital tool for long-term firearms maintenance.  It "
"requires 1 charge of battery power per use."
msgstr ""
"Un equipo completo de herramientas hecho para reparar armas de fuego "
"dañadas. Alimentado con baterías normales, es una herramienta vital para el "
"mantenimiento a largo plazo de las armas de fuego. Necesita 1 carga de "
"batería cada vez que se usa."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "makeshift hammer"
msgid_plural "makeshift hammers"
msgstr[0] "martillo improvisado"
msgstr[1] "martillos improvisados"
msgstr[2] "martillos improvisados"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift hammer"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A crude hammer made from a piece of metal affixed to a stick.  It functions "
"adequately, but really can't compare to a proper hammer."
msgstr ""
"Un martillo crudo hecho de una pieza de metal pegado a un palo. Funciona "
"adecuadamente como martillo, pero realmente no se puede comparar con uno "
"apropiado."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "bronze fileset"
msgid_plural "bronze filesets"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "metal fileset"
msgid_plural "metal filesets"
msgstr[0] "lima metálica"
msgstr[1] "limas metálicas"
msgstr[2] "limas metálicas"

#. ~ Description of "metal fileset"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A set of tools commonly used to remove small amounts of material from the "
"surface of metal objects."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de herramientas que se usan comúnmente para limar pequeñas "
"cantidades de material de la superficie de objetos metálicos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "metallic smoother"
msgid_plural "metallic smoothers"
msgstr[0] "llana de metal"
msgstr[1] "llanas de metal"
msgstr[2] "llanas de metal"

#. ~ Description of "metallic smoother"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A tool that is most often used to smooth concrete or mortar in construction "
"projects."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta metálica utilizada comúnmente para alisar el hormigón o el "
"mortero en las obras."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "miscellaneous repair kit"
msgid_plural "miscellaneous repair kits"
msgstr[0] "equipo de reparación misceláneo"
msgstr[1] "equipos de reparación misceláneos"
msgstr[2] "equipos de reparación misceláneos"

#. ~ Description of "miscellaneous repair kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A portable tool kit consisting of a small craft knife for precise carving of"
" replacement parts from raw materials, a wood saw for more heavy-duty wood "
"cutting, and a patch of soft material for cleaning surfaces.  If supplied "
"with duct tape, it can be used to repair certain items."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de herramientas portátil, que consiste en un pequeño cuchillo de"
" trinchar para tallar con precisión las piezas de recambio de las materias "
"primas, una sierra para madera para cortar madera más resistente y un parche"
" de material blando para limpiar las superficies. Si se suministra con cinta"
" americana, se puede usar para reparar ciertos artículos."

#. ~ The multitool is a bit more of a toolkit than a knife.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "multitool"
msgid_plural "multitools"
msgstr[0] "multiherramienta"
msgstr[1] "multiherramientas"
msgstr[2] "multiherramientas"

#. ~ The multitool is a bit more of a toolkit than a knife.
#. ~ Description of "multitool"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A cleverly designed all-in-one tool which combines several smaller tools "
"into the handles of a pair of pliers."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta multifunción ingeniosamente diseñada, que combina varias "
"herramientas pequeñas en los mangos del par de pinzas."

#. ~ power usage: acy torch delivers about 20 kj per gram adjusted for
#. efficiency, needs about 800 degrees c to ignite steel, which is specific
#. heat 420j so to ignite a kg of steel, it is about 16units of acetylene
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "acetylene torch"
msgid_plural "acetylene torches"
msgstr[0] "soplete de acetileno"
msgstr[1] "sopletes de acetileno"
msgstr[2] "sopletes de acetileno"

#. ~ power usage: acy torch delivers about 20 kj per gram adjusted for
#. efficiency, needs about 800 degrees c to ignite steel, which is specific
#. heat 420j so to ignite a kg of steel, it is about 16units of acetylene
#. ~ Description of "acetylene torch"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A compact tool kit intended for welding and cutting metal, this portable "
"oxygen-acetylene torch includes a torch handle and cutting attachment in an "
"easy-to-carry tote.  It needs to be connected to a pressurized cylinder of "
"an appropriate welding gas before use.  In addition to its metalworking "
"uses, you can activate it in order to destroy metal barriers."
msgstr ""
"Un equipo de herramientas compacto diseñado para la soldadura y corte de "
"metal, este soplete de acetileno portátil incluye un mango del soplete y el "
"accesorio de corte en una bolsa fácil de llevar. Requiere conexión a "
"cilindros a presión de un gas de soldadura apropiado antes de ser usado. "
"Además de usarse para metalurgia, se puede activar para destruir las "
"barreras metálicas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "paint brush"
msgid_plural "paint brushes"
msgstr[0] "brocha"
msgstr[1] "brochas"
msgstr[2] "brochas"

#. ~ Description of "paint brush"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "A wide brush, suitable for painting walls."
msgstr "Un pincel ancho, adecuado para pintar muros."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "pickaxe"
msgid_plural "pickaxes"
msgstr[0] "pico"
msgstr[1] "picos"
msgstr[2] "picos"

#. ~ Description of "pickaxe"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A large steel pickaxe, suitable for breaking up hard things or (with enough "
"skill) hard targets.  Strike the earth!"
msgstr ""
"Un pico grande de acero, útil para romper cosas duras o (con suficiente "
"habilidad) enemigos duros. ¡Pica la tierra!"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "bronze pickaxe"
msgid_plural "bronze pickaxes"
msgstr[0] "pico de bronce"
msgstr[1] "picos de bronce"
msgstr[2] "picos de bronce"

#. ~ Description of "bronze pickaxe"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A heavy-headed cast and worked tool with a pointed wedge on one side for "
"breaking stone and a flat wedge on the other for prying it out.  You could "
"mine with this."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta resistente con cabeza de fundición, con una punta en un lado"
" para romper piedra y un borde plano en el otro lado para hacer palanca.  "
"Con esta herramienta puedes hacer minería."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "pin reamer"
msgid_plural "pin reamers"
msgstr[0] "escariador de pin"
msgstr[1] "escariadores de pin"
msgstr[2] "escariadores de pin"

#. ~ Description of "pin reamer"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"Handheld pin reamers of this kind are used to enlarge existing holes, or "
"remove any burs and such from them."
msgstr ""
"Los escariadores manuales de este tipo se utilizan para agrandar los "
"agujeros existentes, o para quitar cualquier broca y tal de ellos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "pliers"
msgid_plural "pliers"
msgstr[0] "tenaza"
msgstr[1] "tenazas"
msgstr[2] "tenazas"

#. ~ Description of "pliers"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A basic pair of slip-joint pliers, able to handle basic mechanical work.  "
"Anything more complex will require a wrench."
msgstr ""
"Un par de alicates comunes con junta deslizante, útil para usar en trabajos "
"mecánicos básicos. Para otras cosas más complejas vas a necesitar una llave "
"inglesa. "

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "tongue-and-groove pliers"
msgid_plural "tongue-and-groove pliers"
msgstr[0] "alicates pico de loro"
msgstr[1] "alicates pico de loro"
msgstr[2] "alicates pico de loro"

#. ~ Description of "tongue-and-groove pliers"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A large pair of slip-joint pliers bent at the elbow, able to handle basic "
"mechanical work.  Anything more complex will require a wrench."
msgstr ""
"Un gran par de alicates con junta deslizante doblados en el codo, capaces de"
" realizar trabajos mecánicos básicos. Cualquier cosa demasiado compleja "
"requerirá una llave inglesa."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "locking pliers"
msgid_plural "locking pliers"
msgstr[0] "pinza de presión"
msgstr[1] "pinzas de presión"
msgstr[2] "pinzas de presión"

#. ~ Description of "locking pliers"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A pair of pliers with extra-hefty jaws and an adjustable mechanism to clamp "
"them in a locked grip on whatever unfortunate object is trapped between "
"them.  They could grip and turn a fairly large bolt head, or clamp two parts"
" together temporarily."
msgstr ""
"Un par de alicates con mandíbulas extra fuertes y un mecanismo ajustable "
"para sujetar cualquier objeto desafortunado que quede atrapado entre ellas. "
"Pueden agarrar y girar la cabeza de un tornillo bastante grande, o sujetar "
"dos piezas juntas temporalmente."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "electric polisher"
msgid_plural "electric polishers"
msgstr[0] "pulidor eléctrico"
msgstr[1] "pulidores eléctricos"
msgstr[2] "pulidores eléctricos"

#. ~ Description of "electric polisher"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"An electric polisher, used to buff metal surfaces until they are reflective "
"like a mirror."
msgstr ""
"Un pulidor eléctrico que se utiliza para mejorar superficies de metal y "
"hacerlas tan reflectantes como un espejo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "stone hammer"
msgid_plural "stone hammers"
msgstr[0] "martillo de piedra"
msgstr[1] "martillos de piedra"
msgstr[2] "martillos de piedra"

#. ~ Description of "stone hammer"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A rock affixed to a stick in the crude facsimile of a hammer.  It functions "
"adequately, but really can't compare to a proper hammer, and can't pull out "
"nails either."
msgstr ""
"Una piedra fijada a un palo, es el burdo facsímil de un martillo. Funciona "
"adecuadamente como martillo, pero realmente no se puede comparar con uno "
"adecuado, y tampoco puede sacar clavos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "reciprocating saw"
msgid_plural "reciprocating saws"
msgstr[0] "sierra reciprocante"
msgstr[1] "sierras reciprocantes"
msgstr[2] "sierras reciprocantes"

#. ~ Description of "reciprocating saw"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A battery-powered tool, commonly known by the generic trademark Sawzall, "
"that uses an electric motor to push a straight sawblade back and forth to "
"rapidly cut wood or metal.  It is useful for heavy demolition and "
"construction work, but poorly suited to precision tasks."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta con batería, conocida comúnmente por la marca genérica "
"Sawzall, utiliza un motor eléctrico para empujar una hoja de sierra recta "
"hacia adelante y hacia atrás para cortar rápidamente madera o metal. Es útil"
" para trabajos pesados de demolición y construcción, pero es poco adecuada "
"para tareas de precisión."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "Hub 01 HWP maintenance kit"
msgid_plural "Hub 01 HWP maintenance kits"
msgstr[0] "equipo de mantenimiento Hub 01 HWP"
msgstr[1] "equipos de mantenimiento Hub 01 HWP"
msgstr[2] "equipos de mantenimiento Hub 01 HWP"

#. ~ Description of "Hub 01 HWP maintenance kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A heavy-duty bag marked with the Hub 01 logo.  It contains space for "
"barrels, adapters, and proprietary tools.  Embossed on the inside is a "
"sketch of the Hybrid Weapons Platform."
msgstr ""
"Una bolsa reforzada marcada con el logo del Hub 01. Tiene sitio para "
"tanques, adaptadores y herramientas propietarias. Dentro tiene grabado el "
"boceto de la Plataforma de Armas Híbrida."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "screwdriver"
msgid_plural "screwdrivers"
msgstr[0] "destornillador"
msgstr[1] "destornilladores"
msgstr[2] "destornilladores"

#. ~ Description of "screwdriver"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A Philips-head screwdriver.  It is important for almost all electronics "
"crafting, most mechanics crafting, and has many more uses."
msgstr ""
"Es un destornillador con cabeza cruciforme Philips. Es una herramienta "
"importante para casi todas las fabricaciones electrónicas, la mayoría de las"
" mecánicas, aparte de muchos otros usos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "screwdriver set"
msgid_plural "screwdriver sets"
msgstr[0] "juego de destornilladores"
msgstr[1] "juegos de destornilladores"
msgstr[2] "juegos de destornilladores"

#. ~ Description of "screwdriver set"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A set of screwdrivers in several sizes and blade types.  Guaranteed to have "
"the right tools for more precise work."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de destornilladores de varios tamaños y tipos de punta. Te "
"garantiza tener la herramienta adecuada para un trabajo preciso."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "socket screwdriver set"
msgid_plural "socket screwdriver sets"
msgstr[0] "juego de destornilladores de vaso"
msgstr[1] "juegos de destornilladores de vaso"
msgstr[2] "juegos de destornilladores de vaso"

#. ~ Description of "socket screwdriver set"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A ratcheting screwdriver with a collection of hex sockets for turning small "
"bolts or nuts, including a couple standard screwdriver bits."
msgstr ""
"Un destornillador de carraca con una colección de casquillos hexagonales "
"para girar pequeños tornillos o tuercas, incluyendo un par de puntas de "
"destornillador estándar."

#. ~ Modeled after 40-piece Walmart set, 2.85 lb, case 9.75 x 1.5 x 5 inches
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "socket wrench set"
msgid_plural "socket wrench sets"
msgstr[0] "juego de llaves de vaso"
msgstr[1] "juegos de llaves de vaso"
msgstr[2] "juegos de llaves de vaso"

#. ~ Modeled after 40-piece Walmart set, 2.85 lb, case 9.75 x 1.5 x 5 inches
#. ~ Description of "socket wrench set"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A thick-handled ratchet wrench with an assortment of interchangeable sockets"
" in common hex bolt sizes.  You could loosen or tighten fairly large bolts "
"with this, and the ratchet makes a satisfying clicking sound."
msgstr ""
"Una llave de carraca de mango grueso con un surtido de casquillos "
"intercambiables en tamaños de pernos hexagonales comunes. Puedes aflojar o "
"apretar pernos bastante grandes con esto, y el trinquete hace un sonido de "
"clic satisfactorio."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "firearm repair kit"
msgid_plural "firearm repair kits"
msgstr[0] "equipo de reparación de armas"
msgstr[1] "equipos de reparación de armas"
msgstr[2] "equipos de reparación de armas"

#. ~ Description of "firearm repair kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A portable tool kit made to repair damaged firearms.  Powered by standard "
"batteries, it is a vital tool for long-term firearms maintenance.  It "
"requires one charge of battery power per use."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "soldering iron"
msgid_plural "soldering irons"
msgstr[0] "soldadora de mano"
msgstr[1] "soldadoras de mano"
msgstr[2] "soldadoras de mano"

#. ~ Description of "soldering iron"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A device with a metal tip that can get very hot.  It is necessary for "
"advanced electronics crafting.  Has a short cable that you can plug to your "
"grid."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "portable soldering iron"
msgid_plural "portable soldering irons"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "portable soldering iron"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A device with a metal tip that can get very hot.  It is necessary for "
"advanced electronics crafting.  This one is a portable version, and contains"
" a slot for a battery."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Based on https://www.amazon.com/dp/B06XPWS3HJ
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "lug wrench"
msgid_plural "lug wrenches"
msgstr[0] "llave de tuerca"
msgstr[1] "llaves de tuerca"
msgstr[2] "llaves de tuerca"

#. ~ Based on https://www.amazon.com/dp/B06XPWS3HJ
#. ~ Description of "lug wrench"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A steel rod bent 90 degrees with a socket on the shorter end, made to hold "
"the lug nuts of a car's wheels to either fasten or loosen for convenient "
"removal and replacement.  Makes for a decent melee weapon in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Una varilla de acero doblada a 90 grados con un casquillo en el extremo más "
"corto, hecha para sujetar las tuercas de las ruedas de un coche para "
"sujetarlas o aflojarlas para su conveniente retirada y sustitución. Es un "
"arma de combate c. a c. decente en caso de necesidad."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "toolbox"
msgid_plural "toolboxes"
msgstr[0] "caja de herramientas"
msgstr[1] "cajas de herramientas"
msgstr[2] "cajas de herramientas"

#. ~ Description of "toolbox"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A stout metal box for holding tools.  It has a handle on the top and a latch"
" on the front."
msgstr ""
"Una resistente caja metálica para contener herramientas. Tiene un asa en la "
"parte superior y un pestillo en la parte delantera."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "workshop toolbox"
msgid_plural "workshop toolboxes"
msgstr[0] "caja de herramientas para el taller"
msgstr[1] "cajas de herramientas para el taller"
msgstr[2] "cajas de herramientas para el taller"

#. ~ Description of "workshop toolbox"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A stout metal box for holding tools.  It is much bigger than a regular "
"toolbox, and can be used to store more tools as a result."
msgstr ""
"Una resistente caja metálica para contener herramientas. Es mucho más grande"
" que una caja de herramientas normal y podría utilizarse para guardar más "
"herramientas de lo habitual."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "arc welder"
msgid_plural "arc welders"
msgstr[0] "soldador de arco"
msgstr[1] "soldadores de arco"
msgstr[2] "soldadores de arco"

#. ~ Description of "arc welder"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A cable-powered tool for welding metal pieces together using an electric "
"arc.  It is an indispensable tool for construction or repair."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "makeshift arc welder"
msgid_plural "makeshift arc welders"
msgstr[0] "soldador de arco improvisado"
msgstr[1] "soldadores de arco improvisados"
msgstr[2] "soldadores de arco improvisados"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift arc welder"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A crude arc welder fashioned from a few small transformers, some wire, an "
"improvised electrode holder, and a complete disregard for personal safety.  "
"While it's not as efficient as a factory-made welder, it will serve in a "
"pinch."
msgstr ""
"Un soldador de arco crudo diseñado a partir de unos pocos transformadores "
"pequeños, algunos cables, un portaelectrodos improvisado y un total "
"desprecio por la seguridad personal. Si bien no es tan eficiente como un "
"soldador de fábrica, servirá en caso de necesidad."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "high-temperature welding kit"
msgid_plural "high-temperature welding kits"
msgstr[0] "equipo de soldadura de altas temperaturas"
msgstr[1] "equipos de soldadura de altas temperaturas"
msgstr[2] "equipos de soldadura de altas temperaturas"

#. ~ Description of "high-temperature welding kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A welder combined with a fireproof insulating blanket allows for advanced "
"welds and repairs to tempered steels."
msgstr ""
"Un soldador combinado con una manta aislante ignífuga que permite hacer "
"soldaduras avanzadas y reparaciones en aceros templados."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "wooden smoother"
msgid_plural "wooden smoothers"
msgstr[0] "llana de madera"
msgstr[1] "llanas de madera"
msgstr[2] "llanas de madera"

#. ~ Description of "wooden smoother"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A large makeshift tool used in smoothing concrete or mortar in construction "
"projects.  You could also use it as an improvised head-basher."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta improvisada usada para alisar el hormigón o el mortero en "
"las obras. También lo puedes usar para reventar algunas cabezas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "wool staple"
msgid_plural "wool staples"
msgstr[0] "fibra de lana"
msgstr[1] "fibras de lana"
msgstr[2] "fibras de lana"

#. ~ Description of "wool staple"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A natural cluster of wool fibers.  Could be processed into felt patches or "
"yarn."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto natural de fibras de lana. Puede ser procesado para hacer trozos"
" de fieltro o hilos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "X-Acto knife"
msgid_plural "X-Acto knives"
msgstr[0] "navaja de precisión"
msgstr[1] "navajas de precisión"
msgstr[2] "navajas de precisión"

#. ~ Description of "X-Acto knife"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A small, sharp knife, designed for making precise cuts for textiles or "
"crafts.  It could cause decent damage, but is difficult to land a solid hit "
"with.  Its small, sharp blade allows for precision strikes in the hands of "
"the skilled."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo pequeño y afilado, diseñado para hacer cortes precisos "
"trabajando con telas o en alguna fabricación. Puede causar un daño decente, "
"pero es difícil acertarle a las cosas con esto. Su pequeña hoja afilada "
"permite golpes precisos en las manos de alguien hábil."

#. ~ Measured weight of 6-inch Craftsman wrench with 150mm jaws, assume 8g/ml
#. steel density plus some margin for mechanism and empty space.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "small adjustable wrench"
msgid_plural "small adjustable wrenches"
msgstr[0] "llave inglesa pequeña"
msgstr[1] "llaves inglesas pequeñas"
msgstr[2] "llaves inglesas pequeñas"

#. ~ Measured weight of 6-inch Craftsman wrench with 150mm jaws, assume 8g/ml
#. steel density plus some margin for mechanism and empty space.
#. ~ Description of "small adjustable wrench"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A compact adjustable crescent wrench, with a short handle that fits in the "
"palm of your hand.  It could be used for turning small hex-head nuts or "
"bolts."
msgstr ""
"Una llave inglesa ajustable compacta, con un mango corto que cabe en la "
"palma de la mano. Puede utilizarse para girar tuercas o tornillos pequeños "
"de cabeza hexagonal."

#. ~ Based on: https://www.amazon.com/Crescent-AC210VS-Tools-Wrenches-
#. Adjustable/dp/B00002N5L1/ref=sr_1_5?crid=2979KVN9DXDUH&keywords=10+inch+crescent+wrench+adjustable&qid=1680859779&sprefix=10+inch+crescent+wrench+adjustable%2Caps%2C555&sr=8-5
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "adjustable wrench"
msgid_plural "adjustable wrenches"
msgstr[0] "llaves inglesa"
msgstr[1] "llaves inglesas"
msgstr[2] "llaves inglesas"

#. ~ Based on: https://www.amazon.com/Crescent-AC210VS-Tools-Wrenches-
#. Adjustable/dp/B00002N5L1/ref=sr_1_5?crid=2979KVN9DXDUH&keywords=10+inch+crescent+wrench+adjustable&qid=1680859779&sprefix=10+inch+crescent+wrench+adjustable%2Caps%2C555&sr=8-5
#. ~ Description of "adjustable wrench"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"An adjustable crescent wrench.  It is used in many mechanics crafting "
"recipes."
msgstr ""
"Una llave inglesa ajustable. Se usa en muchas recetas de fabricación "
"mecánicas."

#. ~ WESTWARD 31D018 from Walmart, 18-inch length, 2-3/8-inch jaws, 4.23 lb,
#. assume 8g/ml steel density with some margin for mechanism and other empty
#. space.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "large adjustable wrench"
msgid_plural "large adjustable wrenches"
msgstr[0] "llave inglesa grande"
msgstr[1] "llaves inglesas grandes"
msgstr[2] "llaves inglesas grandes"

#. ~ WESTWARD 31D018 from Walmart, 18-inch length, 2-3/8-inch jaws, 4.23 lb,
#. assume 8g/ml steel density with some margin for mechanism and other empty
#. space.
#. ~ Description of "large adjustable wrench"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"An unusually large adjustable crescent wrench, with a long handle and jaws "
"that widen over two inches.  This could easily turn most bolts, and should "
"even work on wheel lug nuts."
msgstr ""
"Una inusualmente larga llave inglesa ajustable, con un mango largo y "
"mandíbulas que se ensanchan más de cinco centímetros. Esto podría girar "
"fácilmente la mayoría de los tornillos, e incluso debería funcionar en las "
"tuercas de las ruedas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "leather hose"
msgid_plural "leather hoses"
msgstr[0] "manguera de cuero"
msgstr[1] "mangueras de cuero"
msgstr[2] "mangueras de cuero"

#. ~ Description of "leather hose"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A hose made of leather.  Watertight and flexible, it can be used to siphon "
"fuel from a vehicle tank.  However, it's not as elastic as a rubber hose."
msgstr ""
"Una manguera hecha de cuero. Hermética y flexible, puede utilizarse para "
"transvasar el combustible del depósito de un vehículo. Sin embargo, no es "
"tan elástica como una manguera de goma."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "makeshift hand drill"
msgid_plural "makeshift hand drills"
msgstr[0] "taladro manual improvisado"
msgstr[1] "taladros manuales improvisados"
msgstr[2] "taladros manuales improvisados"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift hand drill"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A makeshift manual drill made with a pipe and an improvised drill bit.  "
"Using it is very slow, and will exhaust you quickly."
msgstr ""
"Un taladro manual casero con un tubo y una broca improvisada. Es muy lento y"
" te agotará rápidamente."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "wire draw machine"
msgid_plural "wire draw machines"
msgstr[0] "máquina de trefilado"
msgstr[1] "máquinas de trefilado"
msgstr[2] "máquinas de trefilado"

#. ~ Description of "wire draw machine"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "A machine designed specifically for turning metal rods into wire."
msgstr ""
"Una máquina diseñada específicamente para convertir varillas de metal en "
"cables."

#. ~ power usage: propane torch delivers about 2.5 kj per ml adjusted for
#. efficiency, needs about 800 degrees c to ignite steel, which is specific
#. heat 420j so to ignite a kg of steel, it is about 128 units of propane
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "propane torch"
msgid_plural "propane torches"
msgstr[0] "soldador de propano"
msgstr[1] "soldadores de propano"
msgstr[2] "soldadores de propano"

#. ~ power usage: propane torch delivers about 2.5 kj per ml adjusted for
#. efficiency, needs about 800 degrees c to ignite steel, which is specific
#. heat 420j so to ignite a kg of steel, it is about 128 units of propane
#. ~ Description of "propane torch"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A compact tool kit intended for cutting metal, this portable propane torch "
"includes a torch handle and cutting attachment in an easy-to-carry tote.  It"
" needs to be connected to a pressurized propane cylinder before use.  While "
"not appropriate for welding, you can activate it in order to destroy metal "
"barriers."
msgstr ""
"Un equipo compacto de herramientas destinadas a cortar metal, este soldador "
"de propano portátil incluye un mango de soplete y un accesorio de corte en "
"una bolsa fácil de transportar. Requiere la conexión a bombonas de propano "
"presurizadas antes de su uso. Aunque no es apropiado para soldar, se puede "
"usar para destruir barreras metálicas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "block and tackle"
msgid_plural "blocks and tackles"
msgstr[0] "aparejo"
msgstr[1] "aparejos"
msgstr[2] "aparejos"

#. ~ Description of "block and tackle"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy metal housing with a number of pulleys that can be used with a "
"thick rope or a chain to gain mechanical advantage on a lift."
msgstr ""
"Una estructura resistente con un número de poleas que pueden usarse con una "
"soga o cadena gruesa para ganar ventaja mecánica al levantar cosas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "wooden block and tackle"
msgid_plural "wooden blocks and tackles"
msgstr[0] "aparejo de madera"
msgstr[1] "aparejos de madera"
msgstr[2] "aparejos de madera"

#. ~ Description of "wooden block and tackle"
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid ""
"A wooden housing with a pair of pulleys that can be used with a thick rope "
"or a chain to gain mechanical advantage on a lift.  Not as durable as a "
"metal set."
msgstr ""
"Una estructura de madera con un par de poleas que pueden usarse con una soga"
" o cadena gruesa para ganar ventaja mecánica al levantar cosas. No es tan "
"resistente como el aparejo de metal."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
msgid "welding blanket"
msgid_plural "welding blankets"
msgstr[0] "manta de soldadura"
msgstr[1] "mantas de soldadura"
msgstr[2] "mantas de soldadura"

#. ~ Description of "welding blanket"
