#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Mr. Lapin"
msgstr "Sr. Lapin"

#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
#. ~ A survivor raising rabbits, all by themselves. Give special quests to
#. give rabbits to player
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Warrener"
msgstr "Warrener"

#. ~ Job description of "Mr. Lapin" NPC class
#. ~ This is a unique NPC who doesn't get randomly selected background traits
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "I raise rabbits."
msgstr "Crío conejos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Are you here to protect us?"
msgstr "¿Estás aquí para protegernos?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Pleased to meet you."
msgstr "Encantado de conocerte."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "I'm just trying to get by."
msgstr "Sólo estoy tratando de salir adelante."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
msgid "Heard anything about the outside world?"
msgstr "¿Escuchaste algo del mundo exterior?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "You look different?"
msgstr "¿Pareces diferente?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Anything I can help with?"
msgstr "¿Puedo ayudar en algo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "About that work…"
msgstr "Sobre ese trabajo…"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Do you need any resources?"
msgstr "¿Necesitas algún recurso?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Where did you get that giant firefly terrarium?"
msgstr "¿De dónde has sacado ese terrario de luciérnagas gigante?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Getting by will do for now."
msgstr "Por ahora es suficiente."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "I guess it has to."
msgstr "Supongo que sí."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "I raise my rabbits, I seem to have more in common with them every day."
msgstr ""
"Yo crío mis conejos, parece que cada día tengo más en común con ellos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid "Well, then…"
msgstr "Bueno, entonces..."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid ""
"People come to me to learn how to keep rabbits.  They learn and they go.  I "
"like to think I'm making the world better."
msgstr ""
"La gente viene a mí para aprender a criar conejos. Aprenden y se van. Me "
"gusta pensar que estoy haciendo un mundo mejor."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Anyone nearby I should meet?"
msgstr "¿Hay alguien cerca que deba conocer?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "That sounds optimistic?"
msgstr "¿Suena optimista?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid ""
"There is a family of nearby farmers that I trade with.  I'd appreciate it if"
" you could go check on them."
msgstr ""
"Hay una familia de granjeros cercana con la que comercio. Te agradecería que"
" fueras a verlos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Seems like a deal to me."
msgstr "A mí me parece un buen trato."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "That seems rather dangerous, I think I'll pass."
msgstr "Eso parece bastante peligroso, creo que voy a pasar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid ""
"It can be quite a hike depending on your transportation.  Lot of bad news "
"between here and there."
msgstr ""
"Puede ser una gran caminata dependiendo de tu transporte. Muchas malas "
"noticias entre aquí y allá."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Don't worry, I'll be careful."
msgstr "No te preocupes, tendré cuidado."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Just a walk in the woods."
msgstr "Sólo un paseo por el bosque."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid ""
"If I teach one hundred people how to raise rabbits, that's potentially a "
"hundred communities given food and fur before those people teach anyone "
"else."
msgstr ""
"Si enseño a cien personas a criar conejos, son potencialmente cien comunidSi"
" enseño a cien personas a criar conejos, son potencialmente cien comunidades"
" a las que se les da comida y pieles antes de que esas personas enseñen a "
"nadie más.ades a las que se les da comida y pieles antes de que esas "
"personas enseñen a nadie más."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "That's the most hopeful thing I've heard so far."
msgstr "Es lo más esperanzador que he escuchado hasta ahora."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid ""
"A traveler brought this to me in return for some rabbits.  Said that he'd "
"gotten it from a scientist out in the swamps but it took up too much space "
"in his car."
msgstr ""
"Un viajero me trajo esto a cambio de unos conejos. Dijo que lo había "
"conseguido de un científico en los pantanos, pero que ocupaba demasiado "
"espacio en su coche."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "It's quite unique!"
msgstr "¡Es bastante único!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Same way you got yours, I bet."
msgstr "De la misma manera que tú tienes la tuya, apuesto."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "CRISPR?  Radiation?  Something in the water?  Maybe it was bunnies."
msgstr "¿CRISPR? ¿Radiación? ¿Algo en el agua? Tal vez fueron conejos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "So it goes."
msgstr "Así es."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid "You're disgusting."
msgstr "Eres desagradable."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "I'm very sorry to tell you this, but you should look in a mirror."
msgstr "Siento mucho decirle esto, pero deberías mirarte en un espejo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Insulting people who could help you is unlikely to aid survival."
msgstr ""
"Insultar a la gente que podría ayudarte es poco probable que ayude a la "
"supervivencia.Insultar a la gente que podría ayudarte es poco probable que "
"ayude a la supervivencia."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid ""
"The bunnies and I love adding some diversity to the menu and I always need "
"materials for patching fences."
msgstr ""
"A los conejitos y a mí nos encanta añadir algo de diversidad al menú y "
"siempre necesito materiales para remendar las vallas."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_FORGE_MERCHANT.json
msgid "That's all for now.  Can we discuss something else?"
msgstr "Eso es todo por ahora. ¿Podemos hablar de otra cosa?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_FORGE_MERCHANT.json
msgid "That's all for now.  I'd best get going."
msgstr "Eso es todo por ahora. Será mejor que me vaya."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Timber!"
msgstr "¡Madera!"

#. ~ Description of mission "Timber!"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Bring five logs."
msgstr "Trae cinco leños."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Timber!"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "I need 5 logs for fences."
msgstr "Necesito 5 leños para las vallas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Timber!"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid ""
"I need to build fences and ditches around my rabbits.  Could you find about…"
" five logs for me?"
msgstr ""
"Necesito construir vallas y zanjas alrededor de mis conejos. ¿Podrías "
"encontrar unos... cinco leños para mí?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Timber!"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "There's a lot of places to look.  Trees are pretty common."
msgstr "Hay muchos lugares para buscar. Los árboles son bastante comunes."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Timber!"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Big Game Hunting"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
msgid "How is the search going?  Have you found'em?"
msgstr "¿Cómo va la búsqueda? ¿Los has encontrado?"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Sweets"
msgstr "Dulces"

#. ~ Description of mission "Sweets"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Find 25 blackberries."
msgstr "Encuentra 25 moras."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sweets"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "I need 25 blackberries."
msgstr "Necesito 25 zarzamoras."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sweets"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Fruits would let me break the monotony of grains and meats."
msgstr ""
"Las frutas me permitirían romper la monotonía de los granos y las carnes."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sweets"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid ""
"Thanks for accepting this task.  Otherwise I might kill a stranger for some "
"oranges.  Just kidding."
msgstr ""
"Gracias por aceptar esta tarea. De lo contrario, podría matar a un extraño "
"por unas naranjas. Es una broma."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sweets"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Find someone growing berries or an orchard."
msgstr ""
"Encuentra a alguien que cultive bayas o un huerto de árboles frutales."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sweets"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Have you found the fruit?"
msgstr "¿Has encontrado la fruta?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sweets"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bread"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
msgid "Thank you for your help.  Here's your reward."
msgstr "Gracias por tu ayuda. Aquí está tu recompensa."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid "Visit the Isherwoods"
msgstr "Visita los Isherwoods"

#. ~ Description of mission "Visit the Isherwoods"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
msgid ""
"There is a family nearby that I'd like you to check in on.  After you talk "
"to all of them, come back to me and tell me how they are doing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Visit the Isherwoods"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Go check out this island"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/draco_dune.json
msgid "Have you checked on them?"
msgstr "¿Has comprobado que estan bien?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Visit the Isherwoods"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Go check out this island"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/draco_dune.json
msgid "Good, that's one less thing to worry about."
msgstr "Bien, es una cosa menos de la que preocuparse."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Visit the Isherwoods"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Go check out this island"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/draco_dune.json
msgid "I'm glad to hear they are fine.  Why haven't they been by then?"
msgstr ""
"Me alegra saber que están bien. ¿Por qué no lo han estado para entonces?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Visit the Isherwoods"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Go check out this island"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/draco_dune.json
msgid "At least you came back with your life…"
msgstr "Al menos volviste con tu vida..."

#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
#. ~ Hunter with indigenous ancestry and big ideas.
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "Glooscap"
msgstr "Glooscap"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "Good to see you again, how can I help you?"
msgstr "Qué bueno verte de nuevo, ¿en qué te puedo ayudar?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"They say I turned a man into a cedar tree once.  That's a terrible thing to "
"say."
msgstr ""
"Dicen que una vez convertí un hombre en un cedro. Es una cosa horrible para "
"andar diciendo por ahí."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"You like maple syrup?  That was me.  Not the syrup, that was the trees, but "
"I figured out how to make it much harder to concentrate it, used to be way "
"too easy.  Pretty nice right?"
msgstr ""
"¿Te gusta el jarabe de arce? Eso era mío. No la savia, eso era del árbol, "
"pero descubrí cómo hacerla mucho más difícil de concentrar, antes era "
"demasiado fácil. ¿Está bastante bueno, no?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"Did I tell you the one about the beavers?  Used to be way too big.  Like "
"giant beavers, it was a mess.  I fixed that.  Of course there seem to be a "
"bunch of new giant things out here now.  I'll have to think about that."
msgstr ""
"¿Te conté lo de los castores? Antes eran muy grandes. Como castores "
"gigantes, era un desastre. Por supuesto, parece que hay un montón de cosas "
"nuevas gigantes ahora. Voy a tener que pensar en eso."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"You know storms?  Used to be more.  Took me a lot of work, but there aren't "
"as many now.  That was me, I did that.  Fewer storms, pretty good.  There's "
"a big eagle, it's a long story really.  I'm good with rope though."
msgstr ""
"¿Conoces las tormentas? Antes había más. Me llevó mucho trabajo pero ahora "
"ya no hay tantas. Fui yo, yo hice eso. Menos tormentas, bastante bueno. Hay "
"un águila grande, es una historia larga la verdad. Pero soy bueno con la "
"soga."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "It's decided then.  I will be Glooscap.  Who will you be?"
msgstr "Entonces, está decidido. Yo voy a ser Glooscap. ¿Tu quién vas a ser?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "Glooscap?  That's a funny name.  Is it foreign?"
msgstr "¿Glooscap? Qué nombre mas gracioso. ¿Es extranjero?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "[INT 11]  Like the Wabanaki myth?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "So.  You're dressed like a hunter.  Are you a hunter?"
msgstr "Así que. Estás vestido como un cazador. ¿Eres un cazador?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "Have you had any luck out there?"
msgstr "¿Tuviste suerte ahí afuera?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"Whatever, I don't have time for whatever this is.  Try not to get your face "
"eaten I guess."
msgstr ""
"No importa, no tengo tiempo para lo que sea eso. Intenta que no te coman la "
"cara y eso."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"I'm used to it.  No, Glooscap has been a name here for a very long time.  Is"
" your name foreign?"
msgstr ""
"Estoy acostumbrado. No, Glooscap ha sido un nombre común por mucho tiempo. "
"¿Tu nombre es extranjero?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "No, my name has been a name here for a very long time too."
msgstr "No, mi nombre ha sido un nombre aquí por mucho tiempo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "No, I just made it up."
msgstr "No, me lo acabo de inventar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "Yes, I just got here.  What's happening?"
msgstr "Sí, recién llegue. ¿Qué pasa?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "I don't know about names, let's talk about something more interesting."
msgstr "No sé nada sobre nombres, hablemos de algo más interesante."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "You know the real people's stories?  Yes, a lot like that."
msgstr "¿Conoces las historias de la gente real? Sí, muy parecido a eso."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "Cool, cool.  So you like myths and stuff?"
msgstr "Genial. ¿Así que te gustan los mitos y esas cosas?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "[INT 14] Do you have a twin named Malsumis?"
msgstr "[INT 14] ¿Tienes un gemelo que se llama Malsumis?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"Yes, I'm a very smart survivor of the apocalypse.  Anyway, I need to move "
"along.  Later Glooscap."
msgstr ""
"Sí, soy un sobreviviente muy inteligente del apocalipsis. De todas maneras, "
"me tengo que ir. Hasta luego, Glooscap."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"And stuff sure.  How can I help you stranger?  They say I'm the nice one.  "
"See this smile?  Nice smile right?"
msgstr ""
"Y esas cosas, seguro. ¿Cómo te puedo ayudar, extraño? Dicen que yo soy el "
"bueno. ¿Ves esta sonrisa? ¿Linda sonrisa, eh?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"[HAS BEER] I am extremely into your smile yes.  I have some drinks with me, "
"want to have some?"
msgstr ""
"[TIENE CERVEZA] Estoy muy encantado con tu sonrisa, sí. Tengo algo para "
"tomar, ¿quieres un poco?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"[HAS IPA] I am extremely into your smile yes.  I have some drinks with me, "
"want to have some?"
msgstr ""
"[TIENE IPA] Estoy muy encantado con tu sonrisa, sí. Tengo algo para tomar, "
"¿quieres un poco?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"[HAS CIGARETTES] I am extremely into your smile yes.  I have some "
"cigarettes, want one with me?"
msgstr ""
"[TIENE CIGARRILLOS] Estoy muy encantado con tu sonrisa, sí. Tengo "
"cigarrillos, ¿quieres que compartamos uno?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"[HAS JOINT] I am extremely into your smile yes.  I have something to smoke, "
"want to have some with me?"
msgstr ""
"[TIENE PORRO] Estoy muy encantado con tu sonrisa, sí. Tengo algo para fumar,"
" ¿quieres un poco?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"You seem cool but I don't have anything fun.  I'll try and find something "
"and come back so we can share."
msgstr ""
"Pareces buena gente pero no tengo nada para divertirnos. Voy a intentar "
"conseguir algo y después vuelvo para compartirlo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "[PRETTY] That smile is very nice.  It makes me smile too."
msgstr "[LINDURA] Esa es una sonrisa muy linda. Me hace sonreír a mí también."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "[GLORIOUS] Worship my beauty."
msgstr "[ESPLÉNDIDO] Admirá mi belleza."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "[TERRIFYING] Fear me!  I am disgusting!"
msgstr "[ATERRADOR] ¡Ten miedo de mi! ¡Soy repugnante!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "[TERRIFYING] Destroy me!"
msgstr "[ATERRADOR] ¡Destrózame!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"I do have a twin.  Malsumis is probably around here somewhere, very tricky."
"  You know I turned Malsumis to stone once?  I'm supposed to be the nice "
"one, but you know how much it hurts turning yourself back from stone?  It "
"takes days."
msgstr ""
"Tengo un gemelo. Malsumis anda por aquí probablemente, medio tramposo. "
"¿Sabías que convertí a Malsumis en piedra una vez? Se supone que yo soy el "
"bueno pero ¿sabes cuánto duele volver a la normalidad desde la piedra? "
"Tardas días."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"[INT 14] I'll look out then, thanks.  Of course if you were Malsumis you "
"probably wouldn't admit it because no one likes Malsumis.  Who would your "
"twin say you are?"
msgstr ""
"[INT 14] Voy a estar atento entonces, gracias. Por supuesto que si fueras "
"Malsumis probablemente no lo admitirías porque a nadie le cae bien Malsumis."
" Si le pregunto a tu gemelo ¿quién dirías que sos vos?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "You know you're not really Glooscap right?  You're joking right?"
msgstr ""
"¿Entiendes que tu no eres realmente Glooscap, no? ¿Estás bromeando, no?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"Of course, that all makes as much sense as anything I guess.  So you have "
"crazy supernatural powers then?  Can you stop whatever is happening and make"
" it like before?"
msgstr ""
"Por supuesto, eso tiene tanto sentido como cualquier otra cosa, creo. ¿Así "
"que tienes unos poderes sobrenaturales? ¿Puedes parar lo que está pasando y "
"hacer que todo vuelva a como era antes?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"I don't know what Malsumis would say, Malsumis is very tricky.  I always "
"tell the truth, it's very boring."
msgstr ""
"No sé qué diría Malsumis, Malsumis es muy tramposo. Yo siempre digo la "
"verdad, es muy aburrido."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "[INT 14] I think you're Malsumis.  Where is Glooscap?"
msgstr "[INT 14] Creo que eres Malsumis. ¿Dónde está Glooscap?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "[INT 14] Yes, that all makes sense to me.  Forget I asked."
msgstr "[INT 14] Sí, eso tiene sentido. Olvídate que pregunté."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"I don't have time for this.  I have serious survival business to do.  I am a"
" serious survival business person."
msgstr ""
"No tengo tiempo para esto. Tengo asuntos serios de supervivencia que hacer. "
"Soy una persona de asuntos serios de supervivencia."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"If I were Malsumis you would be in terrible danger my friend.  But Glooscap "
"would stop me."
msgstr ""
"Si yo fuera Malsumis tu estarías en mucho peligro amigo mio. Pero Glooscap "
"podría detenerme."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "Fight me Malsumis!"
msgstr "¡Peleá contra mí, Malsumis!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"[SKILLED LIAR] Then you're definitely not Malsumis and everything is cool.  "
"So Malsumis wants to kill everybody right?  I guess they're feeling pretty "
"great right now huh?"
msgstr ""
"[MENTIROSO EXPERTO] Entones definitivamente no sos Malsumis y está todo "
"bien. Así que Malsumis quiere matar a todos, ¿no? Supongo que se están "
"sintiendo bastante bien ahora, eh."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "Haha, good one Glooscap.  So funny.  Love that.  Let's move on."
msgstr "Jaja, muy buena Glooscap. Que gracioso. Me encantó. Vamos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "This is awkward.  I need to leave."
msgstr "Esto es raro. Me tengo que ir."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"Maybe.  Is it worse to be unhappy with a goal or to be unhappy without a "
"goal?  You're all right, I feel like we get each other."
msgstr ""
"Tal vez. ¿Es peor ser infeliz con un objetivo o ser infeliz sin un objetivo?"
" Tu me caes bien, siento como si nos entendiéramos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "I feel the same way best friend."
msgstr "Me siento igual, mejor amigo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "No idea what you mean."
msgstr "Ni idea de lo que hablas."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"Haha, right.  What would Glooscap be doing in the sunrise lands at the "
"beginning of the fourth age?  That's silly.  I'm probably some Wabanaki that"
" got hit on the head or something.  And who turns into a beaver?  Haha.  You"
" got me.  Just a normal human made out of trees like the rest."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"No problem, a lot of people are going through some hard times right now.  "
"Honestly, you're doing better than most.  You should follow me, I have a "
"pretty good handle on reality."
msgstr ""
"No hay drama, mucha gente está pasando por momentos difíciles en este "
"momento. Honestamente, tu vas mejor que la mayoría. Deberías venir conmigo, "
"sé bastante bien cómo manejarme."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"I'm not made out of trees, I'm made out of awesome.  Follow me and you will "
"grow fat and rich."
msgstr ""
"No estoy hecho de árboles, estoy hecho de maravillas. Ven conmigo y te vas a"
" poner gordo y rico."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "You shouldn't follow me, but I guess I can't stop you."
msgstr "No deberías venir conmigo pero supongo que no puedo detenerte."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"Another world is going and a new world is coming.  I hope this new one is "
"better than the last, a new golden age.  So far not great."
msgstr ""
"Otro mundo está yendo y un nuevo mundo está viniendo. Espero que este nuevo "
"sea mejor que el anterior, una nueva era dorada. Por ahora, más o menos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "Sure sure.  So are you on drugs?"
msgstr "Seguro, seguro. ¿Tomás drogas?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "Whatever, I don't have time for creepy stuff."
msgstr "Como quieras, no tengo tiempo para estas cosas extrañas."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"Yes, thank you for sharing with me.  So what are you doing here?  What are "
"you trying to accomplish?"
msgstr ""
"Sí, gracias por compartirlo conmigo. ¿Qué estás haciendo aquí? ¿Qué estás "
"intentando lograr?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"[INT 14] I'm trying to understand what happened and see if I can make "
"something better happen."
msgstr ""
"[INT 14] Estoy intentando entender qué pasó y ver si puedo hacer que pase "
"algo mejor."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "I'm trying to become more powerful than whatever else is out there."
msgstr ""
"Estoy intentando volverme más poderoso que cualquier otra cosa que haya "
"dando vueltas por ahí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "I'm trying to make a survivor settlement.  You should join!"
msgstr ""
"Estoy intentando hacer un asentamiento de supervivientes. ¡Deberías unirte!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"Maybe some day.  If you can survive for long enough I may decide to come and"
" stay with you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "I need to move on."
msgstr "Necesito irme."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "Not enough given what's happening."
msgstr "No lo suficiente, dado lo que está pasando."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"Whoah whoah, calm down.  Yikes.  Yeah fine, we're good.  Just stop trying to"
" spook me, I don't like it."
msgstr ""
"Uy, uy, calmate. Uf. Sí, listo, está todo bien. Pero tratá de no asustarme, "
"no me gusta."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "Yes, that worked great."
msgstr "Sí, eso anduvo genial."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "We are not good and I'm done talking to you."
msgstr "No estamos bien y no quiero hablar más contigo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"Among other things, sure.  I have some extra I might be willing to trade, "
"but I only trade with my friends and I don't have a lot of those left."
msgstr ""
"Entre otras cosas, seguro. Tengo algo con lo que puedo comerciar pero solo "
"lo hago con amigos y no me quedan muchos de esos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"[HAS BEER] I don't know about friends, but I have some drinks with me, want "
"to have some?"
msgstr ""
"[TIENE CERVEZA] No sé nada de amigos pero tengo algo para beber, ¿quieres un"
" poco?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"[HAS IPA] I don't know about friends, but I have some drinks with me, want "
"to have some?"
msgstr ""
"[TIENE IPA] No sé nada de amigos pero tengo algo para beber, ¿quieres un "
"poco?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"[HAS CIGARETTES] I don't know about friends, but I have some cigarettes, "
"want one with me?"
msgstr ""
"[TIENE IPA] No sé nada de amigos pero tengo cigarrillos, ¿quieres que "
"compartamos uno?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"[HAS JOINT] I don't know about friends, but I have something to smoke, want "
"to have some with me?"
msgstr ""
"[TIENE PORRO] No sé nada de amigos pero tengo algo para fumar, ¿quieres un "
"poco?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"You seem cool and I'd like to talk more but I don't have anything fun.  I'll"
" try and find something and come back so we can share."
msgstr ""
"Pareces buena gente y me gustaría hablar mas pero no tengo nada para "
"divertirnos. Voy a intentar conseguir algo y después vuelvo para "
"compartirlo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "[PRETTY] I think we're going to be great friends, don't you agree?"
msgstr "[BONITO] Creo que vamos a ser grandes amigos, ¿no te parece?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid ""
"Whoah whoah, calm down.  Yikes.  Yeah fine, we're good.  Just stop making "
"that face, it's too much for me.  Gives me feelings."
msgstr ""
"Uy, uy, cálmate. Uf. Sí, listo, está todo bien. Pero deja de poner esa cara,"
" es demasiado para mí. Me hace sentir cosas."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "I don't think so.  I'm pretty good at hunting though."
msgstr "No creo. Soy bastante bueno cazando."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
msgid "I guess that's something."
msgstr "Supongo que algo es algo."

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ A rural holdout survivor trying to stay safe
#. ~ A rural holdout survivor completely unwilling to talk
#. ~ A rural holdout survivor that gave up on life
#. ~ A rural holdout survivor willing to trade items
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "Survivor cowboy"
msgstr "Vaquero superviviente"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
msgid "Hello again."
msgstr "Hola de nuevo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid ""
"Ayuh, I was thinkin' it's just another monstah skulkin' about.  Who are you?"
msgstr "Ayuh, estaba pensando que eras otro monstruo merodeando. ¿Quién eres?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid "Just a survivor, looking around.  What are you doing here?"
msgstr "Sólo un sobreviviente, mirando alrededor. ¿Qué estás haciendo aquí?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "What did you before all this?"
msgstr "¿Qué hacías antes de todo esto?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid "Is there something I can do for you?"
msgstr "¿Hay algo que pueda hacer por ti?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "How about we travel together?"
msgstr "¿Qué tal si viajamos juntos?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid "What's with the accent?"
msgstr "¿Por qué el acento?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid ""
"I worked on a ranch not too fah from here 'fore it all went down.  I'd love "
"ta get back ta what I did - taking care of horses, cows, all sorts of "
"animals, makin' sure the fields stay safe an' all that.  But now?  I dunno, "
"man.  Just tryin' ta survive, I suppose.  Hopefully, tha world will get back"
" togetha' one day and I can put mah skills ta use doin' what I like."
msgstr ""
"Trabajé en un rancho no muy lejos de aquí antes de que todo se fuera al "
"traste. Me encantaría volver a hacer lo que hacía: cuidar de los caballos, "
"las vacas, todo tipo de animales, asegurarme de que los campos estén a salvo"
" y todo eso. ¿Pero ahora? No sé, hombre. Sólo trato de sobrevivir, supongo. "
"Con suerte, el mundo volverá a funcionar algún día y podré usar mis "
"habilidades para hacer lo que me gusta."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid "Let's hope it will."
msgstr "Esperemos que así sea."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid ""
"I was just sort of wanderin' around, hoping ta maybe find some bettah gear."
"  Decided ta rest up, 'eard someone walkin', and, well, here we are."
msgstr ""
"Estaba vagando por ahí, esperando encontrar algún equipo mejor. Decidí "
"descansar, escuché a alguien caminando, y, bueno, aquí estamos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid ""
"Can't say I can think of summin' specific right now.  Gotta say though, "
"maybe it oughta be a good idea for us ta travel togetha' - safety in numbers"
" an' all that."
msgstr ""
"No puedo decir que pueda pensar en algo específico ahora mismo. Tengo que "
"decir, sin embargo, que tal vez debería ser una buena idea para nosotros "
"viajar juntos - la seguridad en los números y todo eso."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
msgid "I'll think about it."
msgstr "Voy a pensarlo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid "Is it a good idea to trust a stranger like me this easily?"
msgstr "¿Es una buena idea confiar en un extraño como yo tan fácilmente?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid "Sounds like a good idea - want to join me, then?"
msgstr "Me parece una buena idea, ¿quieres unirte a mí, entonces?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid ""
"Wicked.  Been around the old road long enough ta know how ta handle myself "
"in a pinch.  Knew my way around a gun ever since my da taught me when I was "
"a kid, so ya don't have ta worry about me doing my part."
msgstr ""
"Malvado. He estado en el viejo camino lo suficiente como para saber cómo "
"manejarme en caso de necesidad. Sabía cómo manejar un arma desde que mi "
"padre me enseñó cuando era un niño, así que no tienes que preocuparte de que"
" no haga mi parte."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid "On a second thought, let me think about it a bit more"
msgstr "Pensándolo bien, déjame pensarlo un poco más"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid "Great!  Let's go."
msgstr "¡Genial! Vamos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid ""
"Don't have much of a choice, do I?  On my own, a monstah will get lucky "
"sooner or later, and even if I kill it, bleedin' out in some alley is not "
"summin' I fancy.  Plus, we just had a nice, civil chat where no one tried ta"
" kill the otha', so I reckon we're off to ah' good start, all things "
"considered."
msgstr ""
"No tengo muchas opciones, ¿verdad? Por mi cuenta, un monstruo tendrá suerte "
"tarde o temprano, e incluso si lo mato, desangrarme en un callejón no es "
"algo que me guste. Además, acabamos de tener una agradable y civilizada "
"charla en la que nadie ha intentado matar al otro, así que creo que hemos "
"empezado con buen pie."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid "Fair enough.  Want to travel with me, then?"
msgstr "Me parece bien. ¿Quieres viajar conmigo, entonces?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid "Can't say I really agree.  I'll be going now."
msgstr "No puedo decir que esté de acuerdo. Voy a irme ahora."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid ""
"Wha', nevah been ta Boston 'ave ya?  Hope you're not 'avin a hahd time "
"keepin' up with me, but if ya get used ta it, wicked good fun, let me tell "
"ya."
msgstr ""
"¿Qué? ¿Nunca has estado en Boston, verdad? Espero que no lo estés pasando "
"mal para seguirme el ritmo, pero si te acostumbras, es muy divertido, déjame"
" decirte."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid "I like it."
msgstr "Me gusta."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid "I hate it."
msgstr "Lo odio."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
msgid "Okay then."
msgstr "Bien entonces."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
msgid ""
"Hey!  Stop right there!  This here is private property!  Not one step "
"closer, you got it?!"
msgstr ""
"¡Oye! ¡Detente ahí! ¡Esto es propiedad privada! Ni un paso más, ¡¿lo "
"tienes?!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
msgid "Whoa, calm down, no reason to get heated."
msgstr "Whoa, cálmate, no hay razón para calentarse."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
msgid "You better calm down right now."
msgstr "Será mejor que te calmes ahora mismo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
msgid "Does private property even exist anymore?"
msgstr "¿Existe todavía la propiedad privada?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
msgid "Yeah that's right!  And don't bother me again, you hear?!"
msgstr "¡Sí, eso es! Y no me vuelvas a molestar, ¿me oyes?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
msgid "I said stay away!  Don't get any closer or I swear I will kill you."
msgstr "¡He dicho que te alejes! No te acerques más o te juro que te mato."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
msgid "Don't threaten me or you will regret it."
msgstr "No me amenaces o lo lamentarás."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
msgid "I really just want to talk - I mean no harm."
msgstr "En realidad, sólo quiero hablar, no pretendo hacer daño."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
msgid "Alright, I'm leaving."
msgstr "Muy bien, me voy."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
msgid ""
"For the last goddamn time, leave or I will defend myself!  I will kill you!"
msgstr "¡Por última vez, vete o me defenderé! ¡Te mataré!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
msgid "I'd like to see you try."
msgstr "Me gustaría verte intentarlo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
msgid ""
"Did you just fucking threaten me?!  This is your last chance to piss off or "
"I swear I will end you!"
msgstr ""
"¡¿Acabas de amenazarme?! ¡Esta es tu última oportunidad de largarte o te "
"juro que acabaré contigo!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
msgid "Alright, alright, I'm going."
msgstr "Muy bien, muy bien, me voy."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
msgid "It does on my property!  Now blow off!"
msgstr "¡Lo hace en mi propiedad! ¡Ahora lárgate!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
msgid "Okay, I'll leave."
msgstr "Bien, me iré."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
msgid "I just want to talk."
msgstr "Sólo quiero hablar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Yeah?"
msgstr "¿Sí?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "Oh.  Hey there."
msgstr "Oh, Hola."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "Thought I heard someone.  What are you doing here?"
msgstr "Me pareció oír a alguien. ¿Qué estás haciendo aquí?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "Would you like to come with me?"
msgstr "¿Te gustaría venir conmigo?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "I already told you.  Don't want to go through it again."
msgstr "Ya te lo dije. No quiero volver a hacerlo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid ""
"Lived in a nearby town.  Normal life.  9 to 5 job.  When it all happened, we"
" ran away to find some safety.  But there's no safety anymore, is there?"
msgstr ""
"Vivía en un pueblo cercano. Vida normal. Trabajo de 9 a 5. Cuando todo "
"sucedió, huimos para encontrar algo de seguridad. Pero ya no hay seguridad, "
"¿verdad?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "Wait, 'we'?"
msgstr "Espera, ¿\"nosotros\"?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "Right.  Okay."
msgstr "Correcto. Bien."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "I didn't leave the town alone.  I arrived here alone."
msgstr "No dejé la ciudad sola. Llegué aquí solo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid ""
"I'm sorry for your loss.  But you still can't give up.  You have a lot to "
"live for!"
msgstr ""
"Lamento tu pérdida. Pero aún no puedes rendirte.  ¡Tienes mucho por lo que "
"vivir!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "We all lost someone.  No reason to sit down and die."
msgstr "Todos hemos perdido a alguien. No hay razón para sentarse y morir."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "You can't let yourself be consumed by grief.  It will get better."
msgstr "No puedes dejarte consumir por la pena. Todo mejorará."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "No one gets out alive.  Always been that way.  So we keep going."
msgstr "Nadie sale vivo. Siempre ha sido así. Así que seguimos adelante."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "I'm sure your loved one would want you to live on for them."
msgstr ""
"Estoy seguro de que tu ser querido querría que siguieras viviendo por él."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "I… I mean… huh.  I guess."
msgstr "Yo... quiero decir... eh. Supongo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "Good.  Take care."
msgstr "Bien. Cuídate."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "That's a start."
msgstr "Eso es un comienzo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "Just leave me alone."
msgstr "Solo dejame en paz."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "Alright.  Take care."
msgstr "Muy bien. Cuídate"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "I dunno.  Waiting.  Seeing if something happens I guess."
msgstr "No sé. Esperando. A ver si pasa algo, supongo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "You do realize there is an apocalypse going on, right?"
msgstr "Te das cuenta de que hay un apocalipsis en marcha, ¿verdad?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "Yeah.  I do."
msgstr "Sí, así es."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "So shouldn't you be more concerned?  Trying to survive?"
msgstr "¿No deberías estar más preocupado? ¿Intentar sobrevivir?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid ""
"For how long?  You've seen what's out there.  If we survive today, we'll die"
" the day after.  Or the day after that.  And if we live beyond that, we'll "
"just see everyone we care about die.  All of them.  Might as well get it "
"over with."
msgstr ""
"¿Durante cuánto tiempo? Ya has visto lo que hay ahí fuera. Si sobrevivimos "
"hoy, moriremos el día después. O el día después de ese. Y si vivimos más "
"allá de eso, veremos morir a todos los que nos importan. Todos ellos. Será "
"mejor que acabemos con esto."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "So you're just going to give up?"
msgstr "¿Así que te vas a rendir?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "Yeah.  I think I will."
msgstr "Sí. Creo que lo haré."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid ""
"I dunno.  Maybe.  Might give me something to do while I think about all "
"this."
msgstr ""
"No lo sé. Tal vez. Podría darme algo que hacer mientras pienso en todo esto."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "I told you to just leave me alone."
msgstr "Te dije que me dejaras en paz."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "It will.  Let's get going."
msgstr "Lo hare. Vamos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "On a second thought, wait here a while."
msgstr "Pensándolo bien, espera aquí un rato."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
msgid "Alright.  Goodbye."
msgstr "Muy bien. Adiós."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "Hey!  Who goes there?"
msgstr "¡Oye! ¿Quién va allí?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "Just another survivor.  What are you doing here?"
msgstr "Sólo otro superviviente. ¿Qué estás haciendo aquí?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "I'm you, from the future.  I've come to warn you."
msgstr "Soy tú, del futuro. He venido a advertirte."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid ""
"I am a ghost.  I died here 37 years ago, yet I cannot depart this mortal "
"realm."
msgstr ""
"Soy un fantasma. Morí aquí hace 37 años, pero no puedo abandonar este reino "
"mortal."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "Is there something I can help you with?"
msgstr "¿Hay algo en lo que pueda ayudarte?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid ""
"Worked as a salesman - high end farming equipment.  Now I know, it may not "
"sound that fancy, but you'd be shocked at how pricy those machines can get."
"  I was lucky enough to be on a fairly remote farm when everything went to "
"shit.  In a way, being a salesman saved me and the experience from the job "
"might allow me to make a living in the apocalypse, bartering for gear and "
"trinkets, so I got that going for me, I suppose."
msgstr ""
"Trabajé como vendedor de equipos agrícolas de alta gama. Lo sé, puede que no"
" suene tan elegante, pero te sorprendería lo caras que pueden llegar a ser "
"esas máquinas. Tuve la suerte de estar en una granja bastante remota cuando "
"todo se fue a la mierda. En cierto modo, ser vendedor me salvó y la "
"experiencia del trabajo podría permitirme ganarme la vida en el apocalipsis,"
" haciendo trueques por equipos y baratijas, así que supongo que tengo eso a "
"mi favor."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "Speaking of which, I'd like to see your wares."
msgstr "Hablando de eso, me gustaría ver tu mercancía."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "Not a bad way to live."
msgstr "No es una mala manera de vivir."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid ""
"Hah, real cute.  Seem the End times didn't take your sense of humor, eh, "
"stranger?"
msgstr ""
"Hah, muy lindo. Parece que el Fin de los Tiempos no se llevó tu sentido del "
"humor, ¿eh, forastero?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "I have my moments.  So what are you doing here?"
msgstr "Tengo mis momentos. Entonces, ¿qué estás haciendo aquí?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid ""
"Ah, not much really.  Passing through, trying to make a living by trading "
"with folk.  If you're interested, I got a lot of good things on sale, "
"stranger."
msgstr ""
"Ah, no mucho en realidad. De paso, tratando de ganarme la vida comerciando "
"con la gente. Si te interesa, tengo un montón de cosas buenas en venta, "
"extraño."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "You do?  Let me take a look."
msgstr "¿tienes? Déjame ver."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid ""
"You seem like a decent sort, but I'm not really looking for company right "
"now.  Think I'm better off on my own."
msgstr ""
"Pareces un tipo decente, pero no estoy buscando compañía en este momento. "
"Creo que estoy mejor por mi cuenta."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "If you think so."
msgstr "Si lo crees así."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "Fair enough.  Goodbye."
msgstr "Justo. Adiós."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
msgstr "Conseguir una escopeta Remington 870 Express"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "Well, now that you mention it…"
msgstr "Bien, ahora que lo mencionas..."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid ""
"You see, some time ago, I ran into this guy who offered me a substantial "
"payment in exchange for a Remington 870 Express.  I asked if he'd like "
"another weapon, since nowadays, any gun will do, but for some reason, he's "
"dead set on that particular model.  If you could obtain one for me, well, "
"I'd be quite grateful."
msgstr ""
"Verás, hace algún tiempo, me encontré con un tipo que me ofreció un "
"importante pago a cambio de una Remington 870 Express. Le pregunté si quería"
" otra arma, ya que hoy en día, cualquier arma sirve, pero por alguna razón, "
"se ha quedado con ese modelo en particular. Si pudiera conseguirme una, te "
"lo agradecería mucho."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid ""
"Great!  Let me know when you get it, and I'll try to get in touch with him."
msgstr ""
"¡Genial! Avísame cuando lo tengas y trataré de ponerme en contacto con él."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "Suit yourself.  Ain't a rush."
msgstr "Como quieras. No hay prisa."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid ""
"Well, a gun store is a solid bet, but the model is common enough.  Maybe you"
" can find one in a police station, or a store with hunting gear."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, una tienda de armas es una apuesta sólida, pero el modelo es bastante"
" común. Tal vez usted puedas encontrar uno en una estación de policía, o una"
" tienda con equipo de caza."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "Any news on that Remington?"
msgstr "¿Alguna noticia sobre esa Remington?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid ""
"Fantastic!  I'll try and get it to the buyer, if he's still alive.  If not, "
"well, still a good gun to sell.  Now, how would you like to be compensated?"
msgstr ""
"¡Fantástico! Intentaré llevársela al comprador, si es que sigue vivo. Si no,"
" bueno, sigue siendo una buena arma para vender. Ahora, ¿cómo te gustaría "
"ser compensado?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "How did you even get this option to display the hell."
msgstr "¿Cómo has conseguido esta opción para mostrar el infierno?."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
msgid "Then where is it?"
msgstr "Entonces, ¿dónde está?"

#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ A naked prisoner, from the isherwood faction trapped in a horrifying
#. cage, watching horrible things happen.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
msgid "Barry Isherwood"
msgstr "Barry Isherwood"

#. ~ Job description of "Barry Isherwood" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
msgid "Missing member of the Isherwood family."
msgstr "Miembro desaparecido de la familia Isherwood."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
msgid "I can't believe my eyes.  Please get me outta here…"
msgstr "No puedo creer lo que veo. Por favor, sácame de aquí..."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
msgid "I've come to take you home, let's go."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hey buddy, feel like talking about what you saw in that tower?"
msgstr "Oye amigo, ¿te apetece hablar de lo que viste en esa torre?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, I think we need to talk about it, but I'm not ready yet.  Let me "
"reclaim my life for a while."
msgstr ""
"Sí, creo que tenemos que hablar de ello, pero aún no estoy listo. Déjame "
"reclamar mi vida por un tiempo. "

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
msgid "Sounds good, Barry."
msgstr "Suena bien, Barry."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
msgid "Return Barry to Eddie at the dairy."
msgstr "Devuélve Barry a Eddie en la lechería."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return Barry to Eddie at the dairy."
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
msgid "I just want to go home."
msgstr "Sólo quiero irme a casa."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return Barry to Eddie at the dairy."
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
msgid "I can't believe you are here, please take me back to the ranch."
msgstr "No puedo creer que estés aquí, por favor llévame de vuelta al rancho."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return Barry to Eddie at the dairy."
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
msgid "Thank you, I thought I was dead."
msgstr "Gracias, pensé que estaba muerto."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return Barry to Eddie at the dairy."
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
msgid "Please god no!"
msgstr "¡Por favor, Dios, nooo!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return Barry to Eddie at the dairy."
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
msgid "We shouldn't stay here too long, more might show up."
msgstr "No deberíamos quedarnos aquí mucho tiempo, má- podrían aparecer."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return Barry to Eddie at the dairy."
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Thanks, we'll never be able to repay you, Here's a token of my gratitude, I "
"made these suits for my family and always keep a few extra around."
msgstr ""
"Gracias, nunca podremos pagartelo. Aquí tienes una muestra de mi gratitud. "
"Hice estos trajes para mi familia y siempre tengo algunos extra por aquí."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return Barry to Eddie at the dairy."
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
msgid "I don't feel saved…"
msgstr "No me siento salvado..."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return Barry to Eddie at the dairy."
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
msgid "Tell my family that I love them…"
msgstr "Dile a mi familia que los quiero..."

#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Dairy farmer the Isherwood family.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "Carlos Isherwood"
msgstr "Carlos Isherwood"

#. ~ Job description of "Carlos Isherwood" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "I'm Jesse's husband, part of the Isherwood family."
msgstr "Soy el marido de Jesse, soy parte de la familia Isherwood."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I see that badge, I think you need to keep on walking, straight off this "
"property."
msgstr ""
"Veo esa placa, creo que debes seguir caminando, directamente fuera de esta "
"propiedad."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hello Sir, what brings you here?"
msgstr "Hola señor, ¿qué le trae por aquí?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hello Ma'am, what brings you here?"
msgstr "Hola señora, ¿qué la trae por aquí?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Yeah, I'm a Marshal, what are you going to do about it?"
msgstr "Sí, soy un Alguacil, ¿qué vas a hacer al respecto?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hi, looks like you are building a forge setup."
msgstr "Hola, parece que estás construyendo una instalación para la forja."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hi, Jack and Claire suggested I come talk to you about a job."
msgstr ""
"Hola, Jack y Claire me sugirieron que viniera a hablar contigo sobre un "
"trabajo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"It is coming together.  I want to make our own tools, repair our items and "
"even create some weapons and ammunition reloading."
msgstr ""
"Se está armando. Quiero hacer nuestras propias herramientas, reparar "
"nuestros artículos e incluso crear algunas armas y recargas de municiones."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "I heard about Barry, can you tell me what captured him?"
msgstr "Me enteré de lo de Barry, ¿puede decirme qué lo capturó?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"It was pink and really fast, it had lots of limbs, definitely not human.  It"
" easily kept up with us when we tried to escape, horrifying stuff.  Barry "
"just dropped to the ground, and the thing swept him away."
msgstr ""
"Era rosa y muy rápido, tenía muchas extremidades, definitivamente no era "
"humano. Se mantenía fácilmente al ritmo de nosotros cuando tratábamos de "
"escapar, cosa horrible. Barry se cayó al suelo, y la cosa lo arrastró."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "You all just gonna leave him out there to his fate?"
msgstr "¿Vais a dejarle ahí fuera a su suerte?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"We tracked it for a while, but lost the trail.  Right now we don't have the "
"resources to try to rescue him.  Chris has been trying to pick up the trail "
"again and figure out a rescue plan."
msgstr ""
"Lo rastreamos por un tiempo, pero perdimos el rastro. Ahora mismo no tenemos"
" los recursos para intentar rescatarlo. Chris ha estado tratando de retomar "
"el rastro de nuevo y elaborar un plan de rescate."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"The big item I need is an anvil, once I have that I can get a lot of repairs"
" done."
msgstr ""
"El gran artículo que necesito es un yunque, una vez que lo tenga podré hacer"
" muchas reparaciones."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Chris is hiking the perimeter of our land, planning some defense options."
msgstr ""
"Chris está recorriendo el perímetro de nuestra tierra, planeando algunas "
"opciones de defensa."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "Is your forge operational?"
msgstr "¿Está operativa tu forja?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "Where can I find Chris?"
msgstr "¿Dónde puedo encontrar a Chris?"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "Find an anvil"
msgstr "Encuentra un yunque"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an anvil"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "I need an anvil to do advanced metal work."
msgstr "Necesito un yunque para hacer un trabajo de metal avanzado."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an anvil"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "I could really use an anvil."
msgstr "Me vendría muy bien un yunque."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an anvil"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "You might be able to find one in a hardware store or similar."
msgstr "Podrías ser capaz de encontrar uno en una ferretería o similar."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an anvil"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "Thanks anyway, we'll find the time to make it ourselves."
msgstr ""
"Gracias de todos formas, ya encontraremos el tiempo para hacerlo nosotros "
"mismos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an anvil"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "If you can't find one, maybe you can make one for me."
msgstr "Si no puedes encontrar uno, tal vez puedas hacer uno para mí."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an anvil"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "Do you have the anvil?"
msgstr "¿Tienes el yunque?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an anvil"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I appreciate it, this will really make a difference, here's some horse armor"
" I've been working on.  Eventually I'll have the whole herd outfitted."
msgstr ""
"Lo aprecio, esto realmente marcará la diferencia, aquí hay una armadura de "
"caballo en la que he estado trabajando. Eventualmente tendré a toda la "
"manada equipada."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "Find Chris Isherwood"
msgstr "Encuentra a Chris Isherwood"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Chris Isherwood"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Chris hasn't come back from his latest search for Barry, I'm getting "
"concerned."
msgstr ""
"Chris no ha regresado de su última búsqueda por Barry, me estoy preocupando."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Chris Isherwood"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "Can you go find my son and tell him to check in with us."
msgstr ""
"¿Puedes ir a buscar a mi hijo y decirle que se ponga en contacto con "
"nosotros?."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Chris Isherwood"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "Oh well.  I hope he turns up soon."
msgstr "Oh, bien. Espero que aparezca pronto."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Chris Isherwood"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"He might be on the property somewhere, maybe by that old cabin near the "
"entrance, sometimes he camps there."
msgstr ""
"Puede que esté en la propiedad en algún sitio, tal vez cerca de la vieja "
"cabaña, en la entrada, a veces acampa allí."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Chris Isherwood"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Thanks, I was getting ready to go look myself.  Now that I have the anvil, "
"I've been working on new armor for the horses, take this prototype I made."
msgstr ""
"Gracias, me estaba preparando para ir a ver yo mismo. Ahora que tengo el "
"yunque, he estado trabajando en una nueva armadura para los caballos, "
"llévate este prototipo que he hecho."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Chris Isherwood"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
msgid "I hope he didn't meet Barry's fate…"
msgstr "Espero que no haya encontrado el destino de Barry..."

#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Part of the Isherwood family.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid "Chris Isherwood"
msgstr "Chris Isherwood"

#. ~ Job description of "Chris Isherwood" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid "I'm Jesse and Carlos' son, part of the Isherwood family"
msgstr "Soy el hijo de Jesse y Carlos, parte de la familia Isherwood."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I see that badge.  You need to leave our land, my relatives have no fondness"
" for Marshals."
msgstr ""
"Veo esa placa. Tienes que dejar nuestra tierra, mis parientes no tienen "
"ningún cariño por los Alguaciles."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hi, what's up?"
msgstr "Hola, ¿qué pasa?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Hi, Your dad asked me to come find you, said you've been looking for your "
"uncle."
msgstr ""
"Hola, tu padre me pidió que viniera a buscarte, dijo que has estado buscando"
" a tu tío."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I was talking to Luke earlier, said you had some interesting ideas about the"
" world ending.  Is it tied to Barry's abduction?"
msgstr ""
"Estuve hablando con Luke antes, dijo que tenías algunas ideas interesantes "
"sobre el fin del mundo. ¿Está relacionado con el secuestro de Barry?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, they are always worried about us, I prefer to survey the land and try "
"to track the changes.  I'm thinking about fixing up this cabin for some "
"peace and quiet…"
msgstr ""
"Sí, siempre están preocupados por nosotros, prefiero hacer un reconocimiento"
" de la tierra y tratar de seguir los cambios. Estoy pensando en arreglar "
"esta cabaña para tener un poco de paz y tranquilidad..."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid "Sounds like you are restless, why not leave?"
msgstr "Parece que estás inquieto, ¿por qué no te vas?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid "What sort of changes have you seen?"
msgstr "¿Qué tipo de cambios has visto?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I was talking to Luke earlier, said you had some interesting ideas about the"
" world ending."
msgstr ""
"Estuve hablando con Luke antes, dijo que tenías algunas ideas interesantes "
"sobre el fin del mundo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"My family is convinced that if we stay here, we'll be able to weather this "
"catastrophe.  Since technology has failed, they've doubled down on older "
"traditions.  I think we need to get out there and find some answers before "
"settling on a path."
msgstr ""
"Mi familia está convencida de que si nos quedamos aquí, podremos capear esta"
" catástrofe. Dado que la tecnología ha fallado, han doblado las viejas "
"tradiciones. Creo que tenemos que salir y encontrar algunas respuestas antes"
" de emprender el camino."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"In one of my longer trips looking for Barry, I saw something out in a field."
"  I didn't get close but I swear unbelievable monsters were coming out of "
"it.  It kinda shimmered, almost like it wasn't quite there.  I've been "
"tracking those monsters for a while…"
msgstr ""
"En uno de mis viajes más largos buscando a Barry, vi algo en un campo. No me"
" acerqué, pero juro que monstruos increíbles salían de él. Se iluminó un "
"poco, casi como si no estuviera allí. He estado siguiendo a esos monstruos "
"por un tiempo..."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid "What did you find?"
msgstr "¿Qué has encontrado?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"They made their way to this weird spire like structure, I've never seen "
"anything like it, it glistened in the sun like something organic.  I think "
"they could be holding Barry there, I've seen them arrive and leave with "
"other humans."
msgstr ""
"Se dirigieron a esta extraña estructura en forma de aguja, nunca he visto "
"nada como esto, brillaba en el sol como algo orgánico. Creo que podrían "
"estar reteniendo a Barry allí, los he visto llegar y salir con otros "
"humanos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"If you join up with me, we can go check it out, I want to see what they are "
"doing."
msgstr ""
"Si te unes a mí, podemos ir a comprobarlo, quiero ver lo que están haciendo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Well, wildlife is more hostile and I've seen gigantic insects around, never "
"mind all these monsters.  I've also found mysterious dead spots and mutated "
"vegetation.  I don't think staying on a farm is sustainable forever, there "
"are big planet wide changes occurring."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, la vida salvaje es más hostil y he visto insectos gigantes alrededor,"
" sin importar todos estos monstruos. También he encontrado misteriosos "
"puntos muertos y vegetación mutada. No creo que quedarse en una granja sea "
"sostenible para siempre, hay grandes cambios en el planeta."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid "You should leave before my family sees you."
msgstr "Deberías irte antes de que mi familia te vea."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Your dad asked me to come find you, said you've been looking for your uncle."
msgstr ""
"Tu padre me pidió que viniera a buscarte, dijo que has estado buscando a tu "
"tío."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I was talking to Luke earlier, he said you had some interesting ideas about "
"the world ending."
msgstr ""
"Estuve hablando con Luke antes, dijo que tenías algunas ideas interesantes "
"sobre el fin del mundo."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
msgstr "Libera a Barry de la estructura misteriosa"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"We need to investigate the alien encampment and try to find out what "
"happened to Barry."
msgstr ""
"Tenemos que investigar el campamento alienígena e intentar averiguar qué le "
"ocurrió a Barry."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid "I can take you to the structure, I tracked them to it."
msgstr "Puedo llevarlos a la estructura, los he seguido hasta ella."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid "Awesome, I want some answers!"
msgstr "¡Increíble, quiero algunas respuestas!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid "Thanks anyway, I'll keep my eye on it, maybe I'll find a way one day."
msgstr ""
"Gracias de todos modos, le echaré un vistazo, tal vez algún día encuentre la"
" manera."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I feel like we are underprepared if they see us, I marked the location for "
"you."
msgstr ""
"Siento que no estamos preparados si nos ven, te he marcado la ubicación."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid "You ready?"
msgstr "¿Estás listo?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"It's taller then I remember, we should look for prisoners.  I left a note "
"for my family before we left.  If we survive, the cabin should be fixed up "
"and ready for you to move in if you want to stay."
msgstr ""
"Es más alto de lo que recuerdo, deberíamos buscar a los prisioneros. Dejé "
"una nota para mi familia antes de irnos. Si sobrevivimos, la cabaña debería "
"estar arreglada y lista para que te mudes si quieres quedarte."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
msgid "Well it was here…"
msgstr "Bien, estuvo aquí..."

#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ Matriarch of the Isherwood family.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "Claire Isherwood"
msgstr "Claire Isherwood"

#. ~ Job description of "Claire Isherwood" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "I'm the matriarch of the Isherwood family"
msgstr "Soy la matriarca de la familia Isherwood"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Is that a U.S. Marshal's badge you're wearing?"
msgstr "¿Es una insignia de Alguacil U.S.  la que llevas?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hello, what brings you here?"
msgstr "Hola, ¿qué te trae por aquí?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hi, what brings you here?"
msgstr "Hola, ¿qué te trae por aquí?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Yes, I'm a marshal."
msgstr "Sí, soy un alguacil."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hi, nice farm you have here."
msgstr "Hola, bonita granja la que tienes aquí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hi, Jack suggested I stop by and say hello."
msgstr "Hola, Jack sugirió que me pasara a saludar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/ROBOFAC_SURFACE_FREEMERCHANT.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_FORGE_ARDELIA.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_FORGE_HELEN_TAVREL.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_FORGE_MERCHANT.json
msgid "Let's trade."
msgstr "Comerciemos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hey, when would more of this stuff be ready?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Around <interval>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Alright then, bye."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "I live here with my husband, Jack.  He is working out in his shop."
msgstr "Vivo aquí con mi marido, Jack. Está trabajando en su tienda."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "You are lucky to have your family still together."
msgstr "Tienes suerte de tener a tu familia todavía junta."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "Must be nice, to have the quiet place amid so much madness."
msgstr ""
"Debe ser agradable, tener un lugar tranquilo en medio de tanta locura."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"You don't need as much luck if you are prepared and work together.  We've "
"had our losses, my brother in law, Barry, was our best hunter but things are"
" so different now…"
msgstr ""
"No necesitas tanta suerte si estás preparado y trabajas en equipo. Hemos "
"tenido nuestras pérdidas, mi cuñado, Barry, era nuestro mejor cazador pero "
"las cosas son tan diferentes ahora..."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "What happened to Barry?"
msgstr "¿Qué le pasó a Barry?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "A farm must be a pretty safe place these days."
msgstr "Una granja debe ser un lugar bastante seguro en estos días."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Well, nice to meet you.  I imagine Jack was boasting about my herbal "
"remedies, he's proud of what we've put together here."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, encantado de conocerte. Imagino que Jack estaba presumiendo de mis "
"remedios herbales, está orgulloso de lo que hemos reunido aquí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "He did mention you make remedies, are they effective?"
msgstr "Mencionó que haces remedios, ¿son efectivos?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "I'd like to ask you something else…"
msgstr "Me gustaría preguntarle algo más..."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I have always studied and made some natural remedies, but now they are more "
"essential than ever.  Who knows the next time we'll see a trained doctor.  "
"These remedies aren't always as effective, but they can do the job in a "
"pinch."
msgstr ""
"Siempre he estudiado e inventado algunos remedios naturales, pero ahora son "
"más esenciales que nunca. Quién sabe si la próxima vez veremos a un médico "
"capacitado. Estos remedios no siempre son tan efectivos, pero pueden hacer "
"el trabajo en caso de necesidad."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Some of their cows were killed before we realized what was happening, Barry "
"and Carlos went into the forest to find the predator but it was like nothing"
" they'd ever seen.  Carlos may be willing to tell you more."
msgstr ""
"Algunas de sus vacas fueron asesinadas antes de que nos diéramos cuenta de "
"lo que estaba pasando, Barry y Carlos fueron al bosque para encontrar al "
"depredador, pero no se parecía a nada de lo que habían visto. Carlos puede "
"estar dispuesto a contarles más."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"We've always tried to live a quiet life out here, I suppose we are doing "
"better than most."
msgstr ""
"Siempre hemos tratado de vivir una vida tranquila aquí, supongo que nos va "
"mejor que a la mayoría."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Jack and I have been together for 40 years.  He's been my anchor through all"
" of this chaos."
msgstr ""
"Jack y yo hemos estado juntos durante 40 años. Ha sido mi ancla en todo este"
" caos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Jesse and her family live up at the horse farm.  They may have some jobs for"
" you."
msgstr ""
"Jesse y su familia viven en la granja de caballos. Puede que tengan algunos "
"trabajos para ti."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Eddie's dairy is at the end of the road.  He's may have some jobs for you if"
" you are interested."
msgstr ""
"La lechería de Eddie está al final del camino. Puede que tenga algunos "
"trabajos para ti si estás interesado."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "You should get off our land, you have no business here."
msgstr "Deberías salir de nuestra tierra, no tienes nada que hacer aquí."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "Ask away."
msgstr "Pregunte."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "Tell me about your husband, is he around?"
msgstr "Hábleme de su marido, ¿está por aquí?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Your daughter lives down the road?"
msgstr "¿Su hija vive bajando por la carretera?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Where is your brother's place?"
msgstr "¿Dónde está la casa de su hermano?"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "Gather 50 dandelions"
msgstr "Reúne 50 dientes de león"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 dandelions"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "I could use some help foraging ingredients."
msgstr ""
"Me vendría bien algo de ayuda para buscar ingredientes para la comida."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 dandelions"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I could use some fresh dandelions for the next batch of wine.  Can you bring"
" me 50 dandelions?"
msgstr ""
"Me vendrían bien unos dientes de león frescos para la próxima tanda de vino."
" ¿Puedes traerme 50 dientes de león?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 dandelions"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "Thank you, I'll put these to good use."
msgstr "Gracias, les daré un buen uso."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 dandelions"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 bee balm seeds"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "Oh well.  Maybe some other time, thanks."
msgstr "Oh, bueno. Tal vez en otro momento, gracias."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 dandelions"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "You can find them in the fields during the spring and summer months."
msgstr ""
"Los puedes encontrar en los campos durante los meses de primavera y verano."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 dandelions"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "Thanks.  Here's a small reward to show my appreciation for your help."
msgstr ""
"Gracias. Aquí hay una pequeña recompensa para mostrar mi aprecio por tu "
"ayuda."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 dandelions"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "I wonder if the wildlife ate all the greens…"
msgstr "Me pregunto si la vida silvestre se ha comido todo lo verde..."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "Find 20 bee balm seeds"
msgstr "Encuentra 20 semillas de bálsamo de abeja"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 bee balm seeds"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "I could use some seeds from the forest."
msgstr "Me vendrían bien algunas semillas del bosque."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 bee balm seeds"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"We could use some seeds for the next planting season.  Can you bring me 20 "
"bee balm seeds?"
msgstr ""
"Podríamos usar algunas semillas para la próxima temporada de siembra. "
"¿Puedes traerme 20 semillas de bergamota?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 bee balm seeds"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Thank you.  It's important to have a good stock before the flu season hits."
msgstr ""
"Gracias. Es importante tener una buena reserva antes de que llegue la "
"temporada de gripe."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 bee balm seeds"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"You should search through the forest, make sure to check in the underbrush "
"for bee balm and then harvest its seeds."
msgstr ""
"Deberías buscar en el bosque y asegurarte de buscar entre la maleza para "
"encontrar monardas y recolectar sus semillas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 bee balm seeds"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Wow, perfect.  Here are some of my own remedies and if those don't work try "
"my other gift."
msgstr ""
"Vaya, perfecto. Aquí hay algunos de mis propios remedios y si no funcionan, "
"prueba mi otro regalo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 bee balm seeds"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "I'll have to find someone more at home in the forest…"
msgstr "Tendré que encontrar a alguien más en casa en el bosque..."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "Find and capture a cat"
msgstr "Encuentra y captura un gato"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "I could use a barn cat to keep the mice down."
msgstr ""
"Podría usar un gato de granero para mantener a los ratones bajo control."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I saw some feral cats out by the old cabin.  Can you capture one for me?"
msgstr ""
"Vi algunos gatos salvajes en la vieja cabaña. ¿Puedes atrapar uno para mí?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Thank you!  Please hurry back!  Take this cage so you have a chance of "
"capturing one."
msgstr ""
"¡Gracias! ¡Por favor, regresa rápido! Toma esta jaula para que tengas la "
"oportunidad de capturar a uno."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "I didn't want to use chemicals on these rats."
msgstr "Yo no qui usar químicos en estas ratas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Take this pet carrier; if you can get close to a cat, you can put it inside."
"  If you're having problems, try befriending it with cat food."
msgstr ""
"Toma este porta-mascotas; si puedes acercarte a un gato, puedes ponerlo "
"dentro. Si tienes problemas, intenta hacerte su amigo con comida para gatos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "Have you found a cat?"
msgstr "¿Has encontrado un gato?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Thank you so much, I want you to have this copy of my natural remedy "
"journal.  I'll name this handsome fellow Joshua."
msgstr ""
"Muchas gracias, quiero que tengas esta copia de mi diario de remedios "
"naturales. Nombraré a este guapo compañero como Joshua."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "What?!  You're lying, I can tell!  Did you even bring back my cage?"
msgstr "¿Qué? ¡Estás mintiendo, lo sé! ¿Al menos me trajiste mi jaula?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
msgid "Oh no!  I guess they are too nimble for you…"
msgstr "¡Oh no! Asumo que son demasiado ágiles para ti..."

#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Dairy farmer of the Isherwood family.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "Eddie Isherwood"
msgstr "Eddie Isherwood"

#. ~ Job description of "Eddie Isherwood" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "I'm a dairy farmer, part of the Isherwood family"
msgstr "Soy un granjero lechero, parte de la familia Isherwood."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "Nice dairy, must be tough keeping it running."
msgstr "Bonita lechería, debe ser difícil mantenerla en funcionamiento."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hi, Jack and Claire suggested I come down here and meet you."
msgstr "Hola, Jack y Claire me sugirieron que viniera a conocerle."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "When will your cows produce again?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "If the cows don't get anything nasty it should be around <interval>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "Cheers, bye."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I run this dairy with my son, Luke.  It's been a tough job keeping the herd "
"together, hasn't left a lot of time for other projects."
msgstr ""
"Dirijo esta lechería con mi hijo, Luke. Ha sido un trabajo duro mantener el "
"rebaño unido, no me ha dejado mucho tiempo para otros proyectos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I heard about Barry, such a tragedy.  Can you tell me more about what "
"happened?"
msgstr ""
"Me enteré de lo de Barry, una tragedia tan grande. ¿Puedes contarme más "
"sobre lo que pasó?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Barry and Carlos went to hunt down something that killed our livestock, they"
" tracked it into the forest.  It grabbed Barry and ran off, you might be "
"able to get Carlos to tell you the story, if he can bring himself to share "
"what happened."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, I could use some help getting materials.  I want to outfit that old "
"building across the road with some kilns.  We want to make our own jars and "
"pottery so we aren't dependent on scavenging."
msgstr ""
"Sí, me vendría bien algo de ayuda para conseguir materiales. Quiero equipar "
"ese viejo edificio de enfrente con algunos hornos. Queremos hacer nuestros "
"propios frascos y cerámica para no depender de la recolección."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "That is a good idea, what do you need?"
msgstr "Es una buena idea, ¿qué necesitas?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "I'm not interested right now, I'd better get going."
msgstr "No estoy interesado ahora mismo, mejor me voy."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Luke was going to start college this year, now everything is upside down.  "
"He is adaptable though, had an idea to begin manufacturing our own jars and "
"pottery.  He's out in the old outbuilding right now, cleaning up the place."
msgstr ""
"Luke iba a empezar la universidad este año, ahora todo patas arriba. Sin "
"embargo, es flexible, tuvo una idea para empezar a fabricar nuestros propios"
" tarros y piezas de cerámica. Ahora mismo está en la vieja estructura "
"externa, limpiando el lugar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Jesse manages the horses and other livestock, she is amazing with animals."
msgstr ""
"Jesse maneja los caballos y el resto del ganado, es increíble con los "
"animales."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Carlos will be in his workshop if he isn't out hunting.  He is trying to get"
" a forge set up."
msgstr ""
"Carlos estará en su taller si no está cazando. Está intentando montar una "
"forja."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "Your son helps with the dairy?"
msgstr "¿tu hijo ayuda con la lechería?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "So, Jesse runs the horse farm?"
msgstr "Entonces, ¿Jesse dirige la granja de caballos?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "Where can I find Carlos?"
msgstr "¿Dónde puedo encontrar a Carlos?"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "Gather 120 Rocks"
msgstr "Recoger 120 rocas"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 120 Rocks"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "We need to build some kilns."
msgstr "Necesitamos construir algunos hornos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 120 Rocks"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "I could use 120 rocks to construct some kilns."
msgstr "Podría usar 120 piedras para construir algunos hornos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 120 Rocks"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"You can break up some larger stones, or gather them up from the fields."
msgstr ""
"Puedes romper algunas piedras más grandes, o recogerlas de los campos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 120 Rocks"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "Thanks anyway, we'll find the time to get them ourselves."
msgstr ""
"Gracias de todos formas, ya encontraremos el tiempo para conseguirlos "
"nosotros mismos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 120 Rocks"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 75 Rocks"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
msgid "Mining would always be an option if you had the resources."
msgstr "La minería siempre sería una opción si tuvieras los recursos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 120 Rocks"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Season Of The Stones"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/missions.json
msgid "Do you have the stone?"
msgstr "¿Tienes una piedra?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 120 Rocks"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "I appreciate it, this will make Luke happy."
msgstr "Te lo agradezco, esto hará feliz a Luke."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "Gather 2000 units of sand"
msgstr "Reúne 2000 unidades de arena"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2000 units of sand"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "I do have some resource gathering I could use help with."
msgstr ""
"Creo que tengo algunos recursos recogidos con los que podría ayudarte."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2000 units of sand"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Now that the forge is set up, we could use 2000 units of sand to get "
"production going."
msgstr ""
"Ahora que la forja está instalada, podríamos usar 2000 unidades de arena "
"para poner en marcha la producción."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2000 units of sand"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 100 units of clay"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "Oh well.  I'll try to find time to get it myself, thanks."
msgstr ""
"Oh, bueno. Intentaré encontrar tiempo para conseguirlo yo mismo, gracias."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2000 units of sand"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"You can find it along river banks, or maybe landscaping supplies and "
"hardware stores."
msgstr ""
"Puedes encontrarlo a lo largo de las orillas del río, o tal vez en los "
"suministros de jardinería y ferreterías."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2000 units of sand"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "Thanks, now Luke can get started.  Here's a token of my thanks."
msgstr ""
"Gracias, ahora Luke puede empezar. Aquí tienes una muestra de mi aprecio."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2000 units of sand"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 100 units of clay"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "I wonder where all the sand went…"
msgstr "Me pregunto dónde se fue toda la arena..."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "Gather 100 units of clay"
msgstr "Reúne 1000 unidades de arcilla"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 100 units of clay"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid "I do have some resource gathering I could use help if you have time."
msgstr ""
"Tengo algunos recursos que debo recolectar, podría utilizar tu ayuda si "
"tienes tiempo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 100 units of clay"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Now that the clay kiln is set up, we could use 100 units of clay to get "
"production going."
msgstr ""
"Ahora que el horno de arcilla está instalado, podríamos usar 1000 unidades "
"de arcilla para poner en marcha la producción."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 100 units of clay"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"You can find it along river banks, or maybe look for deposits in the forest."
msgstr ""
"Puedes encontrarlo a lo largo de las orillas del río, o tal vez buscar "
"depósitos en el bosque."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 100 units of clay"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Thanks, now Luke can get started making jugs, We'd like to give you a cow, "
"Here's Daisy, take good care of her and she'll provide you with milk."
msgstr ""
"Gracias, ahora Luke puede empezar a hacer jarras, Nos gustaría darte una "
"vaca, Aquí está Daisy, cuídala bien y te dará leche."

#. ~ Nickname for creature 'mon_cow'
#. ~ Snippet in category "<dog_name>"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/snippets/snippets.json
msgid "Daisy"
msgstr "Daisy"

#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Patriarch of the Isherwood family.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Jack Isherwood"
msgstr "Jack Isherwood"

#. ~ Job description of "Jack Isherwood" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "I'm the patriarch of the Isherwood family"
msgstr "Soy el patriarca de la familia Isherwood"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hello traveler, what brings you here?"
msgstr "Hola viajero, ¿qué te trae por aquí?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "I'm here to deliver some resources."
msgstr "Estoy aquí para entregar algunos recursos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "This is a lot of land, you been here since the collapse?"
msgstr "Es mucha tierra, ¿has estado aquí desde el colapso?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I live here with my wife, this is our family's land.  My daughter's family "
"and son live down the road."
msgstr ""
"Vivo aquí con mi esposa, esta es la tierra de nuestra familia. La familia de"
" mi hija y mi hijo viven en la carretera."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Your whole family survived?"
msgstr "¿Toda tu familia sobrevivió?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"We've had our losses… now we stay close to home, preparing for trouble.  "
"We've always taken disaster preparedness seriously, but we didn't expect "
"anything like this though."
msgstr ""
"Hemos tenido nuestras pérdidas... ahora nos quedamos cerca de casa, "
"preparándonos para los problemas. Siempre hemos tomado en serio la "
"preparación para desastres, pero no esperábamos nada como esto."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Even out here we've had some attacks and seen… other things.  We have been "
"working on our defenses, but it takes time.  We've been able to keep up with"
" the crops and animals though so we won't have to risk our necks for "
"supplies."
msgstr ""
"Incluso aquí hemos tenido algunos ataques y hemos visto... otras cosas. "
"Hemos estado trabajando en nuestras defensas, pero lleva tiempo. Hemos sido "
"capaces de mantenernos al día con los cultivos y los animales, así que no "
"tendremos que arriesgar el cuello por los suministros."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "What sort of defenses do you want?"
msgstr "¿Qué clase de defensas quieres?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"We want to put up more fencing and build some look out spots, maybe lay some"
" traps for the monsters.  We could use some extra resources.  If you want to"
" bring me logs, sand, clay, wire, nails, wood planks, and metal chunks, I'll"
" give you signed chits you can use to buy goods from any of the family."
msgstr ""
"Queremos poner más vallas y construir algunos puntos de observación, tal vez"
" poner algunas trampas para los monstruos. Podríamos usar algunos recursos "
"extra. Si quieres traerme leños, arena, arcilla, alambre, clavos, tablones "
"de madera y trozos de metal, te daré fichas firmadas que podrás usar para "
"comprar bienes de cualquiera de la familia."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Sounds reasonable, I'll see what I can do."
msgstr "Suena razonable, veré qué puedo hacer."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Claire and I have been together for 40 years now, couldn't run this place "
"without her.  She's quite the herbalist too, been real useful lately.  She "
"is probably in the house, you should stop in."
msgstr ""
"Claire y yo hemos estado juntos durante 40 años, no podríamos dirigir este "
"lugar sin ella. Ella también es una buena herbolaria, ha sido muy útil "
"últimamente. Probablemente esté en la casa, deberías pasarte por allí."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Jesse and her family live up at the horse farm.  Her husband, Carlos, may "
"have some jobs for you."
msgstr ""
"Jesse y su familia viven en la granja de caballos. Su marido, Carlos, puede "
"que tenga algunos trabajos para ti."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Eddie's dairy is at the end of the road.  It's just him and his son since "
"Barry was taken by that thing in the woods."
msgstr ""
"La lechería de Eddie está al final del camino. Es sólo él y su hijo desde "
"que Barry fue llevado por esa cosa en el bosque."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"You should get off my land, the government proved its incompetence with this"
" catastrophe."
msgstr ""
"Deberías salir de mi tierra, el gobierno demostró su incompetencia con esta "
"catástrofe."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Tell me about your wife, is she around?"
msgstr "Hábleme de su esposa, ¿está por aquí?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
msgid "Excellent.  What've you brought us?"
msgstr "Excelente. ¿Qué nos has traído?"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Find 10 3L jars"
msgstr "Encuentra 10 tarros de 3L"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 3L jars"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "I could use some help scavenging."
msgstr "Me vendría bien un poco de ayuda para rebuscar."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 3L jars"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"We could use some 3 liter jars to preserve our produce.  Can you bring me 10"
" large three liter jars?  I'll give you some preserves in exchange."
msgstr ""
"Podríamos usar unos tarros de 3 litros para preservar nuestros productos. "
"¿Puedes traerme 20 tarros grandes de tres litros? Te los intercambiaré por "
"algunas conservas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 3L jars"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Thank you.  It's important to preserve foods while we can."
msgstr "Gracias. Es importante preservar los alimentos mientras podamos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 3L jars"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Oh well.  I'll see if I can find another way, thanks."
msgstr "Oh, bien. Veré si puedo encontrar otra manera, gracias."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 3L jars"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 100 wheat seeds"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle Pt. 2"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Grocery stores, house kitchens, there's plenty of places to look."
msgstr ""
"Tiendas de comestibles, cocinas de casa, hay muchos lugares donde buscar."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 3L jars"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 100 wheat seeds"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Wow, perfect.  Thanks.  Here's your reward."
msgstr "Vaya, perfecto. Gracias. Aquí está tu recompensa."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 3L jars"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle Pt. 2"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
msgid "I wonder where all the jars went…"
msgstr "Me pregunto adónde fueron todos los tarros..."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Find 100 wheat seeds"
msgstr "Encuentra 100 semillas de trigo"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 100 wheat seeds"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "I do have some more scavenging for you."
msgstr "Tengo algo más de recolección para ti."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 100 wheat seeds"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"We could use some seeds for the next planting season.  Can you bring me 100 "
"wheat seeds?  I'll give you some fresh produce."
msgstr ""
"Podríamos usar algunas semillas para la próxima temporada de siembra. "
"¿Puedes traerme 100 semillas de trigo? Te daré a cambios algunos productos "
"frescos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 100 wheat seeds"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "Thank you.  It's important to preserve healthy foods while we can."
msgstr ""
"Gracias. Es importante preservar los alimentos saludables mientras podamos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 100 wheat seeds"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle Pt. 2"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
msgid "Oh well.  I'll see if I can find another supplier, thanks."
msgstr "Oh, bueno. Ya buscaré otro proveedor, gracias."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 100 wheat seeds"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
msgid "I wonder where all the seeds went…"
msgstr "Me pregunto a dónde fueron todas las semillas..."

#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ Horse trainer for the Isherwood family.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Jesse Isherwood"
msgstr "Jesse Isherwood"

#. ~ Job description of "Jesse Isherwood" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "I'm a horse trainer, part of the Isherwood family"
msgstr "Soy un entrenador de caballos, parte de la familia Isherwood."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Leave our property, Marshal."
msgstr "Deje nuestra propiedad, Alguacil."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hello.  We don't see many people these days."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hi, it looks like you are doing well here."
msgstr "Hola, parece que te va bien aquí."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"It would be a lot harder without family.  Keeping the animals safe is "
"essential to our future."
msgstr ""
"Sería mucho más difícil sin la familia. Mantener a los animales a salvo es "
"esencial para nuestro futuro."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Sounds like you are betting on civilization not coming back."
msgstr "Suena como si apostaras a que la civilización no volvería."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Do you have any animal care tips?"
msgstr "¿Tienes algún consejo para el cuidado de los animales?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"We can't wait for someone else to fix things, we need to take care of "
"ourselves."
msgstr ""
"No podemos esperar a que alguien más arregle las cosas, tenemos que "
"cuidarnos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Horses make good all around companions.  They can get places that cars can't"
" and also help when all the engines fail.  They become very trusting if you "
"feed them some nice fodder."
msgstr ""
"Los caballos son buenos compañeros. Pueden llegar a lugares que los coches "
"no pueden y también ayudan cuando todos los motores fallan. Se vuelven muy "
"confiados si les das un buen forraje."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Oh good, I'm sure Jack wanted to put you to work.  If you're interested, I "
"could use a hand clearing out the woods.  My son, Chris has his hands full "
"trying to keep the predators under control."
msgstr ""
"Oh bien, estoy seguro de que Jack quería ponerte a trabajar. Si te interesa,"
" me vendría bien una mano para limpiar el bosque. Mi hijo, Chris tiene las "
"manos llenas tratando de mantener a los depredadores bajo control."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "I'd like to speak with Carlos too about some work."
msgstr "También me gustaría hablar con Carlos sobre algo de trabajo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Is Chris around?  I'd like to know what he's run into out in the woods."
msgstr ""
"¿Está Chris por aquí? Me gustaría saber con qué se encontró en el bosque."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "What needs killing?"
msgstr "¿Qué hay que matar?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "He's out back in the workshop."
msgstr "Está atrás en el taller."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"He's out doing some surveying, we are planning on adding a fence line and "
"some defenses."
msgstr ""
"Está fuera haciendo algunas mediciones, estamos planeando añadir una línea "
"de vallas y algunas defensas."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "You should get off my farm, I won't deal with a government stooge."
msgstr ""
"Deberías salir de mi granja, no voy a tratar con un títere del gobierno."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Looks like you are doing well here."
msgstr "Parece que te va bien aquí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Jack and Claire suggested I come talk to you."
msgstr "Jack y Claire me sugirieron que viniera a hablar contigo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Is Chris around?"
msgstr "¿Está Chris por aquí?"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Kill wolves"
msgstr "Matar lobos"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill wolves"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "We could use some help killing some wolves."
msgstr "Nos vendría bien algo de ayuda para matar algunos lobos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill wolves"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"There's been some wolves that keep scaring our chickens and horses, I'd be "
"grateful if you can kill them."
msgstr ""
"Ha habido algunos lobos que no dejan de asustar a nuestras gallinas y "
"caballos, te agradecería que acabaras con ellos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill wolves"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Wonderful, let me know when it is done."
msgstr "Maravilloso, avísame cuando esté hecho."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill wolves"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill monsters"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Thanks anyway, we will try some traps."
msgstr "Gracias de todas formas, probaremos con algunas trampas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill wolves"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill monsters"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "A gun will probably help."
msgstr "Un arma probablemente ayudariá."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill wolves"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill monsters"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Did you kill it?"
msgstr "¿Lo mataste?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill wolves"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I appreciate it, I've got this old saddle I want you to have.  I'll be happy"
" to put a horse under it if you want to do some more heroics."
msgstr ""
"Te lo agradezco, tengo esta vieja silla de montar que quiero que tengas. "
"Estaré encantado de ponersela al caballo que quieras si pudieras hacer algo "
"más heroico."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill wolves"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill monsters"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Show me the bodies."
msgstr "Muéstrame los cuerpos."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Kill monsters"
msgstr "Matar monstruos"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill monsters"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "We could use some help killing some monsters."
msgstr "Nos vendría bien algo de ayuda para matar a algunos monstruos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill monsters"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"We could use some help killing a pack of monsters.  I don't know what they "
"are, but they're very fast, I'm willing to outfit you with a horse if you "
"succeed."
msgstr ""
"Nos vendría bien algo de ayuda para matar a una manada de monstruos. No sé "
"qué son, pero son muy rápidos, estoy dispuesto a equiparte con un caballo si"
" tienes éxito."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill monsters"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Be ready for anything."
msgstr "Prepárate para cualquier cosa."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill monsters"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I appreciate it, this will help keep our animals safe.  This is, Steve, he's"
" a good, steady horse.  You should talk to Carlos about some armor for him."
msgstr ""
"Lo aprecio, esto ayudará a mantener a nuestros animales a salvo. Este es, "
"Steve, un caballo bueno y estable. Deberías hablar con Carlos sobre una "
"armadura para él."

#. ~ Nickname for creature 'mon_horse'
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
msgid "Steve"
msgstr "Steve"

#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ Part of the Isherwood family.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
msgid "Lisa Isherwood"
msgstr "Lisa Isherwood"

#. ~ Job description of "Lisa Isherwood" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
msgid "Part of the Isherwood family"
msgstr "Parte de la familia Isherwood"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hi, this is a nice farm, your family lives here?"
msgstr "Hola, esta es una linda granja, ¿tu familia vive aquí?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hi, I'm looking for Jesse."
msgstr "Hola, estoy buscando a Jesse."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hi, I'm looking for Chris."
msgstr "Hola, estoy buscando a Chris."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"My family owns all the land around here, my parents are out in the barn and "
"my other family is down he road."
msgstr ""
"Mi familia es dueña de todas las tierras de aquí, mis padres están en el "
"granero y mi otra familia está en el camino."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
msgid "Ok, I'll go find them."
msgstr "Bien, iré a buscarlos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Mom is in her office, in the barn.  Be careful that you don't let our horses"
" out."
msgstr ""
"Mamá está en su oficina, en el granero. Ten cuidado de no dejar salir a "
"nuestros caballos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
msgid "Chris is out hunting or something right now."
msgstr "Chris está fuera cazando o algo así ahora mismo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
msgid "Oh, ok."
msgstr "Oh, ok."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
msgid "Or something?"
msgstr "¿O algo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
msgid "Nice talking to you, bye."
msgstr "Encantado de hablar contigo, adiós."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Well he's supposed to be hunting, but since you've been talking to Luke, I "
"bet he mentioned Chris wants to learn more about the end of the world.  "
"Sometimes he'll take off for a few days and I end up patching him up so my "
"parents don't know he left the property."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, se supone que está cazando, pero ya que has estado hablando con Luke,"
" apuesto a que mencionó que Chris quiere aprender más sobre el fin del "
"mundo. A veces se va por unos días y termino curándolo para que mis padres "
"no sepan que se fue de la propiedad."

#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Dairy farmer's son in the Isherwood family.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "Luke Isherwood"
msgstr "Luke Isherwood"

#. ~ Job description of "Luke Isherwood" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "I'm Eddie's son, part of the Isherwood family"
msgstr "Soy el hijo de Eddie, parte de la familia Isherwood."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "I see that badge, you should leave before my father sees you."
msgstr "Si veo esa placa, deberías irte antes de que mi padre te vea."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "Your dad said you were out here fixing up this place."
msgstr "Tu padre dijo que estabas aquí arreglando este lugar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "Hey, what are you doing out here?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, I work on it when I have the time.  I can't leave the farm too long, "
"so I can't find some things I need."
msgstr ""
"Sí, trabajo en ello cuando tengo tiempo. No puedo dejar la granja mucho "
"tiempo, así que no puedo encontrar algunas cosas que necesito."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Must be tough having the world fall apart when you had you future to look "
"forward to."
msgstr ""
"Debe ser duro que el mundo se desmorone cuando tenías tu futuro por delante."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I've been cleaning up this old building to make it into a workshop.  I want "
"to put up a pottery kiln and forge.  My dad doesn't want me leaving the farm"
" to find some things, says it is too dangerous."
msgstr ""
"He estado limpiando este viejo edificio para convertirlo en un taller. "
"Quiero poner un horno de cerámica y forja. Mi padre no quiere que salga de "
"la granja para encontrar algunas cosas, dice que es demasiado peligroso."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I know all the grown-ups worry about us, but I think we can adapt better "
"than them in the long run.  Chris has some interesting thoughts on the "
"matter."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "What sort of ideas does Chris have?"
msgstr "¿Qué clase de ideas tiene Chris?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Things have been tough for my dad since Barry was captured.  He works till "
"he falls asleep most nights…"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Chris is a little older than me, he's up at the horse farm with his parents "
"and sister, Lisa."
msgstr ""
"Chris es un poco mayor que yo, está en la granja de caballos con sus padres "
"y su hermana, Lisa."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"Well, he doesn't agree that what we're doing here will last.  He thinks "
"things will only get worse.  It's tough to get the adults to listen though, "
"much less agree with his solution.  You can go talk to him more about it if "
"you want."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, el no está de acuerdo con que lo que estamos haciendo aquí dure. "
"Piensa que las cosas sólo empeorarán. Es difícil hacer que los adultos "
"escuchen, y mucho menos que estén de acuerdo con su solución. Puedes ir a "
"hablar más con él si quieres."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "You won't find any help here."
msgstr "No encontrarás ayuda aquí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "Tell me about your dad."
msgstr "Háblame de tu padre."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
msgstr "Encuentra el libro El Arte de Soplar Vidrio"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "I need more knowledge to get the glass blowing started."
msgstr "Necesito más conocimientos para empezar a soplar el vidrio."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I could really use a book on glass blowing.  With the internet gone, I don't"
" have any handy references."
msgstr ""
"Me vendría bien un libro sobre el soplado de vidrio. Con la desaparición de "
"Internet, no tengo ninguna referencia útil."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "Fantastic, I'm not supposed to leave our land."
msgstr "Fantástico, se supone que no debo dejar nuestra tierra."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "Oh well, figured I'd have to do a lot of practice anyway."
msgstr "Oh, bien, me imaginé que tendría que practicar mucho de todas formas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "A library, bookstore or a glass blower's studio should have one."
msgstr ""
"Una biblioteca, librería o un estudio de soplado de vidrio debería tener "
"uno."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of Homebrewer's Bible"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
msgid "Do you have the book?"
msgstr "¿Tienes el libro?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "I appreciate it, this will make my life so much easier."
msgstr "Te lo agradezco, esto hará mi vida mucho más fácil."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "I don't see a book…?"
msgstr "¿No veo un libro...?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "At least you escaped with your life…"
msgstr "Al menos escapaste con tu vida..."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
msgstr "Encuentra una copia del Compendio DIY(Hazlo Tu Mismo)."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "I need more knowledge to get better pottery."
msgstr "Necesito más conocimiento para mejorar la alfarería."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid ""
"I could really use the book, DIY Compendium.  With the internet gone, I "
"don't have any handy references."
msgstr ""
"Me vendría muy bien el libro Compendio de DIY(Hazlo Tu Mismo). Con la "
"desaparición de Internet, no tengo ninguna referencia útil."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
msgid "A library, bookstore should have one, schools are another good idea."
msgstr ""
"Una biblioteca, una librería debería tener una, las escuelas son otra buena "
"idea."

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Former prisoner with a melee or ranged weapon and prison clothing.
#. Sometimes they also have prison guards' gear.
#. ~ A naked prisoner trapped in a horrifying cage, watching horrible things
#. happen.
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
msgid "prisoner"
msgstr "prisionero"

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Former prisoner with a melee or ranged weapon and prison clothing.
#. Sometimes they also have prison guards' gear.
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "gatekeeper"
msgstr "portero"

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Former prisoner with a melee or ranged weapon and prison clothing.
#. Sometimes they also have prison guards' gear.
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "leader of prisoners"
msgstr "lider de prisioneros"

#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Skills intentionally kept low.  This character should probably have a
#. higher chance of having insanity type traits eventually.
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
msgid "Prisoner"
msgstr "Prisionero"

#. ~ Job description of "Prisoner" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "I'm here to kick ass."
msgstr "Estoy aquí para patear culos,"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Ok, sorry, I'm already leaving!"
msgstr "Vale, lo siento, ¡ya me voy!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Hey, <fuck_you>!"
msgstr "¡Oye, <fuck_you>!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Hey, who the fuck are you?  I haven't seen you 'round.  Ah, fuck it, it doesn't matter.\n"
"Here's the rules.  The first and most important one: ALWAYS CLOSE THE FUCKING ENTRY DOOR BEHIND YOUR ASS!  If you're okay with that, the following rules are: don't fuck with us, don't steal from us, don't start a fight without a reason with someone from us.  Got it, punk?  Now get lost."
msgstr ""
"Oye, ¿quién coño eres tú? No te he visto por aquí. Ah, a la mierda, no importa.\n"
"Estas son las reglas. La primera y más importante: ¡CIERRA SIEMPRE LA PUTA PUERTA DE ENTRADA DETRÁS DE TU CULO! Si te parece bien, las siguientes reglas son: no nos jodas, no nos robes, no empieces una pelea sin motivo con alguien de nosotros. ¿Entendido, gamberro? Ahora piérdete."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Yeah, I got it.  See ya."
msgstr "Sí, lo tengo. Nos vemos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "I just wanted to ask if you have a job for me."
msgstr "Sólo quería preguntar si tienen un trabajo para mí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"I'm just hungry, and I thought you might give me some food for some job."
msgstr ""
"Sólo tengo hambre, y pensé que podrías darme algo de comida a cambio de "
"trabajo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Can we just talk it over?"
msgstr "¿Podemos hablarlo?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Do I have a <swear> exclamation sign over my <swear> head, like I'm a "
"<swear> quest-giver from some <swear> video game?"
msgstr ""
"¿Tengo un <swear>signo de exclamación sobre mi <swear>cabeza, como si fuera "
"un <swear>buscador de algún <swear>videojuego?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "No, of course not!  Sorry, I'm leaving."
msgstr "No, por supuesto que no. Lo siento, me voy."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Are you deaf or stupid?  I said I don't give a fuck for you and your <swear>"
" problems.  Bother me one more time, and you'll regret that.  <get_lost>"
msgstr ""
"¿Eres sordo o estúpido? He dicho que me importa un carajo tú y tus "
"<swear>problemas. Moléstame una vez más y te arrepentirás. <get_lost>"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Ok, sorry, I promise I won't bother you anymore."
msgstr "Vale, lo siento, prometo que no te molestaré más."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "You think you're immortal, huh, <name_b>?"
msgstr "¿Te crees inmortal, eh,<name_b>?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Gee, what's the matter with you?  Okay, okay, I'm leaving."
msgstr "Caray, ¿qué te pasa? Vale, vale, me voy."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "It would be you who will regret talking to me like that."
msgstr "Serás tú quien se arrepienta de haberme hablado así."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Not so fast, I think you need to pay for breaking your promise and bothering"
" me.  Give me your shit, now!"
msgstr ""
"No tan rápido, creo que tienes que pagar por romper tu promesa y molestarme."
" ¡Dame tus cosas, ahora!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Please don't hurt me!  Take all that you want."
msgstr "¡Por favor, no me hagas daño! Toma todo lo que quieras."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "What, <no>!"
msgstr "¡Que, <no>!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "I have nothing more to say to you.  <get_lost>"
msgstr "No tengo nada más que decirte. <get_lost>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "So, what are you waiting for?"
msgstr "Entonces, ¿qué estas esperando?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"I don't know if you know, but there are sewers underneath the prison.  I was"
" planning an escape long before <the_cataclysm>, and while I was working on "
"cleaning the sewers, I noticed a damaged wall section.  There was a flow of "
"fresh air coming out of it, so I think it's leading to the surface.  It "
"could be your way to freedom.  Feel free to use it."
msgstr ""
"No sé si lo sabes, pero hay alcantarillas debajo de la prisión. Estaba "
"planeando una fuga mucho antes de <the_cataclysm>, y mientras trabajaba en "
"la limpieza de las alcantarillas, me di cuenta de una sección de muro "
"dañado. Había un flujo de aire fresco que salía de ella, así que creo que "
"lleva a la superficie. Podría ser tu camino a la libertad. Siéntete libre de"
" usarlo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "You are what you eat, as they say."
msgstr "Eres lo que comes, como dicen."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "It's you again."
msgstr "Eres tú otra vez."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Hello there.  Haven't seen you around before.  You must be from the other "
"wing.  Managed to survive, huh?"
msgstr ""
"Hola. No te he visto antes por aquí. Debes ser del otro pabellón. Te las "
"arreglaste para sobrevivir, ¿eh?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Yeah, I've been through situations far worse than that."
msgstr "Sí, he pasado por situaciones mucho peores que esa."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"It was a nightmare, lots of <zombies>, blood everywhere!  Thank god I'm "
"among living people again."
msgstr ""
"Fue una pesadilla, muchos <zombies>, sangre por todas partes. Gracias a Dios"
" estoy entre gente viva de nuevo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"[Cannibal] It's hard to die of hunger when there's so many tasty corpses "
"lying around."
msgstr ""
"[Canibal] Es difícil morir de hambre cuando hay tantos cadáveres sabrosos "
"por ahí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"I want to get out of this <swear> prison.  I hoped you could help me with "
"that."
msgstr ""
"Quiero salir de esta <swear> prisión. Esperaba que pudieras ayudarme con "
"eso."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "I'm on my way."
msgstr "Estoy en camino."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "I don't know if I'll take your advice, but thanks nevertheless."
msgstr "No sé si seguiré tu consejo, pero gracias de todos modos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Wait, what?  A <swear> can of beans?!  I went through hell to get this "
"<swear> thing for you, and all you give me as reward is a <swear> can of "
"beans?!  I demand something more substantial."
msgstr ""
"Espera, ¿qué? ¡¿Una <swear> lata de judías?! He pasado por un infierno para "
"conseguir esta <swear>cosa para ti, ¿y todo lo que me das como recompensa es"
" una <swear>lata de judías? Exijo algo más sustancial."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Nice talking to ya.  Farewell."
msgstr "Un placer hablar contigo. Hasta la vista."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Huh, even so?  I'm not saying I approve your… tastes, but I definitely "
"respect people who use all possibilities life has to offer."
msgstr ""
"Huh, ¿aún así? No digo que apruebe tus... gustos, pero definitivamente "
"respeto a la gente que utiliza todas las posibilidades que la vida le "
"ofrece."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Yeah, we share the same opinions on this matter."
msgstr "Sí, compartimos las mismas opiniones sobre este asunto."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Well, that's a boastful statement.  Not that I don't believe it, it's just…."
"  Ah, nevermind.  Let's get to the point.  What do you want?"
msgstr ""
"Bien, es una afirmación jactanciosa. No es que no lo crea, es sólo.... Ah, "
"no importa. Vayamos al grano. ¿Qué es lo que quieres?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Hold the horses, pal.  Nobody allowed you to stay here - yet."
msgstr ""
"Aguanta los caballos, amigo. Nadie te ha permitido quedarte aquí, todavía."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Please!  I don't want to go back there!  I'm tired and hungry!  I just need "
"time to rest!"
msgstr ""
"¡Por favor! ¡No quiero volver allí! Estoy cansado y hambriento. ¡Sólo "
"necesito tiempo para descansar!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Shit!  Looks like I'm on my own now.  Thanks for nothing.  Bye."
msgstr "¡Mierda! Parece que ahora estoy solo. Gracias por nada. Adiós."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"We don't have much space, and there's not much food.  Besides, I don't know "
"you at all, and something tells me you won't survive another day."
msgstr ""
"No tenemos mucho espacio y no hay mucha comida. Además, no te conozco de "
"nada, y algo me dice que no sobrevivirás un día más."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "[STR 11] I'm tougher than it seems!"
msgstr "[FUE 11] ¡Soy más duro de lo que parece!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "[Survival 2] I have some survival expertise!"
msgstr "[Supervivencia 2] ¡Tengo algo de experiencia en supervivencia!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "I guess I need to find some other place…"
msgstr "Supongo que tengo que encontrar otro lugar..."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"The answer is still no.  In fact it might be better for us to kill you right"
" away - you know, the less mouths to feed, the better.  But I'm in a good "
"mood today, so I've decided to help you get out of this island."
msgstr ""
"La respuesta sigue siendo no. De hecho, podría ser mejor para nosotros "
"matarte de inmediato, ya sabes, cuantas menos bocas que alimentar, mejor. "
"Pero hoy estoy de buen humor, así que he decidido ayudarte a salir de esta "
"isla."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Ok, I'm listening."
msgstr "Vale, te escucho."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "You know, I think I'll manage without your help.  Bye."
msgstr "Sabes, creo que me las arreglaré sin tu ayuda. Adiós."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "I need you to retrieve some stuff from a locked safe.  Interested?"
msgstr ""
"Necesito que recuperes algunas cosas de una caja fuerte cerrada. ¿Te "
"interesa?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "[Show the military id card] You mean this stuff?"
msgstr ""
"[Mostrar la tarjeta de identificación militar] ¿Te refieres a esta cosa?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "What's in the safe?"
msgstr "¿Qué hay en la caja fuerte?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "What for do you need it?"
msgstr "¿Para qué lo necesitas?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "schizo_self_talk"
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#: data/json/snippets/schizophrenia.json
msgid "Yeah, sure."
msgstr "Si, seguro."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "I have a bad feeling about this.  Sorry, I'll pass."
msgstr "Tengo un mal presentimiento sobre esto. Lo siento, paso."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"As I said, that's the thing I need.  You don't need to know what's that "
"exactly.  Just grab all things you find in the safe, and call it a day."
msgstr ""
"Como he dicho, eso es lo que necesito. No necesitas saber qué es eso "
"exactamente. Simplemente coge todas las cosas que encuentres en la caja "
"fuerte, y dalo por hecho."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "That's weird."
msgstr "Eso es raro."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Let's say that's none of your <swear> business.  Other questions?"
msgstr "Digamos que eso no es de tu <swear> incumbencia. ¿Otras preguntas?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Hey, where did you get it?  Nevermind, just give it to me.  Just <swear> "
"now."
msgstr ""
"Eh, ¿de dónde lo has sacado? No importa, sólo dámelo. Ahora <swear> mismo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Hey, no need to be hostile.  Here you go, I don't need it anyway."
msgstr ""
"Eh, no hay necesidad de ser hostil. Aquí tienes, no lo necesito de todos "
"modos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"I went through incredible hardships to get it.  Please, can I keep this to "
"myself?"
msgstr ""
"Pasé por grandes penurias para conseguirlo. Por favor, ¿podría quedarme con "
"esto?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"I killed tons of <zombies> while I was trying to get this thing.  Do you "
"really think you and your handful of losers pose a threat to me?"
msgstr ""
"Maté toneladas de<zombies> mientras intentaba conseguir esta cosa. "
"¿Realmente crees que tú y tu puñado de perdedores representais una amenaza "
"para mí?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Okay.  It was convincing.  I'll still get what I want, one way or another.  "
"You better watch your back from now on."
msgstr ""
"Bien. Fue convincente. Aún así conseguiré lo que quiero, de una forma u "
"otra. Será mejor que vigiles tu espalda a partir de ahora."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Noted.  Bye."
msgstr "Tomo nota. Adiós."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"I'm afraid you're not in the position to demand anything from me, <name_b>."
"  <get_lost>"
msgstr ""
"Me temo que no estás en posición de exigirme nada, <name_b>.  <get_lost>"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Hey, <fuck_you>!  You'll regret that!"
msgstr "¡Eh <fuck_you>! ¡Te vas a arrepentir!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Okay, fine.  Cheapskate!"
msgstr "De acuerdo, bien. ¡Tacaño!"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
msgstr "Coge La Cosa de la oficina del jefe"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Here's the job…"
msgstr "Este es el trabajo..."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"My snitch whispered in my ear that the thing I need is located in the "
"chief's safe in his office.  You need to crack it open and bring the "
"contents to me.  Don't try to use anything you find in there!  Just bring "
"all the stuff to me, and I'll help you.  Deal?"
msgstr ""
"Mi soplón me susurró al oído que lo que necesito se encuentra en la caja "
"fuerte del jefe en su oficina. Tienes que abrirla y traerme el contenido. "
"¡No intentes usar nada de lo que encuentres allí! Sólo tráeme todo el "
"material y te ayudaré. ¿Trato?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Great!  Don't forget that I need all stuff from the safe, try not to lose a "
"thing."
msgstr ""
"¡Genial! No olvides que necesito todas las cosas de la caja fuerte, trata de"
" no perder nada."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Fine, I'll get the thing in any case, sooner or later."
msgstr "Bien, lo conseguiré en cualquier caso, tarde o temprano."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"The chief's office is on the other side of the prison.  I think the road "
"there is full of <zombies>, so you better find a weapon.  Also you probably "
"will need some tools to crack the safe open."
msgstr ""
"La oficina del jefe está al otro lado de la prisión. Creo que el camino está"
" lleno de <zombies>, así que será mejor que encuentres un arma. También es "
"probable que necesites algunas herramientas para abrir la caja fuerte."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Did you get the stuff already?"
msgstr "¿Ya tienes las cosas?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"At last!  Give me a few moments to check if it isn't damaged.  Here, take "
"this for your troubles."
msgstr ""
"¡Por fin! Dame unos momentos para comprobar que no está dañado. Toma, coge "
"esto por tus problemas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find reference material about air rifles for
#. Jenny."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an electric motor"
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Huh.  This isn't going to work like I thought."
msgstr "Huh. Esto no va a funcionar como yo pensaba."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "You're useless.  I should've killed you when I met you."
msgstr "Eres un inútil. Debería haberte matado cuando te conocí."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "Hiya darlin', welcome to the shop."
msgstr "Hola, cariño, bienvenido al local."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "Hey, killer!  How's it going?"
msgstr "¡Eh, asesino! ¿Cómo va?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "You look like you haven't eaten in days."
msgstr "Parece como si no hubieras comido hace días."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "Still the apocalypse out there, huh?"
msgstr "Todavía está el apocalipsis ahí afuera, ¿eh?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "See anything you like?"
msgstr "¿Ves algo que te guste?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "About that contract…"
msgstr "Sobre ese contrato..."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "What's with all the weapons and armor?"
msgstr "¿Qué pasa con todas las armas y armaduras?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "Are you and Jay close?"
msgstr "¿Eres tú y Jay cercanos?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "[Motion to the sketches.] What is it that you are working on?"
msgstr "[Gesto hacia los bocetos.] ¿En qué estás trabajando?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"[Motion to the sketches.] You seem more excited about this stuff recently."
msgstr ""
"[Gesto hacia los bocetos.] Pareces más emocionado acerca de estas cosas, "
"últimamente."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "I'd like to know more about some of your 'special' projects."
msgstr "Me gustaría saber un poco más sobre tus proyectos 'especiales'."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"[Show the nomad jumpsuit blueprint.] Hey - I met a group with some "
"interesting ideas for armor design.  Is any of this of use to you?"
msgstr ""
"[Muestra un boceto de un mono de nómada.] Eh - Conocí un grupo de gente con "
"algunas ideas interesantes sobre diseño de armaduras. ¿Te sirve algo de "
"esto?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "[100 merch] I'd like to become a member of the co-op."
msgstr "[100 merc] Me gustaría ser miembro de la co-op"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "About those contracts…"
msgstr "Sobre esos contratos..."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "Why do you hate merch?"
msgstr "¿Por qué odias el merc?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "Could you make me a suit of armor?"
msgstr "¿Podrías hacerme una armadura?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "How is my armor coming?"
msgstr "¿Cómo va mi armadura?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"You mentioned you'd need some special materials to make that nomad armor?"
msgstr ""
"¿Mencionaste que necesitarías algunos materiales especiales para hacer esa "
"armadura nómada?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "Interesting.  When would be the next batch of merchandise ready?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "I heard you might want some metal…"
msgstr "Me dijeron que estabas interesado en un poco de metal…"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "With how the things are goin'? <interval>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "I'll leave you to your work then.  Bye."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"I'm Cody, was an engineer before everything went to hell.  I guess I still "
"am, but I don't have to consult anymore, so I consider that a plus at least."
msgstr ""
"Soy Cody, era ingeniero antes de que todo se convirtiera en un infierno. "
"Supongo que todavía lo soy pero ya no tengo que consultar, así que eso lo "
"considero algo bueno."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"I don't know if you've met Jay yet, but he and I split a garden out here.  "
"We both work - well, worked - in technology, and we were convinced the world"
" was ending so we both got property outside town.  We met when he moved in "
"next door.  So this is our little homestead with a few upgrades.  We aren't "
"really sweating property lines at this point."
msgstr ""
"No sé si ya conociste a Jay pero él y yo dividimos un jardín. Trabajamos los"
" dos - bueno, trabajábamos - en tecnología y estábamos convencidos de que el"
" mundo se terminaba así que los dos compramos propiedades fuera del pueblo. "
"Nos conocimos cuando se mudó al lado. Así que esta es nuestra pequeña "
"hacienda con algunas mejoras. No estamos preocupados por las medianeras en "
"este momento."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"I make them myself!  I've always loved traditional armaments and am a proud "
"member of the SCA!  Figured now that everything has gone to hell I can make "
"it a full-time thing.  Lots of survivors in need of a big ol' hammer or some"
" armored guards to keep the biters off."
msgstr ""
"¡Las hago yo mismo! Siempre me ha gustado el armamento tradicional y soy un "
"orgulloso miembro del SCA. Ahora que todo se ha ido al infierno, he pensado "
"que puedo dedicarme a ello a tiempo completo. Hay muchos supervivientes que "
"necesitan un gran martillo o unos guardabrazos blindados para mantener "
"alejados a los mordedores."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "It must take some serious equipment to make all this."
msgstr "Debe ser necesario un buen equipo para hacer todo esto."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"Well, what can I say, I had lots of disposable income.  Kept me busy and all"
" that.  So yeah, I've got a pretty impressive shop in the back."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, qué puedo decir, tenía muchos ingresos disponibles. Me mantenía "
"ocupada y esas cosas. Así que sí, tengo un local bastante impresionante en "
"la parte de atrás."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"[INT 8+] Still this is a lot of equipment.  Wouldn't it have been easier to "
"buy this stuff from a manufacturer?"
msgstr ""
"[INT 8+] Esto es mucho equipamiento. ¿No hubiera sido más fácil comprárselo "
"a un fabricante?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "Can anyone use the workshop?"
msgstr "¿Puede cualquiera usar el taller?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"Honey, I have a hard time finding a bra that fits.  Good luck finding a "
"breastplate."
msgstr ""
"Cariño, tuve problemas para encontrar un corpiño que me quede bien. Que "
"tengas suerte encontrando un peto."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"Tell me about it, finding anything that fits in this apocalypse has been a "
"nightmare."
msgstr ""
"Dímelo a mí, encontrar algo que encaje en este apocalipsis ha sido una "
"pesadilla."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "Oh, uh.  Right, uh."
msgstr "Oh, uh. Bueno, uh."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"Well, not *anyone*, but I've always been a believer in community.  The shop "
"is run as a co-op, so if you want access you'll have to buy a share.  As a "
"partial owner, you will have full access to the shop.  Shares are currently "
"100 merch; I hate the currency but it's the closest thing we've got to a "
"representation of labor."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, no *cualquiera* pero siempre tuve confianza en la comunidad. Este "
"local funciona como una cooperativa así que si quieres tener acceso vas a "
"tener que comprar una participación. Como dueño parcial, vas a tener acceso "
"completo al local. Las participaciones actualmente valen 100 merc, odio la "
"moneda pero es lo mejor que tenemos para representar el trabajo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "[100 merch] Yeah, I can do that."
msgstr "[100 merc] Sí, puedo pagar eso."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"There yah go, one co-op membership with your name on it.  Shop's in the "
"back, keep it tidy and share if anyone else is around workin'.  Just as a "
"heads-up, you'll need to bring your own charcoal.  There's a kiln in there "
"too, so if you got things to burn, just throw 'em in there there and light "
"up."
msgstr ""
"Aquí tienes, una membresía de la cooperativa con tu nombre. El local está en"
" la parte de atrás, mantén el orden y compartí el lugar si alguien más está "
"trabajando. Te aviso que vas a tener que traer tu propio carbón. Hay una "
"fosa de carbonización también ahí así que si tienes cosas para quemar, "
"tíralas ahí y enciéndela."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "Money is part of what got us into this mess in the first place."
msgstr "El dinero es parte de lo que nos metió en este lío en primer lugar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "[PER 8+] Is that why you don't carry any cash?"
msgstr "[PER 8+] ¿Por eso no andan con dinero encima?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "B-I-N-G-O.  If you bring it, I'll take it, but that's about it."
msgstr "E-X-A-C-T-O. Si la traes, lo cogeré, pero nada más."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, we've always got along great.  He comes over for supper every Friday."
"  Have a few drinks, maybe take some guns out.  Or, well… we used to.  A "
"little while ago, we had a huge fight.  It was right after this stuff got "
"real bad… I'm fuzzy on the details or what I said, all I remember was being "
"so angry that I could kill him.  We haven't talked much since."
msgstr ""
"Sí, siempre nos llevamos bien. Él viene a cenar todos los viernes. Tomamos "
"unos tragos, sacamos algunas armas. O, bueno… lo hacíamos antes. Hace un "
"tiempo, nos peleamos. Fue justo después de que esto se pusiera mal… No tengo"
" bien claros los detalles o qué dije, lo que me acuerdo fue que estaba tan "
"cabreado que lo podría haber matado. No hablamos mucho desde entonces."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "Have you apologized?"
msgstr "¿Te has disculpado?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "Is there anything I can do?"
msgstr "¿Hay algo que pueda hacer?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"It just seemed like it wouldn't be enough.  I know it's silly but I have to "
"do more than that."
msgstr ""
"Me pareció que no sería suficiente. Sé que es una tontería pero tengo que "
"hacer más que eso."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"If you're offering.  Before everything went to hell, Jay was talking about "
"going to some gun show.  There was a guy there who had managed to sneak some"
" Russian gun into the US.  It was a massive deal for Jay, it was all he "
"could talk about.  I know it's a long shot, but maybe that guy was already "
"at the gun show?  If you find the gun you can keep it, but it would mean a "
"lot to Jay if he could take a look.  All he wanted was to pull it apart and "
"put it back together."
msgstr ""
"Si lo estás ofreciendo. Antes de que todo se convierta en un infierno, Jay "
"hablaba de ir a un espectáculo de armas. Había un chaval que había metido "
"algunas armas rusas en Estados Unidos. Era algo muy importante para Jay, "
"solamente hablaba de eso. Sé que no hay muchas chances pero ¿tal vez el tipo"
" ya estaba en el espectáculo? Si encuentras el arma te la puedes quedar pero"
" significaría mucho para Jay si solamente la pudiera ver. Todo lo que quería"
" era desarmarla y volverla a armar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "I'll bring you back a souvenir."
msgstr "Te traeré de vuelta un recuerdo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "Not really interested."
msgstr "No me interesa realmente."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"Sure, honey!  I'm always in need of more material!  What's the price, "
"though?"
msgstr ""
"¡Seguro, cariño! ¡Siempre ando necesitando materiales! ¿Pero cuál es el "
"precio?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
msgid "Well, how about 100 merch for every 70 pounds of metal…"
msgstr "Bueno, qué te parecen 100 merc por cada 30 kilos de metal…"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"Sorry, I don't really have the time to work on something like that.  I've "
"got lots of pieces for sale on the shelves."
msgstr ""
"Lo siento, no tengo tiempo para trabajar en algo así. Tengo muchas piezas a "
"la venta en las estanterías."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"Sure.  After what you did for me, I'd equip an army for you.  I'll need some"
" money to negotiate with the caravans and scavengers that come by.  What "
"level of protection are you thinking?  I can do 2mm, 4mm, and 6mm suits "
"depending on how much you want to resemble a tank, or I can make you a suit "
"of chainmail instead if you want a little more flexibility.  Materials costs"
" are 300 merch to pay for the food I need to do the labor plus 100 merch per"
" 2mm or 50 merch for the chainmail.  Whatever I save in non-scaling bits "
"like the chain and leather, I get gouged in looking for so much bulk metal."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "Forget it."
msgstr "Olvidalo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid "[350 merch, 1.2mm] I'd prefer to just have chainmail."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid "[400 merch, 2mm] I like to stay light."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid "[500 merch, 4mm] A middle ground would be good."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid "[600 merch, 6mm] Never skimp on protection."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"Alright, <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm, so the next "
"question is time.  Currently, it's the classic problem: if you want quality,"
" you gotta wait.  Two processes I could offer that you would be hard-pressed"
" to find anywhere else are either really great high carbon steel, or I can "
"go through the lengthy process of tempering.  High carbon will take three "
"weeks to process and do the work, and tempering will take me four.  For five"
" I could, I think, create a suit of that nomad armor.  It would incorporate "
"climate control, help you support more weight, and it'll have a jumpsuit "
"built in, but you won't be able to wear normal clothes with it."
msgstr ""
"De acuerdo, <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm, vamos con la "
"siguiente pregunta. En este momento, es el clásico problema: si quieres "
"calidad, vas a tener que esperar. Te puedo ofrecer dos procesos que te va a "
"costar encontrar en otra parte, que son el genial acero de alto carbono, o "
"el largo proceso del templado. El acero de alto carbono me lleva tres "
"semanas de trabajo, y el templado lo puedo hacer en cuatro semanas. En cinco"
" semanas, podría crear una armadura de nómada. Esa incorpora control de "
"clima, te ayuda a cargar más peso y tiene un mono integrado pero no vas a "
"poder usar ropa normal a la vez."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"Alright, <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm, so the next "
"question is time.  Currently, it's the classic problem: if you want quality,"
" you gotta wait.  Two processes I could offer that you would be hard-pressed"
" to find anywhere else are either really great high carbon steel, or I can "
"go through the lengthy process of tempering.  High carbon will take three "
"weeks to process and do the work, and tempering will take me four."
msgstr ""
"De acuerdo, <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm, vamos con la "
"siguiente pregunta. En este momento, es el clásico problema: si quieres "
"calidad, vas a tener que esperar. Te puedo ofrecer dos procesos que te va a "
"costar encontrar en otra parte, que son el genial acero de alto carbono, o "
"el largo proceso del templado. El acero de alto carbono me lleva tres "
"semanas de trabajo, y el templado lo puedo hacer en cuatro semanas."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid "[3 weeks, great protection] High carbon steel sounds great."
msgstr "[3 semanas, gran protección] Acero de alto carbono suena bien."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid "[4 weeks, exceptional protection] I'll wait for the best you can do."
msgstr ""
"[4 semanas, protección excepcional] Prefiero esperar para lo mejor que "
"puedas hacer."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid "[5 weeks, CBM-integrated protection] I'd like nomad armor."
msgstr ""
"[5 semanas, protección con MBC integrado] Quiero la armadura de nómada."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"Alright, so it'll be <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm armor "
"made of the best high carbon steel a woman can scavenge.  If you're good "
"with that, I'll take the merch up front and we can start taking some very "
"invasive measurements."
msgstr ""
"De acuerdo, entonces la armadura de "
"<u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm hecha con el mejor acero de "
"alto carbono que una mujer puede rebuscar. Si eso te parece bien, te voy a "
"cobrar merc por adelantado y podemos empezar a tomar unas medidas invasivas."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"Alright, so it'll be <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm armor "
"made with some of the best fabrication techniques the world has ever seen.  "
"If you're good with that, I'll take the merch up front and we can start "
"taking some very invasive measurements."
msgstr ""
"De acuerdo, entonces la armadura de "
"<u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm hecha con algunas de las "
"mejores técnicas de fabricación que el mundo ha visto. Si eso te parece "
"bien, te voy a cobrar merc por adelantado y podemos empezar a tomar unas "
"medidas invasivas."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"Alright, so it'll be <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm armor "
"made with some of the best fabrication techniques the world has ever seen, "
"as well as help from some extradimensional friends.  I'd be lying if I said "
"I wasn't excited.  If you're good with that, I'll take the merch up front "
"and we can start taking some very invasive measurements."
msgstr ""
"De acuerdo, entonces la armadura de "
"<u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm hecha con algunas de las "
"mejores técnicas de fabricación que el mundo ha visto, y también un poco de "
"ayuda de amigos extradimensionales. Si eso te parece bien, te voy a cobrar "
"merc por adelantado y podemos empezar a tomar unas medidas invasivas."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"[350 merch] Sounds good.  See you in <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_wait>"
" weeks."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"[400 merch] Sounds good.  See you in <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_wait>"
" weeks."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"[500 merch] Sounds good.  See you in <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_wait>"
" weeks."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"[600 merch] Sounds good.  See you in <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_wait>"
" weeks."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"It's all done!  Sorry for the long wait; hopefully it's worth it.  If you "
"need it refitted, let me know."
msgstr ""
"¡Está terminada! Perdón por la larga espera, espero que haya valido la pena."
" Si necesitas que la reajuste, házmelo saber."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid "Still working on it."
msgstr "Todavía trabajando en ello."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid "See you when it's done."
msgstr "Te veo cuando este hecho."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"Oh wow, this is really interesting, huh?  The way they balance weight for "
"travel is genius.  If you wanted a real suit of armor for a traveling "
"warrior, I think I could do it with this.  I'll need one of each of these "
"wire kits, though, for each set I make.  Bring some to me if you want me to "
"use them."
msgstr ""
"Oh, vaya, ¿es muy interesante, eh? La manera en que pone en equilibrio el "
"peso para viajar es genial. Si querías un verdadero traje de armadura para "
"un guerrero viajero, creo que puedo hacerlo con esto. Voy a necesitar uno de"
" estos equipos de cables para cada parte que haga. Tráeme alguno si quieres "
"que lo use."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"I have some right now.  [Hand over a CBM interface wire kit and an external "
"climate control kit.]"
msgstr ""
"Tengo alguno en este momento. [Entregar el MBC equipo de cables de interfaz "
"y equipo de control externo de temperatura.]"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid "I'll try and find some."
msgstr "Voy a intentar conseguir alguno."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"Yeah; the designs you showed me call for 'em.  Not sure what they are "
"myself, but the pictures are real descriptive about how to use them.  To "
"make anything, I'll need one of each of those wire kits.  Got any?"
msgstr ""
"Sí, los diseños que me mostraste los necesitan. No estoy seguro de qué son "
"pero las imágenes son bastante descriptivas sobre cómo usarlas. Para hacer "
"algo voy a necesitar uno de esos equipos de cables. ¿Tienes alguno?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"Here you go.  [Hand over a CBM interface wire kit and an external climate "
"control kit.]"
msgstr ""
"Aquí esta. [Entregar el MBC equipo de cables de interfaz y equipo de control"
" externo de temperatura.]"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
msgid "Not right now."
msgstr "En este momento, no."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"Thanks, sugar!  If you ever have me make some armor, just let me know if you"
" want me to use these in it."
msgstr ""
"¡Gracias, cariño! Si alguna vez quieres que te haga alguna armadura, avísame"
" si quieres que lo use."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid ""
"Oh, these.  With the end of the world, Jay and I had been talking about some"
" new projects for the wasteland warriors.  Anyways, it doesn't matter "
"anymore since… well, it doesn't matter."
msgstr ""
"Oh, estos. Con el fin del mundo, Jay y yo hablamos de unos proyectos nuevos "
"para los luchadores del páramo. Igual, ahora ya no importa desde que… bueno,"
" no importa."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "I'm sure we'll fix things soon!"
msgstr "¡Estoy seguro de que pronto arreglaremos las cosas!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid ""
"Yeah!  I feel a lot better now that Jay and I are talking again, and we've "
"been putting some serious work into this stuff.  If you wanted to help "
"source parts and do some testing, we could definitely get some prototypes "
"made."
msgstr ""
"¡Sí! Me siento mucho mejor ahora que con Jay volvimos a hablarnos, y hemos "
"estado trabajando en estas cosas. Si quieres ayudar con partes y hacer "
"alguna prueba, definitivamente podríamos hacer algunos prototipos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid ""
"I'm already working on something for you.  I only got two hands and 24 hours"
" in a day."
msgstr ""
"Ya estoy trabajando en algo que me pediste. No soy un caballo, tengo dos "
"manos y 24 horas del día."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "I'm still working on it, can't rush perfection."
msgstr "Todavía estoy trabajando en eso, no se puede apurar la perfección."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "Sure, what would you like to know more about?"
msgstr "Seguro, ¿de qué te gustaría que te cuente un poco más?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "Can you work on one of these projects for me?"
msgstr "¿Puedes trabajar en uno de esos proyectos para mí?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "[Motion to the picture of some kind of rifle.] What's the 'OBREZ'?"
msgstr "[Señalando la imagen de una clase de rifle.] ¿Qué es el 'OBREZ'?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "Is the Obrez finished?"
msgstr "¿Está terminado el Obrez?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "[Motion to the picture of a switchblade.] What's the 'PRESSIN'?"
msgstr "[Señalando la imagen de una navaja automática.] ¿Qué es la 'PRESSIN'?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "Is the Pressin finished?"
msgstr "¿Está terminada la Pressin?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid ""
"[Motion to the picture of a mace styled with fire on the head.] What's the "
"'LOUVERTURE'?"
msgstr ""
"[Señalando la imagen de una maza con fuego en la cabeza.] ¿Qué es la "
"'LOUVERTURE'?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "Is the Louverture finished?"
msgstr "¿Está terminada la Louverture?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid ""
"[Motion to the picture of a sledge hammer with a piston jutting from one "
"face of the head.] What's the 'DISORDER'?"
msgstr ""
"[Señalando la imagen de una almádena con un pistón sobresaliendo de un lado "
"de la cabeza.] ¿Qué es la 'DISORDER'?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "Is the Disorder finished?"
msgstr "¿Está terminada la Disorder?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid ""
"The Obrez is a classic Mosin-Nagant that someone has cut down and removed "
"the stock of.  The idea was that in some parts of the world a surplus rifle "
"was easier than finding a pistol to conceal.  Way I see it, a sturdy classic"
" gun like that with a bit of reinforcement could make a great mace.  You "
"find me a functioning Mosin - any variant will do - and 50 merch for parts, "
"and I can get this one working in a week."
msgstr ""
"El Obrez es un Mosin-Nagant clásico al que le recortaron y sacaron la "
"culata. La idea era que en algunas partes del mundo, un rifle extra era más "
"fácil de encontrar que una pistola para ocultar. Tal y como lo veo, una "
"clásica arma resistente un poco reforzada podría ser una buena maza. Si me "
"consigues un Mosin que funcione - de cualquier variante me servirá - y 50 "
"merc para partes y te lo puedo fabricar en una semana."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "[Mosin-Nagant M44, 50 merch] See you in a week."
msgstr "[Mosin-Nagant M44, 50 merc] Vuelve en una semana."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "[Mosin-Nagant 1891/30, 50 merch] See you in a week."
msgstr "[Mosin-Nagant 1891/30, 50 merc] Vuelve en una semana."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
msgid "What about another project?"
msgstr "¿Y qué hay de otro proyecto?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
msgid "I want to talk about something else."
msgstr "Quiero hablar de otra cosa."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
msgid "I'll check in later."
msgstr "Lo comprobaré más tarde."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid ""
"The gun is done, looking pretty sleek if you ask me.  All loaded and ready "
"to cave in a zombie."
msgstr ""
"El arma está lista, se ve muy buena si me preguntas a mí. Cargada y lista "
"para derribar zombi."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid ""
"The Pressin was a self defense weapon for politicians in Spain.  It was a "
"small breach loaded handheld pistol that could fit in a glasses case and be "
"fired subtly.  I figure that we can improve on the design by adding a "
"retracting blade while keeping the surprise shots.  To get this working I'm "
"gonna need a .32 gun like a SIG Sauer P230, Kel-Tec P-32, or a Walther PPK."
"  I'll also need a switchblade, 20 merch, and a week."
msgstr ""
"La Pressin fue un arma de auto defensa de los políticos de España.  Era una "
"pequeña pistola de chispa que podía caber en un estuche de gafas y ser "
"disparada sutilmente.  Me imagino que podríamos mejorar el diseño añadiendo "
"una hoja retráctil mientras mantenemos los disparos por sorpresa.  Para que "
"esto funcione voy a necesitar un arma del .32 como la SIG Sauer P230, la "
"Kel-Tec P-32, o la Walter PPK.  También necesitare una navaja plegable, 20 "
"merc y una semana."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "[P230, switchblade, 20 merch] See you in a week."
msgstr "[P230, navaja, 20 merc] Nos vemos en una semana."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "[PPK, switchblade, 20 merch] See you in a week."
msgstr "[PPK, navaja, 20 merc] Nos vemos en una semana."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "[P-32, switchblade, 20 merch] See you in a week."
msgstr "[P-32, navaja, 20 merc] Nos vemos en una semana."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid ""
"The gun's done.  Mind the safety on the side, this guy is pretty dangerous."
msgstr ""
"El arma está lista. Ten cuidado con el seguro al costado, es bastante "
"peligrosa."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid ""
"Oh, that's one of my sillier ideas.  Jay is convinced it'll never work but I"
" really want to give it a shot.  A traditional mace with gas-venting ports "
"and an ignition system for mini bursts of fire.  Maybe I've just played too "
"many RPGs, but it seems worth a shot.  To get this one working I'm gonna "
"need a real deal mace -  something that can handle the pressure - as well as"
" a military grade flamethrower.  Fabrication will definitely take two weeks "
"on this one."
msgstr ""
"Oh, esa es una de mis ideas más tontas. Jay está convencido de que nunca va "
"a funcionar pero yo quiero intentarlo. Es una maza tradicional con aberturas"
" que liberan gas y un sistema de ignición para causar pequeñas ráfagas de "
"fuego. Tal vez sea porque jugué muchos juegos de rol pero me parece que vale"
" la pena intentarlo. Para hacer que funcione voy a necesitar una buena maza "
"- algo que pueda aguantar la presión - y también un lanzallamas de grado "
"militar. La fabricación me llevará dos semanas."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "[Mace, flamethrower] See you in 2 weeks."
msgstr "[Maza, lanzallamas] Nos vemos en 2 semanas."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid ""
"The mace is done.  It honestly works pretty great too.  Hope you get some "
"good use out of it."
msgstr ""
"La maza ya está lista. Honestamente, funciona bastante bien. Espero que le "
"puedas dar un buen uso."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid ""
"The Disorder is already kind of a real thing.  I got the idea from a viral "
"video I saw of a guy making something similar with a baseball bat for "
"hitting home runs.  Takes a sledge hammer with a center mounted piston that "
"you can arm with .22 caliber blanks.  When you hit a zombie with that sweet "
"spot… boom.  The blank goes off and sends the piston straight down into "
"whatever poor fucker you hit it with.  I'll need a sledge hammer, 80 merch, "
"and at least 20 .22 LR rounds.  Fabrication will definitely take two weeks "
"on this one."
msgstr ""
"El Disorder es bastante real. Se me ocurrió la idea de un video viral que vi"
" de un tipo haciendo algo similar con un bate de béisbol. Es con una "
"almádena con un pistón en el medio que puedes armar con salvas calibre .22. "
"Cuando golpeas a un zombi con el lugar indicado… bum. La salva se dispara y "
"envía el pistón hacia abajo metiéndose en el pobre desgraciado. Voy a "
"necesitar una almádena, 80 merc y por lo menos 20 balas .22 LR. Su "
"fabricación me llevará dos semanas."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid "[Sledge hammer, 80 merch, 20 .22 LR] See you in 2 weeks."
msgstr "[Almádena, 80 merc, 20 .22 LR] Nos vemos en 2 semanas."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
msgid ""
"The beast is done!  Really heavy-duty, but really packs a punch.  Be careful"
" with your fingers.  I'm serious, this thing could tear 'em off."
msgstr ""
"¡La bestia esta acabada!  Muy pesada, pero pega fuerte.  Ten cuidado con los"
" dedos.  Lo digo en serio, esta cosa podría destrozarlos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_item_groups.json
msgid "engineering notes"
msgid_plural "engineering notes"
msgstr[0] "nota de ingeniería"
msgstr[1] "notas de ingenieria"
msgstr[2] "notas de ingenieria"

#. ~ Description of "engineering notes"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_item_groups.json
msgid ""
"A collection of sketches and CAD designs marked up with pencil.  There are "
"two peoples handwriting."
msgstr ""
"Una colección de bocetos y diseños CAD marcados con lápiz. Hay dos tipos de "
"escrituras."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You hit the nail on the head.  You bring me bullets - 5.56, 7.62, 5.45, or "
".300 - and I'll convert between 'em.  I take a 10% cut, just so you know."
msgstr ""
"Das en el clavo. Me traes balas - 5.56, 7.62, 5.45, o .300 - y las puedo "
"convertir entre esos calibres. Me quedo con el 10%, que lo sepas."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "Can we do that now?"
msgstr "¿Podemos hacer eso ahora?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid ""
"Yup, what would you like to convert?  As a reminder, I do 5.56, 7.62, 5.45, "
"or .300.  You want anything else, we can just trade 'em directly over the "
"counter."
msgstr ""
"Sip, ¿qué te gustaría convertir? Te recuerdo que trabajo con 5.56, 7.62, "
"5.45, o .300. Si quieres alguna otra me las puedes comprar directamente en "
"el mostrador."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "Nothing for now."
msgstr "Por ahora, nada."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "Let's see what you have in stock right now."
msgstr "Muéstrame qué tienes en el almacén ahora."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "[1 day] 200 rounds."
msgstr "[1 día] 200 balas."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "[5 days] 800 rounds."
msgstr "[5 días] 800 balas."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid ""
"Alright, <u_val:number_artisans_gunsmith_ammo_amount> rounds.  First off, "
"what are you looking to give me?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "5.56x45."
msgstr "5.56x45."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "7.62x51."
msgstr "7.62x51."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "7.62x39."
msgstr "7.62x39."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "5.45x39."
msgstr "5.45x39."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid ".300 AAC."
msgstr ".300 AAC."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "Sure, <u_val:artisans_gunsmith_ammo_source_name> to what?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "See you then."
msgstr "Nos vemos entonces."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Alright, that's 200 rounds minus the 10% service fee.  They'll be converted "
"in a day."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, son 200 balas menos el 10% como pago por el servicio. Voy a tardar un"
" día en convertirlas."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Alright, that's 800 rounds minus the 10% service fee.  They'll be converted "
"in 5 days."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, son 800 balas menos el 10% como pago por el servicio. Voy a tardar 5 "
"días en convertirlas."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "There's something else I'd like to talk about."
msgstr "Hay otra cosa de la que te quería hablar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "Sorry, it isn't ready yet."
msgstr "Perdón, todavía no terminé."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "The transaction is complete, here are your items."
msgstr "La transacción está completa, aquí están sus objecto."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "[Take your new ammo.] Thanks."
msgstr "[Agarrar munición nueva.] Gracias."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"Welcome to the first American bank of munitions.  We convert your goods and "
"services to the new gold standard."
msgstr ""
"Bienvenido al primer banco americano de municiones. Convertimos sus bienes y"
" servicios al nuevo patrón de oro."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "What's your deal?"
msgstr "¿Cuál es tu negocio?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "Munitions?"
msgstr "¿Municiones?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"Hey.  Cody wanted to say that she's sorry.  She thought that you would want "
"to see this."
msgstr ""
"Eh. Cody quiere disculparse contigo. Ella pensó que tu ibas a querer ver "
"esto."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "I'm interested in helping with that thing for Cody."
msgstr "Estoy interesado en ayudar con eso a Cody."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "How are my rounds coming?"
msgstr "¿Cómo van mis balas?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "I'd like to exchange some rounds."
msgstr "Me gustaría intercambiar algunas balas."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "Are you and Cody close?"
msgstr "¿Son tú y Cody cercanos?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "How's the 'printing' thing going?"
msgstr "¿Cómo va lo de 'imprimir'?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"Next series of currency gotta be ready in around <interval>, fresh off the "
"print!"
msgstr ""
"La próxima serie de monedas debería estar lista en aproximadamente "
"<interval>, ¡recién salidas de la impresora!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "I'll make sure to take a look.  Bye."
msgstr "Me aseguraré de echar un vistazo. Hasta luego."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "Fuck yeah.  New currency is death and I'm dealing it."
msgstr "Sí, joder. La nueva moneda es muerte y la estoy repartiendo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "I understand, but how does this work exactly?"
msgstr "Lo entiendo, pero ¿cómo funciona exactamente?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"Pretty simple stuff, bud.  I barter in pre-shitshow ammo, and to stimulate "
"the growing economy, I print and issue more.  I take your goods - Cody would"
" call it labor - and exchange it for the new universal currency.  If you "
"want to convert currency I'm happy to facilitate, but it'll take a few days "
"and there is a service charge."
msgstr ""
"Es bastante simple. Yo negocio con munición de antes del Cataclismo y para "
"estimular la creciente economía, imprimo y emito más. Recibo tus recursos - "
"Cody lo llamaría fuerza laboral - y lo cambio por la nueva moneda universal."
" Si quieres convertir moneda, con gusto te ayudo pero me lleva unos días y "
"hay un cargo por el servicio."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "So you're really going all in on this bank thing?"
msgstr "¿Así que realmente vas a ir a por todas en esto de los bancos?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "So you'll exchange bullets for other bullets directly?"
msgstr "¿Así que cambiarás las balas por otras directamente?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "I did a boring IT job and prepped for this shit.  Look at me now."
msgstr ""
"Trabajaba en un aburrido trabajo de informática y me preparaba para esta "
"mierda. Mírame ahora."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "Look at you now."
msgstr "Mirate ahora."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"It's my house.  Cody's in the other building, if you've met her.  We dug a "
"trench and set up some milspec turrets.  I programmed them, Cody armored "
"them.  Now we're just trying to get by.  This ain't the wizard of Oz, you "
"can look behind the curtain over there."
msgstr ""
"Es mi casa. Cody está en el otro edificio, si ya la conociste. Cavamos una "
"trinchera y establecimos algunas torretas milspec. Yo las programé y Cody "
"las armó. Ahora, solo tratamos de sobrevivir. Esto no es el Mago de Oz, "
"puedes ver detrás de la cortina ahí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "Where'd you get half a dozen milspec turrets?"
msgstr "¿Y de dónde sacaron media docena de torretas milspec?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"*stares off into the distance.  \"The owners didn't need them anymore.  Not "
"anymore…\""
msgstr "*mira hacia el horizonte. \"Los dueños no las necesitaban más. Ya no…\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"Stuff is fucked all over, bud.  How about we stick to talking business?"
msgstr ""
"Las cosa esta jodida por todas partes, ¿qué tal si nos limitamos a hablar de"
" negocios?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"Where did you… I- I don't know what to say.\"  Jay takes the rifle reverently.  He turns it over so carefully that you could mistake him for holding a child instead of a gun.  \"This thing is is beautiful.  Modern rails, ergonomic furniture, recoil balancing system.  I know Cody thinks that she did something wrong, but all I remember is being so angry… just blindingly furious.  Then I was running.  When I woke up, everything was fine.\"\n"
"\n"
"Jay hands back the Kord.  \"Thank you for letting me see this, and for getting Cody and I talking.  If you could help me out with something for Cody, I'll hook you up with a casket mag for that thing and a box of the good ammo.  Stuff from my reserves."
msgstr ""
"¿Dónde lo encontraste... Yo- Yo no sé qué decir.\" Jay coge el rifle reverentemente. Lo gira tan cuidadosamente que podrías confundirlo con alguien sosteniendo a un niño en lugar de un arma. \"Esto es hermoso. Rieles modernos, armazón ergonómico, sistema de equilibrio de retroceso. Sé que Cody piensa que hizo algo mal, pero todo lo que recuerdo es estar tan enfadado... cegadora-mente furioso. Luego estaba corriendo. Cuando desperté, todo estaba bien.\"\n"
"\n"
"Jay devuelve el Kord. \"Gracias por dejarme ver esto y por hacer que Cody y yo hablemos. Si pudieras ayudarme con algo para Cody, te conseguiré un cargador de caja para esa cosa y una caja de munición buena. Cosas de mis reservas."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the debug software"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid ""
"Alright, so Cody has talked about some cutting-edge tech she's seen "
"displayed.  This thing is called a nano-fabricator.  It's like a "
"complicated, robotic 3D printer.  Cody used to run with some hackers that "
"steal IP, schematics, that sort of thing.  I guess a problem they were "
"running into was the newest tech stuff is all encrypted as templates for "
"these printers.  Well, I know of a colleague who went home with debug "
"software for the system.  You get that for her, and we're in business."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, entonces Cody habló de alguna tecnología de punta que estaba "
"mostrando. Esta cosa se llama nanofabricador. Una cosa complicada, como una "
"impresora 3D robótica. Cody andaba con unos hackers que robaban IP, "
"esquemas, esa clase de cosas. Supongo que el problema con el que se "
"encontraban fue que la tecnología más nueva está encriptada como los "
"esquemas para esas impresoras. Bueno, conozco un colega que se fue a casa "
"con un programa de depuración para el sistema. Si conseguís eso para ella "
"haremos negocios."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "I'll see if I can find it."
msgstr "Veré si puedo encontrarlo."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid "Find the gun"
msgstr "Encuentra el arma"

#. ~ Description of mission "Find the gun"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid ""
"Cody wants you to go to a gun show and find a rare gun that Jay wanted to "
"see.  It was an AK of some kind with a weird name… something like CARD or "
"CORE."
msgstr ""
"Cody quiere que vayas a una feria de armas y encuentres un arma rara que Jay"
" quería ver. Era un AK de algún tipo con un nombre raro... algo así como "
"CARD o CORE."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the gun"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid ""
"Before everything went to hell Jay was talking about going to some gun show."
"  There was a guy there who had managed to sneak some Russian gun into the "
"US.  It was a massive deal for Jay, it was all he could talk about.  I know "
"it's a long shot but maybe that guy was already at the gun show?  If you "
"find the gun you can keep it, but it would mean a lot to Jay if he could "
"take a look all he wanted was to pull it apart and put it back together."
msgstr ""
"Antes de que todo se fuera al infierno Jay hablaba de ir a una feria de "
"armas. Había un tipo que había conseguido colar un arma rusa en los Estados "
"Unidos. Era un asunto enorme para Jay, era todo de lo que podía hablar. Sé "
"que es una posibilidad remota, pero tal vez ese tipo ya estaba en la feria "
"de armas. Si encuentras el arma puedes quedarte con ella, pero significaría "
"mucho para Jay si pudiera echar un vistazo, todo lo que quería era "
"desmontarla y volver a montarla."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the gun"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the debug software"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid "Thanks.  I'll start working on an apology."
msgstr "Gracias. Voy a empezar a trabajar en la disculpa."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the gun"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the debug software"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid "Let me know if you change your mind."
msgstr "Avísame si cambias de opinión."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the gun"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid ""
"I'd be careful there; Jay was saying they were bringing some new autonomous "
"hardware to the show.  You're looking for a Russian rifle that should be "
"modded to the moon.  CARD, CORE rifle, something like that."
msgstr ""
"Yo tendría cuidado ahí; Jay contaba que iban a llevar un nuevo aparato "
"autónomo al espectáculo. Tienes que buscar un rifle ruso que debe estar "
"modificado al infinito. Rifle CARD, CORE, algo así es el nombre."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the gun"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid ""
"Any luck finding that gun show?  I think it was a Russian gun, maybe a CARD "
"or CORE rifle?  Something like that."
msgstr ""
"¿Tuviste suerte en el espectáculo de armas? Creo que era un arma rusa, ¿tal "
"vez el rifle CARD o CORE? Algo así."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the gun"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid ""
"Thanks, darlin'.  If you could show it to Jay, that would mean a lot to me."
"  If there's anything I could ever make for you as payment after that, just "
"let me know."
msgstr ""
"Gracias, cariño. Si se la puedes mostrar a Jay, eso significaría mucho para "
"mí. Si hay algo que yo pueda hacer para pagarte este favor, házmelo saber."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the gun"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid "That's great!  Make sure to show it to Jay."
msgstr "¡Eso es genial! Asegúrate de enseñárselo a Jay."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the gun"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid "Well you tried at least…"
msgstr "Bueno, al menos lo intentaste..."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid "Find the debug software"
msgstr "Encuentra el software de depuración"

#. ~ Description of mission "Find the debug software"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid ""
"Jay wants you to go to someone's house and get some software that they had "
"taken home."
msgstr ""
"Jay quiere que vayas a la casa de alguien a buscar un programa que se llevó."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the debug software"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid ""
"I'd be careful.  Guy was a bit of a nut, I don't know what he was planning "
"to do with that software."
msgstr ""
"Yo tendría cuidado. El tipo estaba un poco loco, no sé qué pensaba hacer con"
" ese programa."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the debug software"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid "Any luck finding that USB?"
msgstr "¿Hubo suerte encontrando ese USB?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the debug software"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid "Thanks bud, I'll take it from here.  Enjoy those bullets."
msgstr "Gracias, amigo, yo me encargo ahora. Disfrutá de esas balas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the debug software"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid "Shame.  Shame, shame."
msgstr "Qué lástima, una lástima."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the debug software"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid "Well fuck me then."
msgstr "Pues que me jodan entonces."

#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ A blacksmith for the faction.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_npcs.json
msgid "Cody Miller"
msgstr "Cody Miller"

#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ A blacksmith for the faction.
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_npcs.json
msgid "Blacksmith"
msgstr "Herrera"

#. ~ Job description of "Cody Miller" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_npcs.json
msgid "A blacksmith who wants everyone to get along."
msgstr "Una herrera que quiere que todos se lleven bien."

#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ A gunsmith for the faction.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_npcs.json
msgid "Jay Ruckers"
msgstr "Jay Ruckers"

#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
#. ~ A gunsmith for the faction.
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_npcs.json
msgid "Banker"
msgstr "Banquero"

#. ~ Job description of "Jay Ruckers" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_npcs.json
msgid "A gunsmith looking to become the new central bank."
msgstr "Un armero que busca convertirse en el nuevo banco central."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"We've still got a few things available, but that last order is gonna take us"
" a while to restock.  Come back in a little while if you're looking for the "
"big stuff.  The crew is fast, so it won't be long.  A few hours at most, I "
"promise."
msgstr ""
"Todavía tenemos algunas cosas disponibles pero nos va a llevar un tiempo "
"reponernos del último pedido. Vuelve dentro de un tiempo si estás buscando "
"por cosas más importantes. El equipo trabaja rápido así que no vas a tener "
"que esperar mucho. Con unas horas es suficiente."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
msgid ""
"Sure, we offer various specialty cuts direct to our customers in batches of "
"10.  Anything larger than these planks is gonna take us a while to refresh, "
"though.  A couple hours, maybe longer if we have to source more wood.  So, "
"what would you like?"
msgstr ""
"Seguro, ofrecemos varios cortes especiales directos a nuestros clientes en "
"grupos de 10. Eso sí, cualquier cosa más grande que estas tablas nos va a "
"llevar un tiempo poder reponerla. Un par de horas, más o menos, si tenemos "
"que buscar más madera. ¿Que prefieres?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
msgid "[10$]  I'll buy some sticks."
msgstr "[10$] Comprare unos palos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
msgid "[20$]  I'll buy some long sticks."
msgstr "[20$] Comprare unos palos largos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
msgid "[30$]  I'll buy some planks."
msgstr "[30$] Comprare algunas tablas."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
msgid "[100$]  I'll buy some logs."
msgstr "[100$] Comprare algunos troncos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
msgid "[120$]  I'll buy some wooden panels."
msgstr "[120$] Comprare algunos paneles de madera."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
msgid "[240$]  I'll buy some large wooden sheets."
msgstr "[240$] Comprare algunas láminas grandes de madera."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
msgid "[350$]  I'll buy some wooden beams."
msgstr "[350$] Comprare algunas vigas de madera."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
msgid "Is there anything else you want?"
msgstr "¿Algo más?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
msgid "Hello there.  Nice to see you, <name_g>."
msgstr "Hola que tal. Qué bueno verte, <name_g>."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
msgid "A stranger out here?  Who are you?"
msgstr "¿Un desconocido por aquí? ¿Quién eres?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
msgid "Pleasure to see you again."
msgstr "Me alegra volver a verte."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
msgid "See ya."
msgstr "Nos vemos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
msgid "Do you need something?"
msgstr "¿Necesitás algo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
msgid "How do things work around here now?"
msgstr "¿Cómo van las cosas por aquí?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
msgid "Nah, see ya."
msgstr "No, nos vemos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
msgid ""
"You mean you're still looking for wood?  Crazy… but we had a suspicion folks"
" might show up in an emergency.  Talk to the manager if you want to make an "
"order."
msgstr ""
"¿O sea que todavía necesitas madera? Qué loco… pero teníamos la sospecha de "
"que algunos aparecerían con la emergencia. Habla con el gerente si quieres "
"hacer un pedido."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
msgid ""
"Well, the machinery works just fine.  We were always self-sufficient and "
"<the_cataclysm> only really made that more apparent.  So if you want to "
"place an order and help keep the operation running, talk to the manager.  "
"We'll trade you for our wood."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, la máquina funciona bien. Siempre fuimos autosuficientes y el "
"<the_cataclysm> solo lo hizo más perceptible. Así que si quieres realizar un"
" pedido y ayudarnos a mantener esto funcionando, habla con el gerente. "
"Podemos ofrecerte nuestra madera."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
msgid ""
"Not much to it.  I worked here as a logger before <the_cataclysm> began.  "
"When all went to hell, I was on the job and had to hole up here with my "
"coworkers.  Good news is we all came out fine, and the boss decided to keep "
"the mill running.  I don't know how much longer we can last, though; not "
"unless we make some contact with other people.  Customers, I guess you might"
" call 'em."
msgstr ""
"No hay mucho que decir. Trabajaba aquí como leñador antes de comenzar el "
"<the_cataclysm>. Cuando todo se fue a la mierda, estaba trabajando y me tuve"
" que refugiar con mis compañeros. Lo bueno es que todos salimos bien y el "
"jefe decidió mantener funcionando la empresa. Pero no sé cuánto más podremos"
" aguantar; necesitamos contactar con otras personas. Clientes, supongo que "
"podemos llamarlos así."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
msgid ""
"Well, I'm a logger here.  Seasonal work but good pay… or it was, at least.  "
"Before that first <zombie> showed up and made it clear how bad things were "
"really getting."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, soy leñador aquí. Es un trabajo por temporada pero la guita está "
"bien… o estaba, por lo menos. Hasta que apareció el primer <zombie> y dejó "
"bien en claro lo mal que estaba todo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
msgid ""
"I'm a lumberjack out here.  Things were quiet for a long time.  We're pretty"
" far out in the woods so it was kind of a shock to find out just how bad "
"it'd gotten in civilization.  We had a couple close run-ins ourselves.  My "
"friend over there almost got eaten!  But we still have resources that I'm "
"sure people can use."
msgstr ""
"Soy leñador aquí. Las cosas estuvieron tranquilas por mucho tiempo. Estamos "
"bastante metidos en el bosque así que fue una sorpresa encontrarnos lo mal "
"que estaba la civilización. Tuvimos un par de encuentros cercanos nosotros "
"también. A mi amigo, el que está ahí, ¡casi se lo comen! Pero todavía "
"tenemos suministros que estoy seguro que la gente puede necesitar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
msgid ""
"My comrades and I were lucky to be in the right place at the right time, I "
"suppose.  We keep really busy out here, so we didn't expect <the_cataclysm> "
"to land right in our lap like that.  Luckily these axes can chop more than "
"wood.  They'll take a good chunk out of anything nasty that threatens our "
"mill."
msgstr ""
"Mis compañeros y yo tuvimos la suerte de estar en el lugar y momento "
"indicados, diría. Nos mantenemos bastante ocupados aquí, así que no nos "
"esperábamos que el <the_cataclysm> apareciera aquí encima nuestro de esta "
"manera. Por suerte, estas hachas pueden cortar más que madera. Le pueden "
"sacar un buen pedazo a cualquier porquería que nos quiera amenazar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
msgid ""
"Well, I work here.  Welcome to the mill.  Used to be trucks in and out of "
"here all the time but you're the first face we've seen in a while."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, trabajo aquí. Bienvenido al aserradero. Antes había camiones entrando"
" y saliendo todo el tiempo pero ahora eres la primera cara que veo en mucho "
"tiempo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
msgid ""
"New to the job… or, well, whatever's happening now.  I still cut trees and "
"run logs through the saw from time to time, so I guess you'd call me a "
"logger.  Things have only gotten weirder after those fucking <zombies> "
"nearly killed us.  I'm not sure how much longer we'll last…"
msgstr ""
"Soy nuevo en este trabajo… o, bueno, cómo se llame esto ahora. Todavía corto"
" árboles y paso los troncos por la sierra de vez en cuando, así que puedes "
"decir que soy leñador. Las cosas se fueron poniendo cada vez más raras "
"después de que esos <zombies> de mierda casi nos matan. No sé cuánto más "
"podremos aguantar…"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
msgid "Hope it goes well."
msgstr "Espero que vaya bien."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
msgid "Hello there.  Nice to see you again."
msgstr "Hola que tal. Qué bueno verte otra vez."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
msgid "A new face at the mill?  Who might you be?"
msgstr "¿Una cara nueva en el aserradero? ¿Y quién eres tu?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid "Can I purchase some of your wares?"
msgstr "¿Puedo comprar algo de lo que tienen?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
msgid ""
"I'm the manager here at the mill.  It's a tight-knit crew, unionized "
"operation.  When <the_cataclysm> broke out, we didn't even know about it "
"till some <zombies> wandered onto the yard.  Now, we've just held up here.  "
"I imagine any folks left out there might be needing our machinery and skills"
" to keep civilization alive.  Might make new customers yet."
msgstr ""
"Soy el gerente aquí en el aserradero. Es un grupo muy unido, sindicado. "
"Cuando empezó el <the_cataclysm>, no nos enteramos hasta que unos <zombies> "
"aparecieron en el patio. Ahora, aguantamos aquí. Me imagino que cualquiera "
"que ande por ahí puede necesitar nuestras máquinas y habilidades para "
"mantener la civilización funcionando. Podemos tener nuevos clientes."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid "Hm."
msgstr "Hm."

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_employees.json
msgid "logger"
msgstr "leñador"

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_employees.json
msgid "manager"
msgstr "gerente"

#. ~ Job description of "Lumberjack" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_employees.json
msgid "I felled trees before the apocalypse.  Zombies shouldn't be as tough."
msgstr ""
"Bajaba árboles antes del apocalipsis. Los zombis no deberían costar tanto."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "Find Drive Belts"
msgstr "Conseguir Correas de Transmisión"

#. ~ Description of mission "Find Drive Belts"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "Obtain 3 drive belts in exchange for credit with the loggers."
msgstr "Consigue 3 correas de transmisión para venderle a los leñadores."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "I need three drive belts."
msgstr "Necesito tres correas de transmisión."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid ""
"Some of our machinery received some damage before <the_cataclysm> and we "
"were waiting on replacement parts.  Now everything's changed and those parts"
" are more important than ever.  Get us three drive belts and I'll give you "
"some credit with us."
msgstr ""
"Algunas de nuestras máquinas se rompieron antes del <the_cataclysm> y "
"estábamos esperando los repuestos. Ahora cambió todo y esas partes son más "
"importantes que nunca. Consíguenos tres correas de transmisión y te daré "
"crédito con nosotros."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder Wire"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
msgid "Someone's got to do it."
msgstr "Alguien tiene que hacerlo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid ""
"If you can't find actual drive belts on engines, a good replacement can be "
"made from a belt and some duct tape.  Nothing difficult."
msgstr ""
"Si no puedes conseguir las correas de transmisión de los motores, un buen "
"reemplazo se puede hacer con cinturones y cinta americana. No es tan "
"complicado."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "Do you have the belts?"
msgstr "¿Tienes las correas?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "Wonderful!  Thanks, <name_g>, we'll be fine for a long while from now."
msgstr ""
"¡Genial! Gracias, <name_g>, con esto vamos a andar bien por mucho tiempo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder Wire"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
msgid "Where are they?  I don't believe you."
msgstr "¿Dónde están? No te creo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "That's unfortunate.  I guess we'll have to find someone else to do it."
msgstr ""
"Qué lástima. Supongo que le vamos a tener que pedir a otra persona que lo "
"haga."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "Get 1,000 Nails"
msgstr "Conseguir 1000 clavos"

#. ~ Description of mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "Obtain 1,000 nails in exchange for credit with the loggers."
msgstr "Conseguir 1000 clavos para venderle a los leñadores."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "I need 1,000 nails."
msgstr "Necesito 1000 clavos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid ""
"Along with those drive belts, we were waiting for some nails for structural "
"repairs.  Due to <the_cataclysm>, we obviously never received them.  So, I "
"need you to get us 1,000 nails.  We'll pay you fairly."
msgstr ""
"Además de esas correas de transmisión, también estábamos esperando unos "
"clavos para hacer reparaciones. Y por el <the_cataclysm>, obviamente que "
"nunca llegaron. Así que necesito que nos traigas 1000 clavos. Te lo vamos a "
"retribuir de manera justa."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "Taking apart some furniture in town should get what you need."
msgstr "Desmontando algunos muebles del pueblo vas a poder conseguirlos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "Do you have the nails?"
msgstr "¿Tienes los clavos?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid ""
"Our warehouse was about to fall apart.  These will be extremely helpful to "
"us."
msgstr ""
"Nuestro depósito se está cayendo a pedazos. Esto nos va a venir muy bien."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgstr "Consigue 6800 clavos"

#. ~ Description of mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "Obtain 6,800 nails in exchange for credit with the loggers."
msgstr "Obtén 6800 clavos para venderle a los leñadores."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "I need 6,800 nails."
msgstr "Necesito 6800 clavos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid ""
"While fairly sturdy, the metal fence around this place won't hold out for "
"long.  So, we've decided to replace it with a wall.  However, the nails we "
"had were used to repair our existing structures, and they weren't nearly "
"enough.  After some calculations, we need 6,800 nails to do it.  That may "
"seem like a lot, but we're willing to give you a TON of credit for it."
msgstr ""
"Aunque la valla de metal es bastante resistente, no va a aguantar por mucho "
"tiempo más. Así que decidimos reemplazarla con una pared. Sin embargo, los "
"clavos que teníamos los usamos para reparar las estructuras que ya había, y "
"no eran suficientes. Después de algunos cálculos, necesitamos 6800 clavos. "
"Te pueden parecer un montón pero estamos dispuestos a darte un MONTÓN de "
"crédito a cambio de ellos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "Well, I suppose that's reasonable."
msgstr "Bueno, supongo que es razonable."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid ""
"You might have to do more than just scrapping a bunch of furniture.  "
"Dismantling a building somewhere in town could get you what you need."
msgstr ""
"Vas a tener que hacer un poco más que ir desmontando muebles para "
"conseguirlos. Desarmar un edificio en alguna parte del pueblo te puede dar "
"lo que necesitas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "That's absolutely amazing!  I can't thank you enough for this!"
msgstr "¡Absolutamente maravilloso! ¡No sé cómo agradecerte esto!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "You're a fucking scammer, <name_b>!"
msgstr "¡Eres un estafador de mierda, <name_b>!"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "Find 6 Blankets"
msgstr "Encuentra 6 Mantas"

#. ~ Description of mission "Find 6 Blankets"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "Obtain 6 blankets or quilts in exchange for credit with the loggers."
msgstr "Consigue 6 mantas o edredones a cambio de credito con los madereros."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "I need 6 blankets."
msgstr "Necesito 6 mantas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid ""
"Now that we should be safe from harm, I decided to start adding a few things"
" to this place.  Right now, we don't have anywhere to comfortably sleep, so "
"we're building a small sleeping quarter.  We just need 6 big, warm blankets "
"or quilts to finish our project."
msgstr ""
"Ahora que deberíamos estar a salvo del peligro, decidí empezar a agregar "
"algunas cosas al lugar. Ahora mismo, no tenemos ningún sitio cómodo para "
"dormir así que queremos construir una pequeña habitación. Necesitamos 6 "
"sabanas o colchas grandes y calentitas para terminar nuestro proyecto."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "I figure any hotel or motel in town should have lots of blankets."
msgstr ""
"Supongo que cualquier hotel o motel del pueblo debería tener muchas sabanas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "Did you find us some bedding yet?"
msgstr "¿Nos conseguiste el abrigo de cama?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid ""
"Thanks!  Feel free to sleep here if you want.  It's the least we can do for "
"the help."
msgstr ""
"¡Gracias! Quédate a dormir aquí si quieres. Es lo menos que podemos hacer "
"por ti."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "How is this supposed to help us?"
msgstr "¿Y cómo se supone que nos ayuda esto?"

#. ~ Description of mission "Establish A Trade Route"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid ""
"Establish trade relations between the loggers and a refugee center, and "
"bring back a writ of the agreement."
msgstr ""
"Establece relaciones comerciales entre los leñadores y el centro de "
"refugiados y traer el acuerdo por escrito."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid ""
"While some of us were out scavenging, we spotted an old evac shelter that "
"looks like it might have some people inside.  I want you to go over there, "
"find whoever runs the joint, and see if we can make a deal with them for "
"some processed lumber.  This will be invaluable to our survival."
msgstr ""
"Mientras algunos de nosotros fuimos a buscar cosas, encontramos un viejo "
"refugio de evacuación que parece tener gente dentro. Quiero que vayas hasta "
"ahí, encuentres quién lo maneja y veas si podemos hacer un acuerdo por "
"nuestra madera. Eso sería de valor incalculable para nuestra supervivencia."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "Please give it a try?  This is really important to us."
msgstr "Por favor, ¿podrías intentarlo? Es muy importante para nosotros."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "What did they say about the deal?"
msgstr "¿Qué dijeron acerca del acuerdo?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
msgid "Thank you!  We're set for life on this one!"
msgstr "¡Gracias! ¡Con esto nos salvamos de por vida!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/missions.json
msgid "How does this help us?"
msgstr "¿Y eso cómo nos ayuda a nosotros?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
msgid ""
"That's unfortunate.  I guess we'll have to find someone else to trade with."
msgstr ""
"Qué lástima. Supongo que vamos a tener que encontrar a otros para comerciar."

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Former miner, poor fellow succumbed to spiral madness.
#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
msgid "miner"
msgstr "minero"

#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
msgid "Miner"
msgstr "Minero"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
msgid "Spirals?"
msgstr "¿Espirales?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
msgid "Hello there!"
msgstr "¡Hola ahí!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
msgid "I'm outta here.  Bye."
msgstr "Me largo de aquí. Adios."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
msgid ""
"Poor fellow - looks like you're out of your mind.  Can't help you, sorry.  "
"I'm outta here.  Bye."
msgstr ""
"Pobre tipo - parece que estás totalmente ido. No te puedo ayudar, lo siento."
" Me largo de aquí. Adios."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
msgid "Sorry, what?"
msgstr "Lo siento, ¿qué?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
msgid "Why are you repeating 'spirals' over and over again?"
msgstr "¿Por qué repites la palabra 'espirales' una y otra vez?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
msgid "Are you nuts?"
msgstr "¿Estás loco?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_Soldier_1.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NPC_Old_Guard_RED_Soldier_1.json
msgid "I'm afraid I can't talk now."
msgstr "Me temo que ahora no puedo hablar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_Soldier_1.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NPC_Old_Guard_RED_Soldier_1.json
msgid "Stay safe out there."
msgstr "Ten cuidado ahí fuera."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_Soldier_1.json
msgid "Welcome to camp Arabella"
msgstr "Bienvenido al campamento Arabella"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_Soldier_1.json
msgid "I'm supposed to direct all questions to my leadership."
msgstr "Se supone que debo dirigir todas las preguntas a mis lideres."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_Soldier_1.json
msgid "If you're looking to trade you'll need to talk to the quartermaster."
msgstr "Si quieres comerciar tendrás que hablar con el intendente."

#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Generic guard for the old guard.
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
msgid "Duhring"
msgstr "Duhring"

#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
#. ~ Generic guard for the old guard.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
msgid "Officer"
msgstr "Oficial"

#. ~ Job description of "Officer" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
msgid "I'm an officer for FOB Arabella"
msgstr "Soy un oficial del Campo De Batalla Arabella"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
msgid ""
"I don't have any use for you right now.  You will be informed if I need you,"
" soldier."
msgstr ""
"No tengo ningún uso para ti en este momento. Serás informado si te necesito,"
" soldado."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
msgid "Can you tell me about yourself?"
msgstr "¿Puede hablarme sobre ti?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
msgid "If it wasn't clear, you are dismissed soldier."
msgstr "Por si no quedaba claro, puedes retirarte soldado."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
msgid "I am clearly busy, soldier."
msgstr " Estoy claramente ocupado, soldado."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
msgid "Can I just ask you some questions?"
msgstr "¿Puedo hacerte unas preguntas?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
msgid "Go. Away."
msgstr "Vete. Fuera."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
msgid "If I have to tell you one more time so help me god…"
msgstr "Si tengo que decírtelo una vez más, que Dios te ayude..."

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Generic guard for the old guard.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_pilot.json
msgid "Pilot"
msgstr "Piloto"

#. ~ Job description of "Pilot" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_pilot.json
msgid "I'm a pilot."
msgstr "Soy un piloto."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_quartermaster.json
msgid "Welcome to camp Arabella, What will it be?"
msgstr "Bienvenido al campamento Arabella, ¿Qué es lo que quieres?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_quartermaster.json
msgid ""
"I'm the camp quartermaster.  Come and see me if you have anything valuable "
"to trade."
msgstr ""
"Soy el intendente del campamento. Ven a verme si tienes algo valioso para "
"comerciar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_quartermaster.json
msgid "If you're looking to trade you've come to the right place."
msgstr "Si quieres comerciar, has llegado al lugar adecuado."

#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "pizzaiolo"
msgstr "pizzaiolo"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "I got the cake.  Shall we move, <name_g>?"
msgstr "Tengo la tarta. ¿Nos vamos, <name_g>? "

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "If you still want to travel with me, let's go."
msgstr "Si todavía quieres viajar conmigo, vamos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "Lead the way, <name_g>."
msgstr "Te sigo, <name_g>."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "Are we there yet, my <name_g>?"
msgstr "¿Todavía no hemos llegado, mi <name_g>?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "We're here, <name_g>.  Let's celebrate."
msgstr "Ya llegamos, <name_g>. Vamos a celebrarlo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "Be patient.  We'll be there soon, <name_g>"
msgstr "Ten paciencia. Ya estamos llegando, <name_g>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid ""
"Ah, home sweet home.  It feels like I haven't been here for ages.  <swear>, "
"it looks so horrible now.  I guess it's because of <the_cataclysm>.  Thank "
"you for bringing me here, <name_g>.  Let's eat the cake."
msgstr ""
"Ah, hogar dulce hogar. Se siente como si no hubiera estado aquí por años. "
"<swear>, se ve tan horrible ahora. Supongo que es por <the_cataclysm> . "
"Gracias por traerme aquí, . Vamos a comernos el pastel."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "[*NOM-NOM*]"
msgstr "[*RICO-RICO*]"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid ""
"Mmm, delicious.  You know, you are good friend, and a good cook.  I'm glad "
"that I'm with you at the day like this.  Say, what do you think about me "
"going with you?  As you can see, my restaurant is thrashes, my house ruined,"
" the only option left is to travel somewhere, and it's better if I do it "
"with someone."
msgstr ""
"Mmm, delicioso. Sabes, eres un buen amigo, y un buen cocinero. Me alegro de "
"estar contigo en un día como hoy. Dime, ¿qué te parece si te acompaño? Como "
"puedes ver, mi restaurante está destrozado, mi casa arruinada y la única "
"opción que me queda es viajar a algún lugar, y creo que es mejor hacerlo con"
" alguien."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "Sure, <name_g>.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Por supuesto, <name_g>.<end_talking>"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid ""
"I'm just a regular pizzaiolo.  My father was a pizzaiolo, my grandfather was"
" a pizzaiolo and I also became a pizzaiolo.  I was making pizza my whole "
"life, until some american <name_b>s ruined my business!  I couldn't do "
"anything about this, but now, with <the_cataclysm> and <zombies> around, I "
"have a chance to get my revenge!"
msgstr ""
"Soy un pizzaiolo cualquiera. Mi padre era pizzaiolo, mi abuelo era pizzaiolo"
" y yo también me hice pizzaiolo. He hecho pizza toda mi vida, hasta que unos"
" <name_b> americanos me arruinaron el negocio. No pude hacer nada al "
"respecto, pero ahora, con <the_cataclysm>y  <zombies> alrededor, ¡tengo la "
"oportunidad de vengarme!"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "Angry pizzaiolo"
msgstr "Pizzaiolo enfadado"

#. ~ Description of mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid ""
"Bring the pizzaiolo to <color_light_blue>their rival's house</color> and "
"don't forget to <color_yellow>bring atleast 200 units of gasoline</color>.  "
"After you got there, talk to the pizzaiolo to start burning the house."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid ""
"I'm so <swear> angry!  I have an enemy that ruined my life, and I want "
"revenge for it!  I don't care about <the_cataclysm>, I just want to burn his"
" <swear> restaurant!  Will you help me?"
msgstr ""
"¡Estoy muy <swear> enfadado! ¡Tengo un enemigo que arruinó mi vida, y quiero"
" vengarme por ello! No me importa <the_cataclysm>, ¡sólo quiero quemar su "
"<swear> restaurante! ¿Me ayudarás?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid ""
"Good.  Let's go to his restaurant and <swear> burn it!  Oh, by the way, "
"could you bring gasoline with you, <name_g>?  I was so angry I forgot to "
"bring it with me…"
msgstr ""
"Bien. ¡Vamos a su restaurante y <swear> quemémoslo! Por cierto, ¿podrías "
"traer gasolina, <name_g>? Estaba tan enfadado que me olvidé de traerla..."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Family house"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "What?!  Why do you… ah, forget it."
msgstr "¿Qué? Por qué... ah, olvídalo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "Maybe we can find some gasoline at gas station."
msgstr "Tal vez podamos encontrar algo de gasolina en la gasolinera."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid ""
"Sweet, sweet revenge!  It smells so nice!  His restaurant burns, his legacy "
"is now ruined!  Even if he became a <zombie>, it still <swear> good."
msgstr ""
"¡Dulce, dulce venganza! ¡Huele tan bien! ¡Su restaurante arde, su legado "
"está ahora arruinado! Incluso si se convirtió en un<zombie> , todavía es "
"<swear> bueno."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "Find TrueFoodperson"
msgstr "Encuentra al verdadero FoodPerson"

#. ~ Description of mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "Help pizzaiolo find TrueFoodperson and kick his ass."
msgstr ""
"Ayuda a pizzaiolo a encontrar al verdadero FoodPerson y patéale el culo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid ""
"Ah, it's you, <name_g>.  Wanna continue on my revenge to all american "
"<name_b>s?"
msgstr ""
"Ah, eres tú, <name_g>. ¿Quieres seguir con mi venganza a todos los <name_b>s"
" americano?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid ""
"Good.  Next stop, Foodplace.  I always hated that place, especially that "
"<swear> <name_b> in his <dumb> mask.  I know he's still alive, hiding in his"
" <swear> <dumb> parody of a restaurant.  Take this bat.  Let's take a visit "
"to him, <name_g>, and kick his <swear> ass!"
msgstr ""
"Bien. Siguiente parada, Lugarcomida. Siempre odié ese lugar, especialmente "
"ese <name_b> con su <dumb>máscara. Sé que sigue vivo, escondido en su "
"<swear><dumb>parodia de restaurante. Toma este bate. ¡Vamos a "
"visitarle<name_g> y a patearle el trasero!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid ""
"I heard that these 'restaurants' use some kind of locking system for staff "
"room, so we would need to find a way to get there."
msgstr ""
"He oído que estos \"restaurantes\" utilizan algún tipo de sistema de cierre "
"para la sala de personal, por lo que tendríamos que encontrar una manera de "
"llegar allí."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Family house"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "I'm waiting."
msgstr "Estoy esperando."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "Another one bite the dust!  We did good, <name_g>."
msgstr "Otro que muerde el polvo. Lo hicimos bien, <name_g>."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "Pizza parlor"
msgstr "Pizzeria"

#. ~ Description of mission "Pizza parlor"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "Help pizzaiolo take back his restaurant."
msgstr "Ayuda a pizzaiolo a recuperar su restaurante."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid ""
"I need to make a last step to achieve my revenge, and the step is - my pizza"
" parlor.  Before <the_cataclysm>, the bank took my place, and now, some "
"<swear> <name_b>s occupied it and made it their base!  <swear> unbelievable,"
" I tell ya.  It's time for me to fight back, deal with this <swear> "
"<name_b>s and regain my honor.  Are you with me, <name_g>?"
msgstr ""
"Necesito hacer un algo más para lograr mi venganza, y  es - mi pizzería. "
"¡Antes del <the_cataclysm>, el banco tomó mi local, y ahora, algunos "
"<swear><name_b>s lo ocuparon y lo convirtieron en su base! <swear>increíble,"
" te digo. Es hora de que me defienda, de que me enfrente a estos "
"<swear><name_b>s y de que recupere mi honor. ¿Estás conmigo, <name_g>?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "<very> good.  Let's go."
msgstr "<very> bien. Vamos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid ""
"These <name_b>s might be heavily armed, so we need to prepare to face them."
msgstr ""
"Esos <name_b>s podrían estar fuertemente armados, así que tenemos que "
"prepararnos para enfrentarnos a ellos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid ""
"Nice, <very><swear> nice.  <swear>, this placed is thrashed.  "
"<swear><name_b>s thrashed my restaurant!  Okay, calm down, calm down, will "
"ya… At least I retrieved my place.  Thank you, <name_g>.  I couldn't make it"
" without you."
msgstr ""
"Bien, <very><swear>bien. <swear>, este lugar está destrozado. "
"¡<swear><name_b>han destrozado mi restaurante! Vale, cálmate, cálmate, "
"¿quieres? Al menos he recuperado mi sitio. Gracias, <name_g>. No podría "
"hacerlo sin ti."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "Family house"
msgstr "Casa Familiar"

#. ~ Description of mission "Family house"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid ""
"First bring pizzaiolo some chocolate cake then lead him to his family house."
msgstr ""
"Primero trae el pastel de chocolate al pizzero y después llevalo a la casa "
"de su familia."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Family house"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid ""
"Now, as my competitors dead, their places are ruined, it's time to relax… I "
"know, let's celebrate it!  Lead me to my house.  Also, we need a cake for "
"that.  What celebration without a cake, right?  I can teach you how to cook "
"it, if you want."
msgstr ""
"Ahora, que mis competidores han muerto, sus lugares están arruinados, es "
"hora de relajarse... ¡Ya sé, celebrémoslo! Llévame a mi casa. Además, "
"necesitamos un pastel para eso. ¿Qué celebración sin un pastel, no? Puedo "
"enseñarte a cocinarlo, si quieres."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Family house"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "Good.  Bring me chocolate cake and talk to me."
msgstr "Bien. Tráeme un pastel de chocolate y habla conmigo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Family house"
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid ""
"If you listened to me very closely, it wouldn't be hard for you to make it."
"  Good luck, <name_g>."
msgstr ""
"Si me escuchas con atención, no te será difícil lograrlo. Buena suerte, "
"<name_g>."

#. ~ Message about the player in an effect
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "You learn how to craft cake."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "Are we there yet, <name_g>?  I can't wait to burn that building!"
msgstr "¿Ya hemos llegado, <name_g>? ¡No puedo esperar a quemar ese edificio!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/missiondef.json
msgid "We're here.  Let's do it!"
msgstr "Estamos aquí. Vamos a hacerlo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
msgid "Be patient, <name_g>, we're getting there soon."
msgstr "Ten paciencia,<name_g>, pronto llegaremos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "Finally, someone who isn't part of those <zombies>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, today's your lucky day.  Hand over your stuff, or you'll be one "
"yourself."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "Hey, nice to meet you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "<greet>"
msgstr "<greet>"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/TALK_valhallist_gode.json
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/TALK_valhallist_mechanic.json
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/TALK_valhallist_member.json
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/TALK_valhallist_shopkeeper.json
msgid "Who are you, exactly?"
msgstr "¿Quién eres tu?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "Wanna buy something, maybe sell off what you don't need?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "Could I buy one of your pets?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid ""
"I worked here before <the_cataclysm> dumped everything in the <swear> bin.  "
"I took care of all the animals here, and when the <zombies> started roaming "
"the streets, I gathered every pet or stray I could.  I still take care of "
"them, just gotta worry about the <zombies> now on top of disease, "
"cleanliness, etc."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid ""
"That's quite noble of you, but how do you take care of so many animals?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid ""
"To be honest with you, it's been pretty difficult.  I sneak out at night or "
"whenever there's an opening to grab whatever I need and come back before "
"something notices me.  I've been held up for quite a while whenever a horde "
"decides to pass by.  Good thing we had some spare bookcases lying around, or"
" I'd be a goner by now."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scrapper.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NC_Yoshimi.json
msgid "Interesting."
msgstr "Interesante."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid ""
"I hate to see them go, but I think you'd be able to take better care of one "
"than I can right now.  I can sell you a cat or dog of your choosing, for $25"
" and $50, respectively."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "I've changed my mind, let's talk about something else."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "I'll have a dog."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "I'll have a cat."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "Hey stranger.  How's life treatin' ya these days?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#: data/mods/Defense_Mode/dialogue/TALK_WANDERING_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "Hand over your stuff!  Don't make any sudden moves, or you die!"
msgstr "¡Dame tus cosas! ¡No hagás ningún movimiento brusco o te mato!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "What brings you around here?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "Would you be interested in trading at all?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "Can I stay here for a while?"
msgstr "¿Puedo quedarme aquí un rato?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
msgid "Why don't you come with me?"
msgstr "¿Por qué no vienes conmigo?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
msgid ""
"I'm just an average person, really.  When a horde of those <swear> <zombies>"
" came knockin' on my door, I ran for it.  Good for me that someone left this"
" store open in the chaos, I ran inside and locked the place down.  There "
"isn't a thing in all of <city> that can bust through these walls and barred "
"windows, I'd reckon I'm the luckiest <name_b> in town."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "Why would someone leave a gun store open in all this chaos?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
msgid ""
"Well, they weren't really around to lock it up.  Whoever got here first blew"
" their head off with a 12-gauge, but they were up and movin', tried to kill "
"me too.  They're out in the dumpster now."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "I'm sorry to hear that.  Mabye we should change the subject."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/mods/Defense_Mode/dialogue/TALK_WANDERING_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "Freeze you <swear> <zombies>!"
msgstr "¡Quieto ahí <swear> <zombies>!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/mods/Defense_Mode/dialogue/TALK_WANDERING_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "&Hold up your hands.  \"Don't worry, I'm not going to hurt you\""
msgstr ""
"&Mantén las manos donde pueda verlas.  \"No te preocupes, no te haré daño\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid ""
"Oh, you're not one of the <zombies>.  Come on in, just don't cause any "
"trouble."
msgstr ""
"Ah, no eres uno de ellos. A esos <zombies>, me refiero. Ven, pasa, pero no "
"hagas ruido."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
#: data/mods/Defense_Mode/dialogue/TALK_WANDERING_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "I'll be back later."
msgstr "Vuelvo después."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "What are you doing in this deathtrap?"
msgstr "¿Qué estás haciendo aquí afuera?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
msgid ""
"I used to live here before <the_cataclysm>.  I was asleep when a horde of "
"<zombies> busted through the front, and in the chaos I wound up here.  When "
"the screaming stopped, I peaked out the door to find my neighbor stumbling "
"about with his face half-eaten, and I haven't left since."
msgstr ""
"Antes vivía aquí <the_cataclysm>.  Estaba dormido cuando una horda de "
"<zombies> rompió la puerta principal, y en el caos acabe aquí.  Cuando los "
"gritos cesaron, eche un vistazo por la puerta y encontré a mi vecino dando "
"tumbos con la mitad de su cara comida, y no me he ido desde entonces."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
msgid "Wow."
msgstr "Wow."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
msgid "<greet>."
msgstr "<greet>."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
msgid "Hey, stranger.  Glad to see a new face around here."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
msgid "Glad to see you too.  Now, hand over your things."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
msgid ""
"I was out here camping when <the_cataclysm> disturbed me.  I didn't know "
"anything was wrong until two <zombies> stumbled up here, and tried to kill "
"me.  I figured staying here would be my best bet, away from the cities."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
msgid "Haven't seen someone new in a while.  What brings you around here?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
msgid "Just wandering, <name_g>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
msgid ""
"I'll make this real simple for you.  Hand over your stuff, and no one gets "
"hurt, capiche?"
msgstr ""
"Voy a decirlo lo mas simple para ti. Dame tus cosas y nadie saldrá herido, "
"¿lo pillas?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
msgid "Can I purchase any of your liquor?"
msgstr "¿Puedo comprar algo de licor?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
msgid ""
"It's a bit dangerous to be out here alone.  Why don't you come with me?"
msgstr ""
"Es un poco peligroso estar aquí fuera solo. ¿Porque no vienes conmigo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
msgid "Anything I could do for you?"
msgstr "¿Algo que pueda hacer por ti?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
msgid ""
"I run this distillery you're standing in, before <the_cataclysm> it wasn't "
"so legal with the law.  I was in <city> making a deal on my product when a "
"horde of rioters busted in, so I ran for it.  I thought my business would be"
" a nice place to stay, so I came out here."
msgstr ""
"Regento la destilería sobre la que te asientas, antes del <the_cataclysm> no"
" era muy legal.  Estaba en <city> haciendo un trato con mi mercancía cuando "
"una horda de asaltantes entro a saco, así que salí corriendo. Pensé que mi "
"negocio seria un buen lugar donde quedarme, así que vine aquí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "Would you be interested in bartering?"
msgstr "¿Te interesaría intercambiar?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid ""
"They all said I was crazy for preparing for <the_cataclysm>.  Now, they're "
"all dead, and I'm still kickin'.  When the riots turned to hordes, I was "
"ready; all I had to do was dodge a few <zombies> to get back to my bastion."
"  I've been living safely here ever since."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid ""
"Well, I guess you could borrow one of the spare beds, just don't hog it.  I "
"kept a few in case someone else joined me, but no one I knew came here."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
msgid "Don't come any closer!"
msgstr "¡No te acerqués más!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_sickly_laborer.json
msgid "What's wrong?"
msgstr "¿Qué pasa?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
msgid ""
"Oh, you're not one of them.  Those <zombies>, I mean.  Come on in, just "
"don't cause any trouble."
msgstr ""
"Ah, no eres uno de ellos. A esos <zombies>, me refiero. Ven, pasa, pero no "
"hagas ruido."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
msgid ""
"When shit hit the fan, I ran out here to this emergency shelter.  "
"Fortunately, the place hadn't been looted yet and there weren't any "
"<zombies> lurking around."
msgstr ""
"Cuando se fue todo a la mierda, corrí hasta este refugio de evacuación. Por "
"suerte, el lugar todavía estaba impecable y no había ningún <zombies> dando "
"vueltas."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/camp_start.json
msgid ""
"Hey, I did some surveying and I believe this is a good spot to set up at."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/camp_start.json
msgid "Let's stay here, then.  I trust your decisions."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "meteorologist"
msgstr "meteorólogo"

#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Meteorologist"
msgstr "Meteorólogo"

#. ~ Job description of "Meteorologist" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Meteorologist."
msgstr "Meteoróloga"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Run, I need to run, where to run…"
msgstr "Correr, necesito correr, hacia donde correr…"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid ""
"Air temperature, precipitation, but what about… oh, I'm sorry, I didn't "
"notice you.  Hello."
msgstr ""
"Temperatura del aire, precipitaciones, pero qué… oh, lo siento, no me di "
"cuenta que estabas ahí. Hola."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid ""
"I have not seen living people for a long time.  Glad to see another "
"survivor.  Greetings, <name_g>."
msgstr ""
"Hace mucho tiempo que no veo a gente viva. Me alegra ver otro superviviente."
" Saludos, <name_g>."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Maybe I can help you with your problem?"
msgstr "¿Quizás pueda ayudarte con tu problema?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "I need more time.  Come back later."
msgstr "Necesito más tiempo. Vuelve más tarde."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid ""
"Help?  Help with what?  Oh, yes, yes.  If you know a place with many "
"survivors, can you take me there?  I doubt I can survive alone…"
msgstr ""
"¿Ayuda? ¿Ayuda con qué? Ah, sí, sí. Si conoces un lugar con muchos "
"supervivientes, ¿me podrias llevar hasta ahí? Dudo que pueda sobrevivir "
"solo…"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Yes, you can relax now."
msgstr "Sí, ya puedes relajarte."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Don't worry, we're getting there soon."
msgstr "No te preocupes, ya estamos llegando."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid ""
"Thank you.  I will never forget your kindness, <name_g>.  Take this book as "
"token of my gratitude."
msgstr ""
"Gracias. Nunca olvidaré tu amabilidad, <name_g>. Acepta este libro como "
"muestra de mi gratitud."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "I'm glad you still alive."
msgstr "Contento de verte con vida."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Me too."
msgstr "Yo también."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid ""
"I'm just a regular meteorologist.  In recent years I have worked at a "
"weather station, monitored the weather, state of air, read and wrote "
"reports, drew up schedules… in general, complete boredom.  In my free time I"
" was studying electronics and radio engineering, making various devices, "
"some for work, some just for fun.  When the first riots began, I gathered "
"all my things that I managed to take with me and settled here.  Since then "
"I've been sitting here, wasting my time doing all sorts of nonsense."
msgstr ""
"Solo soy un meteorólogo regular. En los últimos años estuve trabajando en la"
" estación del clima, monitoreando el clima, el estado del aire, leyendo y "
"escribiendo informes, planificando horarios… en general, aburrimiento total."
" En mi tiempo libre estaba estudiando electrónica e ingeniería de radio, "
"fabricando diversos dispositivos, a veces por trabajo y otras por diversión."
" Cuando empezaron los primeros disturbios, cogi todas mis pertenencias que "
"fui capaz de cargar y me establecí aquí. Desde entonces he estado sentado "
"aquí, malgastando mi tiempo en toda clase de tonterias."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
msgstr "Conseguir chatarra para el meteorólogo"

#. ~ Description of mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "The meteorologist asked to bring him 50 pieces of scrap."
msgstr "El meteorólogo me pidió que le trajera 50 trozos de chatarra."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "We need scrap metal to assemble a drone…"
msgstr "Necesitamos chatarra para ensamblar un dron…"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid ""
"I've been sitting here for a long time, and all that time I was wondering "
"how bad everything is outside.  I want to build a drone that I can use to "
"fly over New England, check the air condition, take a few pictures from "
"above to get a glimpse of how is it.  There were a lot of things in our back"
" room that could be useful, but still I'm missing a lot of things.  You look"
" like an experienced survivalist.  Can you help me?"
msgstr ""
"Llevo mucho tiempo sentado aquí, y todo ese tiempo me preguntaba cómo de mal"
" está todo fuera. Quiero construir un dron con el que pueda sobrevolar Nueva"
" Inglaterra, comprobar el estado del aire y tomar unas cuantas fotos desde "
"las alturas para hacerme una idea de cómo está la cosa. Hay un montón de "
"cosas en nuestra habitación trasera que podrían ser útiles, pero todavía me "
"faltan muchas cosas. Pareces un experimentado supervivencialista. ¿Puedes "
"ayudarme?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid ""
"Good.  I just need a little stuff: 50 scrap, 6 medium batteries, 5 small "
"high-quality lenses and a radio remote control.  Bring the scrap for now, "
"but don't forget about the rest."
msgstr ""
"Bien. Solo necesito unas pocas cosas: 50 chatarras, 6 baterías medianas, 5 "
"lentes pequeñas de alta calidad y un control remoto por raido. Trae la "
"chatarra por ahora, pero no te olvides del resto."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_barber.json
msgid "Maybe another time…"
msgstr "Tal vez en otro momento..."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid ""
"I don't think this is a difficult task.  Surely there is a lot of it "
"underfoot."
msgstr ""
"No creo que sea una tarea muy difícil. Seguro que hay un montón tirada por "
"ahí."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "How's it going?"
msgstr "\"¿Cómo te va?\""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Great, I'm starting to work on it…"
msgstr "Genial, me pongo a trabajar en ello..."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Why do you say that?"
msgstr "¿Por qué dices eso?"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
msgstr "Encuentra baterías para el meteorólogo"

#. ~ Description of mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "The meteorologist asked to bring him 6 medium batteries."
msgstr "El meteorólogo te pidió que le trajeras 6 baterías medianas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "We need batteries to assemble a drone…"
msgstr "Necesitamos baterías para ensamblar un dron…"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid ""
"Well, what's next on the list… yeah, batteries.  6 medium batteries would be"
" enough."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, ¿Qué sigue en la lista?… sí, baterías. Con 6 baterías medianas será "
"suficiente."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "I'm waiting for you."
msgstr "Te estoy esperando."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Try looking for some battery-powered trinkets and take them apart."
msgstr "Intenta buscar algún cachivache que funcione con pilas y desármalo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Great, I'm continue to work on it…"
msgstr "Genial, sigo trabajando en el dron..."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "The meteorologist asked to bring him 5 small high-quality lenses."
msgstr ""
"El meteorólogo me pidió conseguirle 5 lentes pequeñas de alta calidad."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "We need small high quality lenses for our drone…"
msgstr "Necesitamos lentes pequeñas de alta calidad para nuestro dron…"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid ""
"Well, what's next on the list… yeah, lenses.  5 small high-quality lenses "
"would be enough."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, ¿qué es lo siguiente en la lista?... Sí, lentes. 5 pequeños lentes de"
" alta calidad serían suficientes."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Try looking for telescopes or microscopes to dismantle."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Great, I'm continuing to work on it…"
msgstr "Genial, sigo trabajando en con ello..."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "The meteorologist asked to bring him a radio controller."
msgstr "El meteorólogo te pidió que le trajeras un control remoto por radio."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "We need an RC to assemble a drone…"
msgstr "Necesitamos un RC para ensamblar un dron…"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid ""
"Well, what's next on the list… yeah, radio control.  Any kind will do, but "
"the simplest one is better, so I can easily reconfigure it for my drone."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, ¿qué es lo siguiente en la lista?... Sí, el control remoto por radio."
" Cualquier tipo servirá, pero el más sencillo es mejor, así puedo "
"reconfigurarlo fácilmente para mi dron."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "I advise you to search in a store, such as electronics or toy store."
msgstr ""
"Te aconsejo que busques en una tienda, por ejemplo de electrónica o de "
"juguetes."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid ""
"Great, very little work left.  I need a few days to finish all this, and to "
"try it in work.  I hope everything will work fine!  While I'm working on the"
" drone, you can read this book.  Maybe you can learn something new from it."
msgstr ""
"Genial, queda muy poco trabajo. Necesito unos días para terminar todo esto, "
"y probarlo. ¡Espero que todo funcione bien! Mientras trabajo en el dron, "
"puedes leer este libro. Quizás puedas aprender algo nuevo de él."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "The meteorologist asked to bring him his crashed drone."
msgstr "El meteorólogo te pidió que le trajeras su dron estrellado."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid "I've lost the drone, we should find out what happened…"
msgstr "He perdido el dron, debemos averiguar que ocurrió..."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid ""
"I'm glad that you are alive and that you haven't forgot about me.  The drone"
" turned out to be great, it managed to take off and even was able to fly "
"several hundred meters!  Unfortunately, after that, I lost control of it… I "
"don't know what happened to it, though.  Maybe you can check?  I'm a little "
"afraid to go out there…"
msgstr ""
"Me alegro de que estes vivo y de que no te hayas olvidado de mí. El dron "
"resultó ser genial, consiguió despegar e incluso fue capaz de volar varios "
"cientos de metros. Desgraciadamente, después de eso, perdí el control del "
"mismo... Aunque no sé qué ocurrió con él. ¿Quizás puedas comprobarlo? Me da "
"un poco de miedo salir ahí fuera..."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid ""
"I don't know quite what happened.  Maybe something noticed my drone and "
"tried to bring it down.  Be careful."
msgstr ""
"No sé muy bien qué ocurrió. Tal vez algo se dio cuenta de mi dron y trató de"
" derribarlo. Ten cuidado."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
msgid ""
"Hmm, I see that the drone is not with you.  Maybe at least the memory module"
" remains?  Okay, show it to me… hmm, situation is worse than I expected, "
"much, much worse… I'm not feeling good.  I don't feel safe in this place "
"anymore.  I have to run, run somewhere.  But where to run if these "
"<monster>s are everywhere…"
msgstr ""
"Hmm, veo que no llevas el dron contigo. ¿Quizás al menos queda el módulo de "
"memoria? Vale, enséñamelo... hmm, la situación es peor de lo que esperaba, "
"mucho, mucho peor... No me siento bien. Ya no me siento seguro en este "
"lugar. Tengo que correr, correr a algún lugar. Pero a dónde correr si están "
"(<monster>) por todas partes..."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
msgid ""
"I was homeless before everything went down, just camping out here for a "
"while.  Stuck up <name_b>s shunned me for my condition, but they're all dead"
" now.  I guess I'm better off than they are."
msgstr ""
"Era un vagabundo antes de que todo se derrumbara, acampando por ahí. Los "
"creídos de <name_b> me evitaban por mi estado pero ahora están todos "
"muertos. Creo que estoy en mejores circunstancias que ellos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
msgid ""
"I guess you probably wouldn't have noticed this place before shit hit the "
"fan, but I've been down here for quite a while."
msgstr ""
"Supongo que ni te habías enterado de este lugar hasta que todo se fue a la "
"mierda, pero yo estoy aquí desde hace un tiempo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
msgid ""
"Nothing to it.  Before <the_cataclysm>, it didn't take much to find yourself"
" here.  And I guess it just made sense to stay.  We seem to be doing better "
"than most, anyway."
msgstr ""
"No mucho. Antes del <the_cataclysm>, no era muy difícil terminar aquí. Y "
"supongo que tenía sentido quedarse. Parece que estamos mejor que la mayoría,"
" de todos modos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
msgid "Surviving, as I always have.  Is that what you mean?"
msgstr "Sobreviviendo, como siempre hice. ¿Te referías a eso?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
msgid ""
"It's hard to say exactly what I'm doing out here, but I guess one thing just"
" leads to another and… well, you're just being nice when you ask, aren't "
"you?  It doesn't matter now anyway.  I'm here and I'm still alive."
msgstr ""
"Es difícil decir exactamente lo que estoy haciendo pero supongo que una cosa"
" lleva a la otra y… bueno, ¿me preguntas solo por ser simpático, no? Ahora "
"ya no importa. Estoy aquí y estoy vivo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid "Who are you?  Would you like to trade?"
msgstr "¿Quién eres? ¿Quieres comerciar?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
msgid "Where might your friends be?"
msgstr "¿Dónde están tus amigos?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
msgid "Can I stay here?"
msgstr "¿Me puedo quedar aquí?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid "How's that smoker coming along?"
msgstr "¿Y cómo va el ahumador?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid ""
"I was homeless for a while before <the_cataclysm>.  I met some buddies out "
"on the road and we were camping out here.  Now we're just scraping by on "
"what we can find, mostly.  We're willing to trade, though.  Who knows, you "
"might find yourself a good deal."
msgstr ""
"Fui vagabundo por un tiempo antes del <the_cataclysm>. Conocí a unos amigos "
"en la ruta y estábamos haciendo camping acá. Ahora estamos haciendo durar "
"las cosas que encontramos, casi todo el tiempo. Queremos comerciar, igual. "
"Vete a saber, tal vez encuentres un buen negocio aquí."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid ""
"Making ends meet, even in the worst circumstances.  We've been camping out "
"here now, trading with whoever passes by.  If something catches your eye, "
"let me know."
msgstr ""
"Sobreviviendo económicamente, incluso en las peores circunstancias. "
"Estuvimos de camping aquí, comerciando con el que pasara. Si te interesa "
"algo, házmelo saber."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid ""
"We got tired of being out on the road and decided to stay here for a bit.  "
"We've found a lot of useful stuff out and about, so if you see anything you "
"need I'll make you a deal."
msgstr ""
"Nos cansamos de estar en la ruta y decidimos quedarnos aquí un tiempo. "
"Encontramos muchas cosas útiles en varios lugares, así que si ves algo que "
"necesitas, lo hablamos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid ""
"They should be around here somewhere.  We usually go out in teams to "
"scavenge, and they haven't told me about anything yet.  They might have "
"something for you to do."
msgstr ""
"Deben andar por aquí. Generalmente, salimos en grupos a rebuscar y no me "
"avisaron nada todavía. Tal vez tengan algún trabajo para ti."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid ""
"Well, I don't see anything wrong with it.  We should have a spare bed in "
"that tent you could sleep on.  Just don't cause any trouble."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, no veo nada malo en eso. Deberíamos tener una cama para que duermas "
"en alguna carpa. Pero no generes ningún problema."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid ""
"Sure!  It turned out well enough for us, and it's one of the few fresh meats"
" we can find.  I'll pay fairly for it."
msgstr ""
"¡Seguro! Resultó ser suficiente para nosotros y es una de las carnes más "
"frescas que podemos encontrar. Voy a pagar un precio justo por ella."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid "I have nothing."
msgstr "No tengo nada."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid "I have nothing.  I'd best get going."
msgstr "No tengo nada. Mejor me voy yendo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid ""
"It's wonderful!  We've been preserving a lot more of what we manage to "
"scavenge so we won't have to worry about our food going bad for a while.  "
"We'd be willing to sell some of the excess, if you want."
msgstr ""
"¡Es maravilloso! Hemos preservado mucho más de lo que pudimos rebuscar así "
"no nos tenemos que preocupar de que nuestra comida se pudra. Estamos "
"dispuestos a vender un poco del exceso, si te interesa."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid "I think I'll buy 10 slices.  [$20]"
msgstr "Creo que voy a comprar 10 pedazos. [$20]"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid "You think 20 slices would be alright?  [$40]"
msgstr "¿Te parece que 20 pedazos está bien? [$40]"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid "I'll take 50 slices of the stuff.  [$100]"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
msgid "Who are you, and what are you doing here?"
msgstr "¿Quién eres y qué estás haciendo aquí?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
msgid "Nice to meet you.  I mean no harm."
msgstr "Un gusto conocerte. No tengo malas intenciones."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
msgid "What's with that guy in the tent?"
msgstr "¿Qué le pasa a ese chaval en la carpa?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
msgid "Want to trade?"
msgstr "¿Quieres comerciar?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
msgid ""
"Oh, they're right over there, and one of us is in that tent over there.  "
"They handle any stuff we manage to scavenge, so feel free to trade for what "
"you want."
msgstr ""
"Oh, están ahí y uno de nosotros está en esa carpa de ahí. Manejan todo lo "
"que podemos rebuscar así que siéntete libre de comerciar por lo que quieras."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
msgid ""
"Thanks for the offer, but I don't have anything to spare right now.  One of "
"my buddies over in that tent handles stuff like this, though.  You might "
"find something."
msgstr ""
"Gracias por la oferta pero no tengo nada para ofrecer en este momento. Uno "
"de mis compañeros en esa carpa maneja cosas como estas. Tal vez consigas "
"algo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
msgid ""
"Well, they were the brightest of us when all hell broke loose.  They managed"
" to get us some food and weapons early on.  I guess that just kinda made "
"them the leader."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, era el más inteligente de nosotros cuando todo se volvió un infierno."
" Logró conseguirnos comida y armas desde el inicio. Supongo que eso lo "
"convirtió en el líder."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Sticky Situation"
msgstr "Situación Pegajosa"

#. ~ Description of mission "Sticky Situation"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid ""
"Kill some slimes in exchange for credit with some of the traders and bring "
"back six of their slime scraps."
msgstr ""
"Matar unos légamos a cambio de crédito con algunos comerciantes y traer seis"
" pedazos de légamo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "I need some help."
msgstr "Necesito ayuda."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid ""
"We've had some trouble with slimes not far from us.  It's been hard going "
"through there with all them around, so I want you to go take care of it."
msgstr ""
"Tuvimos algunos problemas con légamos no muy lejos de aquí. Es difícil pasar"
" por ahí con todos esos bichos alrededor así que me gustaría que lo pudieras"
" solucionar."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "I'll be here when you get back."
msgstr "Estaré aquí cuando vuelvas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "No problem.  I'm sure one of us will get to it anyway."
msgstr "No hay problema. Seguro que uno de nosotros lo va a hacer."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid ""
"Sure, they can be cut, but I'd say it's better to splatter them with "
"something large and heavy."
msgstr ""
"Seguro, pueden ser cortados pero te diría que es mejor aplastarlos con algo "
"grande y pesado."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Are those slimes dead yet?"
msgstr "¿Ya te encargaste de esos légamos?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid ""
"Nice.  I'll just take those off your hands.  Might be good for greasing the "
"bike chains and door hinges around here even though it is a bit… abnormal."
msgstr ""
"Genial. Déjame encargarme de esto. Puede servir para engrasar cadenas de "
"bicicletas y bisagras aunque sea un poco… anormal."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid ""
"You don't look nearly as sticky as you're supposed to.  Get back to it."
msgstr ""
"No pareces tan pegajoso como se supone que deberías estar. Vete a hacerlo, "
"hazme el favor."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Did they give you the slip?  It's worse than I thought, then."
msgstr "¿Se te escaparon? Es peor de lo que pensé, entonces."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Arthropod Hunting"
msgstr "Cacería de Artrópodos"

#. ~ Description of mission "Arthropod Hunting"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid ""
"Kill some ants and bring back ten slices of their meat in exchange for "
"credit with some of the traders."
msgstr ""
"Matar algunas hormigas y traer diez pedazos de su carne para venderle a los "
"comerciantes."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid ""
"The last time we went out scouting we found some gargantuan ants crawling "
"around.  We thought we might see how they taste, if they could be cooked and"
" whatnot.  I want you to go kill one and bring back some of its meat."
msgstr ""
"La última vez que salimos a explorar encontramos hormigas pantagruélicas "
"dando vueltas. Pensamos que podríamos probar su sabor si pueden ser "
"cocinadas. Quiero que vayas a matar una y nos traigas un poco de su carne"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Alright, I can understand that."
msgstr "Bueno, puedo entenderlo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "A shotgun of some sort might work well."
msgstr "Una escopeta de alguna clase podría funcionar bien."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Do you have the meat?"
msgstr "¿Tienes la carne?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid ""
"Nice.  I'll get these cooked up.  Who knows, we might want some more in the "
"future."
msgstr ""
"Bien. Voy a cocinar esto. Vete a saber, tal vez queramos conseguir más en el"
" futuro."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "You sure?  I don't see my meat anywhere."
msgstr "¿Seguro? No veo la carne por aquí."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Ah, well.  It's no big deal."
msgstr "Ah, bueno. No es para tanto."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Refurbishments"
msgstr "Remodelación"

#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Obtain 100 planks."
msgstr "Conseguir 100 tablones."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid ""
"My buddies and I have decided to stay here for a while.  This is about the "
"only safe place out here, and it's kinda become our home.  Anyway, we're "
"going to build a wall.  Our old logs have provided a bunch of the wood, but "
"we still need quite a few planks.  About 100 of them.  If you could get it "
"for us, I'd be grateful."
msgstr ""
"Mis compañeros y yo decidimos quedarnos aquí por un tiempo. Es el único "
"lugar más o menos seguro y se está convirtiendo en nuestra casa. De todas "
"maneras, vamos a construir una pared. Nuestros viejos troncos nos han dado "
"un montón de madera pero todavía necesitamos varios tablones. Unos 100 mas o"
" menos. Si los puedes conseguir, estaríamos muy agradecidos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Thank you.  We'll be sure to compensate your efforts."
msgstr ""
"Gracias. Vamos a asegurarnos de que seas recompensando por tus esfuerzos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Alright, I can understand that.  I guess I'll have to get it myself."
msgstr "Bueno, te entiendo. Supongo que las voy a tener que conseguir yo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid ""
"Any nearby forest should have all you need.  Otherwise, you might try "
"breaking down some furniture in town."
msgstr ""
"Cualquier bosque cercano debería tener lo que buscas. Si no, puedes intentar"
" rompiendo algunos muebles en el pueblo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Do you have my lumber?"
msgstr "¿Conseguiste mis madera?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Thank you.  We'll start right away."
msgstr "Gracias. Vamos a empezar inmediatamente."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "I can tell you're lying.  I don't see shit."
msgstr "Me doy cuenta que estás mintiendo. No trajiste un carajo."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Refurbishments Pt. II"
msgstr "Remodelación II"

#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Obtain 150 planks."
msgstr "Conseguir 150 tablones."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid ""
"Now that we've got the wall done, we decided to move out of these old tents."
"  We still have some leftover nails but we need more wood.  So, if you could"
" get us 150 planks, we'd be grateful."
msgstr ""
"Ahora que ya tenemos la pared, decidimos mudar estas viejas carpas. Todavía "
"tenemos algunos clavos pero vamos a necesitar más madera. Si nos puedes "
"conseguir 150 tablones, te lo agradeceríamos."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Refurbishments Pt. III"
msgstr "Remodelación III"

#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Obtain 6 ropes."
msgstr "Conseguir 6 sogas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid ""
"Our entrance is wide open so we're building a gate over it.  Problem is we "
"don't have any ropes.  If you could find some for us, we'll pay you."
msgstr ""
"Nuestra entrada está abierta así que vamos a construir una verja. El "
"problema es que no tenemos sogas. Si nos pudieras conseguir algunas, te lo "
"pagaremos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid ""
"If you can't find any rope around, one of our books should have something on"
" rope-making.  Most plants can be woven into a halfway decent rope."
msgstr ""
"Si no encuentras ninguna soga por aquí, uno de nuestros libros debería tener"
" algo acerca de la fabricación de la soga. La mayoría de las plantas se "
"pueden atar para hacer una soga decente."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Do you have my ropes?"
msgstr "¿Conseguiste mis sogas?"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
msgstr "Remodelación IV"

#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Obtain a wood saw."
msgstr "Conseguir una sierra para madera."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid ""
"We appreciate all of your help but we can't rely on everyone else to do "
"things for us.  I'd be willing to buy a wood saw of some kind from you so we"
" can cut our own wood as needed."
msgstr ""
"Agradecemos toda tu ayuda pero no podemos pedirle a nadie más que nos traiga"
" cosas. Me gustaría comprar una sierra para madera de algún tipo, así "
"podríamos cortar nuestra madera a medida que la necesitemos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "A hardware store or lumbermill should have one."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Do you have my saw?"
msgstr "¿Conseguiste mi sierra?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Thank you.  Pick what you want from our stash."
msgstr "Gracias. Elegí lo que quieras de nuestro depósito."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Refurbishments Pt. V"
msgstr "Remodelación V"

#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Obtain a shovel."
msgstr "Conseguir una pala."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid ""
"Our sanitation here has become… problematic.  We've mostly just been going "
"outside the walls to piss.  Not only is it kinda unhealthy, but the last "
"time I wandered out I almost got eaten!  So, if you'd get us a shovel, we "
"could make a latrine for ourselves.  We'll pay you fairly, as usual."
msgstr ""
"Nuestra higiene se ha vuelto… problemática. Hemos estado meando apenas "
"afuera de las paredes. Y no solo es poco higiénico si no que la última vez "
"que salí ¡casi me comen! Así que si nos pudieras conseguir una pala, "
"podríamos hacer nuestro baño. Te lo vamos a pagar de manera justa, como "
"siempre."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "A hardware store should have one lying around."
msgstr "En una ferretería debería haber alguna tirada."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Do you have the shovel?"
msgstr "¿Conseguiste mi pala?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Thank you.  We're eternally grateful to you."
msgstr "Gracias. Estamos eternamente agradecidos contigo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "I'll do it myself, then."
msgstr "Entonces lo voy a hacer yo mismo."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgstr "Remodelación VI"

#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Obtain a charcoal smoker."
msgstr "Conseguir un ahumador a carbón."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid ""
"Turns out that ant meat you got us wasn't actually too bad.  A little tough,"
" sure, but perfectly edible.  The problem now is we need a way of preserving"
" it.  One of those portable charcoal smokers would be really great.  Heck, "
"you might even wanna buy some."
msgstr ""
"Resulta que la carne de hormiga que nos trajiste no estaba tan mal. Un poco "
"dura, sí, pero perfectamente comestible. El problema ahora es que "
"necesitamos una manera de preservarla. Uno de esos ahumadores a carbón "
"portátiles nos vendría muy bien. Incluso puede que quieras comprarnos algo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid ""
"Maybe try a farm?  I bet those rural folks were pretty invested in "
"preserving their food."
msgstr ""
"¿Tal vez en una granja? Supongo que la gente de campo teníamos buenas "
"maneras de preservar su comida."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Do you have the charcoal smoker?"
msgstr "¿Conseguiste el ahumador a carbón?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
msgid "Thank you.  We'll get started right away."
msgstr "Gracias. Vamos a empezar ya mismo."

#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ A person from elsewhere.
#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
msgid "Involuntary Traveler"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Job description of "No class" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
msgid "I'm from another world."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
msgid "Dell hastro bovice?  Arand natick res?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
msgid "What?"
msgstr "¿Qué?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
msgid "Jand rawdle?  Ignate hasture."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
msgid ""
"I guess there's no reason to expect an interdimensional traveler to speak "
"English."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
msgid ""
"My god, you've got to get me out of here.  The things… the things they've "
"done… please help."
msgstr ""
"Por dios, tienes que sacarme de aquí. Las cosas... las cosas que han "
"hecho... por favor, ayúdame."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
msgid "Aren't you a little short to be a stormtrooper?"
msgstr "¿No eres un poquito bajo para ser un soldado de asalto?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
msgid "Please, help me."
msgstr "Por favor, ayúdame."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
msgid "Can you get me out of this hell hole?"
msgstr "¿Puedes sacarme de este agujero del infierno?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
msgid "Who are you?  Are you real?"
msgstr "¿Quién eres? ¿Eres real?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
msgid "Can you please save me?  I have to get out of here."
msgstr "¿Puedes salvarme, por favor? Tengo que salir de aquí."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/TALK_valhallist_member.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
msgid "Hallelujah, rescue!"
msgstr "¡Aleluya, rescate!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/TALK_valhallist_member.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
msgid "I can't believe my eyes.  Thank you, thank you!"
msgstr "No puedo creer lo que ven mis ojos. ¡Gracias, gracias!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
msgid "You're… you're actually real!"
msgstr "¡Eres... eres de verdad real!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
msgid "How are you here?  Are you one of them, somehow?  What's going on?"
msgstr ""
"¿Cómo estás aquí? ¿Eres uno de ellos, de alguna tipo? ¿Qué esta pasando?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
msgid "Come with me, if you want to live."
msgstr "Sigueme, si quieres vivir."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
msgid "I've no use for weaklings.  Run.  Now."
msgstr "No me sirven los débiles. Corre. Ahora."

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Random NPC, non persistent, tells you about being a guard and directs you
#. to free merchants.
#. ~ Random NPC, non persistent, doesn't have much to say.
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Caravan Guard"
msgstr "Guardia de Caravana"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Well well, another traveler.  Don't try anything, you're outnumbered here "
"and we're well armed."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, bueno, otro viajero. No intentes nada raro, somos muchos más y "
"estamos armados"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"We're just travelers, making a pit stop.  Might be willing to trade a bit, "
"if you've got anything to share.  We're not looking for trouble, there's "
"plenty of that on the roads already."
msgstr ""
"Solo somos viajeros haciendo una parada técnica. Podría ser buena idea "
"comerciar, si tienes algo para compartir. No estamos buscando problemas, ya "
"hay muchos de esos por los caminos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"We're with a larger group of survivors, working out of one of the old FEMA "
"bunkers.  Folks have taken to calling us Free Merchants, although that "
"sounds kinda on the nose to me.  We know about a few survivor groups and we "
"make regular trips around, sharing supplies back and forth and bringing them"
" home.  We're on the way back now."
msgstr ""
"Estamos con un grupo más grande de supervivientes, trabajando en uno de los "
"viejos búnker de FEMA. Algunos nos llaman Mercaderes Libres, y eso me parece"
" que suena bastante exacto. Sabemos que existen algunos grupos de "
"supervivientes y hacemos viajes regularmente por aquí, compartiendo nuestras"
" cosas, llevando y trayendo hasta nuestra casa. Ahora estamos volviendo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Where is 'home'?"
msgstr "¿Y dónde está su 'casa'?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Here, I'll mark it on your map.  Feel free to come by and trade, or if "
"you're the type, we might have use for your services as a merc."
msgstr ""
"Aquí, lo voy a marcar en tu mapa. Ven cuando quieras a comerciar o, si eres "
"de esa clase, podrías usar tus servicios como mercenario."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Hey, thanks.  Well, let's trade."
msgstr "Eh, gracias. Bueno, vamos a ver qué podemos negociar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Always good to do a little trading."
msgstr "Siempre es bueno comerciar un poco."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Actually I had a little more to trade still."
msgstr "En realidad, todavía tengo un poco más que me gustaría negociar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Sup?  Nice to see a survivor.  If you're here for business, talk to the "
"trader."
msgstr ""
"¿Cómo va? Qué bueno ver otro superviviente. Si estás aquí para hacer algún "
"negocio, habla con el comerciante."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for the tip."
msgstr "Gracias por el consejo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Hi again.  You want something?"
msgstr "Hola, otra vez. ¿Querías algo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "You looking for work?  I might be hiring."
msgstr "¿Estás buscando trabajo? Estoy buscando gente."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Nope, just saying hi."
msgstr "Nop, solamente pasaba a saludar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"I'm a caravan guard, working for the Free Merchants.  I'm an independent "
"contractor though.  Seems like a good way to get safety in numbers and try "
"to find a safe place to settle down."
msgstr ""
"Soy guardia de la caravana, trabajo para los Mercaderes Libres. Pero soy "
"contratista independiente. Parece una buena manera de estar seguros siendo "
"muchos e intentar encontrar un lugar a salvo donde establecernos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "So you're working for these guys, but aren't one of them?"
msgstr "Así que estás trabajando para esta gente pero ¿no eres uno de ellos?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"The Free Merchants?  Do they have some kind of trade outpost or anything "
"like that?"
msgstr ""
"¿Los Mercaderes Libres? ¿Tienen alguna clase de puesto de comercio o algo "
"como eso?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "It's a living, eh?  I'd better get going."
msgstr "Es una manera de vivir, eh. Mejor me voy."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, these guys snagged some kind of FEMA evacuation bunker during the "
"early part of <the_cataclysm> and hoard the space.  They don't let anyone "
"else join, but they need supplies, so they send out traders, and those "
"traders need protection, so they send out guys like me."
msgstr ""
"Sí, estos tipos agarraron una especie de búnker de FEMA durante la primera "
"parte del <the_cataclysm> y acapararon el lugar. No dejan que nadie más se "
"les una pero necesitan suministros así que mandan comerciantes, y esos "
"comerciantes necesitan protección así que los mandan con tipos como yo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "How do I get there?"
msgstr "¿Y cómo llego hasta ahí?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"I'm good for the moment, but you can usually find a merc or two waiting "
"between jobs, back at the Free Merchant base."
msgstr ""
"Por ahora estoy bien pero generalmente, puedes encontrar algún mercenario "
"esperando trabajo en la base de los Mercaderes Libres."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for the tip!  I'll be on my way."
msgstr "¡Gracias por el consejo! Voy a seguir mi camino."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Sure, I can mark it on your map if you like.  Here."
msgstr "Seguro, te lo puedo marcar en tu mapa si quieres. Aquí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for the tip!  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "¡Gracias por el consejo! ¿Qué me estabas diciendo antes?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"*tips their hat down from their eyes and looks at you blearily.  \"Huh?  "
"Hey, I'm tryin'a sleep here.  I was on night watch."
msgstr ""
"*inclina el sombrero y te mira con sueño. \"¿Uh? Eh, estoy tratando de "
"dormir. Estuve en el turno de noche."

#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
#. ~ A survivor who sometimes visits the refugee center.
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "John Bailey"
msgstr "John Bailey"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*looks up at you, taking a moment to place your face, then grins broadly.  "
"He looks about the same as when you last saw him, perhaps a little more fit."
"  \"So, you're still playing on the 'living' team, huh?  Glad to see you're "
"still kicking around.  Always good to run into a familiar face nowadays.\""
msgstr ""
"*levanta la vista para mirarte, se toma un momento para ubicar tu cara, "
"luego sonríe de oreja a oreja. Está casi igual de la última vez que lo "
"viste, tal vez un poco en mejor estado. . \"¿Así que todavía juegas en el "
"equipo de los 'vivos', eh? Me alegra ver que todavía estas dando vueltas. "
"Siempre es bueno encontrarse una cara familiar estos días.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*glances your way, then makes eye contact as you move closer to speak.  He "
"is a strong-looking man in his mid forties, his hair greying and his face "
"flecked with stubble and travel dust.  The clothes he's wearing are clearly "
"scavenged, though they fit well, and he has the build of someone who until "
"recently had the luxury of carrying a few extra pounds.  \"Hi there.\"  He "
"presents his hand to shake.  \"You don't look like you belong here.  Name's "
"Bailey, John Bailey.\""
msgstr ""
"*mira hacia ti, luego hace contacto visual mientras te acercas para hablar. "
"Es un hombre fuerte con cuarenta y tantos años, con su pelo encanecido y su "
"cara manchada con barba y polvo. Tiene ropa que claramente encontró por ahí "
"pero le queda bien, y tiene la estructura de una persona que hasta hace poco"
" tenía el lujo de tener unos kilitos de más. \"Hola.\" Extiende su mano para"
" saludar. \"No parece que seas de este lugar. Mi nombre es Bailey, John "
"Bailey.\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Hi John.  What are you doing here?"
msgstr "Hola, John. ¿Qué haces aquí?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Hi John, I'm afraid I can't stay to talk."
msgstr "Hola, John. Lamento no poder quedarme a conversar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*nods as you approach, then smiles and stretches casually.  \"Anything I can"
" do for you, friend?\""
msgstr ""
"*asiente cuando te acercas, después sonríe y se estira. \"¿Puedo hacer algo "
"por ti, amigo?\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What do you know about this place?"
msgstr "¿Qué sabes de este lugar?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "You looking for any kind of work?"
msgstr "¿Estás buscando algún trabajo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Not at the moment, thanks."
msgstr "Por el momento no, gracias."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Like I said,\" John shrugs.  \"I'm just checking "
msgstr "Como te dije,\" John encoge los hombros. \"Solo estoy mirando "

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Same as you, I imagine,\" John shrugs.  \"Checking "
msgstr "Lo mismo que tu, supongo,\" John encoge los hombros. \"Mirando "

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"the place out, doing a little shopping.  Then I'll be on my way again.  "
"Might see if they have any work that needs done first, if the price is "
"right."
msgstr ""
"el lugar, buscando algo para comprar. Después voy a seguir mi camino. Por "
"ahí miro a ver si tienen algún trabajo para ofrecerme, por el precio "
"adecuado."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What are you shopping for?"
msgstr "¿Qué estas comprando?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "On your way\" where?"
msgstr "¿Tu camino a dónde?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What kind of work are you looking for?"
msgstr "¿Qué clase de trabajo estás buscando?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Got time to teach me anything?"
msgstr "¿Tienes tiempo para enseñarme algo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Sounds about the same as me, yep.  I'd better get back to it."
msgstr "Parece lo mismo que yo, sí. Mejor vuelvo a eso."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"I don't really know.  Food stocks aren't too bad for me and mine, I found a "
"stock of canned goods early on that will last us for a while yet.  I don't "
"use a gun if I can avoid it, too noisy.  I notice these guys seem to keep a "
"lot of building supplies though, and trying to get a vehicle downtown to "
"loot a hardware store or a lumberyard is suicide, so I think that's where "
"they're going to get my money.  I wonder if they deliver."
msgstr ""
"La verdad que no sé. El suministro de comida no está tan mal para los míos, "
"encontré comida enlatada que nos va a durar durante un tiempo. No uso armas "
"si lo puedo evitar, hacen demasiado ruido. Vi que estos tipos parecían tener"
" muchos materiales de construcción e intentar conseguir un vehículo para "
"conseguir botín en una ferretería o un aserradero es suicida, así que pensé "
"que ahí era donde podía conseguir mi dinero. Me pregunto si hacen envíos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Where are you headed next?"
msgstr "¿Y después para dónde vas?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Who is \"you and yours\"?"
msgstr "¿Quiénes son \"los tuyos\"?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Are you looking for work?"
msgstr "¿Estás buscando trabajo?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"You'd do better to talk to the people here about it.  Seems like a bunch of "
"them gathered here in the early days of <the_cataclysm> and managed to make "
"it through.  It's the biggest bunch of survivors I've found yet, but most of"
" them hunker up in the basement.  I can understand the urge.  We've all been"
" through way too much.  They say they don't have room for more people "
"though, so I'm just here to do some shopping, see if there's work to be "
"done, then move on."
msgstr ""
"Te conviene hablar con la gente de aquí sobre eso. Parece como si un grupo "
"se reunió aquí en los primeros días del <the_cataclysm> y lograron "
"sobrevivir. Es el grupo más grande de supervivientes que encontré por ahora,"
" pero la mayoría está refugiado en el sótano. Puedo entender la necesidad. "
"Todos hemos pasado por muchas cosas jodidas. Dicen que no tienen lugar para "
"más gente así que solo vengo a comprar cosas, ver si necesitan algún trabajo"
" y después me voy."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Move on\" where?"
msgstr "¿Te vas a dónde?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Nice talking to you, I've gotta go."
msgstr "Me gusta hablar contigo, ahora me tengo que ir."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Who can say, really?  I don't really have a strong plan.  Depends on how "
"this trip goes.  Once my vehicle is full up, I'll have to head back to my "
"hideout and check on everyone there.  I don't like being gone too long."
msgstr ""
"¿Quién podría decirlo, no? La verdad es que no tengo un plan firme. Depende "
"de cómo vaya el viaje. Cuando mi vehículo esté lleno, voy a volver a mi "
"escondite y ver cómo andan todos. No me gusta irme por mucho tiempo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Who is \"everyone\"?"
msgstr "¿Quiénes son \"todos\"?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Huh, well, the short story is, I got my wife and kids out of town in the "
"really, really early days.  She's got great intuition for stuff and when she"
" told me to get ready to leave town, I figured at worst we'd have an "
"unnecessary early spring vacation in my dad's old cabin, you know?  "
"Obviously, turns out trusting her gut saved us all and then some.  Things "
"were still tough, but from what I've heard, I might be the only person left "
"on the Eastern Seaboard who still has his whole nuclear family.  Still got a"
" lot of survivor's guilt for that… still lost everyone else.  Anyway, one "
"thing led to another and we gathered a few other people that we watch out "
"for.  My man Darius, he joined up early on and he and I do the scouting and "
"scavenging and watch each others' backs."
msgstr ""
"Eh, bueno, la versión corta es que salí con mi esposa y mis hijos del pueblo"
" muy al comienzo de todo. Ella tiene muy buena intuición para las cosas y "
"cuando me dijo que me preparara para salir del pueblo, me imaginé que como "
"mucho eran unas vacaciones innecesarias y tempranas de primavera en la vieja"
" cabaña de mi padre, ¿entiendes? Obviamente, resultó que confiar en su "
"intuición nos salvó. Las cosas siguieron siendo difíciles pero por lo que "
"escuché, puede que haya sido la única persona con la familia entera en toda "
"la costa este. Igual tengo mucha culpa de superviviente por eso… y perdí a "
"todos los demás. De todos modos, una cosa llevó a la otra y nos juntamos con"
" otra gente con la que nos cuidamos. Mi amigo Darius se unió al principio y "
"con él hacemos la exploración, rebuscar y cuidarnos las espaldas de los "
"demás."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Where are you guys located?  Can I join up too?"
msgstr "¿Donde están ubicados? ¿Puedo unirme a ustedes?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Tell me about Darius."
msgstr "Cuéntame acerca de Darius."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "How did you know things were going to go wrong?"
msgstr "¿Cómo sabías que las cosas iban a salir mal?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "That seems like a pretty unlikely story."
msgstr "Eso parece una historia bastante improbable."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Can you give me any advice?"
msgstr "¿Me puedes dar algún consejo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What did you used to do before?"
msgstr "¿Y antes a qué te dedicabas?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Let's change the subject.  What did you say you were doing here?"
msgstr "Vamos a cambiar de tema. ¿Qué me dijiste que hacías aquí?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"I'll be straight with you, I don't want to tell you too much about my "
"people, okay?  You seem all right, don't get me wrong, but I've seen some "
"scary fuckin' people out there, who come on all normal and then try to bite "
"your face off when they get you alone.  Everyone's reaction to the world's "
"end is a bit different.  Things are stable with my people now, but we don't "
"really welcome new faces anymore.  I wish it weren't that way.  Maybe if you"
" and I get to know each other better some day, I'll change my mind."
msgstr ""
"Te voy a ser sincero, no te quiero decir mucho acerca de mi gente, "
"¿entiendes? No es por ti, no me malinterpretes, pero conocí gente bastante "
"siniestra dando vueltas que van de normalitos y después intentan arrancarte "
"la cara de un mordisco cuando pueden. Es diferente la reacción de cada uno "
"frente al fin del mundo. Las cosas están bien ahora entre mi gente pero ya "
"no recibimos personas nuevas. Me gustaría que no tuviera que ser de esa "
"manera. Tal vez si nos conocemos mejor, algún día cambie mi parecer."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Your whole story seems a bit unlikely."
msgstr "Toda tu historia parece poco probable."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Talk to Darius if you want to know about Darius.  He's a good man, and he "
"won't bite-- ugh, sorry, that's a turn of phrase we should probably retire, "
"hey?  Anwyay.  I don't know if we'd have made it through the first days "
"without him.  He gets a bit jumpy around crowds since the riots though, so "
"he's out watching our stuff."
msgstr ""
"Habla con Darius si quieres saber algo de Darius. Es un buen tipo y no "
"muerde-- uh, perdón, esa frase deberíamos dejar de usarla ahora, ¿eh? Bueno."
" No sé si hubiéramos podido pasar los primeros días sin él. Se pone un poco "
"nervioso cuando hay mucha gente desde los disturbios, así que está cuidando "
"nuestras cosas."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Sometimes, I kinda wonder why other people *didn't* know things were going "
"to go wrong.  Hindsight is twenty-twenty, I guess.  I'll be honest though, "
"as much as I'd like to pat myself on the back, it wasn't me that figured it "
"out.  When the really early riots started out, even though they were way up "
"in the Midwest, my wife just had a bad feeling.  We'd been thinking of a "
"getaway anyway, and I had some time off, so we took it as an excuse to get "
"out to the cabin and wait for everything to blow over.  Here we are.  It "
"wasn't so much knowing how things were going to go, more just straight luck "
"that we trusted our - *her* - gut at the right time and lucked out."
msgstr ""
"A veces, me pregunto por qué otra gente *no sabía* que todo iba a salir mal."
" Pero es fácil con el diario del lunes, supongo. Para ser honesto, por mucho"
" que quiera felicitarme a mí mismo, yo no fui el que se dio cuenta. Cuando "
"empezaron los primeros disturbios, incluso aunque fueron bastante lejos en "
"el oeste, mi señora tuvo un mal presentimiento. Igual ya estábamos pensando "
"en irnos y yo tenía un poco de tiempo libre, así que lo usamos como excusa "
"para ir a la cabaña y esperar que todo explotara. Y aquí estamos. No "
"sabíamos qué iba a pasar, fue más bien suerte que confiamos en su instinto "
"en ese momento y tuvimos suerte."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*chuckles.  \"Lucky for me then it doesn't matter if you believe me.  I do "
"gotta say though, it's funny you and I, a pair of actual real-live zombie "
"hunters, are talking face to face and you think my *survival story* is the "
"unlikely thing.\""
msgstr ""
"*se ríe por lo bajo. \"Por suerte no importa si me crees o no. Tengo que "
"decir, eso sí, que es gracioso que tu y yo, un par de cazadores de zombi "
"verdaderos, estemos hablando cara a cara y tu pienses que mi *historia de "
"supervivencia* es una cosa bastante improbable.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"I do odd jobs if people need help.  Not on a volunteer basis you understand,"
" but I try not to be unfair about it either.  Lots of people need a bit of "
"help these days, often just with little things a scavenger like me can find "
"for them.  It's easy for folks like you and me to underestimate how scared a"
" lot of people are to go back out in that place.  The situation's bad enough"
" as it is, but these kind of people took refuge back when it was true chaos "
"out there.  Lots of trauma to unpack there.  Anyway, if there's little "
"things I can do for them, I try to help where I can, so long as it doesn't "
"put me in too much danger."
msgstr ""
"Hago trabajos raros si la gente necesita ayuda. No como voluntario, sabes, "
"pero trato de no ser injusto tampoco. Mucha gente necesita un poco de ayuda "
"estos días, a menudo es suficiente con lo poco que puede encontrar un "
"rebuscador como yo. Es fácil para la gente como tu y yo subestimar qué tanto"
" miedo de volver a ese lugar tienen las personas. La situación es "
"suficientemente mala pero este tipo de personas se refugiaron cuando comenzó"
" el verdadero caos. Muchos traumas para establecerse ahí. De todas maneras, "
"si hay alguna cosita que pueda hacer por ellos, intento ayudar cuando puedo,"
" siempre que no me ponga en peligro."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"You look like you can handle yourself in a fight.  What's your zombie kill "
"count?"
msgstr ""
"Tienes la apariencia de alguien que se maneja bien en las peleas. ¿Cuántos "
"zombi mataste?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I could use someone like you.  Want to travel with me?"
msgstr "Me vendría bien estar con alguien como tu. ¿Quieres viajar conmigo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "You seem to know a lot about how people feel."
msgstr "Parece que sabes mucho sobre cómo se siente la gente."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"You've got that right.  People like you and I are made of stronger stuff."
msgstr ""
"En eso tienes razón. La gente como tu y yo estamos hechos de complexión "
"robusta."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"People should learn to fend for themselves, not just get you to hand "
"everything to them."
msgstr ""
"La gente tiene que aprender a defenderse por sí sola, y no esperar que tu "
"les des todo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*laughs a bit sheepishly.  \"Seems distasteful to keep track of that stuff, "
"doesn't it?\"  He touches a series of notches on his <mywp>.  \"I'm human "
"though.  I'm up to <npc_val:zkc_john> so far.  Seems like a lot to me, "
"especially since I try to avoid actually engaging the enemy if I can help "
"it.\""
msgstr ""
"*se ríe un poco tímidamente. \"Parece de mal gusto tener registro de eso, "
"¿no te parece?\" Toca una serie de muescas en su <mywp>. \"Pero soy humano, "
"eh. Estoy por los <npc_val:zkc_john> por ahora. Parece mucho para mí, "
"especialmente porque intento evitar enfrentarme al enemigo si puedo.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*sizes you up and down, and shakes his head sadly.  \"Darius and I have a "
"good thing going, and a third person would be hard to justify, especially "
"these days.  Trust comes hard.  I'm sorry.  I hope you've got someone to "
"watch your back, but it can't be me.\""
msgstr ""
"*te evalúa de arriba abajo y mueve su cabeza tristemente. \"Darius y yo "
"tenemos algo bueno funcionando y una tercera persona sería difícil de "
"justificar, especialmente estos días. La confianza es difícil. Lo lamento. "
"Espero que tengas alguien que te cuide la espalda pero no puedo ser yo.\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"That's a shame.  We'd be a good team.  People like you and I are made of "
"stronger stuff."
msgstr ""
"Qué lástima. Haríamos un buen equipo. La gente como tu y yo estamos hechos "
"de complexión robusta."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Damn straight.  People should learn to fend for themselves."
msgstr "Exactamente. La gente debería aprender a defenderse por sí sola."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, I, uh… I know a bit about that stuff.  Hard not to empathize, "
"especially when I know I'm not quite as hard as others, by sheer luck.  "
"Besides, there are so few of us left now.  What's the point in wasting time "
"judging other people for how hard they took the end of the world?"
msgstr ""
"Sí, yo, eh… conozco un poco sobre eso. Es difícil no sentir empatía, "
"especialmente cuando sé que no soy tan duro como otros, de pura suerte. "
"Además, quedamos tan pocos ahora. ¿Para qué gastar tiempo juzgando a otras "
"personas sobre su manera de recibir el fin del mundo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "It sounds like you have some past there.  You want to talk about it?"
msgstr "Pareciera que tenias una historia ahí. ¿Quieres hablar sobre eso?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Not really, no.  It's old stuff, and there's enough going on.  Let's just "
"say I'm no stranger to loss, either my own or others'."
msgstr ""
"La verdad que no. Lo pasado, pasado esta, y el presente es suficiente. "
"Digamos solamente que estoy acostumbrado a la pérdida, sea la propia o la de"
" otros."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*raises an eyebrow.  \"I don't know about that.  You should be careful about"
" thinking people who don't make the same choices as you are inferior.  Sure,"
" not everyone's suited to scavenge, but a scavenger's got to have a safe "
"home, too.\""
msgstr ""
"*levanta una ceja. \"No sé. Tendrías que tener cuidado con eso de pensar que"
" los que no toman las mismas decisiones que tu son personas inferiores. Sí, "
"no todos están capacitados para rebuscar pero un rebuscador también tiene "
"que tener un lugar seguro.\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Fuck that.  People should learn to fend for themselves."
msgstr "Una mierda. La gente debería aprender a defenderse por sí sola."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*rubs his stubble, looking thoughtful.  \"I agree it's important to be "
"independent, but don't forget, working together is what makes us better than"
" the undead.  It's how we got out of the trees and fields, and into "
"civilization.  Anyway, I don't want to talk philosophy at you.  If you're "
"doing well on your own, more power to you!\""
msgstr ""
"*se toca la barba, como pensando. \"Estoy de acuerdo con que es importante "
"ser independiente pero no te olvides, trabajar en grupo es lo que nos hace "
"mejores que los muertos vivientes. Es por eso que salimos de los árboles y "
"los campos y fuimos hacia la civilización. Pero de todas maneras, no quiero "
"hablar de filosofía. Si tu estás bien solo, ¡más poder para ti!\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"That's for the weaklings.  People like you and I are made of stronger stuff."
msgstr ""
"Eso es para los debiluchos. La gente como tu y yo estamos hechos de "
"complexión robusta."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I don't know, the zombies sure seem to work together to me."
msgstr "No sé, a mí me parece que los zombi trabajan en grupo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*chuckles.  \"If you can call it that, sure.  So maybe we should do our best"
" to be better at that than the zombies.  Seems pretty reasonable to me, and "
"it's a pretty low bar to clear.\""
msgstr ""
"*se ríe. \"Puedes decirlo así si quieres, sí. Así que tal vez tengamos que "
"hacer mejor trabajo que los zombi en eso. A mí me parece razonable y la vara"
" de medir está bastante baja.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Sure, I guess.  I don't know if I know anything you don't, you seem like you"
" can handle yourself.  I've made it this far by not engaging whenever "
"possible.  I'm never going to kill all the zombies out there.  Darius and I "
"try not to fight if we can avoid it, and if we can't, we try to always have "
"the advantage.  Numbers, weaponry, terrain.  Zombies are clumsy and stupid "
"so we lead them across bushes and things to trip and stumble.  We take high "
"ground and let them plough into ladders like idiots while we stick 'em with "
"spears from above.  Mostly, though, we try not to be seen.  We use bikes "
"instead of cars because they don't make noise and don't need gas, plus we "
"can take forest trails and things and avoid traffic jams.  Those things are "
"suicide.  We try to avoid the cities, and when we do go close, we stick to "
"the outskirts and raid the outlying houses.  In those, we keep crouched and "
"try to get deep into the building fast, or down into the basement, so that "
"little noises don't carry much and nothing from outside can see us.  Also, "
"zombies being idiots, closing the blinds is a great move.  I always keep a "
"crowbar for opening doors and windows, but I try not to use it if I can "
"avoid it.  Darius can pick locks, which is slower but doesn't make noise.  "
"We get a lot more mileage from raiding gas stations and other rural sites, "
"where if there are a few zombies, we can usually lead them away."
msgstr ""
"Seguro, creo. No sé si sé algo que tu no sepas, tienes pinta de saber "
"manejarte. Sobreviví hasta ahora esquivando todo en la medida de lo posible."
" Nunca voy a poder matar a todos los zombis que andan por ahí. Darius y yo "
"tratamos de evitar el enfrentamiento y si no podemos, intentamos tener "
"siempre la ventaja. Cantidad, armas, terreno. Los zombis son torpes y "
"estúpidos así que los llevamos hacia los arbustos y cosas que los hagan "
"tropezar y caerse. Los esperamos en terreno elevado y los dejamos apilarse "
"en escaleras como idiotas mientras los atacamos con lanzas desde arriba. "
"Pero mayormente tratamos de que no nos vean. Usamos bicicleta en lugar de "
"autos porque no hacen ruido y no necesitan combustible, y además podemos "
"pasar por caminos en bosques y evitar los embotellamientos. Es casi un "
"suicidio andar en auto. Intentamos evitar las ciudades y cuando nos "
"acercamos, nos mantenemos por la parte externa saqueando las casas. Y "
"adentro de las casas nos mantenemos agachados y tratamos de meternos rápido "
"lejos de las aberturas o en el sótano, para que los ruidos no atraigan nada "
"de afuera que nos pudiera ver. Además, como los zombis son idiotas, cerrar "
"las cortinas es una buena idea. Siempre llevo una barreta para abrir puertas"
" o ventanas pero trato de no usarla si no es necesario. Darius puede abrir "
"cerraduras, es más lento pero no hace ruido. Sacamos mucho provecho de las "
"estaciones de servicio y de otros sitios rurales, donde si hay zombis los "
"podemos guiar hacia otro lado."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What about things other than zombies?"
msgstr "¿Y qué pasa con las otras cosas, las cosas que no son zombi?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Oh, jeez, yeah.  The world really went to shit, didn't it?  Well, I've seen "
"some weird alien things.  Our rule is 'scared is better than dead'.  If we "
"don't know what something is and how to kill it, we steer wide and clear.  "
"One time I saw this flaming eyeball a long way off, I was scouting from a "
"cell phone tower.  It made eye contact with me and I just started "
"hallucinating shit.  Darius stopped me from falling right off the tower.  "
"Stuff like that is why I think you have to be a bit off your rocker to "
"travel these days unless you have no choice.  Anything we don't know, we "
"turn around and pedal hard.  So far, we haven't met anything our bikes can't"
" outrun."
msgstr ""
"Ah, mierda, sí. El mundo se fue al carajo en serio, ¿no? Bueno, vi algunas "
"cosas raras extraterrestres. Nuestra regla es 'mejor asustado que muerto'. "
"Si no sabemos qué es y cómo matarlo, nos mantenemos alejados. Una vez vimos "
"un ojo llameante a lo lejos, yo estaba mirando desde una torre de telefonía "
"celular. Hizo contacto visual conmigo y yo empecé a alucinar cosas raras. "
"Darius evitó que me cayera de la torre. Las cosas como esa son las que me "
"hacen pensar que tienes que estar un poco mal de la cabeza para viajar en "
"estos tiempos, salvo que no tengas otra opción. Cualquier cosa que no "
"conozcamos, damos la vuelta y pedaleamos fuerte. Hasta ahora, no nos "
"cruzamos con nada que sea más rápido que nuestras bicicletas."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"That's a tougher question than you might think.  I've had quite the life.  "
"My dad was a mechanic, and when I was young I used to help around the shop "
"quite a bit.  I started out thinking I was going to get into that line of "
"work, but then I got sidetracked and wound up getting into computers and "
"electrical work for a long time.  Did part of an electrical engineering "
"degree, then decided it wasn't for me and quit that.  Spent a bit of time "
"doing freelance electrical and programming work, then got recruited by a "
"startup that was designing and programming medical equipment.  I was "
"supposed to be a general technician, but through a weird series of events I "
"wound up in sales, then management.  I hated management, and I'd made a big "
"nest egg from my share stock, so I cashed out and tried to retire young.  "
"That was a dumb move, I was bored as hell, so I finished off my degree and "
"started doing on-call teaching work for shop, computers, math, and things "
"like that at a college and high school level.  Just part time, and I spent "
"the rest of my time outdoors, hiking and whatnot."
msgstr ""
"Esa es una pregunta más difícil de lo que piensas. Tuve una buena vida. Mi "
"papá era mecánico y cuando era niño lo ayudaba bastante en el negocio. "
"Empecé a pensar que me iba a quedar en ese trabajo pero me desvié y terminé "
"metiéndome en ordenadores y electrónica por mucho tiempo. Hice parte de la "
"carrera de ingeniería electrónica y después decidí que no era para mí y la "
"dejé. Estuve un tiempo haciendo trabajos electrónicos y de programación, "
"después me contrataron para una empresa nueva que estaba diseñando y "
"programando equipamiento médico. Se suponía que yo era técnico general pero "
"por una serie rara de eventos terminé en ventas, y después en la gerencia. "
"Odiaba estar en gerencia y había juntado unos ahorros, así que vendí mis "
"acciones e intenté jubilarme joven. Eso fue una mala idea, me aburría un "
"montón así que termine la carrera y empecé a enseñar comercio, informática, "
"matemática y cosas así en la universidad y en secundaria. Pero solo media "
"jornada y pasaba el resto fuera, en excursiones y caminatas."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"That is one hell of a life.  You must have some useful skills to teach."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"I'd be happy to.  I can't spare a lot of free time, but for a little trade, "
"I'll tell you about whatever I can help with."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Sorry, but that's all I have time for at the moment.  Darius is waiting "
"outside."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Sure, let's talk trade."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I'll bear that in mind.  What did you say you were doing here?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Thanks, I'll think about it.  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "Gracias, lo pensare. ¿Qué estabas diciendo antes?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I might take you up on that, but for now I've gotta go."
msgstr ""

