msgid_plural "copies of Memoirs of the Champion of Earth"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ 5 earthshaper spells
#. ~ Description of "Memoirs of the Champion of Earth"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid ""
"A book written by someone obviously very self-absorbed who describes himself"
" as \"Chosen of Gaia, the Only Champion of Terra\".  Despite his arrogance, "
"his mastery in combining different earthshaper's abilities as described in "
"the book make him an accomplished sorcerer worth learning from."
msgstr ""

#. ~ 1 earthshaper spell. yes, the whole book is only for one, that's the idea
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid "One Spell is All You Need!"
msgid_plural "copies of One Spell is All You Need!"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ 1 earthshaper spell. yes, the whole book is only for one, that's the idea
#. ~ Description of "One Spell is All You Need!"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid ""
"This advertising booklet promotes one spell that allows you to create a "
"different tool for different purposes.  Surprisingly, it works as the book "
"says - you can change the shape of your tool, depending on your needs."
msgstr ""

#. ~ 5 Magus spells
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid "The Tome of Magical Movement"
msgid_plural "copies of The Tome of Magical Movement"
msgstr[0] "El Tomo del Movimiento Mágico"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Tomo del Movimiento Mágico"
msgstr[2] "copias de El Tomo del Movimiento Mágico"

#. ~ 5 Magus spells
#. ~ Description of "The Tome of Magical Movement"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This small lightweight book seems to almost not entirely exist, let's say it"
" 97% does.  It contains Magus spells focused on movement."
msgstr ""
"Este pequeño libro ligero parece no existir completamente, digamos que  "
"existe en un 97%. Contiene hechizos del Magus centrados en el movimiento."

#. ~ Druid spell
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid "Smudged Scroll"
msgid_plural "Smudged Scrolls"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino Manchado"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos Manchados"
msgstr[2] "Pergaminos Manchados"

#. ~ Druid spell
#. ~ Description of "Smudged Scroll"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid ""
"This looks like someone was designing a new spell, but spilled a mug of "
"coffee on it and crumpled it up in anger.  You can tell that it will "
"definitely cast something, but you can't be sure that it will work very "
"well."
msgstr ""
"Parece que alguien estaba diseñando un nuevo hechizo, pero derramó una taza "
"de café sobre él y lo arrugó con rabia. Te das cuenta de que definitivamente"
" invocará algo, pero no puedes estar seguro de que funcione muy bien."

#. ~ 3 Animist spells
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid "Necromantic Minions for Dummies"
msgid_plural "copies of Necromantic Minions for Dummies"
msgstr[0] "Esbirros Necrománticos para Tontos"
msgstr[1] "copias de Esbirros Necrománticos para Tontos"
msgstr[2] "copias de Esbirros Necrománticos para Tontos"

#. ~ 3 Animist spells
#. ~ Description of "Necromantic Minions for Dummies"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid ""
"This book details various ways of summoning an undead minion to fight for "
"you.  They all appear to disappear after a short time, crumbling to dust."
msgstr ""
"Este libro detalla varias formas de invocar a un esbirro no-muerto para que "
"pelee por ti. Todos desaparecen después de un corto tiempo, deshaciéndose en"
" polvo."

#. ~ 4 Technomancer spells
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid "Fundamentals of Technomancy"
msgid_plural "copies of Fundamentals of Technomancy"
msgstr[0] "Fundamentos de la Tecnomancía"
msgstr[1] "copias de Fundamentos de la Tecnomancía"
msgstr[2] "copias de Fundamentos de la Tecnomancía"

#. ~ 4 Technomancer spells
#. ~ Description of "Fundamentals of Technomancy"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid ""
"This thick manual instructs the spellcaster on manipulating and empowering "
"various forms of matter and energy."
msgstr ""
"Este grueso manual instruye al hechicero en la manipulación y potenciación "
"de varias formas de materia y energía."

#. ~ 2 Technomancer spells
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid "Complete Idiot's Guide to Technomancy"
msgid_plural "copies of Complete Idiot's Guide to Technomancy"
msgstr[0] "Guía Completa del Idiota Sobre la Tecnomancia"
msgstr[1] "copias de la Guía Completa del Idiota Sobre la Tecnomancia"
msgstr[2] "copias de la Guía Completa del Idiota Sobre la Tecnomancia"

#. ~ 2 Technomancer spells
#. ~ Description of "Complete Idiot's Guide to Technomancy"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid ""
"This colorful guide, full of diagrams and cartoons, teaches a couple of very"
" basic Technomancy spells for the not-so-bright pupils."
msgstr ""
"Esta colorida guía, llena de diagramas y dibujos animados, enseña un par de "
"hechizos muy básicos de Tecnomancía para los alumnos no tan brillantes."

#. ~ 3 Technomancer spells
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid "Technomancy and the Electromagnetic Spectrum"
msgid_plural "copies of Technomancy and the Electromagnetic Spectrum"
msgstr[0] "Tecnomancia y el Espectro Electromagnético"
msgstr[1] "copias de Tecnomancia y el Espectro Electromagnético"
msgstr[2] "copias de Tecnomancia y el Espectro Electromagnético"

#. ~ 3 Technomancer spells
#. ~ Description of "Technomancy and the Electromagnetic Spectrum"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid ""
"This lab reference material book is thick and overflowing with information "
"on combining magic with EM radiation."
msgstr ""
"Este libro de referencia de laboratorio es grueso y desborda con información"
" sobre combinar magia con radiación electromagnética."

#. ~ 2 animist and 1 classless spells
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid "Liminal Pathways"
msgid_plural "copies of Liminal Pathways"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ 2 animist and 1 classless spells
#. ~ Description of "Liminal Pathways"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid ""
"A famous animist grimoire from early modernity.  Its cryptic passages "
"describe and map connections between the spiritual world and ours."
msgstr ""

#. ~ 2 animist spells
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid "Runic Tablet shard"
msgid_plural "Runic Tablet shards"
msgstr[0] "fragmento de Tableta Rúnica"
msgstr[1] "fragmentos de Tableta Rúnica"
msgstr[2] "fragmentos de Tableta Rúnica"

#. ~ 2 animist spells
#. ~ Description of "Runic Tablet shard"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid ""
"A small tablet of blackened stone, apparently cut from a much larger slab.  "
"Golden runes glow over its surface, and slowly shift into intelligible "
"sentences when you stare at them."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña tableta de piedra ennegrecida, aparentemente cortada de una losa"
" mucho más grande. Las runas doradas brillan sobre su superficie, y "
"lentamente se convierten en frases inteligibles cuando las miras."

#. ~ 1 classless spell
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid "Geospatial Systems: The Lie Of Linearity"
msgid_plural "copies of Geospatial Systems: The Lie Of Linearity"
msgstr[0] "Sistemas Geoespaciales: La Mentira de la Linealidad"
msgstr[1] "copias de Sistemas Geoespaciales: La Mentira de la Linealidad"
msgstr[2] "copias de Sistemas Geoespaciales: La Mentira de la Linealidad"

#. ~ 1 classless spell
#. ~ Description of "Geospatial Systems: The Lie Of Linearity"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid ""
"This book outlines in great detail how time and space are wibbly-wobbly and "
"non-Euclidean.  It also appears to have a dozen different coordinate systems"
" that it uses nearly interchangeably, which makes it hard to follow.  "
"There's lots of jargon, but with intense study you can probably learn a "
"thing or two about portals."
msgstr ""
"Este libro describe con gran detalle cómo el tiempo y el espacio son "
"tambaleantes y no son euclidianos. También parece tener una docena de "
"sistemas de coordenadas diferentes que utiliza casi indistintamente, lo que "
"hace que sea difícil de seguir. Hay mucha jerga, pero con un intenso estudio"
" probablemente puedas aprender una o dos cosas sobre los portales."

#. ~ 1 Magus spell, 1 Druid spell, 2 Animist spells
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid "Forbidden Tome"
msgid_plural "Forbidden Tomes"
msgstr[0] "Tomo Prohibido"
msgstr[1] "Tomos Prohibidos"
msgstr[2] "Tomos Prohibidos"

#. ~ 1 Magus spell, 1 Druid spell, 2 Animist spells
#. ~ Description of "Forbidden Tome"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid ""
"A very, very old and heavy tome of various spells lost to the ages, either "
"for good reason, or simply through the passage of time.  There are very few "
"copies in existence, usually owned by those of great power, and yet all of "
"them seem to have the last dozen pages or so torn out, in haste."
msgstr ""
"Un tomo muy, muy antiguo y pesado de varios hechizos perdidos en el tiempo, "
"ya sea por una buena razón, o simplemente por el paso del tiempo. Existen "
"muy pocos ejemplares, normalmente propiedad de personas de gran poder, y sin"
" embargo todos parecen tener la última docena de páginas arrancadas a toda "
"prisa."

#. ~ 4 Magus spells
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid "Transcendence of the Human Condition"
msgid_plural "copies of Transcendence of the Human Condition"
msgstr[0] "Trascendencia de la Condición Humana"
msgstr[1] "copias de Trascendencia de la Condición Humana"
msgstr[2] "copias de Trascendencia de la Condición Humana"

#. ~ 4 Magus spells
#. ~ Description of "Transcendence of the Human Condition"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid ""
"The Human is the only creature that seeks to improve himself.  This study "
"examines different spells that can heighten various senses temporarily, in "
"hopes to discover a more permanent solution."
msgstr ""
"El Humano es la única criatura que busca mejorarse a sí mismo. Este estudio "
"examina diferentes hechizos que pueden aumentar varios sentidos "
"temporalmente, con la esperanza de descubrir una solución más permanente."

#. ~ 3 Magus spells, 1 Technomancer spell
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid "Wherever You've Gone, There You Can Be"
msgid_plural "copies of Wherever You've Gone, There You Can Be"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ 3 Magus spells, 1 Technomancer spell
#. ~ Description of "Wherever You've Gone, There You Can Be"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid ""
"A very sarcastically-written guide to using magic to get into and out of "
"places you absolutely are not supposed to be."
msgstr ""

#. ~ 3 Druid spells, 1 Earthshaper spell, 1 Biomancer spell, 2 Kelvinist
#. spells
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid "It's the End of the World, But You'll Feel Fine"
msgid_plural "copies of It's the End of the World, But You'll Feel Fine"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ 3 Druid spells, 1 Earthshaper spell, 1 Biomancer spell, 2 Kelvinist
#. spells
#. ~ Description of "It's the End of the World, But You'll Feel Fine"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
msgid ""
"This thick paperback book is a collection of the proper magical preparations"
" to survive various disasters.  Unfortunately, the zombie apocalypse section"
" doesn't account for everything that's gone wrong in the Cataclysm, but "
"there's still a lot of useful knowledge here."
msgstr ""

#. ~ I went ahead and gave this a level of 2 for when magical mutagens become
#. a thing as I figured dragonblood for instance should need different tools
#. than making alpha mutagen.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/tools.json
msgid "cauldron of purification"
msgid_plural "cauldrons of purification"
msgstr[0] "caldera de purificación"
msgstr[1] "calderas de purificación"
msgstr[2] "calderas de purificación"

#. ~ I went ahead and gave this a level of 2 for when magical mutagens become
#. a thing as I figured dragonblood for instance should need different tools
#. than making alpha mutagen.
#. ~ Description of "cauldron of purification"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/tools.json
msgid ""
"This cauldron made of demon spider chitin seems to absorb the light.  It "
"will hold 16 liters of material and will absorb poisons from it.  It may "
"have other properties that require discovery."
msgstr ""
"Este caldero hecho de quitina de araña demoníaca parece absorber la luz. "
"Contendrá 16 litros de material y absorberá venenos de él. Puede tener otras"
" propiedades que requieren ser descubiertas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/tools.json
msgid "orichalcum cauldron"
msgid_plural "orichalcum cauldrons"
msgstr[0] "caldera de oricalco"
msgstr[1] "calderas de oricalco"
msgstr[2] "calderas de oricalco"

#. ~ Description of "orichalcum cauldron"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/tools.json
msgid ""
"This is an alchemical cauldron made of orichalcum.  The metal is especially "
"resistant to the unique types of corrosion caused by alchemy."
msgstr ""
"Este es un caldero alquímico hecho de oricalco. El metal es especialmente "
"resistente a los tipos únicos de corrosión causados por la alquimia."

#. ~ Description of "demon forge"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/tools.json
msgid ""
"This is a portable version of the charcoal forge that is magically enhanced "
"and fortified with demon spider chitin in order to be able to resmelt "
"magical metals into their workable ingot form."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una versión portátil de la fragua de carbón vegetal que está "
"mejorada mágicamente y fortificada con quitina de araña demoníaca para poder"
" refundir metales mágicos en forma de lingote."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/tools.json
msgid "fireproof mortar"
msgid_plural "fireproof mortar"
msgstr[0] "mortero ignífugo"
msgstr[1] "mortero ignífugo"
msgstr[2] "mortero ignífugo"

#. ~ Description of "fireproof mortar"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/tools.json
msgid ""
"Some alchemical mortar, ready to be used in building projects expecting "
"temperatures on par with dragonbreath."
msgstr ""
"Mortero alquímico, listo para ser usado en proyectos de construcción que "
"esperan temperaturas a la par con el aliento de dragón."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/tools.json
msgid "parabolan wool staple"
msgid_plural "parabolan wool staples"
msgstr[0] "fibras de lana de parabolan"
msgstr[1] "fibras de lana de parabolan"
msgstr[2] "fibras de lana de parabolan"

#. ~ Description of "parabolan wool staple"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/tools.json
msgid ""
"The natural cluster of parabolan wool fibers.  Could be processed to felt "
"patches or yarns."
msgstr ""
"El racimo natural de fibras de lana parabólica. Se puede transformar en "
"parches o hilos de fieltro."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/tools.json
msgid "glassteel shard"
msgid_plural "glassteel shards"
msgstr[0] "fragmento de cristal de acero"
msgstr[1] "fragmentos de cristal de acero"
msgstr[2] "fragmentos de cristal de acero"

#. ~ Description of "glassteel shard"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/tools.json
msgid ""
"A broken shard of glassteel covered in sharp edges.  You could use it as a "
"weapon, but you might want to wear gloves."
msgstr ""
"Un fragmento roto de cristal de acero cubierto de bordes afilados. Podrías "
"usarlo como arma, pero quizá quieras usar guantes."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/tools.json
msgid "Magic Circle Rank 1"
msgid_plural "Magic Circles Rank 2"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "Magic Circle Rank 1"
#. ~ Description of "Magic Circle Rank 2"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/tools.json
msgid ""
"This is the pseudo-tool provided by having a nearby magic circle.  You "
"shouldn't see this as an individual item."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/tools.json
msgid "Magic Circle Rank 2"
msgid_plural "Magic Circles Rank 2"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "bulette plating"
msgstr "chapado de bulette"

#. ~ A heavier version of the standard shillelagh (from melee.json) with a
#. different description to match the lizardfolk lore.  Not craftable, but
#. wieldable if discovered.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/weapons.json
msgid "greatclub"
msgid_plural "greatclubs"
msgstr[0] "garrote grande"
msgstr[1] "garrotes grandes"
msgstr[2] "garrotes grandes"

#. ~ A heavier version of the standard shillelagh (from melee.json) with a
#. different description to match the lizardfolk lore.  Not craftable, but
#. wieldable if discovered.
#. ~ Description of "greatclub"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/weapons.json
msgid ""
"A stout knotty club with a large knob at the top.  While it's very heavy, "
"it's a very effective weapon in the hands of a strong opponent."
msgstr ""
"Es un palo robusto y nudoso con una gran perilla en la parte superior. "
"Aunque es muy pesado, es un arma muy efectiva en las manos de un oponente "
"fuerte."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/weapons.json
msgid "wood trident"
msgid_plural "wood tridents"
msgstr[0] "tridente de madera"
msgstr[1] "tridentes de madera"
msgstr[2] "tridentes de madera"

#. ~ Description of "wood trident"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/weapons.json
msgid ""
"A wooden melee weapon with a hand-forged steel forked spearhead attached to "
"the end.  It can be used for stabbing opponents either in close-range or as "
"a thrown weapon, and in the right hands can also readily disarm opponents."
msgstr ""
"Un arma de madera c. a c. con una punta de acero forjado a mano y con una "
"horquilla en el extremo. Puede ser usada para apuñalar a los oponentes, ya "
"sea a corta distancia o como arma arrojada, y en las manos correctas también"
" puede desarmar fácilmente a los oponentes."

#. ~ A barbed version of the standard javelin (from spears_and_polearms.json)
#. with a different description to match the lizardfolk lore.  Not craftable,
#. but wieldable if discovered.
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/weapons.json
msgid "barbed javelin"
msgid_plural "barbed javelins"
msgstr[0] "jabalina con alambre de púas"
msgstr[1] "jabalinas con alambre de púas"
msgstr[2] "jabalinas con alambre de púas"

#. ~ A barbed version of the standard javelin (from spears_and_polearms.json)
#. with a different description to match the lizardfolk lore.  Not craftable,
#. but wieldable if discovered.
#. ~ Description of "barbed javelin"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/weapons.json
msgid ""
"This weapon measures about 3 feet in length and is fletched like an arrow "
"for better accuracy.  The business end of the javelin has wicked-looking "
"barbs which could cause significant bleeding."
msgstr ""
"Esta arma mide alrededor de 3 pies de largo y se flexiona como una flecha "
"para una mejor precisión. El extremo de la jabalina tiene púas de aspecto "
"malvado que podrían causar una hemorragia significativa."

#. ~ Description of gun "barbed javelin"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/weapons.json
msgid "Fake gun that fires barbed javelins."
msgstr "Pistola falsa que dispara jabalinas de púas."

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/vehicle/frames.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/vehicleparts/frames.json
msgid "foldable orichalcum frame"
msgid_plural "foldable orichalcum frames"
msgstr[0] "chasis plegable de oricalco"
msgstr[1] "chasis plegables de oricalco"
msgstr[2] "chasis plegables de oricalco"

#. ~ Description of "foldable orichalcum frame"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/vehicle/frames.json
msgid ""
"A folding frame made of orichalcum pipes.  Not as light as aluminum, but "
"significantly sturdier."
msgstr ""
"Un chasis plegable hecho de tubos de oricalco. No tan ligero como el "
"aluminio, pero significativamente más resistente."

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/vehicle/frames.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/vehicleparts/frames.json
msgid "orichalcum frame"
msgid_plural "orichalcum frames"
msgstr[0] "chasis de oricalco"
msgstr[1] "chasis de oricalco"
msgstr[2] "chasis de oricalco"

#. ~ Description of "orichalcum frame"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/vehicle/frames.json
msgid ""
"A frame made of orichalcum.  Significantly sturdier than steel, but also "
"much more expensive."
msgstr ""
"Un chasis hecho de oricalco. Significativamente más robusto que el acero, "
"pero también mucho más caro."

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/vehicle/frames.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/vehicleparts/frames.json
msgid "light orichalcum frame"
msgid_plural "light orichalcum frames"
msgstr[0] "chasis ligero de oricalco"
msgstr[1] "chasis ligeros de oricalco"
msgstr[2] "chasis ligeros de oricalco"

#. ~ Description of "light orichalcum frame"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/vehicle/frames.json
msgid ""
"A frame made of orichalcum.  Partially torn down in order to reduce weight "
"at the cost of durability."
msgstr ""
"Un chasis hecho de oricalco. Parcialmente desmontado para reducir el peso a "
"costa de la durabilidad."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/vehicle/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "magic v-twin combustion engine"
msgid_plural "magic v-twin combustion engines"
msgstr[0] "motor de combustión bicilíndrico mágico"
msgstr[1] "motores de combustión bicilíndricos mágicos"
msgstr[2] "motores de combustión bicilíndricos mágicos"

#. ~ Description of "magic v-twin combustion engine"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/vehicle/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A magically manifested combustion engine.  Despite operating entirely off of"
" mana rather than normal fuel, it otherwise functions exactly as a "
"conventional internal combustion engine."
msgstr ""
"Un motor de combustión manifestado mágicamente. A pesar de funcionar "
"completamente con maná en lugar de con combustible normal, su funcionamiento"
" es idéntico al de un motor de combustión interna convencional."

